        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST003328</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Germline polymorphisms in an enhancer of PSIP1 are associated with progression-free survival in epithelial ovarian cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26840454</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4872719/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In Phase 1, we conducted a genome-wide scan on germline DNA from 385 patients from the Australian Ovarian Cancer Study (AOCS, n = 183), the Mayo Clinic (MAYO, n = 68) and The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA, n = 134) and performed a meta-analysis summarizing results from these cohorts (refer to Methods for details of genotyping and imputation).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
