        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of men and women, mostly aged 35–70 years, recruited during 1992–2000 at 23 centres in ten European countries and followed prospectively to investigate relationships between nutrition, lifestyle, cancer and other diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12639222</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000065"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">519978</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants recruited in 23 centres, 10 countries (2002)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:12639222</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study currently includes 519 978 participants (366 521 women and 153 457 men, mostly aged 35-70 years) in 23 centres located in 10 European countries, to be followed for cancer incidence and cause-specific mortality for several decades.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
