        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19765918+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Extremely low gestational age newborns (ELGANs) are at increased risk for structural and functional brain abnormalities.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid937"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>brain damage</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19765918+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Extremely low gestational age newborns (ELGANs) are at increased risk for structural and functional brain abnormalities.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ohiostate.elsevierpure.com/en/publications/histologic-chorioamnionitis-and-risk-of-neurodevelopmental-impair/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>enrolled extremely preterm newborns from 2002 to 2004 at 14 hospitals in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001003635</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide postnatal changes in immunity following fetal inflammatory response.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33006196</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8049052/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>raw microarray gene expression data files from paired frozen and unfrozen DBS samples from nine neonates of the US ELGAN cohort, where two were affected by FIR and seven were not.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104362</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Innovative computational approaches shed light on genetic mechanisms underlying cognitive impairment among children born extremely preterm.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35240980</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8903548/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>we utilized samples from the extremely low gestational age newborns (ELGAN) cohort [37], the largest US-based study of children born extremely preterm, to identify genetic factors associated with cognitive impairment at age 10 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32721520</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Placental genomic and epigenomic signatures associated with infant birth weight highlight mechanisms involved in collagen and growth factor signaling.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32721520</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7855285/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>data were leveraged from the previously established Extremely Low Gestational Age Newborns (ELGAN) cohort</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PXD041694</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Prenatal Metal Exposure Alters the Placental Proteome in a Sex-Dependent Manner in Extremely Low Gestational Age Newborns: Links to Gestational Age.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37834424</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pride/ws/archive/v2/projects/PXD041694</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We hypothesized that sex-specific patterns of metal-associated placental protein expression would be observed, and metals presence would be positively associated with the altered expression of inflammation-associated pathways Using samples banked from the Extremely Low Gestational Age Newborn Study (ELGAN), umbilical cord tissue samples were analyzed via ICP-MS/MS for trace elements, and placental samples underwent a global untargeted proteomics analysis via LC-MS/MS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A birth cohort of infants born before 28 weeks of gestation at 14 sites, followed to investigate exposures associated with brain injury and subsequent neurological and developmental outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19765918</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1506</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>infants born before 28 weeks enrolled at 14 sites</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19765918</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We enrolled 1506 ELGANs born before 28 weeks gestation at 14 sites; 1201 (80%) survived to 2 years corrected age.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ELGAN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


