        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001241</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale genome-wide association analysis of bipolar disorder identifies a new susceptibility locus near ODZ4.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21926972</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pmc&amp;id=3637176</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Psychiatric Genome-wide Association Study Consortium (PGC)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of genome-wide association studies that combines data on attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, autism, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder and schizophrenia through meta-analysis to investigate genetic susceptibility to psychiatric disorders.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20955924</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">33332</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls (controls include trio pseudocontrols) across the five disorders in the 2013 cross-disorder analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3714010/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The final dataset consisted of 33 332 cases and 27 888 controls (including pseudocontrols formed from non-transmitted alleles) distributed among the five disorder groups: autism spectrum disorders (4788 trio cases, 4788 trio pseudocontrols, 161 cases, 526 controls), attention deficit-hyperactivity disorder (1947 trio cases, 1947 trio pseudocontrols, 840 cases, 688 controls), bipolar disorder (6990 cases, 4820 controls), major depressive disorder (9227 cases, 7383 controls), and schizophrenia (9379 cases, 7736 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">27888</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls (controls include trio pseudocontrols) across the five disorders in the 2013 cross-disorder analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3714010/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The final dataset consisted of 33 332 cases and 27 888 controls (including pseudocontrols formed from non-transmitted alleles) distributed among the five disorder groups: autism spectrum disorders (4788 trio cases, 4788 trio pseudocontrols, 161 cases, 526 controls), attention deficit-hyperactivity disorder (1947 trio cases, 1947 trio pseudocontrols, 840 cases, 688 controls), bipolar disorder (6990 cases, 4820 controls), major depressive disorder (9227 cases, 7383 controls), and schizophrenia (9379 cases, 7736 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
