    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/abstract/MED/32367290</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Rotterdam Study is an ongoing prospective cohort study that started in 1990 in the city of Rotterdam, The Netherlands</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001008117</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Plasma MicroRNA Signatures of Aging</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001008117</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>2,684 participants from the population-based Rotterdam Study cohort</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013658</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common and Rare Variants Genetic Association Analysis of Circulating Neutrophil Extracellular Traps.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33717105</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:33717105%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) and exome-sequencing analysis to identify common and rare genetic variants associated with plasma myeloperoxidase (MPO)-DNA complex levels, a biomarker for NETs, in the population-based Rotterdam Study cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PXD057946</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Extreme MetaboHealth scores in three cohort studies associate with plasma protein markers for inflammation and cholesterol transport.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40926231</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12418662/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Using a Luminex cytokine assay and liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry-based proteomics we explored the plasma proteins associating with the difference in 100 extreme scoring individuals selected from two large population cohorts, the Leiden Longevity Study (LLS) and the Rotterdam Study (RS), and discordant monozygotic twin pairs from the Netherlands Twin Register (NTR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of middle-aged and older residents of Rotterdam, the Netherlands, established in 1990 and followed prospectively to investigate the causes, early development and natural history of chronic diseases and possible targets for intervention.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32367290</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17931</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants aged 40 and over across the four sub-cohorts (RS-I to RS-IV), 2024</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38324224</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study currently includes 17,931 participants (overall response rate 65%), aged 40 years and over, who are examined in-person every 3 to 5 years in a dedicated research facility, and who are followed-up continuously through automated linkage with health care providers, both regionally and nationally.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>RS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


