        <obo:IAO_0000116>autism spectrum disorders</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.sfari.org/funded-project/the-simons-simplex-collection/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Simons Simplex Collection (SSC) is a rigorously characterized set of data drawn from 2,700 families, designed to enrich the discovery of rare and de novo events in autism spectrum disorders.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0137725</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The simplex families were recruited through 12 university affiliated research clinics located in Canada and the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001005753</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Rare Variant Score Associates With Morphological Subtypes of Autism Spectrum Disorder</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001005753</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>442 ASD probands that had accompanying morphology data in the Simons Simplex Collection</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST002639</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of autism using the Simons Simplex Collection: Does reducing phenotypic heterogeneity in autism increase genetic homogeneity?</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25534755</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:25534755%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genome-wide genotypic data of 2576 families from the Simons Simplex Collection were analyzed in the overall sample and phenotypic subgroups defined on the basis of diagnosis, IQ, and symptom profiles.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of families recruited through 12 North American clinical sites, each with one child aged 4–18 with an autism spectrum disorder and unaffected biological parents, often including unaffected siblings, assembled to investigate rare and de novo genetic contributions to autism.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.sfari.org/funded-project/the-simons-simplex-collection/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
