        <rdfs:comment>The BMES protocol has been described in detail by Mitchell et al.32 Participants were genotyped with Human660W-Quad (Illumina) as part of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 (WTCCC2) at the Sanger Institute, Hinxton, United Kingdom.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3299635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used genome-wide association data generated by the Wellcome Trust Case-Control Consortium 2 (WTCCC2) from UK patients with Parkinson&apos;s disease and UK control individuals from the 1958 Birth Cohort and National Blood Service.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2719288/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Individuals included in the study were living within England, Scotland and Wales (‘Great Britain’)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00000000097</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study in multiple human prion diseases suggests genetic risk factors additional to PRNP</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00000000097</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>6015 control individuals (provided by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium and KORA-gen)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90204200</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of REM sleep behavior disorder identifies polygenic risk and brain expression effects.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36470867</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9722930/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Accordingly, for controls, we used genotype data obtained from (a) French and French-Canadian controls from McGill University (N = 871); (b) the HYPERGENES Project54 (N = 557 Italian samples); (c) the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium55 (N = 5516 British samples);</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of disease-specific case collections and shared controls, coordinated by United Kingdom research groups to identify genetic variants associated with common diseases and evaluate methods for genome-wide association analysis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17554300</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2938</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases of 7 diseases and shared controls retained after QC in the 2007 WTCCC1 GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2719288</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We excluded 809 samples after checks for contamination, false identity, non-Caucasian ancestry and relatedness (see Methods and Supplementary Table 4); 16,179 individuals remained in the study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16179</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases of 7 diseases and shared controls retained after QC in the 2007 WTCCC1 GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2719288</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We excluded 809 samples after checks for contamination, false identity, non-Caucasian ancestry and relatedness (see Methods and Supplementary Table 4); 16,179 individuals remained in the study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
