    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid2124">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid2124"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10348471/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ely study, established in 1990, is a prospective study of the etiology of type 2 diabetes, as described in detail elsewhere (18, 19).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20576086/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We recruited from a population-based cohort in Cambridgeshire, UK, (Medical Research Council Ely Study)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267567</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study and functional characterization identifies candidate genes for insulin-stimulated glucose uptake.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37291194</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PXD039023</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Impact of Acute Nutritional Interventions on the Plasma Proteome.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36658456</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/pride/ws/archive/v2/projects/PXD039023</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ely study comprises individuals of European ancestry aged 50–79 years, registered at a single medical practice in Ely, Cambridgeshire, UK and evaluated in three phases. All participants of the Ely study gave their written informed consent and the study was approved by the local ethics committee. Two hundred participants from Ely phase 3 with complete fasting and OGTT sample availability were selected for measurement (105 women / 95 men).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of adults without diabetes aged 40–69 at baseline in Ely, England, followed from 1990 with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical assessments to investigate type 2 diabetes incidence and its relationship to impaired fasting glucose.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17257284</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000198"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1040</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>non-diabetic adults aged 40-69 at baseline analysed for 1990-2000 incidence (analysed subset)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17257284</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Population-based longitudinal study (1990-2000) with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements, including an oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT), in 1040 non-diabetic adults aged 40-69 years at baseline.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
