        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000022"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>EGAS00001007563</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of women with HER2-positive breast cancer enrolled in the Cancer and Leukemia Group B 40601 phase III trial of neoadjuvant paclitaxel with trastuzumab and/or lapatinib, profiled alongside NeoALTTO for immune features that predict prognosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">305</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#EGA_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CALGB 40601</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid2302">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0006244"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000227"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid2302"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HER2-positive breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001007563</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we investigated the complexity of B and T cell receptor (BCR and TCR) repertoires, reflecting antigen-specific immune response, in the context of two phase III trials, namely NeoALTTO and CALGB 40601, evaluating neoadjuvant paclitaxel with trastuzumab and/or lapatinib in women affected by HER2-positive breast cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000227"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001007563</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Immune and clinicopathological features predict HER2-positive breast cancer prognosis in the neoadjuvant NeoALTTO and CALGB 40601 trials</dcterms:title>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000227"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of women with HER2-positive breast cancer enrolled in the Cancer and Leukemia Group B 40601 phase III trial of neoadjuvant paclitaxel with trastuzumab and/or lapatinib, profiled alongside NeoALTTO for immune features that predict prognosis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001007563</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000227"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">305</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients randomised in the phase III trial</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26527775</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among 305 randomly assigned patients (THL, n = 118; TH, n = 120; TL, n = 67), the pCR rate was 56% (95% CI, 47% to 65%) with THL and 46% (95% CI, 37% to 55%) with TH (P = .13)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


