        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">219</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lymphoma genomes with matched normals analysed (adult cohort plus Burkitt lymphomas), analysed subset</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33953289</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We identified 4538 clusters of very high mutation density (termed kataegis clusters) [27, 28] in 219 lymphoma genomes (consisting of 179 genomes from this study plus 39 pediatric BLs [17] and one adult BL, Supplementary Table S2), using a definition of a maximal intermutation distance of 1000 bp and a minimum of five mutations per cluster.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


