    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An Innovative Medicines Initiative consortium that builds prospective cohorts of cancer patients, including head and neck, lung and breast cancer cohorts, with integrated tumour immune profiling and longitudinal clinical data to understand how the immune system interacts with tumours and therapy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS50000001533</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2500</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cancer patients across five cancer types profiled by the consortium (stated as &apos;more than 2,500&apos;)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40930089</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we present two such workflows for multiplexed immunofluorescence and imaging mass cytometry of cancer tissues, which are applied to a total of roughly 10,000 samples from more than 2,500 patients over 6 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


