    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000100"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>MeDALL epigenetics study includes illumina 450k methylation measurements from 4 cohorts: Infancia y Medio Ambiente (INMA)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000252"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Etudes des Déterminants pré et postnatals précoces du développement et de la santé de l’ENfant (EDEN)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000324"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Prevention and Incidence of Asthma and Mite Allergy (PIAMA)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6071724/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study is based on data from five ongoing European birth cohorts in three different countries participating in MeDALL. Of the cohorts included, we selected those with a) relevant information on maternal smoking during pregnancy or SHS exposure during the first year of life; b) follow-up between 14 and 16 y of age; and c) suitable outcome assessments from three predefined age intervals (4–6, 8–10, and 14–16 y).The following five cohorts were included: Children, Allergy, Milieu, Stockholm, Epidemiology (BAMSE) (single-center, Sweden) (Wickman et al. 2002), German Infant Nutritional Intervention (GINIplus) (multicenter, Germany) (Berg et al. 2010), Influences of Lifestyle-Related Factors on the Immune System and the Development of Allergies in Childhood (LISAplus) (multicenter, Germany) (Zutavern et al. 2008), Multicentre Allergy Study (MAS) (multicenter, Germany) (Bergmann et al. 1994), and Prevention and Incidence of Asthma and Mite Allergy (PIAMA) (multicenter, the Netherlands) (Wijga et al. 2014).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001002169</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>MeDALL epigenetics study</dcterms:title>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project that combines European birth cohorts, including INMA, EDEN, BAMSE and PIAMA, to investigate the mechanisms of the development of allergy through harmonised phenotypes and epigenetic and other omic measurements.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">44000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants of the 14 member birth cohorts in the MeDALL knowledge base (approximate), 2016</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5248602/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The MeDALL knowledge base integrates historical and newly collected data from around 44 000 participants on 398 clinical and phenotypic attributes (harmonized from 7495 individual cohort variables) and 160 different follow‐ups at 25 different time points between pregnancy and age 20.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MeDALL</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


