        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of adults with newly diagnosed active Crohn&apos;s disease enrolled in the multicentre, biomarker-stratified, randomised PROFILE trial in the United Kingdom, whose stool samples were sequenced to relate the gut microbiome to treatment response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym PROFILE also denotes the Genetic Prostate cancer risk stratification for targeted screening study (COHO:0000080); this term is the Crohn&apos;s disease trial, which is what the EGA study EGAS00001007958 tagged PROFILE used.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">386</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROFILE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROFILE (PRedicting Outcomes For Crohn&apos;s disease using a moLecular biomarker)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROFILE trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#EGA_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PRedicting Outcomes For Crohn&apos;s disease using a moLecular biomarker</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid2916">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005011"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000320"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid2916"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Crohn&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001007958</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>PROFILE was a multicentre, open-label, biomarker-stratified, randomised controlled trial that enrolled adults with newly diagnosed active Crohn&apos;s disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000320"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001007958</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Crossreplicate microbiome associations and predictive algorithms in an independent UK-based cohort (IBD-RESPONSE)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000320"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001007958</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>PROFILE_Metagenomics</dcterms:title>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000320"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of adults with newly diagnosed active Crohn&apos;s disease enrolled in the multicentre, biomarker-stratified, randomised PROFILE trial in the United Kingdom, whose stool samples were sequenced to relate the gut microbiome to treatment response.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001007958</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000320"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">386</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults with newly diagnosed Crohn&apos;s disease randomised in PROFILE (2022)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38402895</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between Dec 29, 2017, and Jan 5, 2022, 386 patients (mean age 33·6 years [SD 13·2]; 179 [46%] female, 207 [54%] male) were randomised: 193 to the top-down group and 193 to the accelerated step-up group.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
