    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000336"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of about 1,600 persistently thin, healthy adults with a body mass index below 18 kg/m2 and no chronic disease or eating disorder, recruited through primary care in the United Kingdom from 2005 to investigate the genetic basis of thinness.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000923</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000336"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>UK thin healthy adults in the cohort (approximate), 2019</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6345421/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We were able to take advantage of the UK National Health Service (NHS) research infrastructure to recruit from primary care ( Methods ) using body mass index (BMI: weight in kg/height in metres 2 ) criteria and personal review of individual case files to identify a cohort of approximately 2000 UK European descent thin adults (Study Into Lean and Thin Subjects, STILTS cohort; mean BMI = 17.6 kg/m 2 ) who are well, without medical conditions or eating disorders ( Methods ).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000336"/>
