    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001004593</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Mutation signatures of pediatric acute myeloid leukemia and normal blood progenitors associated with differential patient outcomes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34642666</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7611805/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Next, we combined our pAML genome dataset ( n = 9) with samples of 15 patients from the Therapeutically Applicable Research to Generate Effective Treatments (TARGET; 13 ) initiative.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29489755</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pan-cancer genome and transcriptome analyses of 1,699 paediatric leukaemias and solid tumours.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29489755</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A National Cancer Institute initiative that assembles cohorts of children with hard-to-treat cancers, including leukaemias, neuroblastoma, Wilms tumour and osteosarcoma, for comprehensive molecular characterisation to accelerate the development of markers and therapies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29489755</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1699</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>paediatric leukaemia and solid tumour cases in the 2018 TARGET pan-cancer analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29489755</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we present a pan-cancer study of somatic alterations, including single nucleotide variants, small insertions or deletions, structural variations, copy number alterations, gene fusions and internal tandem duplications in 1,699 paediatric leukaemias and solid tumours across six histotypes, with whole-genome, whole-exome and transcriptome sequencing data processed under a uniform analytical framework.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000339"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TARGET</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000340 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000340">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3063"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>EGAS00001002247</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of patients with early-stage non-small cell lung cancer recruited across the United Kingdom, whose tumours are sampled in multiple regions before and through therapy to investigate intratumour heterogeneity and clonal evolution in relation to outcome.</obo:IAO_0000115>
