        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000082"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>EGAS00001001460</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of United States and United Kingdom groups that sequenced the exomes of 6,546 type 2 diabetes cases and 6,457 controls of African American, East Asian, South Asian, Hispanic and European ancestry, drawn from member cohorts, to assess common, low-frequency and rare variants in diabetes risk.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6504</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6436</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12940</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>T2D-GENES</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#EGA_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Type 2 Diabetes Genetic Exploration by Next-generation sequencing in multi-Ethnic Samples</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3080">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3080"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001460</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The T2D-GENES/GoT2D 13K exome sequencing study includes ~13,000 samples, half T2D cases and half T2D controls, from five ancestries (~5K Europeans, ~2K each of African-American, East-Asian, South-Asian, and Hispanic).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000082"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002937</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GoDARTS T2D-GENES Exome Sequencing Study is a subset of the ~52,000 Type 2 diabetes exome sequencing project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4145406/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From the SAFS families, 20 large pedigrees, consisting of 1043 individuals, were selected for T2D-GENES Project 2 by focusing on large lineages to maximize the number of potential copies of founder alleles and to get an optimal ratio of sequencing efficiency and number of individuals with type 2 diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EGAS00001001460</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The genetic architecture of type 2 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27398621</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of United States and United Kingdom groups that sequenced the exomes of 6,546 type 2 diabetes cases and 6,457 controls of African American, East Asian, South Asian, Hispanic and European ancestry, drawn from member cohorts, to assess common, low-frequency and rare variants in diabetes risk.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001460</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6504</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>T2D cases and controls in the joint T2D-GENES/GoT2D exome data set after QC (2016)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5034897/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This created a joint data set (after all QC) comprised of 12,940 individuals (6,504 cases; 6,436 controls) drawn from five ancestry groups: 4,541 of European origin, and ~2,000 [range: 1,943-2,217] each of South Asian, East Asian, Hispanic, and African American origin (Extended Data Fig. 1; Extended Data Table 2; Supplementary 4).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000344"/>
