        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese Imaging Genetics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese Imaging Genetics cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chinese Imaging Genetics study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3292">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_8000036"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3292"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>air pollution</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31827248+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition to micro-environmental measurements, this study also collects hundreds of quantitative macro-environmental measurements from remote sensing and national survey databases based on the locations of each participant from birth to present, which will facilitate discoveries of new environmental factors associated with neuroimaging phenotypes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7042768/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim of this study was to collect genomic, neuroimaging, environmental, and behavioral data from 10,000 healthy Chinese Han participants aged 18–30 years in 30 research centers from 21 mainland cities in China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90428575</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of hippocampal blood-oxygen-level-dependent-cerebral blood flow correlation in Chinese Han population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37822511</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10562876/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we conducted the first GWAS on the hippocampal BOLD-CBF correlation in 4,832 Chinese Han participants from the Chinese Imaging Genetics (CHIMGEN) cohort.22 Here, the across-voxel correlation between reginal homogeneity (ReHo) derived from the resting-state fMRI data and CBF measured by the arterial spin labeling (ASL) MRI data within hippocampal voxels was used as a proxy to represent hippocampal NVC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of healthy Chinese Han adults aged 18–30 years recruited at research centres in mainland Chinese cities by the Chinese Imaging Genetics (CHIMGEN) study, collecting genomic, neuroimaging, environmental and behavioural data to identify genetic and environmental factors associated with neuroimaging and behavioural phenotypes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31827248</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants recruited to date (more than 7000)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7042768/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To date, we have recruited more than 7000 participants, becoming the largest and most integrative Chinese neuroimaging genetics cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000372"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHIMGEN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3299"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90232793</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of African American adults aged 18–70 with hypertensive chronic kidney disease, enrolled at clinical centres across the United States in a randomized trial of antihypertensive drug regimens and blood-pressure goals (1995–2001) and then followed in the AASK Cohort Study to identify risk factors for progressive kidney disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1094</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AASK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AASK Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Study of Kidney disease and hypertension</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">African American Study of Kidney Disease and Hypertension</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3299">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0024633"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3299"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>hypertensive kidney disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12819322+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants include African-American men and women aged 18 to 70 yr who have hypertensive kidney disease and GFR between 20 and 65 ml/min per 1.73 m(2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18472682+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The African American Study of Kidney Disease and Hypertension (AASK) was conducted over a 7-year period at 21 clinical centers across the United States to investigate whether one of two levels of blood pressure control and/or one of three classes of antihypertensive medications was more effective at slowing the rate of renal disease in African Americans with renal insufficiency presumed secondary to hypertension.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90232793</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of 969 protein quantitative trait loci in an African American population with kidney disease attributed to hypertension.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35870639</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35870639+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we report the genetic determinants of the serum proteome in 466 African Americans with chronic kidney disease attributed to hypertension from the richly phenotyped African American Study of Kidney Disease and Hypertension (AASK) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of African American adults aged 18–70 with hypertensive chronic kidney disease, enrolled at clinical centres across the United States in a randomized trial of antihypertensive drug regimens and blood-pressure goals (1995–2001) and then followed in the AASK Cohort Study to identify risk factors for progressive kidney disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12819322</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17591527</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18472682</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1094</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>African American adults randomized in the AASK Trial</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17591527</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of 1,094 persons enrolled in the AASK Trial (June 1995 to September 2001; mean age, 55 years; 61% men), 691 enrolled in the AASK Cohort Study (April 2002 to present), 299 died or reached dialysis therapy or transplantation, and 104 declined to participate in the AASK Cohort Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AASK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3306"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3308"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3310"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000551"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90286909</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of patients who have visited the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam at VU University Medical Center (now Amsterdam UMC, location VUmc) in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, since the center opened in 2000 and consented to the research use of their clinical data, numbering almost 7,000 individuals by 2019. Patients undergo a one-day diagnostic screening that includes neuropsychological testing, MRI, EEG and lumbar puncture, are asked to consent to the storage of blood, DNA and cerebrospinal fluid in the center&apos;s biobank, and are mostly followed up annually; the ongoing observational study combines patient care with research on early diagnosis, heterogeneity and vascular factors in dementia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym ADC also denotes National Alzheimer&apos;s Coordinating Center (COHO:0000480); this term is Amsterdam Dementia Cohort.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AmDem</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Amsterdam</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Amsterdam Dementia Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
