    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000380 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000380">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90399837</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A national stratified cohort of 51,338 women and men aged 45–85 years recruited in 2011–2015 from all 10 Canadian provinces, comprising a telephone-interviewed Tracking cohort and an in-person Comprehensive cohort providing physical assessments and blood and urine samples, assembled as a longitudinal research platform for studying health and aging.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">51338</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLSA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian Longitudinal Study of Aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Canadian Longitudinal Study on Aging</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6929533/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the Tracking cohort, participants were recruited across the 10 provinces, and all questionnaire measures are collected by computer-assisted telephone interviews (CATI) administered through CLSA CATI sites established in four regions across Canada to accommodate different time zones and language (English or French) requirements for questionnaire administration.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90399837</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Effect modification by sex of genetic associations of vitamin C related metabolites in the Canadian Longitudinal study on aging.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39144724</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39144724+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Methods: We included individuals of European descent from the Canadian Longitudinal Study on Aging with available genetic and metabolic data (n = 9004).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national stratified cohort of 51,338 women and men aged 45–85 years recruited in 2011–2015 from all 10 Canadian provinces, comprising a telephone-interviewed Tracking cohort and an in-person Comprehensive cohort providing physical assessments and blood and urine samples, assembled as a longitudinal research platform for studying health and aging.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31633757</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000380"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">51338</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women and men aged 45-85 recruited at baseline, 2011-2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
