    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90023981</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym BHS also denotes Bogalusa Heart Study (COHO:0000464) and Baependi Heart Study (COHO:0000623); this term is Busselton Health Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BSN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Busselton Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9170690/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BHS is a community-based study in Western Australia that includes both related and unrelated individuals (predominantly of European ancestry) and has been described in more detail elsewhere46–48.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90023981</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Comprehensive genetic analysis of the human lipidome identifies loci associated with lipid homeostasis with links to coronary artery disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35668104</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35668104+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We quantified 596 lipid species in serum from 4,492 individuals from the Busselton Health Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24099269</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35668104</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Busselton residents who took part in surveys and clinical assessments since 1966 (stated as &apos;more than 20,000&apos;, a lower bound)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://bpmri.org.au/about-us.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Since its inception in 1966, more than 20,000 Busselton residents have participated in surveys and clinical assessments, contributing to over 600 scientific publications and major medical breakthroughs, including early genetic insights into asthma and hereditary haemochromatosis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389"/>
