    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001914"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7611474</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Co-localisation analysis of CVD-I cis-pQTLs and mRNA levels was performed in selected tissues from the GTEx project by first imputing mRNA expression of the CVD-I protein encoding transcripts using the PrediXcan11 algorithm in one of the SCALLOP CVD-I cohorts (IMPROVE), and then testing imputed mRNA levels for association with CVD-I plasma protein levels using linear regression.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90128424</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Landscape of the ACE2 Coronavirus Receptor.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35387486</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9047645/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a genome-wide association meta-analysis in up to 28 204 individuals from 14 cohorts in the SCALLOP Consortium for plasma ACE2 protein measured with the Olink platform.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of principal investigators of cohort studies from the general population, clinical trials and disease-specific patient collections that have Olink proteomics and genome-wide genotyping data, combining summary-level data to discover and follow up genetic associations with plasma protein levels (pQTLs) and identify causal protein biomarkers of disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33067605</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42097137</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.scallop-consortium.com/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">78664</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants of European ancestry in the consortium&apos;s largest pQTL meta-analysis (38 cohorts, including UK Biobank), 2026</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13343581/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a proteogenomic meta-analysis of 1,161 protein targets measured in blood across 38 cohorts, including up to 78,664 participants of European ancestry (Table S1A; for study design see Figure S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SCALLOP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000399 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000399">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Taiwan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90651113</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based cohort of patients of China Medical University Hospital, an academic medical centre in Taichung, Taiwan, and its affiliated hospitals, recruited through the hospital&apos;s Precision Medicine Project, begun in 2018 to collect biospecimens from patients attending for medical visits, from densely populated towns and districts across Taiwan. About 413,000 participants enrolled from 2018 to 2021 were genotyped on the custom Taiwan Precision Medicine (TPMv1) array and linked to their electronic medical records from 2003 to 2021 (the HiGenome resource; 323,397 passed ancestry and quality control), for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk score studies in the Taiwanese Han population.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">413210</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CMUH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CMUHPMP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>China Medical University Hospital</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>China Medical University Hospital Precision Medicine Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HiGenome</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">China Medical University Hospital Biobank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000399"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Taiwan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC12136033/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CMUH is an extensive academic medical center located in Taichung, Taiwan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000399"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90651113</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Diversity and longitudinal records: Genetic architecture of disease associations and polygenic risk in the Taiwanese Han population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40465716</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC12136033/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data were collected from a single institution—China Medical University Hospital (CMUH) and its affiliated branches—through a unified system encompassing nearly 19 years of EMRs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000399"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based cohort of patients of China Medical University Hospital, an academic medical centre in Taichung, Taiwan, and its affiliated hospitals, recruited through the hospital&apos;s Precision Medicine Project, begun in 2018 to collect biospecimens from patients attending for medical visits, from densely populated towns and districts across Taiwan. About 413,000 participants enrolled from 2018 to 2021 were genotyped on the custom Taiwan Precision Medicine (TPMv1) array and linked to their electronic medical records from 2003 to 2021 (the HiGenome resource; 323,397 passed ancestry and quality control), for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk score studies in the Taiwanese Han population.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36769103</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40465716</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
