        <rdfs:comment>The Religious Orders Study (ROS) and Rush Memory and Aging Project (MAP) began in 1994 and 1997 respectively (together referred to as ROSMAP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6380522/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>ROS started in 1994 and enrolls nuns priests and brothers from across the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308732</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide search for pleiotropy in more than 100,000 harmonized longitudinal cognitive domain scores.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37349795</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10286470/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included non-Hispanic white participants of the Framingham Heart Study (FHS), National Institute on Aging sponsored Alzheimer’s Disease Research Centers whose phenotypic information was assembled and curated by the National Alzheimer’s Coordinating Center (NACC), the Adult Changes in Thought (ACT) Study, the Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI), and the Religious Orders Study/Rush Memory and Aging Project (ROSMAP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pair of harmonized longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort studies of aging and Alzheimer&apos;s disease run at Rush University, the Religious Orders Study (from 1994, nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States) and the Rush Memory and Aging Project (from 1997, lay persons from northeastern Illinois), whose older participants enrol without dementia and agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29865057</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3414</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>persons enrolled in ROS and MAP combined, through 31 December 2017</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6380522/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Through December 31, 2017, the studies enrolled 3,414 persons of whom 72.6% are female, 88.2% are non-Latino White, 6.3% are African American, 5.5% are Latino (including African American Latinos), and the remainder are other racial groups.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
