    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000312"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90627781</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13037</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BRRD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIHR BioResource for Rare Diseases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIHR BioResource-Rare Diseases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Institutes of Health Research BioResource-Rare Diseases Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NIHR BioResource Rare Diseases Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7610553/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed WGS of 13,037 individuals enrolled at 57 National Health Service (NHS) hospitals in the United Kingdom and 26 hospitals in other countries (Fig. 1a, Extended Data Fig. 1a, Supplementary Table 1), in three batches, to clinical standard (Fig. 1b).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000312"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7610553/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Study participants were enrolled by one of three mechanisms between December 2012 and March 2017 under the overall coordination of the National Institute for Health Research BioResource (NBR) at the University of Cambridge.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90627781</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-Scale Whole-Genome Sequencing Reveals the Genetic Architecture of Primary Membranoproliferative GN and C3 Glomerulopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31919107</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:31919107%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed whole-genome sequence data from 165 primary membranoproliferative GN cases and 10,250 individuals without the condition (controls) as part of the National Institutes of Health Research BioResource-Rare Diseases Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32581362</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13037</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals enrolled and whole-genome sequenced (9,802 with a rare disease or extreme trait), 2017</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7610553</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed WGS of 13,037 individuals enrolled at 57 National Health Service (NHS) hospitals in the United Kingdom and 26 hospitals in other countries (Fig. 1a, Extended Data Fig. 1a, Supplementary Table 1), in three batches, to clinical standard (Fig. 1b).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BRRD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3578"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid3580"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90024610</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer&apos;s disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer&apos;s disease and cognitive decline.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2359</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABIL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AIBL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Imaging, Biomarker &amp; Lifestyle study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Imaging, Biomarker and Lifestyle Flagship Study of Ageing</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle flagship study of aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Australian Imaging, Biomarker &amp; Lifestyle Flagship Study of Ageing</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3578">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0002039"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3580">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3578"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mild cognitive impairment</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19470201+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants with AD (211) had neuropsychological profiles which were consistent with AD, and were more impaired than participants with mild cognitive impairment (133) or healthy controls (768), who performed within expected norms for age on neuropsychological testing.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19470201+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants with AD (211) had neuropsychological profiles which were consistent with AD, and were more impaired than participants with mild cognitive impairment (133) or healthy controls (768), who performed within expected norms for age on neuropsychological testing.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11103763/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The data were collected over a maximum of 10 time points spanned up to 18 months apart at the study centers in Perth or Melbourne.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90024610</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Comprehensive genetic analysis of the human lipidome identifies loci associated with lipid homeostasis with links to coronary artery disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35668104</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9170690/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a GWAS of the human serum lipidome (Fig. 1) in the BHS discovery cohort (4492 individuals of European ancestry) followed by validation against a meta-analysis of the two validation cohorts (ADNI and AIBL; 670 and 895 individuals of European ancestry, respectively).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer&apos;s disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer&apos;s disease and cognitive decline.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19470201</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38770381</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2359</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants of the Inception (1,112) and Enrichment (1,247) cohorts, as of 10 April 2019</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8293663/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The evolution of the Inception cohort at baseline, 18, 36, 54, 72, 90, 108, and 126 months follow-up, was enriched with recruitment of 1,247 new participants to compensate for attrition (Enrichment cohort), yielding the current database of 2,359 participants with 8,592 person-contact years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ABIL</owl:annotatedTarget>
