        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
