        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90994634</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol at least one million diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">800000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>All of Us</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>All of Us / NIH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AllOfUs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AllofUs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AoU</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIH All of Us Research Program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Precision Medicine Initiative Cohort Program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">All of Us Research Program</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://allofus.nih.gov/"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31412182+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The All of Us Research Program plans to enroll a diverse group of at least 1 million persons in the United States in order to accelerate biomedical research and improve health.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90994634</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Whole-Genome Sequence Genome-Wide Association Study in All of Us Identifies a Novel Glaucoma Risk Locus in African Individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42620341</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42620341+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>ObjectiveTo assess how whole genome sequencing (WGS) and varying phenotype definitions influence genetic discovery for primary open-angle glaucoma (POAG) in a diverse population.DesignAncestry-stratified genome-wide association studies (GWASs) and cross-ancestry meta-analyses of POAG cases and controls using 2 phenotype definitions.ParticipantsCases (age ≥40 years) and controls (age ≥65 years) were identified in the National Institutes of Health All of Us Research Program v8 data release and subdivided into genetically inferred ancestral groups.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol at least one million diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31412182</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">800000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants consented since 2018 (a lower bound, &apos;over 800,000&apos;), 2026</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13092120/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Since its inception in 2018, the AoU program has consented to over 800,000 participants, with more than 560,000 completing the initial enrollment process, including health questionnaires and biospecimen collection.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
