        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90101736</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004233</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MSH also denotes Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea in Sickle Cell Anemia (COHO:0000987) and Mount Sinai Hospital-Princess Margaret Multicancer Study (COHO:0002267); this term is BioMe Biobank.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">60000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
