        <owl:annotatedTarget>An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36216889</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">60000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants enrolled (approximate, &apos;approximately 60,000&apos;)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36216889</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Mount Sinai BioMe Biobank, founded in 2007, is an ongoing electronic health record-linked biorepository that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System, comprising approximately 60,000 participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
