    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000088"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000398"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90179214</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1702</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HELIC-Pomak</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pomak</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">The Pomak cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8640022/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For MANOLIS, biological samples were collected from the mountainous Mylopomatos villages in Crete, Greece; whereas, Pomak refers to a set of mountainous villages in the North of Greece.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90179214</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identifying causal serum protein-cardiometabolic trait relationships using whole genome sequencing.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36349687</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10077504/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Meta-analyzing whole-genome sequencing (WGS) data from two Greek cohorts, MANOLIS (n = 1356; 22.5× WGS) and Pomak (n = 1537; 18.4× WGS), we detect 301 independently associated pQTL variants for 170 proteins, including 12 rare variants (minor allele frequency &lt; 1%).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25373335</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31847144</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34857772</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1702</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adult volunteers recruited 2010-2013</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31847144</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We contacted the local Health Centre in Echinos and, with the cooperation of the local doctors and nurses, a total of 1702 volunteers were recruited between July 2010 and March 2013.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HELIC-Pomak</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90095184</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym KP also denotes Kaiser Permanente Research Bank (COHO:0000541); this term is Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">110266</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GERA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GERA cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Epidemiology Research in Adult Health and Aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kaiser Permanente GERA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kaiser Permanente Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kaiser Permanente Northern California Genetic Epidemiology Research in Adult Health and Aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kaiser Resource for Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Resource for Genetic Epidemiology on Adult Health and Aging</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cohort members reside primarily in a 22-county service area in northern and central California that encompasses over 28,000 square miles and includes urban, suburban, rural and agricultural land use (supplementary Figure 1; http://links.lww.com/EE/A39).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GERA cohort is part of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC) Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90095184</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of actinic keratosis identifies new susceptibility loci implicated in pigmentation and immune regulation pathways.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35449187</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35449187+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a genome-wide association study of AK in non-Hispanic white participants of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort (n = 63,110, discovery cohort), with validation in the Mass-General Brigham (MGB) Biobank cohort (n = 29,130).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26092718</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33778338</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">110266</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>RPGEH participants forming the GERA cohort (genotyped), 2011</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4574249</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohort included 110,266 subjects to ensure that at least 100,000 individuals were successfully genotyped by the end of the project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GERA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90668562</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CEDAR also denotes Center for Education and Drug Abuse Research (COHO:0001618); this term is Correlated Expression and Disease Association Research.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">323</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEDAR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEDAR cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Correlated Expression &amp; Disease Association Research</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Correlated Expression and Disease Association Research</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013502/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We collected peripheral blood as well as intestinal biopsies (ileum, transverse colon, rectum) from 323 healthy Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège as part of a national screening campaign for colon cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90668562</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study in 10,000 individuals links plasma N-glycome to liver disease and anti-inflammatory proteins.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40593539</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a multicenter study using data from seven studies – TwinsUK (N = 3918), EPIC-Potsdam (N = 2192), PainOmics (N = 1873), SOCCS (N = 1742), SABRE (N = 544), QMDiab (N = 325), and CEDAR (N = 170) with a total sample size N = 10,764.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29930244</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">323</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>healthy Europeans with blood and intestinal biopsies</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29930244</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We collected peripheral blood as well as intestinal biopsies (ileum, transverse colon, rectum) from 323 healthy Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège as part of a national screening campaign for colon cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432"/>
