        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002052"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90093093</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based family study of hypertensive sibships, recruited from 1996 among non-Hispanic Black adults in Jackson, Mississippi, non-Hispanic white adults in Rochester, Minnesota and (initially) Hispanic adults in Starr County, Texas, to identify genes influencing blood pressure and hypertensive target-organ damage.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GENOA also denotes Genetics of Opioid Addiction Consortium (COHO:0000466) and Genetics of Opioid Addiction Study (COHO:0000467); this term is Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENOA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENOA Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy (GENOA) study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid3818">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001134"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid3818"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>essential hypertension</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8764761/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the first phase of GENOA (Phase I: 1996–2001), sibships with at least two adults with clinically diagnosed essential hypertension before age 60 were recruited, and all siblings in the sibship were invited to participate regardless of hypertension status.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8764761/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GENOA is a community-based study in Rochester, MN and Jackson, MS that was established to identify genes influencing blood pressure [33].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90093093</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Whole genome sequence analyses of eGFR in 23,732 people representing multiple ancestries in the NHLBI trans-omics for precision medicine (TOPMed) consortium.</dcterms:title>
