        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of 10,000 randomly selected adults, mainly aged 40–79, from the city of Leipzig in eastern Germany, examined in 2011–2014 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) with deep phenotyping to study the prevalence, early markers, genetic predispositions and lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
