        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4499109/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Inclusion criteria were a primary form of type 2 diabetes (for patients) or an absence of type 2 diabetes (for controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000454"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Qatar"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4499109/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All study participants were enrolled between February 2012 and June 2012 at the Dermatology Department of Hamad Medical Corporation (HMC) in Doha, Qatar.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000454"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90668562</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study in 10,000 individuals links plasma N-glycome to liver disease and anti-inflammatory proteins.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40593539</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a multicenter study using data from seven studies – TwinsUK (N = 3918), EPIC-Potsdam (N = 2192), PainOmics (N = 1873), SOCCS (N = 1742), SABRE (N = 544), QMDiab (N = 325), and CEDAR (N = 170) with a total sample size N = 10,764.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000454"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cross-sectional case–control study of 374 people with and without type 2 diabetes, of Arab and Asian descent, enrolled in February–June 2012 at the Dermatology Department of Hamad Medical Corporation in Doha, Qatar, with metabolomic profiling of saliva, blood plasma and urine to study metabolic dysregulation in diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26049400</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000454"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">374</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants with and without type 2 diabetes enrolled February-June 2012</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26049400</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study was embedded in the Qatar Metabolomics Study on Diabetes (QMDiab), a cross-sectional case–control study with 374 participants [13, 20].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
