        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000479"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000542"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000700"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000727"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:27089181</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of about 30 cohorts with genome-wide genotype and personality data, which harmonized personality measures across inventories in more than 63,000 participants for genome-wide association meta-analyses of personality traits such as neuroticism and their relation to major depressive disorder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GPC also denotes Uganda General Population Cohort (COHO:0000345); this term is Genetics of Personality Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">63661</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GPC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Personality Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000016"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Avon Longitudinal Study of Parents and their Children (ALSPAC) is a longitudinal population-based birth cohort that recruited pregnant women residing in Avon, UK, with an expected delivery date between 1st April 1991 and 31st December 1992.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000047"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>9. KORCULA (Polasek et al. 2009) — Croatia. This study was performed in the eastern part of the island of Korčula, Croatia between March and December 2007.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000063"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Erasmus Rucphen Family (ERF) study is a family-based study including over 3 000 individuals from an isolated population in the Southwest region of the Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000064"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Estonian cohort comes from the population-based biobank of the Estonian Genome Project of University of Tartu (EGCUT).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000070"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Finnish twin cohort consisted of 30 654 respondents, of which 28 767 completed the Eysenck Personality Inventory (EPI; an alternative version of the EPQ) at least once.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000125"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data on personality in the Netherlands Twin Register (NTR) were collected as part of a longitudinal study on health, personality and lifestyle in adolescent and adult twins and their relatives</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000128"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>13. NBS (Kiemeney et al. 2008) — The Netherlands. In 2000 a study was initiated among the inhabitants of the municipality of Nijmegen by different departments of the Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Centre</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000132"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Orkney Complex Disease Study (ORCADES) is a genetic epidemiology study based in an isolated population in the north of Scotland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the Swedish Twin Registry (STR), in 1970 a cohort of twins born in 1926–67 was compiled, by use of nationalized birth registrations.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000195"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Baltimore Longitudinal Study of Aging (BLSA) is an ongoing multidisciplinary study of community-dwelling volunteers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Young Finns Study is an ongoing multicenter follow-up study of Finnish children and adolescents started in 1980 with a baseline sample of 3 596 individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4667957/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Generation Scotland cohort (N=9,786) was included for replication of GWA top results.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The NESDA data for the present study were drawn from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety(Penninx et al.), an ongoing longitudinal cohort study aimed at examining the long-term course of depressive and anxiety disorders in different health care settings and phases of illness.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Helsinki Birth Cohort Study (HBCS) is composed of 8 760 individuals born between the years 1934 and 1944 in one of the two main maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000479"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>22. VIS (Ivkovic et al. 2007) — Croatia. Adult participants living in the villages of Komiza and Vis on the Croatian island of Vis were recruited in May 2003 and May 2004 for a large genetic study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000542"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data from the Minnesota Center for Twin and Family Research (MCTFR) were collected as part of two different longitudinal studies, the Minnesota Twin Family Study (MTFS) and the Sibling Interaction and Behavior Study (SIBS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Lothian Birth Cohort 1936 (LBC1936) study consists of a cohort of 1 091 individuals born in 1936.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000700"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Lothian Birth Cohort 1921 (LBC1921) study consists of a cohort of 550 individuals born in 1921.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>17. PAGES (van den Oord et al. 2008) — Germany. In this German cohort, healthy control participants were randomly selected from the general population of Munich, Germany, and contacted by mail.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000727"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>COGEND was initiated in 2001 as a three-part program project grant funded through the National Cancer Institute (NCI; PI: Laura Bierut).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057636/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The sample used in this study consisted of 649 participants drawn from the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism (COGA) that all completed the TCI.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27089181</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic variants associated with subjective well-being, depressive symptoms, and neuroticism identified through genome-wide analyses.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27089181</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4884152/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For neuroticism (N = 170,910), we pooled summary statistics from a published study by the Genetics of Personality Consortium (GPC)4 with results from a new analysis of UKB data.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of about 30 cohorts with genome-wide genotype and personality data, which harmonized personality measures across inventories in more than 63,000 participants for genome-wide association meta-analyses of personality traits such as neuroticism and their relation to major depressive disorder.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25993607</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">63661</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants from 29 cohorts in the 2015 neuroticism GWAS meta-analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25993607</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we report results of the largest GWA study for neuroticism so far, conducted in 63,661 participants from 29 cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GPC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000462 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000462">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid4078"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41795035</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control collection of children with type 1 diabetes and controls from multiple paediatric centres in China, used to validate polygenic risk scores for type 1 diabetes in an East Asian population.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GRACE also denotes Global Registry of Acute Coronary Events (COHO:0000192); this term is Genetic Risk Assessment for Chinese Eaglet-T1D.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GRACE resembles GR@ACE, which denotes Genome Research at Fundació ACE (COHO:0000258); this term is Genetic Risk Assessment for Chinese Eaglet-T1D.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">294</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">303</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">597</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GRACE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GRACE-T1D</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Risk Assessment for Chinese Eaglet-T1D</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid4078">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid4078"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13109230/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We validated our results in two independent type 1 diabetes case–control cohorts (Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia, Center for Applied Genomics [CHOP-CAG] and Genetic Risk Assessment for Chinese Eaglet-T1D [GRACE]) and two population-based cohorts (All of Us and UK Biobank).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13109230/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Ncontrols=427,069) and in a Chinese case–control cohort across multiple paediatric centres named Genetic Risk Assessment for Chinese Eaglet-T1D (GRACE, N=597;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41795035</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Development and validation of a trans-ancestry polygenic risk score for type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41795035</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13109230/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Ncontrols=427,069) and in a Chinese case–control cohort across multiple paediatric centres named Genetic Risk Assessment for Chinese Eaglet-T1D (GRACE, N=597;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control collection of children with type 1 diabetes and controls from multiple paediatric centres in China, used to validate polygenic risk scores for type 1 diabetes in an East Asian population.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41795035</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
