        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international randomized, placebo-controlled trial of darapladib, a lipoprotein-associated phospholipase A2 inhibitor, in 15,828 patients with chronic coronary heart disease recruited at 663 centers in 39 countries from December 2008 to April 2010 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, whose baseline plasma biobank has been used for biomarker, proteomic and genetic studies of cardiovascular outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
