        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adult Changes in Thought Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid4248">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001627"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid4248"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>dementia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11592130/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ACT study is an ongoing population-based prospective cohort study that began in 1994 [20,21,22] and aims to identify risk and preventive factors for dementia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11592130/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1994 and 1996, ACT enrolled 2581 GHC members living in the greater Seattle area who were 65 years of age or older, community dwelling, and did not have a diagnosis of dementia at baseline.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308732</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide search for pleiotropy in more than 100,000 harmonized longitudinal cognitive domain scores.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37349795</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10286470/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included non-Hispanic white participants of the Framingham Heart Study (FHS), National Institute on Aging sponsored Alzheimer’s Disease Research Centers whose phenotypic information was assembled and curated by the National Alzheimer’s Coordinating Center (NACC), the Adult Changes in Thought (ACT) Study, the Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI), and the Religious Orders Study/Rush Memory and Aging Project (ROSMAP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective cohort of dementia-free adults aged 65 and older enrolled since 1994 from the membership of Kaiser Permanente Washington (formerly Group Health Cooperative) in the Seattle area, United States, and followed longitudinally to identify risk and preventive factors for dementia, with brain autopsy, genetic and abstracted medical-record data.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39595838</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5763</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cumulative enrolment to November 2022</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11592130/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As of the most recent data freeze (25 November 2022), total cumulative enrollment in the ACT study was 5763 people with 49,422 person-years of follow-up (mean 8.6, SD = 6.1 years per person).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
