        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000873"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002754"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002052"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90025941</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A National Human Genome Research Institute-funded consortium, established in 2007, of US academic and integrated health systems, each with its own biorepository linking DNA samples to electronic medical records, which pooled its sites&apos; data into a network-wide genome-wide dataset of about 105,000 participants for genomic discovery and later sequenced about 25,000 participants to study the return of genomic results.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">105108</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EMERGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Electronic Medical Records and Genomics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Electronic Medical Records and Genomics (eMERGE) network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Medical Records and Genomics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>eMERGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>eMERGE Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>electronic MEdical Records &amp; GEnomics Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>electronic MEdical Records and GEnomic network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Electronic Medical Records and Genomics Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000383"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4810384/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To facilitate genomic research and participation in eMERGE, the Biobank undertook a plan to conduct genomewide genotyping of 25,000 samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3038887/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The eMERGE type 2 diabetes GWAS population is comprised of samples from NUgene and BioVU at Vanderbilt University</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3795928/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Mount Sinai BioMe Biobank Program is supported by the Andrea and Charles Bronfman Philanthropies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5872076/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Geisinger eMERGE III study involves a subset of participants that are enrolled in the systemwide biobank, MyCodeTM Community Health Initiative (MyCode CHI) who have been consented for re-contact regarding research opportunities and opted to receive research results.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000483"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3038887/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Group Health&apos;s primary phenotype of interest is Alzheimer&apos;s Disease (AD) using dementia cases and controls within the GH biorepository, based on gold-standard research diagnoses. A 2-stage screening process was used to identify cases in ACT.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000489"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3795928/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In August 2012, following a request for applications22 for pediatric sites, eMERGE membership was extended to Children&apos;s Hospital of Philadelphia and a joint membership for Cincinnati Children&apos;s Hospital and Boston Children&apos;s Hospital (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000790"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7033893/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Through its participation in the eMERGE consortium,15, 16 the NUgene biobank selected 900 participants for WGS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000873"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10191288/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>(b) The structured data-driven phenotyping algorithm was used in two eMERGE sites (Marshfield, Mount Sinai).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002754"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001584/phs001584.v2.p2/GapExchange_phs001584.v2.p2.xml</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>KPWA participants were enrolled in the eMERGE Network through the Northwest Institute of Genetic Medicine (NWIGM) biorepository, and provided the appropriate consent to receive clinically relevant genetic results (N~8,073.) NWIGM is based at the University of Washington and co-managed by the University of Washington and KPWA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35216901+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The goal of Electronic Medical Records and Genomics (eMERGE) Phase III Network was to return actionable sequence variants to 25,084 consenting participants from 10 different health care institutions across the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90025941</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A unified framework identifies new links between plasma lipids and diseases from electronic medical records across large-scale cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34140684</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34140684+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We devised a comprehensive three-phase framework to identify new lipid-associated genes and study the relationships among lipids, genotypes, gene expression and hundreds of complex human diseases from the Electronic Medical Records and Genomics (347 traits) and the UK Biobank (549 traits).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A National Human Genome Research Institute-funded consortium, established in 2007, of US academic and integrated health systems, each with its own biorepository linking DNA samples to electronic medical records, which pooled its sites&apos; data into a network-wide genome-wide dataset of about 105,000 participants for genomic discovery and later sequenced about 25,000 participants to study the return of genomic results.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23743551</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35047833</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">105108</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants in the pooled network-wide HRC-imputed GWAS dataset (phase III)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8756524/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The array data were imputed and merged at each phase, and the latest effort utilized the Michigan Imputation Server and HRC version 1.1, thus allowing the aggregation of data from 105,108 eMERGE participants for ∼40 million variants, both common and rare.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EMERGE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>eMERGE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002719"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90840657</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A volunteer-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the self-contained population of Sorbs in eastern Germany, recruited and extensively metabolically phenotyped by the University of Leipzig in 2005–2007 for genome-wide studies of metabolic, anthropometric and other quantitative traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SORBS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Sorbs</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Sorbs cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Sorbs population</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sorbs Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19729412+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We attempted to identify further variants associated with adult height in a self-contained population (the Sorbs in Eastern Germany) as discovery set.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90840657</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic dissection of serum pro-neurotensin suggests potential causal impact on brain structure.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41520650</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12818281/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Four independent cross-sectional studies have been included in the present genetic meta-analysis, namely MDC,11,12 MOS,13 LIFE-Adult and the Sorbs cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A volunteer-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the self-contained population of Sorbs in eastern Germany, recruited and extensively metabolically phenotyped by the University of Leipzig in 2005–2007 for genome-wide studies of metabolic, anthropometric and other quantitative traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19729412</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41520650</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Sorbian individuals enrolled (approximate), 2009</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2773272</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>At present, about 1000 Sorbian individuals are enrolled in the study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000492"/>
