        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The WHI-GARNET sub-study consisted of individuals selected as a nested case- control sample of coronary heart disease, stroke, venous thrombosis, and incident diabetes events from the parent WHI Hormone Therapy Trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000505"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90570665</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry genome-wide association analyses incorporating SNP-by-psychosocial interactions identify novel loci for serum lipids.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40537477</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41398-025-03418-z/MediaObjects/41398_2025_3418_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>WHI Genomics and Randomized Trials Network – GARNET, which included all coronary heart disease, stroke, venous thromboembolic events and selected diabetes cases that happened during the active intervention phase in the WHI HT clinical trials and aged matched controls</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000505"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nested case-control genome-wide association sub-study of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative hormone therapy trials, comprising the coronary heart disease, stroke, venous thromboembolism and selected diabetes cases that arose during the active intervention phase and age-matched controls, genotyped under the NHGRI Genomics and Randomized Trials Network (GARNET).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41398-025-03418-z/MediaObjects/41398_2025_3418_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5714283/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000505"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>WHI hormone-trial women genotyped in the GARNET nested case-control sample</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000315.v8.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the approximately 27,000 women who participated in the HT trial, 4,894 were genotyped on the Illumina Omni-Quad as part of WHI GARNET, a genome-wide association study (GWAS) to identify genetic components involved in differential responses from the HT trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000505"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4894</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>WHI hormone-trial women genotyped in the GARNET nested case-control sample</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000315.v8.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the approximately 27,000 women who participated in the HT trial, 4,894 were genotyped on the Illumina Omni-Quad as part of WHI GARNET, a genome-wide association study (GWAS) to identify genetic components involved in differential responses from the HT trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000505"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
