        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid4489"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28924187+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases were identified as persons with schizophrenia (N=3540), autism (N=16 146), attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (N=18 726) and affective disorder (N=26 380), of which 1928 had bipolar affective disorder.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28924187+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The iPSYCH2012 sample is nested within the entire Danish population born between 1981 and 2005, including 1 472 762 persons.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90239707</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide by Environment Interaction Study of Stressful Life Events and Hospital-Treated Depression in the iPSYCH2012 Sample.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36324662</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36324662+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All individuals were drawn from the iPSYCH2012 case-cohort study, a nationally representative sample identified from Danish national registers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers. Its first wave (iPSYCH2012, 86,189 individuals born 1981-2005) was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28924187</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">93608</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>samples in iPSYCH2015 (cases plus population-based cohort)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The newly updated cohort, named iPSYCH2015, expands the study base with 56,233 samples, to a combined total of 141,265 samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512"/>
