        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000799"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000807"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001041"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001128"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90654647</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24388</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31853</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">56000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ADGC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alzheimer Disease Genetic Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetic Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid4539">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid4539"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39250132+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This was a meta-analysis of genetic association studies in case-control, family-based, population-based, and longitudinal AD-related cohorts from the US Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium, the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Sequencing Project, the UK Biobank, the Finnish health registry, and the US Million Veterans Program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5893779/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ADGC cohorts include: Adult Changes in Thought (ACT), the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Centers (ADC), the Chicago Health and Aging Project (CHAP), the Memory and Aging Project (MAP), Mayo Clinic (MAYO), Mayo Parkinson&apos;s Disease controls, University of Miami, the Multi-Institutional Research in Alzheimer&apos;s Genetic Epidemiology Study (MIRAGE), the National Cell Repository for Alzheimer&apos;s Disease (NCRAD), the National Institute on Aging Late Onset Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Family Study (NIA-LOAD), the Religious Orders Study (ROS), the Texas Alzheimer&apos;s Research and Care Consortium (TARC), Vanderbilt University/Case Western Reserve University (VAN/CWRU), the Washington Heights-Inwood Columbia Aging Project (WHICAP) and the Washington University Sequencing Project (WUSP), the Columbia University Hispanic-Estudio Familiar de Influencia Genetica de Alzheimer (EFIGA), the University of Toronto (UT), and Genetic Differences (GD).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000366"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11245521/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Finally, the Knight-ADRC contributes data to the following genetic and genomic NIH funded initiatives: National Alzheimer Coordinating Center (NCRAD), Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC), National Institute on Aging Genetics of Alzheimer’s Disease Data Storage (NIAGADs), Alzheimer Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI), Alzheimer’s Disease Sequencing Project (ADSP), Global Neurodegeneration Proteomics Consortium (GNPC), and the Alzheimer Clinical Trials Consortium (ACTC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
