        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90292537</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sample of about 7,300 adult volunteers of mixed African, European and Native American ancestry, mostly university students and staff (and, in Chile, mainly soldiers), recruited by a consortium of Latin American and UK groups in México City, Medellín, Lima, Arica and Porto Alegre and characterised for physical appearance, facial photographs, self-perceived ancestry and genetic ancestry, with genome-wide genotyping of about 6,000 of them, to study admixture and the genetics of physical traits in Latin America.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7342</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CANDELA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CANDELA cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Consortium for the Analysis of the Diversity and Evolution of Latin America</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4177621/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Recruitment took place mainly in five locations: México City (México), Medellín (Colombia), Lima (Perú), Arica (Chile) and Porto Alegre (Brazil).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90292537</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Automatic landmarking identifies new loci associated with face morphology and implicates Neanderthal introgression in human nasal shape.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37156940</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10167347/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 6486 individuals examined here are part of the CANDELA cohort, collected in five Latin American countries21.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A sample of about 7,300 adult volunteers of mixed African, European and Native American ancestry, mostly university students and staff (and, in Chile, mainly soldiers), recruited by a consortium of Latin American and UK groups in México City, Medellín, Lima, Arica and Porto Alegre and characterised for physical appearance, facial photographs, self-perceived ancestry and genetic ancestry, with genome-wide genotyping of about 6,000 of them, to study admixture and the genetics of physical traits in Latin America.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25254375</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27193062</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37156940</obo:IAO_0000119>
