        <rdfs:comment>MCPS is a prospective cohort of more than 150,000 adults, aged at least 35 years, who were recruited between 1998 and 2004 from the contiguous urban districts of Coyoacán and Iztapalapa in Mexico City23,55.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000520"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90435341</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Comparative analysis of the Mexico City Prospective Study and the UK Biobank identifies ancestry-specific effects on clonal hematopoiesis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39948438</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906367/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we compared CH in 136,401 participants from the Mexico City Prospective Study (MCPS) to 416,118 individuals from the UK Biobank (UKB)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000520"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of more than 150,000 adults aged 35 and over, recruited in 1998-2004 from the contiguous urban districts of Coyoacán and Iztapalapa in Mexico City with the University of Oxford, and followed to investigate known and new risk factors for mortality in people of Mexican descent; its participants have exome and genome-wide genetic data.</owl:annotatedTarget>
