        <rdfs:comment>The Rotterdam Study (RS) is a prospective, population-based cohort study of determinants of chronic diseases in older adults (7). The first cohort (RS-I) started in 1990 and included 7,983 inhabitants, aged ≥55 years from Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
