    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid4871"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>stroke</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10955659/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The INTERSTROKE study is a case–control study of acute first stroke and was undertaken with 13,462 stroke cases and 13,488 controls recruited between January 11, 2007 and August 8, 2015 in 32 countries worldwide.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10955659/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>seven regions include: Western Europe/North America (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Germany, Sweden, UK, and Ireland), Eastern/central Europe/Middle East (Croatia, Poland, Russia, Turkey, Iran, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, and United Arab Emirates), Africa (Mozambique, Nigeria, Sudan, and Uganda), South Asia (India and Pakistan), China, South East Asia (Philippines, Thailand, and Malaysia), and South America (Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104544</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Stroke genetics informs drug discovery and risk prediction across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36180795</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05165-3/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5165_MOESM1_ESM.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>INTERSTROKE is an international, multi-centered, case-control study of stroke investigating the global burden of risk factors across 32 countries and 18 different ethnic groups around the world.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international multicentre case-control study of risk factors for first acute stroke, which recruited 13,462 stroke cases and 13,488 community or hospital controls matched for age, sex and region from 142 centres in 32 countries between 2007 and 2015, with a genotyped subset of consenting participants used in genetic studies of stroke.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05165-3/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5165_MOESM1_ESM.docx</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10955659/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9841450/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13462</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>first acute stroke cases and matched controls recruited 2007-2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10955659/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With the sample size to 26,950 participants from 32 countries, we reported the association of stroke subtypes with active and environmental tobacco smoking in men and women, young and old, with regions of world and by level of income in countries.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000552"/>
