    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5087"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>smoking</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32963210+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japan Multi-institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) study was launched in 2005 to examine gene-environment interactions in lifestyle-related diseases, including cancers, among the Japanese.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5089"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifestyle factors in gene-environment interactions</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32963210+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japan Multi-institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) study was launched in 2005 to examine gene-environment interactions in lifestyle-related diseases, including cancers, among the Japanese.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5091"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>food intake</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32963210+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japan Multi-institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) study was launched in 2005 to examine gene-environment interactions in lifestyle-related diseases, including cancers, among the Japanese.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5093"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17696755+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Although the main purpose is to confirm and detect gene-environment interactions of lifestyle-related diseases, mainly of cancer, through the cohort analyses, it includes cross-sectional analyses on lifestyle factors, biomarkers, and genotypes, as well as confirmation/ screening of new biomarkers usable for early diagnosis of cancer. The endpoints are cancer diagnosis and death.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938099/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japan Multi-Institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) Study is a large population-based genome cohort study in which about 100,000 participants from 15 study areas of Japan are being followed up for 20 years for cancer incidence.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90090964</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study on meat consumption in a Japanese population: the Japan Multi-Institutional Collaborative Cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34733494</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34733494+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analysed GWAS data using 14 076 participants from the Japan Multi-Institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Japanese multi-institutional genome cohort, launched in 2005, of 92,610 adults aged 35–69 years from 14 study regions in 12 prefectures (respondents to study announcements, people attending local-government health checkups or health checkup centres, and first-visit patients at a cancer hospital), who gave baseline questionnaire data and blood samples in 2005–2014 and are followed until 2025, to examine gene–environment interactions in lifestyle-related diseases, mainly cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17696755</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32963210</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">92610</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults aged 35-69 in the baseline survey (2005-2014)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32963210</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After excluding 8,294 respondents under 35 or over 70 years of age and 578 who withdrew consent or became ineligible, the remaining 92,610 participants (40,880 men and 51,730 women with an average age of 55.2 [standard deviation, 9.4] years) in the baseline survey were included in the present analysis (the dataset was fixed on February 2, 2020).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>J-MICC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid5100"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002164"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST001153</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25429525</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of urinary bladder cancer run from Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in which patients diagnosed from 1995 to 2010 under the age of 76 and living in the catchment area of seven hospitals in the east of the country were identified through the Netherlands Cancer Registry and invited in batches, with controls drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, to study genetic and lifestyle risk factors and outcomes of bladder cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym NBCS also denotes Norwegian Breast Cancer Study (COHO:0000573) and Nigerian Breast Cancer Study (COHO:0001381); this term is Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1809</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4370</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NBCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid5100">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001187"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5100"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>urinary bladder cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4453642/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we analysed data of the Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study (NBCS), one of the largest case–control studies for UBC worldwide, as to gain better insights into the role of recurrent infections of the (lower) urinary tract as a risk factor for UBC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4453642/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Within the framework of the NBCS, UBC patients living in the catchment area of seven hospitals in the eastern part of the country were identified through the Netherlands Cancer Registry (NCR) held by the Comprehensive Cancer Centre the Netherlands (IKNL) (Kiemeney et al, 2008).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001153</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European genome-wide association study identifies SLC14A1 as a new urinary bladder cancer susceptibility gene.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21750109</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Dutch patients were recruited for the Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study (NBCS: http://dceg.cancer.gov/icbc/membership.html).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25429525</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Recurrent urinary tract infection and risk of bladder cancer in the Nijmegen bladder cancer study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25429525</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4453642/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we analysed data of the Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study (NBCS), one of the largest case–control studies for UBC worldwide, as to gain better insights into the role of recurrent infections of the (lower) urinary tract as a risk factor for UBC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of urinary bladder cancer run from Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in which patients diagnosed from 1995 to 2010 under the age of 76 and living in the catchment area of seven hospitals in the east of the country were identified through the Netherlands Cancer Registry and invited in batches, with controls drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, to study genetic and lifestyle risk factors and outcomes of bladder cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4453642/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1809</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>analysed subset: Caucasian bladder cancer patients and Nijmegen Biomedical Study controls</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25429525</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included 1809 UBC patients (81% male) and 4370 controls (45% male).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000572"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4370</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>analysed subset: Caucasian bladder cancer patients and Nijmegen Biomedical Study controls</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25429525</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included 1809 UBC patients (81% male) and 4370 controls (45% male).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
