        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5186"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mild cognitive impairment</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29980228+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Inclusion criteria were having normal cognition (NC) or a diagnosis of mild cognitive impairment (MCI) or AD-type dementia at baseline, age above 50 years, known amyloid-beta (Aβ) status, availability of cognitive test results and at least two of the following materials: plasma, DNA, magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) or cerebrospinal fluid (CSF).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5188"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29980228+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Inclusion criteria were having normal cognition (NC) or a diagnosis of mild cognitive impairment (MCI) or AD-type dementia at baseline, age above 50 years, known amyloid-beta (Aβ) status, availability of cognitive test results and at least two of the following materials: plasma, DNA, magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) or cerebrospinal fluid (CSF).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000374"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6035398/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 11 selected cohorts included three multicenter studies—EDAR (n = 204) [14], PharmaCog (n = 147) [15] and DESCRIPA (n = 29) [16]—and eight single centers: Antwerp (n = 149) [17], Amsterdam (n = 172) [18], Barcelona Sant Pau (n = 45) [19], Barcelona IDIBAPS (n = 120) [20], Leuven (n = 180) [21], San Sebastian GAP (n = 40) [22], Gothenburg (n = 95) [23] and Lausanne (n = 40) [24].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6035398/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 11 selected cohorts included three multicenter studies—EDAR (n = 204) [14], PharmaCog (n = 147) [15] and DESCRIPA (n = 29) [16]—and eight single centers: Antwerp (n = 149) [17], Amsterdam (n = 172) [18], Barcelona Sant Pau (n = 45) [19], Barcelona IDIBAPS (n = 120) [20], Leuven (n = 180) [21], San Sebastian GAP (n = 40) [22], Gothenburg (n = 95) [23] and Lausanne (n = 40) [24].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104685</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Brain Imaging Biomarkers and Neuropsychological Phenotypes in the European Medical Information Framework for Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Multimodal Biomarker Discovery Dataset.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35386118</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35386118+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifically, we utilized genotype and phenotype data from n = 931 individuals collected under the auspices of the European Medical Information Framework for Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Multimodal Biomarker Discovery (EMIF-AD MBD) study to perform a total of 19 separate GWAS analyses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A European multimodal biomarker dataset of 1,221 people aged over 50 with normal cognition, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer-type dementia and known amyloid status, whose existing clinical data, samples and scans were retrospectively combined from 11 prospective European cohort studies (three multicenter and eight single-center studies) within the Innovative Medicines Initiative-funded European Medical Information Framework, with plasma, cerebrospinal fluid, DNA and MRI data for discovery of diagnostic and prognostic Alzheimer disease biomarkers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29980228</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000581"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1221</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people with normal cognition, MCI or AD-type dementia pooled from 11 cohorts</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29980228</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 1221 subjects were included in the study, with a mean age of 67.9 (SD 8.3) years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
