        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90277987</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of about 1,000 people from Carlantino, a small isolated village in Apulia (Foggia province), southern Italy, who underwent clinical and instrumental evaluations between 1998 and 2005; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CAR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INGI-CAR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INGI-CARL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INGI-CARLANTINO</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INGI-Carlantino</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Italian Network on Genetic Isolates-Carlantino</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Italian Network of Genetic Isolates - Carlantino</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4997959/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In particular, our study used 370 individuals from INGI-CARL, a population coming from Carlantino, a small village located in Puglia (Southern Italy), and 843 defined as INGI-FVG, making reference to 6 villages situated in the Friuli Venezia Region in North-Eastern Italy for a total of 1207 samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90277987</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Regulator of G-Protein Signalling 9: A New Candidate Gene for Sweet Food Liking?</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37174278</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The discovery phase was carried out on a total of 1482 participants divided as follows: 1109 from the Val Borbera (VBI) cohort in Northern Italy, and 373 from Carlantino (CAR) in Southern Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
