        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of about 173,000 Korean men and women aged 40 and over recruited in 2004–2013 from the national health examinee registry at health examination centres, mainly in urban areas, as the largest cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans.</obo:IAO_0000115>
