        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST001650</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:42509442</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genome-wide association sub-study of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative comprising a randomly selected sample of about 8,500 African American and 3,600 Hispanic women from WHI, genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array under the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) project.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym SHARe also denotes Sinai-Helmsley Alliance for Research Excellence (COHO:0000725), SNP Health Association Asthma Resource Project (COHO:0002374) and Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe (COHO:0002644); this term is WHI SNP Health Association Resource.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SHARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI-SHARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Women&apos;s Health Initiative SNP Health Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Women&apos;s Health Initiative SNP Health Association Resource GWAS study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Health Initiative SNP Health Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">WHI SNP Health Association Resource</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000604"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41398-025-03418-z/MediaObjects/41398_2025_3418_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 161,838 women aged 50–79 years old were recruited from 40 clinical centers in the US between 1993 and 1998.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000604"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5714283/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Black and Hispanic WHI participants were drawn from the single nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) Health Association Resource Project (SHARe) (National Institutes of Health 2011).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000604"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001650</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association and population genetic analysis of C-reactive protein in African American and Hispanic American women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22939635</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:22939635%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;resultType=core&amp;format=json</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed genome-wide association studies (GWASs) of 8,280 African American (AA) and 3,548 Hispanic American (HA) postmenopausal women from the Women&apos;s Health Initiative SNP Health Association Resource.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000604"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:42509442</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Validation of fracture-derived polygenic scores with FRAX for fracture risk prediction in postmenopausal women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42509442</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13408118/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Model development and internal validation were conducted using participants from the Genomics and Randomized Trials Network (WHI-GARNET), the WHI Memory Study (WHI-MS), and the SNP Health Association Resource (WHI-SHARe).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000604"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide association sub-study of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative comprising a randomly selected sample of about 8,500 African American and 3,600 Hispanic women from WHI, genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array under the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) project.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41398-025-03418-z/MediaObjects/41398_2025_3418_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5714283/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000604"/>
