        <owl:annotatedTarget>An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of over 11,000 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.</owl:annotatedTarget>
