        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Longitudinal, observational study on nutritional and lifestyle factors for colorectal cancer and related outcomes (COLON)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001615"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GECCO and CCFR Study Descriptions Ontario Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry (OFCCR): In GECCO, a subset of the Assessment of Risk in Colorectal Tumors in Canada (ARCTIC) from the Ontario Registry for Studies of Familial Colorectal Cancer (OFCCR) was used.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002144"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>NHS (Advanced Adenoma) USA Cohort 513 100 578 100 1,091 Illumina OmniExpress</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23880798+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All four studies participated in the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90502765</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association studies and Mendelian randomization analyses provide insights into the causes of early-onset colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38408508</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11213623/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study comprised a meta-analysis of existing genotyped and imputed data for 6176 EOCRC cases (&lt;50 years of age) and 65 829 controls from the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO), the Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study (CORECT), the Colon Cancer Family Registry (CCFR), and the UK Biobank.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">130000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants with individual-level data managed by the coordinating center, from 70 studies (stated as over 130,000)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GECCO coordinating center manages individual level genetic and epidemiological data of over 130,000 participants from 70 studies from North America, Australia, Asia, and Europe.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GECCO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


