        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective family study of 1,017 families (both parents and their children) from a postcode-defined area of central Exeter, United Kingdom, with anthropometry and fasting biochemistry at 28 weeks of gestation, cord blood at delivery and child follow-up to age 2 years, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis and identify genetic variants influencing birthweight and early postnatal growth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
