    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5672"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>obesity</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 300-Obese (300-OB) cohort, one of the studies of the Human Functional Genomics Project, comprises a group of more than 300 individuals of Western-European ancestry with a body mass index (BMI) greater than or equal to greater than or equal to 27 kg/m2, aged between 55 and 80 years (12).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>300OB is an obese cohort of 302 individuals aged 54–81 years old, who were enrolled in the study at the Radboud University Medical Center, Nijmegen, the Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90654631</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Unraveling interindividual variation of trimethylamine N-oxide and its precursors at the population level.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38898991</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11183189/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population included participants from Rotterdam Study I‐4 (RSI‐4), Rotterdam Study III‐2 (RSIII‐2), Leiden Longevity Study (LLS), LifeLines‐DEEP (LLD), and 300‐Obese cohort (300‐OB).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of about 300 overweight or obese adults (BMI of 27 kg/m2 or more) aged 54–81 of Western European ancestry, enrolled at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, within the Human Functional Genomics Project to discover pathways, including inflammation and immune responses, that contribute to cardiovascular disease in overweight and obese people.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">302</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>overweight or obese adults enrolled (BMI 27 or more)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 302 individuals with a body mass index greater than or equal to 27 kg/m2 participated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
