        <obo:IAO_0000116>BMT recipients in the two cohorts after QC (their unrelated donors not counted)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28811306</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Replication and validation of these SNP associations were performed using DISCOVeRY-BMT (Determining the Influence of Susceptibility COnveying Variants Related to one-Year mortality after BMT), a well-powered genome-wide association study consisting of 2 cohorts, totaling 2888 BMT recipients with acute myeloid leukemia, acute lymphoblastic leukemia, or myelodysplastic syndrome, and their HLA-matched unrelated donors, reported to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642"/>
