        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000784"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90255376</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16851</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">32473</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16851</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NINDS Stroke Genetics Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NINDS-SiGN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke SiGN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SIGN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SiGN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) Stroke Genetics Network (SiGN)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Stroke Genetics Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid5856">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_1060198"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid5856"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>ischemic stroke</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>National Institute of Neurologic Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) has established the Stroke Genetics Network (SiGN) with the goal of assembling the largest possible sample of individuals with ischemic stroke for genetic studies, where each individual has been uniformly and thoroughly characterized for stroke subtyping.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000150"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6260132/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>DNA was extracted from whole blood and genotyping was performed with either the HumanOmniExpress Exome BeadChip v1.0 at the Broad Institute (SAHLSIS: n = 756; MDC: n = 2,060) or the HumanOmni 5M Exome v1.0 as part of the Stroke Genetics Network (SiGN) study (SAHLSIS: n = 444; Illumina, San Diego, California, United States) as described.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000456"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 4,253 additional CCS-phenotyped cases from 10 GRCs across Europe and the US have been previously genotyped prior to initiating SiGN (BRAINS, EDIN, GASROS, GEOS, ISGS, NHS, MUNICH, OXVASC, ST GEORGE’S, and SWISS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
