        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24124113</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of seven Mexican-American cohorts in the United States (the IRAS Family Study, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero, IRAS and TRIPOD; 4,336 individuals in 1,346 pedigrees) formed to conduct genome-wide association studies of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance measured by euglycemic clamp or frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4336</coho:numberOfParticipants>
