        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Young men were randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area in Sweden using national population registers, contacted by telephone, and invited to participate.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001593</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>WNT16 influences bone mineral density, cortical bone thickness, bone strength, and osteoporotic fracture risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22792071</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Gothenburg Osteoporosis and Obesity Determinants (GOOD) study was initiated to determine both environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass [39]</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of 1,068 young men aged 18–20, randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area of Sweden from national population registers, initiated to determine environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass, with a five-year follow-up examination.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22792071</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1068</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>young men who agreed to participate at baseline</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>There were no other exclusion criteria, and 49% of the study candidates agreed to participate (n = 1068).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GOOD</owl:annotatedTarget>
