        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer&apos;s Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer&apos;s disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium&apos;s Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
