        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of 6,357 Latinos aged 40 years and older, mostly of Mexican origin, from six census tracts in Los Angeles, California, United States, examined from 2000 to assess the prevalence and risk factors of visual impairment and eye diseases such as cataract, glaucoma, diabetic retinopathy and age-related macular degeneration.</owl:annotatedTarget>
