    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000738 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000738">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6665"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mexico"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90095033</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control sample of 967 Mexican adults with type 2 diabetes, preferentially diagnosed before age 55, and 343 normoglycaemic controls from Mexico City, Mexico, who are covered by the Mexican Social Security Institute and were recruited at the Medical Center Siglo XXI, used in genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes and lipid traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MC and the name Mexico City, the PGS Catalog’s id and name for the two Mexico City samples together, also denote Mexico City sample 2 (COHO:0000737); this term is Mexico City sample 1.</obo:IAO_0000116>
