        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6746"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24356592+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DCCT (1982-1993) was a controlled clinical trial in 1,441 subjects with T1DM comparing intensive therapy (INT), aimed at achieving levels of glycemia as close to the nondiabetic range as safely possible, with conventional therapy (CON), which aimed to maintain safe asymptomatic glucose control.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9727532/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DCCT was a multicenter randomized clinical trial, including 1441 volunteers (96%–97% Caucasian), aged 13 years to 39 years, with T1D of 1 year to 15 years duration from 29 medical centers in the United States and Canada conducted from 1983 to 1993</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90662913</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetics of C-Peptide and Age at Diagnosis in Type 1 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39556808</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11755686/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a meta-GWAS of C-peptide that including four T1D studies: the Scottish Diabetes Research Network Type 1 Bioresource (SDRNT1BIO) (4,16), Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) (17,18), Coronary Artery Calcification in T1D (CACTI) (19,20), and Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Diabetic Retinopathy (WESDR) (21).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of 1,441 people aged 13–39 years with type 1 diabetes from 29 centres in the United States and Canada, enrolled in the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (1983–1993), a randomised trial comparing intensive with conventional therapy to test whether glycaemic control prevents or delays the complications of type 1 diabetes, and followed since 1994 in the observational Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications (EDIC) study of the durability of the treatment effects on advanced microvascular complications and cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24356592</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9727532/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1441</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people with type 1 diabetes randomised in the DCCT (the cohort followed in EDIC), 1993</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24356592</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DCCT (1982-1993) was a controlled clinical trial in 1,441 subjects with T1DM comparing intensive therapy (INT), aimed at achieving levels of glycemia as close to the nondiabetic range as safely possible, with conventional therapy (CON), which aimed to maintain safe asymptomatic glucose control.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DCCT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DCCT-EDIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DCCT/EDIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000747"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EDIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6756"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000710"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90275117</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide Danish cohort of about 100,000 pregnant women recruited early in pregnancy between 1996 and 2002, run by Statens Serum Institut, with telephone interviews during pregnancy and after birth, biological samples from mother and umbilical cord, and long-term follow-up of the children through questionnaires and national registry linkage, established to study the causal links between early-life exposures and later disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">92274</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/DNBC</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DNBC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Danish National Birth Cohort/Statens Serum Institut</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Danish National Birth Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Danish National Birth Cohort</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.dnbc.dk"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.dnbc.dk/"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6756">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ExO_0000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6756"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>exposures in early life</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.dnbc.dk/about-the-dnbc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Danish National Birth Cohort (DNBC) was established to investigate the causal link between exposures in early life and disease later on and the possibilities for disease prevention.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.dnbc.dk/about-the-dnbc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data collection started in 1996 and the project covered all regions in Denmark in 1999.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90275117</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic effects on the timing of parturition and links to fetal birth weight.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37012456</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10101852/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Access to the Danish National Birth Cohort (phs000103.v1.p1), Hyperglycemia and Adverse Pregnancy Outcome (phs000096.v4.p1) and Genomic and Proteomic Network (phs000714.v1.p1) individual-level phenotype and genetic data can be obtained through dbGaP Authorized Access portal (https://dbgap.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/aa/wga.cgi?page=login).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide Danish cohort of about 100,000 pregnant women recruited early in pregnancy between 1996 and 2002, run by Statens Serum Institut, with telephone interviews during pregnancy and after birth, biological samples from mother and umbilical cord, and long-term follow-up of the children through questionnaires and national registry linkage, established to study the causal links between early-life exposures and later disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.dnbc.dk/about-the-dnbc</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">92274</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pregnant women recruited 1996-2002</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01343-9/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1343_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DNBC is a collection of data on 92,274 pregnant women recruited between 1996 and 2002, from their first antenatal visit to their general practitioner.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DNBC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000748"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Danish National Birth Cohort/Statens Serum Institut</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6764"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6766"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90239710</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in the Lombardy region of Italy, which enrolled 2,101 incident primary lung cancer cases from 13 hospitals and 2,120 matched population controls in 2002–2005, collecting epidemiological, clinical and molecular data and biospecimens to study lung cancer aetiology from smoking addiction to outcome.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym EAGLE also denotes EArly Genetics and Lifecourse Epidemiology consortium (COHO:0000750) and EAGLE BioVU (COHO:0000751); this term is Environment And Genetics in Lung cancer Etiology study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2101</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2120</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EAGLE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EAGLE study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Environment and Genetics in Lung Cancer Etiology Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Environment And Genetics in Lung cancer Etiology study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6764">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008903"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6766">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000013"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6764"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18538025+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 2002 and 2005, we enrolled 2101 incident primary lung cancer cases and 2120 population controls, with 86.6% and 72.4% participation rate, respectively, from a catchment area including 216 municipalities in the Lombardy region of Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6766"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>smoking</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18538025+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We designed a large population-based case-control study that combines a traditional molecular epidemiology design with a more integrative approach to investigate the dynamic process that begins with smoking initiation, proceeds through dependency/smoking persistence, continues with lung cancer development and ends with progression to disseminated disease or response to therapy and survival.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18538025+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 2002 and 2005, we enrolled 2101 incident primary lung cancer cases and 2120 population controls, with 86.6% and 72.4% participation rate, respectively, from a catchment area including 216 municipalities in the Lombardy region of Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90239710</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide interaction analysis identified low-frequency variants with sex disparity in lung cancer risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35138370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9402242/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The EAGLE study was supported by the intramural program of the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics, National Cancer Institute, NIH.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in the Lombardy region of Italy, which enrolled 2,101 incident primary lung cancer cases from 13 hospitals and 2,120 matched population controls in 2002–2005, collecting epidemiological, clinical and molecular data and biospecimens to study lung cancer aetiology from smoking addiction to outcome.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18538025</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2101</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>incident lung cancer cases and population controls enrolled 2002-2005</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18538025</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 2002 and 2005, we enrolled 2101 incident primary lung cancer cases and 2120 population controls, with 86.6% and 72.4% participation rate, respectively, from a catchment area including 216 municipalities in the Lombardy region of Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2120</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>incident lung cancer cases and population controls enrolled 2002-2005</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18538025</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 2002 and 2005, we enrolled 2101 incident primary lung cancer cases and 2120 population controls, with 86.6% and 72.4% participation rate, respectively, from a catchment area including 216 municipalities in the Lombardy region of Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000749"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EAGLE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
