        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Hawaii, United States, in which Japanese, Caucasian and Native Hawaiian residents of Oahu newly diagnosed with colorectal adenocarcinoma between January 1994 and August 1998 were identified through the Hawaii SEER registry and matched by sex, ethnicity and age to controls from a population-based health survey of the Hawaii State Department of Health and from Health Care Financing Administration participants, with in-person interviews and blood samples; its genotyped participants take part in consortium studies of genetic and lifestyle risk factors for colorectal cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
