        <rdfs:comment>At baseline visit, Malay, Indian, and Chinese subjects from SEED were recruited under 3 studies: the Singapore Malay Eye Study (year 2004–2006), the Singapore Indian Eye Study (year 2007–2009), and the Singapore Chinese Eye Study (year 2009–2011).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000764"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3852120/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the Singapore Indian Eye Study (SINDI), which is part of the Singapore Indian Chinese Cohort Eye Study (SICC) [42], consists of 2538 Indian subjects aged 40 and above, and the Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES) [43-45] is a genome-wide association study of CCT phenotype which contains 2542 Malay subjects aged 40 and above.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
