        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90461907</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of prostate-specific antigen levels in 392,522 men identifies new loci and improves prediction across ancestry groups.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39930085</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11821537/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The AAPC comprises AFR studies with prostate cancer phenotyping</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000768"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of epidemiological studies of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, mainly African American men, assembled to conduct genome-wide association studies of prostate cancer susceptibility in men of African descent.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21602798</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29117387</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33398198</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000768"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4853</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer cases and controls of African ancestry in the AAPC GWAS (as pooled in the 2017 meta-analysis)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29117387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To search for additional PCa risk variants in men of African ancestry that may contribute to their greater disease incidence, we combined genetic association results from the African Ancestry Prostate Cancer GWAS Consortium (AAPC; 4853 case subjects and 4678 control subjects) (9), the Ghana Prostate Study (474 case subjects and 458 control subjects) (10), the Kaiser/ProHealth Prostate Cancer Study (601 case subjects and 1650 control subjects) (11), and the ELLIPSE/PRACTICAL OncoArray Consortium (4274 case subjects and 4024 control subjects) (Supplementary Table 1, available online).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000768"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4678</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer cases and controls of African ancestry in the AAPC GWAS (as pooled in the 2017 meta-analysis)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29117387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To search for additional PCa risk variants in men of African ancestry that may contribute to their greater disease incidence, we combined genetic association results from the African Ancestry Prostate Cancer GWAS Consortium (AAPC; 4853 case subjects and 4678 control subjects) (9), the Ghana Prostate Study (474 case subjects and 458 control subjects) (10), the Kaiser/ProHealth Prostate Cancer Study (601 case subjects and 1650 control subjects) (11), and the ELLIPSE/PRACTICAL OncoArray Consortium (4274 case subjects and 4024 control subjects) (Supplementary Table 1, available online).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000768"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AAPC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


