    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6984"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6986"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000461"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000466"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90308728</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-site, multi-generational family study in which probands recruited through alcohol treatment centres and their relatives, together with community comparison families, have been assessed over more than 30 years (nearly 18,000 individuals from over 2200 families) with psychiatric interviews, questionnaires, electrophysiology and DNA to identify genetic factors in alcohol use disorder and related outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17878</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COGA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative Studies on the Genetics of Alcoholism</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative Study for the Genetics of Alcoholism</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6984">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0021698"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6986">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_0001082"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6984"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>alcohol use disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10550787/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>COGA is a multi‐generational family‐based study in which probands were recruited through alcohol treatment centers, along with a set of community comparison families.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6986"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>alcohol use</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37581339+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants range in age from 7 to 97, with many having longitudinal assessments, providing a valuable opportunity to study alcohol use and problems across the lifespan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10550787/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>At the study&apos;s inception, high‐risk families were ascertained through probands who were undergoing treatment for AUDs at six sites across the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90308728</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genomic risk for post-traumatic stress disorder in families densely affected with alcohol use disorders.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37344610</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37344610+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We examined genome-wide associations for DSM-IV PTSD among 4,978 trauma-exposed participants (31% with alcohol dependence, 50% female, 30% African ancestry) from the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism (COGA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-site, multi-generational family study in which probands recruited through alcohol treatment centres and their relatives, together with community comparison families, have been assessed over more than 30 years (nearly 18,000 individuals from over 2200 families) with psychiatric interviews, questionnaires, electrophysiology and DNA to identify genetic factors in alcohol use disorder and related outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37581339</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17878</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in 2246 families assessed in one or more waves over 30+ years (2023)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10550787/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To date, there have been 17,878 individuals in 2246 families who have participated in one or more of the assessment waves.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>COGA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid6993"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000024"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000547"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000618"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000732"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000774"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90502765</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A colorectal cancer genetic epidemiology consortium, approved at the University of Southern California and funded within the NCI GAME-ON post-GWAS initiative, that pools genome-wide genotype data from colorectal cancer case-control studies such as the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Study, the Colon Cancer Family Registry and the Kentucky and Newfoundland case-control studies to find and characterise colorectal cancer susceptibility variants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7561</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6328</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CORECT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ColoRectal Transdisciplinary Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Colorectal Cancer Transdisciplinary Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid6993">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid6993"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We subsequently replicated these associations in two large colorectal cancer consortia of European-descent populations (allele frequency 0.09): Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study (CORECT) with 7,561 cases and 6,328 controls from 8 participating studies</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000024"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORECT study meta-analysis was conducted using germline DNA the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer study (MECC) (set 1: 484 cases and 498 controls; set 2: 1,120 cases and 820 controls), CCFR (set 1: 1,977 cases and 999 controls; set 2: 1,660 cases and 1,393 controls), Kentucky case-control study (1,038 cases and 1,134 controls), Newfoundland case-control study (548 cases and 538 controls), American Cancer Society CPS II nested case-control study (ACS/CPSII, 539 cases and 469 controls) and the Melbourne nested case-control study (195 cases and 477 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORECT study meta-analysis was conducted using germline DNA the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer study (MECC) (set 1: 484 cases and 498 controls; set 2: 1,120 cases and 820 controls), CCFR (set 1: 1,977 cases and 999 controls; set 2: 1,660 cases and 1,393 controls), Kentucky case-control study (1,038 cases and 1,134 controls), Newfoundland case-control study (548 cases and 538 controls), American Cancer Society CPS II nested case-control study (ACS/CPSII, 539 cases and 469 controls) and the Melbourne nested case-control study (195 cases and 477 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000547"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORECT study meta-analysis was conducted using germline DNA the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer study (MECC) (set 1: 484 cases and 498 controls; set 2: 1,120 cases and 820 controls), CCFR (set 1: 1,977 cases and 999 controls; set 2: 1,660 cases and 1,393 controls), Kentucky case-control study (1,038 cases and 1,134 controls), Newfoundland case-control study (548 cases and 538 controls), American Cancer Society CPS II nested case-control study (ACS/CPSII, 539 cases and 469 controls) and the Melbourne nested case-control study (195 cases and 477 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORECT study meta-analysis was conducted using germline DNA the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer study (MECC) (set 1: 484 cases and 498 controls; set 2: 1,120 cases and 820 controls), CCFR (set 1: 1,977 cases and 999 controls; set 2: 1,660 cases and 1,393 controls), Kentucky case-control study (1,038 cases and 1,134 controls), Newfoundland case-control study (548 cases and 538 controls), American Cancer Society CPS II nested case-control study (ACS/CPSII, 539 cases and 469 controls) and the Melbourne nested case-control study (195 cases and 477 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000618"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORECT study meta-analysis was conducted using germline DNA the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer study (MECC) (set 1: 484 cases and 498 controls; set 2: 1,120 cases and 820 controls), CCFR (set 1: 1,977 cases and 999 controls; set 2: 1,660 cases and 1,393 controls), Kentucky case-control study (1,038 cases and 1,134 controls), Newfoundland case-control study (548 cases and 538 controls), American Cancer Society CPS II nested case-control study (ACS/CPSII, 539 cases and 469 controls) and the Melbourne nested case-control study (195 cases and 477 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000732"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CORECT study meta-analysis was conducted using germline DNA the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer study (MECC) (set 1: 484 cases and 498 controls; set 2: 1,120 cases and 820 controls), CCFR (set 1: 1,977 cases and 999 controls; set 2: 1,660 cases and 1,393 controls), Kentucky case-control study (1,038 cases and 1,134 controls), Newfoundland case-control study (548 cases and 538 controls), American Cancer Society CPS II nested case-control study (ACS/CPSII, 539 cases and 469 controls) and the Melbourne nested case-control study (195 cases and 477 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90502765</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association studies and Mendelian randomization analyses provide insights into the causes of early-onset colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38408508</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11213623/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a GWAS meta-analysis of 6176 EOCRC cases and 65 829 controls from the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO), the Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study (CORECT), the Colon Cancer Family Registry (CCFR), and the UK Biobank.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A colorectal cancer genetic epidemiology consortium, approved at the University of Southern California and funded within the NCI GAME-ON post-GWAS initiative, that pools genome-wide genotype data from colorectal cancer case-control studies such as the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Study, the Colon Cancer Family Registry and the Kentucky and Newfoundland case-control studies to find and characterise colorectal cancer susceptibility variants.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25105248</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7561</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer cases and controls of European descent from 8 CORECT studies (replication in the 2014 trans-ethnic GWAS)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This locus has not previously been reported to be associated with CRC.We subsequently replicated these associations in two large colorectal cancer consortia of European-descent populations (allele frequency 0.09): Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study (CORECT) with 7,561 cases and 6,328 controls from 8 participating studies (combined OR = 1.09, P = 0.036, Table 1) and Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO) with 9,262 cases and 11,883 controls from 18 participating studies (combined OR = 1.09, P = 0.018, Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6328</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer cases and controls of European descent from 8 CORECT studies (replication in the 2014 trans-ethnic GWAS)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This locus has not previously been reported to be associated with CRC.We subsequently replicated these associations in two large colorectal cancer consortia of European-descent populations (allele frequency 0.09): Colorectal Transdisciplinary Study (CORECT) with 7,561 cases and 6,328 controls from 8 participating studies (combined OR = 1.09, P = 0.036, Table 1) and Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO) with 9,262 cases and 11,883 controls from 18 participating studies (combined OR = 1.09, P = 0.018, Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000773"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CORECT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


