        <owl:annotatedTarget>A network of cancer genetic epidemiology consortia, the NIH-funded post-cancer-GWAS initiative, that brings together genome-wide association data from colorectal (CORECT), breast (DRIVE), prostate (ELLIPSE), ovarian (FOCI) and lung (TRICL) cancer consortia, mainly of people of European descent.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27598322</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000774"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">47800</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cancer cases and controls in the GAME-ON GWAS data used for the 2016 height Mendelian randomization analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27598322</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Mendelian randomization analyses were conducted using summary statistics obtained for 423 genetic variants identified from a recent GWAS of adult height and from a cancer genetics consortium study of multiple cancers that included 47,800 cases and 81,353 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000774"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
