    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid7063"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267567</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre sample of healthy non-diabetic offspring of patients with type 2 diabetes, recruited in Denmark, Finland, Germany, Italy and Sweden by the European Network on Functional Genomics of Type 2 Diabetes and examined with glucose tolerance tests and hyperinsulinaemic euglycaemic clamps to study the genetics of insulin secretion and insulin sensitivity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">849</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EUGENE2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EUGENE2 Consortium study populations</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EUGENE2 study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid7063">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7063"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19789630+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Oral and intravenous glucose stimulated insulin release (n = 849) and insulin sensitivity (n = 596) estimated from a hyperinsulinemic euglycemic clamp were measured in non-diabetic offspring of type 2 diabetic patients from five European populations.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2575233/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted our study on SGK genetic variance and potential associations with insulin secretory function in the German TUEF cohort and the EUGENE2 consortium (Denmark, Finland, Germany, Italy, and Sweden), as these two European diabetes risk populations were extensively phenotyped for insulin secretion traits at the prediabetic stage.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267567</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study and functional characterization identifies candidate genes for insulin-stimulated glucose uptake.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37291194</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7614755/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Supplementary Table 1 - cohort specific information Cohort Name KORA FHS Fenland-CoreExome Fenland-GWAS Fenland-OMICS Ely LURIC METSIM LIFE-Adult Sorbs ULSAM HTN-IR MACAD TaiChi RISC ADDITION-PRO RigCoh Inter99 Health_2008 BC1936 PPP Botnia MDC Botnia_families TUEF/TULIP EUGENE2</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre sample of healthy non-diabetic offspring of patients with type 2 diabetes, recruited in Denmark, Finland, Germany, Italy and Sweden by the European Network on Functional Genomics of Type 2 Diabetes and examined with glucose tolerance tests and hyperinsulinaemic euglycaemic clamps to study the genetics of insulin secretion and insulin sensitivity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18985156</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19789630</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">849</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>non-diabetic offspring of type 2 diabetes patients with DNA available, five centres (2009)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2747270/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Altogether DNA from 849 non-diabetic offspring was available for examination: Danes (n = 253), Finns (n = 217), Germans (n = 149), Italians (n = 130), and Swedes (n = 100).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000779"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EUGENE2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid7070"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90704646</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-site case-control study run with GlaxoSmithKline that recruited people with Alzheimer&apos;s disease from memory referral clinics in Canada, with cognitively unimpaired controls from their non-biological relatives, friends or spouses, to find genetic variants associated with Alzheimer&apos;s disease risk and age at onset.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">753</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">736</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENADA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenADA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenADA study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Alzheimer’s Disease Associations</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genotype Phenotype Associations in Alzheimers Disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Multi-Site Collaborative Study for Genotype-Phenotype Associations in Alzheimer&apos;s Disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid7070">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7070"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17998437+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The hypothesis-generating data set consisted of 753 individuals with AD by National Institute of Neurological and Communicative Diseases and Stroke/Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders Association criteria recruited from 9 memory referral clinics in Canada and 736 ethnically matched control subjects;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17998437+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The hypothesis-generating data set consisted of 753 individuals with AD by National Institute of Neurological and Communicative Diseases and Stroke/Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders Association criteria recruited from 9 memory referral clinics in Canada and 736 ethnically matched control subjects;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90704646</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Consensus meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies for Alzheimer&apos;s disease and related dementias.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42237039</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13263136/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Across all studies, we filtered out duplicated variants and those with (1) missing data for effect size, s.e. or P value; (2) an absolute effect size &gt;5 and (3) imputation quality &lt;0.3 (0.8 for the GenADA study).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-site case-control study run with GlaxoSmithKline that recruited people with Alzheimer&apos;s disease from memory referral clinics in Canada, with cognitively unimpaired controls from their non-biological relatives, friends or spouses, to find genetic variants associated with Alzheimer&apos;s disease risk and age at onset.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17998437</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">753</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AD cases from 9 Canadian memory clinics and cognitively normal controls in the discovery GWAS (2008)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17998437</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The hypothesis-generating data set consisted of 753 individuals with AD by National Institute of Neurological and Communicative Diseases and Stroke/Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders Association criteria recruited from 9 memory referral clinics in Canada and 736 ethnically matched control subjects; control subjects were recruited from nonbiological relatives, friends, or spouses of the patients and did not exhibit cognitive impairment by history or cognitive testing.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">736</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AD cases from 9 Canadian memory clinics and cognitively normal controls in the discovery GWAS (2008)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17998437</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The hypothesis-generating data set consisted of 753 individuals with AD by National Institute of Neurological and Communicative Diseases and Stroke/Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders Association criteria recruited from 9 memory referral clinics in Canada and 736 ethnically matched control subjects; control subjects were recruited from nonbiological relatives, friends, or spouses of the patients and did not exhibit cognitive impairment by history or cognitive testing.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000780"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GENADA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
