    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7127"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>stroke</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Miami Stroke Registry and Biorepository (MIAMISR) The MIAMISR at the University of Miami/Jackson Memorial Hospital (Miami, FL, U.S.A.) is an ongoing prospective hospital registry of consecutive patients subjects with prevalent stroke (ischemic and hemorrhagic) and TIA with available neuroimaging (CT or MRI) who provide informed consent.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7129"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>transient ischemic attack</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Miami Stroke Registry and Biorepository (MIAMISR) The MIAMISR at the University of Miami/Jackson Memorial Hospital (Miami, FL, U.S.A.) is an ongoing prospective hospital registry of consecutive patients subjects with prevalent stroke (ischemic and hemorrhagic) and TIA with available neuroimaging (CT or MRI) who provide informed consent.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5570675/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of those sites, 7 are European centers (BASICMAR—Spain, BRAINS—United Kingdom, GRAZ—Austria, KRAKOW—Poland, LEUVEN—Belgium, LUND STROKE REGISTER—Sweden, and SAHLSIS—Sweden) and 5 are based in the United States (GASROS, GCNKSS, GEOS, ISGS, and MIAMISR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST005838</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiancestry genome-wide association study of 520,000 subjects identifies 32 loci associated with stroke and stroke subtypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29531354</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Miami Stroke Registry and Biorepository (MIAMISR) The MIAMISR at the University of Miami/Jackson Memorial Hospital (Miami, FL, U.S.A.) is an ongoing prospective hospital registry of consecutive patients subjects with prevalent stroke (ischemic and hemorrhagic) and TIA with available neuroimaging (CT or MRI) who provide informed consent.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective registry at the University of Miami that offers enrolment to consecutive patients admitted with stroke or transient ischaemic attack, a predominantly Hispanic and Black multiethnic population, contributing cases to the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25041610</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">473</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>stroke patients prospectively enrolled in the registry and analysed for stroke subtypes (2014 paper)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24122024</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among 473 stroke patients (mean age 64 ± 14 years; 63.7% were men) of which 52.9% were Hispanic, 22.6% were AA, 13.5% NHBC and 11.0% were NHW.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
