    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90012825</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Susceptibility to neurofibrillary tangles: role of the PTPRD locus and limited pleiotropy with other neuropathologies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28322283</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5608624/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The subjects consisted of participants from two longitudinal cohort studies operated out of The Rush Alzheimer’s Disease Center in Chicago, the Religious Order Study (ROS) and the Rush Memory and Aging Project (MAP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer&apos;s disease run by the Rush Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22471860</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29865057</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1168</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>persons who agreed to participate, January 1994 to October 2011</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3409291/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From January of 1994 through October of 2011, 1,168 persons agreed to participate and the baseline clinical evaluation has been completed on 1,162.</rdfs:comment>
