        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
