    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000827"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30206078+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HELIX study represents a collaborative project across six established and ongoing longitudinal population-based birth cohort studies in six European countries (France, Greece, Lithuania, Norway, Spain and the UK).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000827"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90302935</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Blood Mercury in European Pregnant Women and Children.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38136945</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10742428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>HELIX comprises subcohorts of mother–child pairs from six European birth cohorts [73,74].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000827"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A European population-based exposome cohort built across six existing longitudinal birth cohorts in France, Greece, Lithuania, Norway, Spain and the UK, with a subcohort of 1,301 mother-child pairs in which biomarkers, omics signatures and child health outcomes were measured at age 6–11 years, to relate multiple early-life environmental exposures to molecular signatures and child health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30206078</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000827"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31472</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mother-child pairs in the entire HELIX study population across six birth cohorts</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6144482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>HELIX used a multilevel study design with the entire study population totalling 31 472 mother-child pairs, recruited during pregnancy, in the six existing cohorts (first level); a subcohort of 1301 mother-child pairs where biomarkers, omics signatures and child health outcomes were measured at age 6–11 years (second level) and repeat-sampling panel studies with around 150 children and 150 pregnant women aimed at collecting personal exposure data (third level).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000827"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HELIX</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000828 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000828">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid7540"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454540</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of COVID-19 phenotypes from participants sequenced with the Helix Exome+ assay, including those of the Healthy Nevada Project, a population health study established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno, Nevada, contributed to COVID-19 host genetics studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym Helix also denotes Human Early Life Exposome (COHO:0000827); this term is Helix Exome+ and Healthy Nevada Project COVID-19 Phenotypes.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Helix</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Helix Exome+ COVID-19 Phenotypes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Helix_Exome</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Helix Exome+ and Healthy Nevada Project COVID-19 Phenotypes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid7540">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100096"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000828"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7540"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>COVID-19</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9632827/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>C) Susceptibility to COVID-19, where cases are anyone who tested positive for COVID-19, self-reported an infection to SARS-CoV-2, or had a mention of COVID-19 in their medical record.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000828"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Healthy Nevada Project (HNP), a population health study developed in collaboration between Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno, Nevada, was established in 2016 to examine the effects genetics may have on Nevadan health outcomes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000828"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454540</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of long COVID.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40399555</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12165857/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Genetics of Long COVID (GOLD), Helix Exome+ and Healthy Nevada Project COVID-19 Phenotypes (Helix), MexGen-COVID Initiative, COVID-19 Ioannina Biobank (Ioannina)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
