    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7617"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bladder cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, in New England, cases included patients newly diagnosed with carcinoma of the urinary bladder between 2001 and 2004 among residents of Maine, New Hampshire, and Vermont and population controls, which were frequency matched to the cases by age at diagnosis/interview, sex, and state of residence (989 White cases and 1,162 White controls with complete exposure information and genotype data).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7619"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>disinfection by-products</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In New England, a trained study interviewer visited participants’ homes and administered a computer-assisted personal interview (CAPI) that elicited information on a variety of factors, including global positioning system (GPS) coordinates of the current residence, and a lifetime residential history that was used to reconstruct lifetime water source information.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7621"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>arsenic in water supply</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In New England, a trained study interviewer visited participants’ homes and administered a computer-assisted personal interview (CAPI) that elicited information on a variety of factors, including global positioning system (GPS) coordinates of the current residence, and a lifetime residential history that was used to reconstruct lifetime water source information.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7623"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>trihalomethanes in drinking water</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In New England, a trained study interviewer visited participants’ homes and administered a computer-assisted personal interview (CAPI) that elicited information on a variety of factors, including global positioning system (GPS) coordinates of the current residence, and a lifetime residential history that was used to reconstruct lifetime water source information.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Early epidemiologic studies suggested that exposure to chlorinated drinking water was related to bladder cancer risk,13 an association that was confirmed in later studies, including the most recent meta-analysis.14 More detailed analyses have recently supported an exposure–response relationship between THM exposure and bladder cancer risk, as reviewed by Costet et al.14 Two case–control studies conducted in Spain 15 and New England, USA,16 respectively, have suggested an exposure–response relationship between increasing exposure to THMs, and bladder cancer risk.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90296729</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Association Study of Bladder Cancer Reveals New Biological and Translational Insights.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37210288</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10330197/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded tumor tissue blocks from the New England Bladder Cancer Study (NEBCS), the Spanish Bladder Cancer EPICURO Study (SBCS), and the UROMOL consortium were used to determine FGFR3 somatic mutations (Supplementary material).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer among residents of Maine, New Hampshire and Vermont, United States, with cases newly diagnosed in 2001–2004 and population controls frequency-matched on age, sex and state, used to study environmental, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35536285</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1213</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bladder cancer patients and population controls interviewed 2001-2004</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2778671/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We interviewed 1213 bladder cancer patients (65% of 1878 eligible patients).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000836"/>
