        <rdfs:comment>The SeBCS has been described above, which also contributed samples to ABCC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001185"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6838373/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For studies participating in the ABCC, the BBJ1 was supported by the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Sciences and Technology from the Japanese Government. The SeBCS was supported by the BRL (Basic Research Laboratory) program through the National Research Foundation of Korea, funded by the Ministry of Education, Science and Technology (2011-0001564). The biospecimens and data of the Hwasun Cancer Epidemiology Study-Breast were provided by the Biobank of Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital, a member of the Korea Biobank Network (07SA2014020).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001229"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7057957/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SBCGS has been described above, which also contributed samples to ABCC</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002347"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2891809/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participating studies (Principal Investigator, grant support) in the consortium are as follows: the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (WZ, R01CA64277), the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (X-OS, R01CA118229)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SGBCC contributed to BCAC and the Asian Breast Cancer Consortium, S3 Table presents three of the recent works where SGBCC had notable contributions [26, 30, 31].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002456"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891809/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participating studies (Principal Investigator, grant support) in the consortium are as follows: the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (WZ, R01CA64277), the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (X-OS, R01CA118229), the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (X-OS, R01CA92585, contributing only controls to the consortium), the Nashville Breast Health Study (WZ, R01CA100374), the Tianjin Study (KC, the National Natural Science Foundation of China Grant No. 30771844)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7057957/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, in the ABCC, genome-wide SNP data were generated from 24,206 breast cancer cases and 24,775 unaffected controls recruited from studies conducted in mainland China, South Korea, and Japan (Supplementary Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90429846</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Refining breast cancer genetic risk and biology through multi-ancestry fine-mapping analyses of 192 risk regions.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39753771</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-02031-y/MediaObjects/41588_2024_2031_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Asia Breast Cancer Consortium (ABCC) Studies conducted among Asian women include (Principal Investigator, grant support): the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (W.Z. and X.-O.S., R01CA064277)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of breast cancer genetic association studies in women of Asian ancestry, with studies in mainland China, Taiwan, South Korea and Japan (genome-wide data on about 24,000 cases and 25,000 controls by 2020), formed to discover breast cancer susceptibility loci in Asian populations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20585626</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32139696</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39753771</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">82000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Asian women (approx.) in the 2020 ABCC+BCAC meta-analysis, GWAS plus replication</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7057957/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To search for novel breast cancer susceptibility loci, we conducted Asian-specific and cross-ancestry meta-analyses combining the data of the ABCC and the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) with a total sample size of approximately 310,000 women (~82,000 Asians and ~228,000 Europeans).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000854"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ABCC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid7789"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624411</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of cohort and case-control studies with genome-wide genotype data that pools them in meta-analyses of genome-wide association studies of atrial fibrillation, to identify genetic loci for atrial fibrillation; together with the Broad AF Study, its studies formed the majority of the 2018 multi-ethnic meta-analysis of more than half a million individuals.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">65446</coho:numberOfCases>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AFGen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AFGen Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Atrial Fibrillation Genetics (AFGen) consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Atrial Fibrillation Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid7789">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004981"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7789"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>atrial fibrillation</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6136836/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were collected from both case-control studies for atrial fibrillation (AF) and population based studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3843/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3843_MOESM307_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The meta-analyses described in this manuscript included the following studies described elsewhere: The Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility Study (AGES) Reykjavik study169 , the Atrial Fibrillation Biobank LMU (AFLMU) in the context of the Arrhythmia-Biobank-LMU (formerly known as AFNET) and the Cooperative Health Research in the Region of Augsburg (KORA)169</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624411</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Cross-population GWAS and proteomics improve risk prediction and reveal mechanisms in atrial fibrillation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40645996</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12254421/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eight studies (the Nord-Trøndelag Health Study [HUNT], deCODE, DiscoverEHR, Michigan Genomics Initiative [MGI], AFGen consortium4, FinnGen R12, Swedish Infrastructure for Medical Population-Based Life-Course and Environmental Research [SIMPLER, https://www.simpler4health.se/], and Million Veteran Program[MVP]) contributed to the discovery analysis for the European GWAS, comprising 192,851 atrial fibrillation (AF) cases and 1,239,541 controls6,41,42.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of cohort and case-control studies with genome-wide genotype data that pools them in meta-analyses of genome-wide association studies of atrial fibrillation, to identify genetic loci for atrial fibrillation; together with the Broad AF Study, its studies formed the majority of the 2018 multi-ethnic meta-analysis of more than half a million individuals.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29892015</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">65446</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AF cases in the 2018 multi-ethnic meta-analysis (AFGen + Broad AF + others); total only as &apos;more than half a million&apos;</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6136836/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In sum, we identified a total of 97 distinct AF loci from 65,446 AF cases and more than 522,000 referents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000855"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AFGen</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90448086</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A placebo-controlled randomized trial of daily low-dose aspirin in 19,114 community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over (65 or over for US minorities) in Australia and the United States without prior cardiovascular events, dementia or independence-limiting physical disability, followed as a cohort after the trial to study healthy ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19114</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ASPREE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ASPREE trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Aspirin in Reducing Events in the Elderly</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The ASPirin in Reducing Events in the Elderly trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">ASPirin in Reducing Events in the Elderly</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12596486/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ASPREE was a large-scale placebo-controlled randomized trial (NCT01038583) of daily low-dose (100 mg) enteric-coated aspirin conducted in 19 114 adults aged over 70 years residing in Australia and the USA (≥ 65 years for US minorities) who had no prior cardiovascular events, dementia, or independence-limiting physical disability at trial enrolment.21 The median enrolment age of the cohort was 74 years [interquartile range (IQR) 72–78 ].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90448086</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Cardiovascular Resilience Identifies Protective Variation in the CETP Gene.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37929782</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37929782+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our discovery genome-wide association study of N=12 031 ASCVD event-free individuals from the ASPREE (Aspirin in Reducing Events in the Elderly) trial identified 2 independent variants, rs9939224 (P-8) and rs56156922 (P-6), in the CETP (cholesteryl ester transfer protein) gene.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A placebo-controlled randomized trial of daily low-dose aspirin in 19,114 community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over (65 or over for US minorities) in Australia and the United States without prior cardiovascular events, dementia or independence-limiting physical disability, followed as a cohort after the trial to study healthy ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40796244</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19114</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants randomized in the trial</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12596486/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Randomization was to daily low-dose aspirin or matching placebo for the 4.7 years of the trial.ResultsOf the 19 114 participants randomized (9525 aspirin, 9589 placebo), 15 668 without in-trial MACE consented to post-trial follow-up.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ASPREE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000857 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000857">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid7801"/>
