        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of 2,919 people aged 65 and older with elevated homocysteine, recruited in 2008–2011 mainly through municipal registries around research centres in Rotterdam, Amsterdam and Wageningen, the Netherlands, testing whether two years of vitamin B12 and folic acid supplementation reduce osteoporotic fracture incidence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2919</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>B Vitamins for the Prevention of Osteoporotic Fractures (B-PROOF) Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>B-PROOF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>B-PROOF study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>B-vitamins for the prevention of osteoporotic fractures</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BPROOF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
