        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study (CAMSCH)3 , the Fudan Lung Cancer Study (FLCS), the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC)4 , the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer, Singapore Study (GEL-S)5 , the South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (SKLCS)6-8 , the Shenyang Lung Cancer Study (SLCS)9 , the Shanghai Women’s Health Cohort Study (SWHS)10, 11 , the Tianjin Lung Cancer Study (TLCS)12 , and the Wuhan lung cancer study (WLCS)13 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study (CAMSCH)3 , the Fudan Lung Cancer Study (FLCS), the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC)4 , the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer, Singapore Study (GEL-S)5 , the South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (SKLCS)6-8 , the Shenyang Lung Cancer Study (SLCS)9 , the Shanghai Women’s Health Cohort Study (SWHS)10, 11 , the Tianjin Lung Cancer Study (TLCS)12 , and the Wuhan lung cancer study (WLCS)13 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001864"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Additional studies included in this GWAS are the Guangdong Study (GDS), the Hong Kong Study (HKS), the Japanese Female Lung Cancer Collaborative Study (JLCS)14 , the Chonnam National University Lung Cancer Study (CNULCS) Study15 , and the Yunnan Lung Cancer Study (YLCS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001949"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Additional studies included in this GWAS are the Guangdong Study (GDS), the Hong Kong Study (HKS), the Japanese Female Lung Cancer Collaborative Study (JLCS)14 , the Chonnam National University Lung Cancer Study (CNULCS) Study15 , and the Yunnan Lung Cancer Study (YLCS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5856088/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>11 study centres in the FLCCA contributed EGFR mutation status data (Supplementary Material, Table S2). These 11 study centres include the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study (CAMSCH), the Guangdong Study (GDS), the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC), the Hong Kong Study (HKS), the Hospital-based Epidemiologic Research Program at Aichi Cancer Center (HERPACC), the Japan National Cancer Center (NCC), the South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (SKLCS- Korea University, Kyungpook University, Seoul National University Department of Preventive Medicine (SNUPM))</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study (CAMSCH)3 , the Fudan Lung Cancer Study (FLCS), the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC)4 , the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer, Singapore Study (GEL-S)5 , the South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (SKLCS)6-8 , the Shenyang Lung Cancer Study (SLCS)9 , the Shanghai Women’s Health Cohort Study (SWHS)10, 11 , the Tianjin Lung Cancer Study (TLCS)12 , and the Wuhan lung cancer study (WLCS)13 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study (CAMSCH)3 , the Fudan Lung Cancer Study (FLCS), the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC)4 , the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer, Singapore Study (GEL-S)5 , the South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (SKLCS)6-8 , the Shenyang Lung Cancer Study (SLCS)9 , the Shanghai Women’s Health Cohort Study (SWHS)10, 11 , the Tianjin Lung Cancer Study (TLCS)12 , and the Wuhan lung cancer study (WLCS)13 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study (CAMSCH)3 , the Fudan Lung Cancer Study (FLCS), the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC)4 , the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer, Singapore Study (GEL-S)5 , the South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (SKLCS)6-8 , the Shenyang Lung Cancer Study (SLCS)9 , the Shanghai Women’s Health Cohort Study (SWHS)10, 11 , the Tianjin Lung Cancer Study (TLCS)12 , and the Wuhan lung cancer study (WLCS)13 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002590"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Additional studies included in this GWAS are the Guangdong Study (GDS), the Hong Kong Study (HKS), the Japanese Female Lung Cancer Collaborative Study (JLCS)14 , the Chonnam National University Lung Cancer Study (CNULCS) Study15 , and the Yunnan Lung Cancer Study (YLCS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13348699/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>FLCCA is an international consortium focusing on never-smoking Asian women, with participating studies from Mainland China, Hong Kong, Singapore, Taiwan, South Korea, and Japan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90297562</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of lung adenocarcinoma in East Asia and comparison with a European population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37236969</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10220065/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the current study, we conducted a two-stage GWAS meta-analysis in EA populations using unpublished and previously published data from four studies: the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia (FLCCA), Nanjing Lung Cancer Study (NJLCS)10,24, National Cancer Center Research Institute (NCC) and Aichi Cancer Center (ACC), with 11,753 cases and 30,562 controls in the discovery set and 9905 cases and 120,114 controls in the replication set.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of lung cancer studies of never-smoking Asian women from mainland China, Hong Kong, Singapore, Taiwan, South Korea and Japan, pooling genome-wide data to identify genetic risk factors for lung cancer, particularly adenocarcinoma, in this population.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42152146</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5510</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>never-smoking female cases and controls scanned in the 2012 FLCCA GWAS (no total stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23143601</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We scanned 5,510 never-smoking female lung cancer cases and 4,544 controls drawn from 14 studies from mainland China, South Korea, Japan, Singapore, Taiwan and Hong Kong.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4544</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>never-smoking female cases and controls scanned in the 2012 FLCCA GWAS (no total stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23143601</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We scanned 5,510 never-smoking female lung cancer cases and 4,544 controls drawn from 14 studies from mainland China, South Korea, Japan, Singapore, Taiwan and Hong Kong.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FLCCA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid7884"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90428600</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium of gout genetics research groups, named as a collective author of a genome-wide association analysis of gout in 2.6 million people, whose own case-control sample set (New Zealand/Ardea Biosciences/EuroGout: 4,713 people with self-reported clinically diagnosed gout or gout meeting the 1977 ARA classification criteria and 2,151 controls, of self-reported European ancestry) was genotyped for that study on the Illumina CoreExome array.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">120295</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2600000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GlobalGout</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">GlobalGout Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid7884">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005393"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid7884"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>gout</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2022/11/29/2022.11.26.22281768.full.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Gout was defined according to self-reported diagnosis and/or use of urate-lowering medication, clinical diagnosis, and/or the American College of Rheumatology (ACR) gout classification criteria122,123 dependent on the information available in each source cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2022/11/29/2022.11.26.22281768.full.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GlobalGout obtained ethical approval from the following committees: the New Zealand Multiregional Ethics Committee (MEC05/10/130); the Northern Y Region Health Research Ethics Committee (Ngāti Porou Hauora Charitable Trust study; NTY07/07/074); Research and Ethics Committee, Repatriation General Hospital, South Australia (32/08); Research Ethics Committee, University of New South Wales; Ethikkommission, Technische Universität Dresden (EK 8012012); South East Scotland Research Ethics Committee (04/S1102/41); Commission Cantonale (VD) D&apos;éthique de la Recherche sur l&apos;être Humain, Université de Lausanne; Commissie Mensgebonden Onderzoek regio Arnhem—Nijmegen; Partners Health Care System Institutional Review Board.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90428600</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association analysis reveals new pathogenic pathways in gout.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39406924</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41588-024-01921-5</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GlobalGout Genetics Consortium</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of gout genetics research groups, named as a collective author of a genome-wide association analysis of gout in 2.6 million people, whose own case-control sample set (New Zealand/Ardea Biosciences/EuroGout: 4,713 people with self-reported clinically diagnosed gout or gout meeting the 1977 ARA classification criteria and 2,151 controls, of self-reported European ancestry) was genotyped for that study on the Illumina CoreExome array.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39406924</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2022/11/29/2022.11.26.22281768/DC1/embed/media-1.xlsx</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">120295</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people (approx., &apos;2.6 million&apos;) in the 2024 gout GWAS the consortium co-authored; includes 23andMe, UK Biobank and other cohorts</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41588-024-01921-5</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we provide insights into the molecular mechanism of the poorly understood inflammatory component of gout from a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of 2.6 million people, including 120,295 people with prevalent gout.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2600000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people (approx., &apos;2.6 million&apos;) in the 2024 gout GWAS the consortium co-authored; includes 23andMe, UK Biobank and other cohorts</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41588-024-01921-5</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we provide insights into the molecular mechanism of the poorly understood inflammatory component of gout from a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of 2.6 million people, including 120,295 people with prevalent gout.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000865"/>
