    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90310275</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic associations vary across the spectrum of fasting serum insulin: results from the European IDEFICS/I.Family children&apos;s cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37420130</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10473990/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The European IDEFICS (Identification and prevention of Dietary- and lifestyle-induced health EFfects In Children and infantS)/I.Family cohort is a multi-centre population-based children’s study that aimed to identify risk factors for diet- and lifestyle-related diseases, with a focus on childhood overweight and metabolic disorders [14, 15].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-centre European population-based cohort of 16,228 children aged 2 to 9 years examined in 2007–2008 in Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden, with a community-based obesity-prevention intervention, followed into adolescence by the I.Family study to identify dietary and lifestyle risk factors for childhood overweight and metabolic disorders.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28040744</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37420130</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16228</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children aged 2-9.9 examined at baseline (2007-2008)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28040744</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The baseline examination (T0) between September 2007 and June 2008 included 16 228 children aged 2 to 9.9 years from eight European countries: Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871"/>
