        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer at The University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center in Houston, Texas, of ever-smoking patients of European ancestry and frequency-matched ever-smoking controls, genotyped genome-wide to find lung cancer susceptibility loci and later pooled in international lung cancer consortia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MDACC also denotes MD Anderson Cancer Center melanoma study (COHO:0000875); this term is MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MDACCS also denotes MD Anderson Cancer Center melanoma study (COHO:0000875), Prostate Cancer Case-Control Studies at MD Anderson (COHO:0002044), MD Anderson Ovarian Cancer Study (COHO:0002047) and MD Anderson Renal Cell Cancer Study (COHO:0002048); this term is MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The name MD Anderson Cancer Center Study also denotes MD Anderson Cancer Center melanoma study (COHO:0000875); this term is MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
