    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001779"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5036513/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The four cohorts (RAPPER, RADIOGEN, Gene-PARE, and CCI) comprised individuals with adenocarcinoma of the prostate treated with radiotherapy with curative intent.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12048210</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The RAPPER, RADIOGEN, GenePARE, UGhent, and CCI-EBRT Radiogenomics Consortium (RGC) cohorts included men with non-metastatic prostate cancer who received curative-intent external beam radiotherapy [EBRT], brachytherapy, or both, with or without surgery and/or anti-androgen therapy, described in published GWAS (15–17,20) and summarized in Table 1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10653584/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>REQUITE-PrCa | Prospective cohort | 2014-2016 | European (Multi-site) | 1348 | 70 (46-88) | 0 | CTCAE v4.0 and PRO questionnaire | End of RT |  | 0.004 (0.494) | 31146072 | https://requite.eu/</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90435416</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale meta-genome-wide association study reveals common genetic factors linked to radiation-induced acute toxicities across cancer types.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37862240</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10653584/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study was done using cohorts involved in the Radiogenomics Consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium, established in 2009, of cohorts of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy (for prostate, head and neck, breast and lung cancer, among others) that shares genotype and normal-tissue toxicity data and develops meta-analysis methods to identify genetic variants associated with radiation-induced toxicity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31095341</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35039627</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37862240</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000880"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12042</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>radiotherapy patients in the 2023 cross-cancer GWAS meta-analysis of 19 cohorts</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37862240</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Methods: A genome-wide association study meta-analysis was performed using 19 cohorts totaling 12042 patients.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
