        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nation-wide Dutch collaborative project that combines genotype data from sixteen population and clinical cohorts in the Netherlands with uniform, DSM-based phenotyping of major depressive disorder, pooled centrally for genetic mega-analysis of depression.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16655</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">48286</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">64941</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIONIC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIONIC consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIONIC project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Biobanks Netherlands Internet Collaboration</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">BIObanks Netherlands Internet Collaboration</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid8178">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0002009"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid8178"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>major depressive disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a genome-wide association (GWAS) mega-analysis of DSM-defined lifetime major depressive disorder (MDD) in 64 941 participants (25.7% cases) from the Dutch BIObanks Netherlands Internet Collaboration (BIONIC) consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety (NESDA) is a longitudinal cohort study that aims to investigate the etiology, course, and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We enriched the existing population and clinical cohorts in the Netherlands with an infrastructure for nation-wide depression phenotyping so that all MDD cases were defined based on DSM-5 (Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders) criteria [3, 23].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841074</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetics of major depressive disorder in a homogeneous population with uniform phenotyping.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42230966</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This genome-wide association (GWAS) mega-analysis combines lifetime major depressive disorder (MDD) and genotype data from sixteen Dutch cohorts in the BIONIC (BIObanks Netherlands Internet Collaboration) project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nation-wide Dutch collaborative project that combines genotype data from sixteen population and clinical cohorts in the Netherlands with uniform, DSM-based phenotyping of major depressive disorder, pooled centrally for genetic mega-analysis of depression.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16655</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the lifetime MDD GWAS mega-analysis (16 655 cases, 48 286 controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association mega-analysis of lifetime MDD case-control status in 64 941 individuals (16 655 cases and 48 286 controls) and evaluated the extent to which this design captured common-variant signal by estimating SNP-based heritability and genetic overlap with the latest Psychiatric Genomics Consortium major depression GWAS [10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">48286</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the lifetime MDD GWAS mega-analysis (16 655 cases, 48 286 controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association mega-analysis of lifetime MDD case-control status in 64 941 individuals (16 655 cases and 48 286 controls) and evaluated the extent to which this design captured common-variant signal by estimating SNP-based heritability and genetic overlap with the latest Psychiatric Genomics Consortium major depression GWAS [10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">64941</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the lifetime MDD GWAS mega-analysis (16 655 cases, 48 286 controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13569458/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association mega-analysis of lifetime MDD case-control status in 64 941 individuals (16 655 cases and 48 286 controls) and evaluated the extent to which this design captured common-variant signal by estimating SNP-based heritability and genetic overlap with the latest Psychiatric Genomics Consortium major depression GWAS [10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000897"/>
