    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002545"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10182045/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Victorian Familial Cancer Trials Group VFCTG Australia Cancer clinic-based study Peter MacCallum Cancer Centre Ethics Committee</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90455659</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of 398,238 women unveils seven loci associated with high-grade serous ovarian cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41266372</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12635163/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We meta-analyzed &gt;22 million variants for 398,238 women from the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (OCAC), UK Biobank (UKBB) and Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/BRCA2 (CIMBA) to identify novel HGSOC susceptibility loci.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of research groups that collect DNA and clinical data from carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, established to identify genetic modifiers of breast and ovarian cancer risk in mutation carriers; it began with about 30 affiliated groups and later brought together more than 60 studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17466083</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41266372</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">32613</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>European-ancestry BRCA1/2 carriers in the consortium&apos;s 2025 HGSOC GWAS (analysed subset)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12635163/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The genome-wide association analyses for HGSOC were based on up to 398,238 women from OCAC (N = 120,248, 30.2%), UKBB (N = 245,377, 61.6%) and CIMBA (N = 32,613, 8.2%) (Table 1, Supplementary Tables 1, 2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CIMBA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


