        <owl:annotatedTarget>A clinic-based case-control study of breast cancer begun in February 2001 at Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, enrolling women aged 18 or over with invasive breast cancer who lived in the six-state region of Mayo Clinic&apos;s primary service population, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched on age, race and region from Mayo Clinic&apos;s general internal medicine practice.</owl:annotatedTarget>
