        <rdfs:comment>NCT00740883) conducted between 2007 and 2014 in 14 French care centers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000929"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90572747</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Molecular determinants of thrombosis recurrence risk across venous thromboembolism subtypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40811855</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/early/2024/12/03/2024.12.02.24317788.source.xml</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The recurrent VT GWAS meta-analysis included eight studies with confirmed unrelated VT cases of European ancestry free of cancer history: EDITH, FHS, HVH (HVH1 and HVH23), MARTHA, MEGA, PADIS-PE and REVERSE-I (Supplementary Material).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000929"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, double-blind trial in which 371 adults with a first unprovoked pulmonary embolism, after six months of vitamin K antagonist treatment, were randomised to a further 18 months of warfarin or placebo and followed between 2007 and 2014 at 14 French centres, comparing recurrent venous thromboembolism and major bleeding.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26151264</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000929"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">371</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults randomised to warfarin or placebo (2014)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26151264</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Randomized, double-blind trial (treatment period, 18 months; median follow-up, 24 months); 371 adult patients who had experienced a first episode of symptomatic unprovoked pulmonary embolism (ie, with no major risk factor for thrombosis) and had been treated initially for 6 uninterrupted months with a vitamin K antagonist were randomized and followed up between July 2007 and September 2014 in 14 French centers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
