    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid8550"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37813642</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym TMM also denotes Tohoku Medical Megabank Project (COHO:0000533) and Tohoku Medical Megabank Project Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (COHO:0000939); this term is Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">87865</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CommCohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TMM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TMM CommCohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TMM CommCohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ToMMo CommCohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort (TMM) Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-based Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid8550">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_with_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_8000011"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid8550"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Great East Japan Earthquake</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31932529+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We established a community-based cohort study to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake on disaster victims and gene-environment interactions on the incidence of major diseases, such as cancer and cardiovascular diseases.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10816704/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 175,672 individuals were included in this GWAS meta-analysis of six Japanese cohorts, namely, the Hospital-based Epidemiologic Research Program at Aichi Cancer Center (HERPACC) Study (n = 4958) (25), the Japan Multi-Institutional Collaborative Cohort (J-MICC) Study (n = 13,236) (26, 27), the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective (JPHC) Study (n = 10,037) (28), the Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort (TMM) Study (n = 7857) (29), the Nagahama Prospective Cohort for Comprehensive Human Bioscience (Nagahama) Study (n = 4591) (30), and the BioBank Japan (BBJ) Study (n = 134,993) (31, 32) after imputation and quality control (QC) of individual subject genotype data (Supplementary Materials and tables S1 and S2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37813642</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Influence of Diabetes Family History on the Associations of Combined Genetic and Lifestyle Risks with Diabetes in the Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-Based Cohort Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37813642</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37813642+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We examined these associations.MethodsThis cross-sectional study included 9,681 participants in the Tohoku Medical Megabank Community-based Cohort Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31932529</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">87865</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults who gave informed consent to join, 2013-2015 baseline</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31932529</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All participants agreed to measure genome information and to distribute their information widely.ResultsAs a result, 87,865 gave their informed consent to join our study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CommCohort</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TMM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
