    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid8561"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Great East Japan Earthquake (GEJE) and subsequent tsunami</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we collected in utero and subsequent exposure and outcome information, including disaster-related information, of newborns and other family members.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10953086/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed genome-wide association studies (GWAS) of NVP in pregnant women (n = 23,040) who participated in the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study in Japan from July 2013 to March 2017.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624209</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of nausea and vomiting during pregnancy in Japan: the TMM BirThree Cohort Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38509478</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10953086/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants included in this study were pregnant women enrolled in the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (TMM BirThree Cohort Study) in Japan reported previously [9, 10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31504573</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
