        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18498636</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
