        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal, prospective, population-based study of two elderly community-dwelling populations, African Americans in Indianapolis, Indiana, and Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria, aged 65 years or older and free of dementia when enrolled in 1992 and 2001, who were re-evaluated every 2-3 years by in-home screening followed by clinical diagnostic assessment, to compare the incidence of dementia and Alzheimer disease between the two sites using identical methods.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IIDP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Indianapolis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
