        <dcterms:title>Genetic Variants Associated with Supernormal Coronary Arteries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35793981</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10164599/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We selected male participants from two cohorts: The Cardiovascular Genome Center (CGC) cohort and Cardiovascular and Metabolic Disease Etiology Research Center-High Risk (CMERC-HI) cohort at a university, Seoul, Korea.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28740058</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3470</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the cohort</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35793981</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among 3470 individuals in the CMERC-HI cohort, 1569 males underwent coronary calcium scoring; 65 individuals with a study-feasible Framingham score but showing a score of 0 for coronary calcium were enrolled as supernormal.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
