        <rdfs:comment>In an attempt to identify novel genetic variants associated with sporadic Alzheimer&apos;s disease (AD), a genome-wide association study was performed on a population isolate from Eastern Canada, referred to as the Québec Founder Population (QFP).</rdfs:comment>
