    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9023"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002563"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244101</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of nine epidemiological studies of breast cancer in the United States, mostly population-based case-control studies, whose African American cases and controls were genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of breast cancer in women of African ancestry.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3153</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2831</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5984</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AABC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Breast Cancer Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Breast Cancer GWAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African American Breast Cancer consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">African American Breast Cancer Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9023">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007254"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9023"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3749077/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A strength of the present study is that it includes most existing case-control studies of breast cancer conducted in women of African ancestry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5445618/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Although WCHS and CBCS participated in AABC, samples from those studies were included as part of the AMBER consortium described above.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002563"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5445618/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>AABC includes cases and controls from the following epidemiologic studies: The Multiethnic Cohort study, 734/1003; The Los Angeles component of The Women’s Contraceptive and Reproductive Experiences (CARE) Study, 380/224; The San Francisco Bay Area Breast Cancer Study, 172/23; The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, 440/53; The Nashville Breast Health Study, 310/186; and The Wake Forest University Breast Cancer Study, 125/153).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244101</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk scores for prediction of breast cancer risk in women of African ancestry: a cross-ancestry approach.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35554533</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9476624/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used data in women of AA from four breast cancer GWAS consortia and the Ghana Breast Health Study (GBHS); the four consortia were: ROOT (The GWAS of Breast Cancer in the African Diaspora consortium), the African American Breast Cancer Epidemiology and Risk (AMBER) consortium, Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) and African American Breast Cancer consortium (AABC)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of nine epidemiological studies of breast cancer in the United States, mostly population-based case-control studies, whose African American cases and controls were genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of breast cancer in women of African ancestry.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21852243</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22923054</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3153</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls sampled from the nine member studies for the GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3749077/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 5,984 samples from these studies (3,153 cases and 2,831 controls), we attempted genotyping of 5,932, removing samples (n = 52) with DNA concentrations &lt; 20 ng/ul.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2831</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls sampled from the nine member studies for the GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3749077/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 5,984 samples from these studies (3,153 cases and 2,831 controls), we attempted genotyping of 5,932, removing samples (n = 52) with DNA concentrations &lt; 20 ng/ul.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5984</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls sampled from the nine member studies for the GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3749077/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 5,984 samples from these studies (3,153 cases and 2,831 controls), we attempted genotyping of 5,932, removing samples (n = 52) with DNA concentrations &lt; 20 ng/ul.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AABC</owl:annotatedTarget>
