    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9045"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>military service in the Vietnam War</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5526098/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies are collectively termed “DOD ADNI,” and aim to enroll approximately 400 elderly Veterans who served in Vietnam.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9047"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28758146+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We are using biomarkers to study Vietnam Veterans with/without mild cognitive impairment with a history of at least one TBI and/or ongoing PTSD to determine whether these contribute to the development of AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9049"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>posttraumatic stress disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28758146+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We are using biomarkers to study Vietnam Veterans with/without mild cognitive impairment with a history of at least one TBI and/or ongoing PTSD to determine whether these contribute to the development of AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9051"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>traumatic brain injury</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28758146+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We are using biomarkers to study Vietnam Veterans with/without mild cognitive impairment with a history of at least one TBI and/or ongoing PTSD to determine whether these contribute to the development of AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13291382/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study examined how traumatic brain injury and post-traumatic stress disorder relate to cognitive function and neuroimaging markers in U.S. veterans from the Department of Defense Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI-DOD).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000367"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13311454/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DoD-ADNI is a multi-site extension of ADNI designed to investigate the effects of TBI and PTSD on AD-related pathology in Vietnam-era Veterans (Weiner et al., 2014, 2017).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841377</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large multi-ethnic genetic analyses of amyloid imaging identify new genes for Alzheimer disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37101235</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134547/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These subjects were recruited from the Memory and Aging Project (MAP) at the Knight Alzheimer Disease Research Center (Knight-ADRC) [16, 17], Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI) [18], the Dominantly Inherited Alzheimer Network (DIAN) [19], Anti-Amyloid Treatment in Asymptomatic Alzheimer&apos;s Disease (A4) [20], ADNI Department of Defense (ADNIDOD) studies, Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle (AIBL) [21], The Harvard Aging Brain Study (HABS) [22], and University of Pittsburgh (UPitt) [23].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI&apos;s clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28758146</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42316769</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">289</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>non-demented veterans with baseline neuropsychological testing</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13311454/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, participant flow proceeded from the full non-demented DoD-ADNI cohort with baseline neuropsychological testing (n = 289) to the analytic WMH sample (n = 228) and the FreeSurfer subset (n = 183), with participants excluded for incomplete neuropsychological data (n = 5), incomplete/inconclusive TBI/PTSD screening data (n = 17), missing WMH data (n = 39), missing T1 data (n = 11), and FreeSurfer QC failures (n = 34).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ADNI-DOD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
