    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9184"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90134661</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GELCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9184">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008903"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9184"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15272417+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify susceptibility genes for familial lung cancer, we conducted a genomewide linkage analysis of 52 extended pedigrees ascertained through probands with lung cancer who had several first-degree relatives with the same disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13259588/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GELCC is a U.S.-based research network studying FLC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90134661</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Cross-ancestry genome-wide meta-analysis of 61,047 cases and 947,237 controls identifies new susceptibility loci contributing to lung cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35915169</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01115-x/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1115_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cross-ancestry genome-wide meta-analyses were conducted in the twelve different studies consisting of Affymetrix Axome Array Study (AFFY), the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia (FLCCA), the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium (GELCC), the Environment and Genetics in Lung cancer Etiology study (EAGLE), Helmholtz-Gemeinschaft Deutscher Forschungszentren Lung Cancer GWAS (GERMAN), the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC), the Institute of Cancer Research (ICR), MD Anderson Cancer Center Study (MDACC), NCI Lung Cancer and Smoking Phenotypes in African- American Cases and Controls (NCI), OncoArray Consortium Lung Study (ONCO), the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO), and Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute Study (SLRI).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15272417</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29924316</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41390056</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.gelcc.org/node/3</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GELCC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9190"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90101797</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">39114</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenHAT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatments</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Hypertension-Associated Treatment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9190">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005044"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9190"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>hypertension</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12439737+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GenHAT is an ancillary study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial, ALLHAT, a double-blind, randomized trial of 42 418 hypertensives, 55 years of age or older, with systolic or diastolic hypertension and one or more risk factors for cardiovascular disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3160956/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We note that both the Black and Hispanic groups likely had diverse ancestry given that participants were recruited in the US, Canada, and the Caribbean; therefore, some degree of population substructure is expected.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90101797</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Contributors of Incident Stroke in 10,700 African Americans With Hypertension: A Meta-Analysis From the Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatments and Reasons for Geographic and Racial Differences in Stroke Studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34992631</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34992631+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Methods: In a population comprising over 10,700 AAs treated for hypertension from the Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatments (GenHAT) and Reasons for Geographic and Racial Differences in Stroke (REGARDS) studies, we performed an inverse variance-weighted meta-analysis of incident stroke.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12439737</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21887284</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26791477</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35886043</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">39114</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>ALLHAT participants in the original GenHAT study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35886043</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The original GenHAT study (n = 39,114) evaluated the interaction between candidate hypertensive genetic variants and different antihypertensive treatments to modify the risk of fatal and non-fatal CVD outcomes [24].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GenHAT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9197"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9199"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90132135</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1671</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenKOLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of COPD in Norway Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of COPD, Norway</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Norway GenKOLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9197">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_with_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000038"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9199">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9197"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>current or former smoker with ≥2.5 pack-years of smoking history</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4169636/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Enrolment criteria were: 1) self-reported Caucasian; 2) aged &gt; 40 years; 3) current or former smoker with ≥2.5 pack-years of smoking history; and 4) no severe α1-antitrypsin deficiency.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9199"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>chronic obstructive pulmonary disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19300482+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) in a homogenous case-control cohort from Bergen, Norway (823 COPD cases and 810 smoking controls) and evaluated the top 100 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in the family-based International COPD Genetics Network (ICGN; 1891 Caucasian individuals from 606 pedigrees) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4169636/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In GenKOLS study, subjects for the case-control study were recruited from Bergen, Norway.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90132135</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of bronchodilator response in participants of European and African ancestry from six independent cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35769418</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9234425/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Six non-overlapping cohorts contributed to our primary analysis: the Framingham Heart Study (FHS) [21]; Genetic Epidemiology of COPD (COPDGene) [22]; Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points (ECLIPSE) [23]; Treatment of Emphysema with a Gamma-Selective Retinoid Agonist (TESRA) [24]; the Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort, Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease (GenKOLS) [25]; and the Subpopulations and Intermediate Outcome Measures in COPD Study (SPIROMICS) [26].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19300482</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25134640</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25241909</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31413559</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32944202</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1671</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>GenKOLS cases and controls analysed in a smoking GWAS (analysed subset)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29767774</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed genome-wide association analyses for average cigarettes per day (CPD) across the Genetic Epidemiology of COPD (COPDGene) non-Hispanic white (NHW) (n = 6659) and African American (AA) (n = 3260), GenKOLS (the Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease) (n = 1671), and ECLIPSE (the Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate Endpoints) (n = 1942) cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GenKOLS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9206"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9208"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000312"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90565869</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King&apos;s College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">79831</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GLAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9206">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0002050"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9208">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005618"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9206"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>depression</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31715324+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression (GLAD) Study (www.gladstudy.org.uk) recruits individuals with depression or anxiety into the NIHR Mental Health BioResource.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9208"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>anxiety</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31715324+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression (GLAD) Study (www.gladstudy.org.uk) recruits individuals with depression or anxiety into the NIHR Mental Health BioResource.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12381276/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GLAD+ Study combines two United Kingdom (UK) cohorts: the Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression (GLAD) Study and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) BioResource COVID-19 Psychiatry and Neurological Genetics (COPING) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000312"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6891252/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Once participants have returned their saliva sample, they become full members of the GLAD Study (and of the NIHR BioResource) and are eligible to take part in future studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90565869</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Sex-stratified genome-wide association meta-analysis of major depressive disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40858613</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12381276/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GLAD+ Study combines two United Kingdom (UK) cohorts: the Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression (GLAD) Study and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) BioResource COVID-19 Psychiatry and Neurological Genetics (COPING) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King&apos;s College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31715324</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
