    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9231">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9231"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9233242/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>It must be noted that the UK GRID cohort included only those individuals with type 1 diabetes, and as such, in this study we do not have access to a population without type 1 diabetes for comparison of C-peptide levels.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33179336+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide meta-analysis for age at diagnosis with cohorts from Finland (Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study), the United Kingdom (UK Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes) and Sardinia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fine-mapping, trans-ancestral and genomic analyses identify causal variants, cells, genes and drug targets for type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34127860</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8273124/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>D.B.D. provided samples for genotyping through the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of people with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 17, assembled by the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory from paediatric and adult diabetes clinics at National Health Service hospitals across mainland United Kingdom, whose DNA and plasma samples are used in genetic and other studies of type 1 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17554300</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22025780</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35499624</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>GRID type 1 diabetes case subjects genotyped for one SNP study (analysed subset)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3198057/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 8,344 type 1 diabetic subjects, 10,008 control subjects, and 3,360 type 1 diabetic families were genotyped at the FUT2 SNP rs601338 and at two HLA tag SNPs rs2187668 and rs660895 using TaqMan 5′ nuclease assay (Applied Biosystems, Warrington, U.K.)</rdfs:comment>
