    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3448/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3448_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The EUGENDA-Neijmegen study was supported by MD Fonds</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST010723</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis for early age-related macular degeneration highlights novel loci and insights for advanced disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32843070</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32843070+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify genetic factors for early AMD, we conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analysis (14,034 cases, 91,214 controls, 11 sources of data including the International AMD Genomics Consortium, IAMDGC, and UK Biobank, UKBB).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of 26 studies of age-related macular degeneration, mainly in the United States, Europe, Israel and Australia, which gathered DNA from advanced and intermediate AMD cases, mostly recruited from ophthalmology clinics, and from controls, predominantly of European ancestry. The samples were genotyped centrally at the Center for Inherited Disease Research on a custom-modified HumanCoreExome array to examine common and rare genetic variants in AMD.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26691988</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16144</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>subjects in the 2016 IAMDGC data set after QC (advanced and intermediate AMD, controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4745342/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our final data set included a total of 43,566 subjects consisting of 16,144 advanced AMD patients and 17,832 control subjects of European ancestry for our primary analysis, as well as 6,657 Europeans with intermediate disease and 2,933 subjects with Non-European ancestry (Supplementary Table 3B, Supplementary Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17832</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>subjects in the 2016 IAMDGC data set after QC (advanced and intermediate AMD, controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4745342/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our final data set included a total of 43,566 subjects consisting of 16,144 advanced AMD patients and 17,832 control subjects of European ancestry for our primary analysis, as well as 6,657 Europeans with intermediate disease and 2,933 subjects with Non-European ancestry (Supplementary Table 3B, Supplementary Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">43566</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>subjects in the 2016 IAMDGC data set after QC (advanced and intermediate AMD, controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4745342/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our final data set included a total of 43,566 subjects consisting of 16,144 advanced AMD patients and 17,832 control subjects of European ancestry for our primary analysis, as well as 6,657 Europeans with intermediate disease and 2,933 subjects with Non-European ancestry (Supplementary Table 3B, Supplementary Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001016"/>
