        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case series of patients with atrial fibrillation enrolled at Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, United States, since 2001, together with affected and unaffected family members of probands with an extensive family history of atrial fibrillation, each assessed at enrolment by a structured interview on medical history, treatment and family history, an electrocardiogram, echocardiogram results and a blood sample; its early-onset cases (onset before age 66) were whole-genome sequenced in the NHLBI TOPMed programme.</owl:annotatedTarget>
