        <rdfs:comment>United States</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001035"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90132135</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of bronchodilator response in participants of European and African ancestry from six independent cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35769418</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9234425/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Six non-overlapping cohorts contributed to our primary analysis: the Framingham Heart Study (FHS) [21]; Genetic Epidemiology of COPD (COPDGene) [22]; Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points (ECLIPSE) [23]; Treatment of Emphysema with a Gamma-Selective Retinoid Agonist (TESRA) [24]; the Bergen, Norway COPD Cohort, Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease (GenKOLS) [25]; and the Subpopulations and Intermediate Outcome Measures in COPD Study (SPIROMICS) [26].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001035"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, double-blind, randomised, placebo-controlled phase II trial sponsored by Hoffmann-La Roche and run from 2007 to 2010 at sites in Europe, Israel, South Africa and the United States, in which ex-smokers over 44 years old with smoking-related moderate to severe COPD with emphysema, on optimised COPD therapy, were assigned to the gamma-selective retinoid agonist palovarotene or placebo.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25306249</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25582225</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00413205</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001035"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">491</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>actual enrolment in the trial (2007-2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00413205</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;enrollmentInfo&quot;:{&quot;count&quot;:491,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;ACTUAL&quot;}</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001035"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TESRA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9479"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90002228</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A single-centre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial in which nondiabetic Hispanic women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus, recruited in the Los Angeles area, United States, were assigned to troglitazone or placebo to test whether treating insulin resistance improves insulin sensitivity, preserves pancreatic beta-cell function and prevents type 2 diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">266</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TRIPOD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Troglitazone In the Prevention Of Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Troglitazone in Prevention of Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Troglitazone in the Prevention of Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TRoglitazone In the Prevention Of Diabetes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9479">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9479"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9551285+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The primary aim of the TRIPOD trial is to test the hypothesis that chronic administration of troglitazone to nondiabetic women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) will improve whole-body insulin sensitivity and reduce the incidence of non-insulin-dependent diabetes (NIDDM).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>TRIPOD recruited non-diabetic women with history of GDM in the Los Angeles area; family members were not recruited.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90002228</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The trans-ancestral genomic architecture of glycemic traits.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34059833</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7610958/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among the Hispanic cohorts, sample sizes ranged from 130 (TRIPOD) to 251 10,065 (SOL) with a minimum imputation score of r2=0.69 and Phet=0.43. 252 20 253 Supplementary Figure 33.Forest plot of FI-associated variant rs13258890.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A single-centre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial in which nondiabetic Hispanic women with prior gestational diabetes mellitus, recruited in the Los Angeles area, United States, were assigned to troglitazone or placebo to test whether treating insulin resistance improves insulin sensitivity, preserves pancreatic beta-cell function and prevents type 2 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24124113</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37594959</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9551285</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">266</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women randomised</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3263195/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>was a randomized, placebo-controlled trial of 266 women with recent gestational diabetes, with 126 completing the treatment of 3.6 years, with an eight-month, post-drug washout period.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TRIPOD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001037 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001037">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90435254</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of healthy adult volunteers without known cardiovascular disease, recruited prospectively by advertisement from 2011 at the MRC Clinical Sciences Centre, Imperial College London, United Kingdom, who underwent standard and high-resolution three-dimensional cardiac magnetic resonance imaging and genotyping, to study the genetic determinants of cardiac structure and function.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1850</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Digital Heart Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UKDHP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">UK Digital Heart Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001037"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90435254</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale genome-wide association analyses identify novel genetic loci and mechanisms in hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39966646</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906354/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Unrelated British HCM cases from the Royal Brompton &amp; Harefield Hospitals NHS Trust Cardiovascular Research Biobank, and healthy controls from the UK Digital Heart Project15 were included.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001037"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of healthy adult volunteers without known cardiovascular disease, recruited prospectively by advertisement from 2011 at the MRC Clinical Sciences Centre, Imperial College London, United Kingdom, who underwent standard and high-resolution three-dimensional cardiac magnetic resonance imaging and genotyping, to study the genetic determinants of cardiac structure and function.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27502059</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27869827</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5032181/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001037"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1850</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>healthy volunteers recruited and imaged (2016)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5032181/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Healthy volunteers (n = 1850; 55% females, mean age 41 ± 13 years) were recruited prospectively to the Digital Heart Project and underwent both standard CMR and high-spatial resolution 3D-CMR (Philips 1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
