    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3046454/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Australian Breast Cancer Family Registry (ABCFR) is a population-based, case control family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset breast cancer that is being carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia [9-11], and is part of the Breast Cancer Family Registry [12].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90128530</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide and transcriptome-wide association studies of mammographic density phenotypes reveal novel loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35414113</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Australian Breast Cancer Family Study (ABCFS) is a population-based, case–control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, that was carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, which enrolled women with a first primary breast cancer identified through cancer registries in 1992-1999, with controls selected from the electoral roll; it is the Australian site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21182766</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30771221</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34887416</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35414113</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1610</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases enrolled 1992-1999 (controls not counted in any source read)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3046454/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Overall, we approached 2,303 eligible individuals (ages at diagnosis: &lt;40 years, 1,208; 40-49 years, 551; 50-59 years, 544), which resulted in 1,610 cases, and blood samples were collected from 94% of these cases.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
