    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9607"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9609"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90854196</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ACTG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AIDS Clinical Trials Group</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9607">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005109"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9609">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0012268"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9607"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HIV infection</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://actgnetwork.org/about/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>ACTG is the world’s largest and longest running clinical trials network focused on HIV and other infectious diseases and the people living with them.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9609"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AIDS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://actgnetwork.org/about/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>ACTG is the world’s largest and longest running clinical trials network focused on HIV and other infectious diseases and the people living with them.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A3044083+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To address many of these issues in the United States, the Federal Government has established an AIDS Clinical Trials Group (ACTG) program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90854196</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiancestry sex-stratified genomic associations with HIV viral load and controller status from the ICGH.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37097752</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10393222/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We additionally used a binary definition of HIV spontaneous control in the subset of samples obtained from the International HIV Controllers Study and the AIDS Clinical Trials Group (Supplemental Table 1) (17).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:14583845</obo:IAO_0000119>
