        <obo:IAO_0000116>cancer of the esophagus</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20506380+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used data from 2,048 cases and 2,173 hospital- and population-based controls from ten European countries (alcohol-related cancers and genetic susceptibility in Europe study) to investigate the relationship with BMI and adult change in BMI on UADT cancer risk.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001056"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9676"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>consumption of alcoholic beverages</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18830131+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Moreover, the role of pattern of smoking and drinking, as well as the exact nature of the implicated dietary variables, has not been clarified. To address these issues, the International Agency for Research on Cancer initiated in 2002 the alcohol-related cancers and genetic susceptibility (ARCAGE) in Europe project, with the participation of 15 centers in 11 European countries.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001056"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9678"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>intake of vegetables and fruits</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18830131+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Moreover, the role of pattern of smoking and drinking, as well as the exact nature of the implicated dietary variables, has not been clarified. To address these issues, the International Agency for Research on Cancer initiated in 2002 the alcohol-related cancers and genetic susceptibility (ARCAGE) in Europe project, with the participation of 15 centers in 11 European countries.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001056"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9680"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>tobacco smoking</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18830131+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Moreover, the role of pattern of smoking and drinking, as well as the exact nature of the implicated dietary variables, has not been clarified. To address these issues, the International Agency for Research on Cancer initiated in 2002 the alcohol-related cancers and genetic susceptibility (ARCAGE) in Europe project, with the participation of 15 centers in 11 European countries.</rdfs:comment>
