        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre case-control study of upper aerodigestive tract cancers (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), initiated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in 2002, that recruited newly diagnosed cases and hospital controls (population controls in the United Kingdom) at centres in about ten European countries, mostly in 2002-2005, with interviews on smoking, drinking and diet and biological samples, to study genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interplay with lifestyle factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18830131</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20506380</obo:IAO_0000119>
