    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9780"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90239836</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sample of people in the United Kingdom with treatment-resistant schizophrenia who were prescribed clozapine, whose anonymised blood samples and clinical monitoring data were obtained through the clozapine monitoring services, first in collaboration with Novartis and later through the Zaponex Treatment Access System (second wave 2013–15, third wave 2019–21), for Cardiff University&apos;s genetic studies of schizophrenia and clozapine metabolism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11260</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLOZUK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The CLOZUK cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CLOZUK study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9780">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005414"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9780"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>treatment-resistant schizophrenia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10824469/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Pharmacokinetic and genomic data from the study participants were acquired as part of the CLOZUK study14 of individuals from the UK who had been prescribed clozapine for treatment-resistant schizophrenia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10824469/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The fact that CLOZUK participants were recruited solely within the UK meant that only small sample sizes were available for individuals of non-European ancestries and that these individuals were identified using a genetics-based approach that relied on discrete biogeographical categories.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90239836</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pharmacokinetics and pharmacogenomics of clozapine in an ancestrally diverse sample: a longitudinal analysis and genome-wide association study using UK clinical monitoring data.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36804072</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36804072+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this GWAS, we analysed data from the UK Zaponex Treatment Access System clozapine monitoring service as part of the CLOZUK study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A sample of people in the United Kingdom with treatment-resistant schizophrenia who were prescribed clozapine, whose anonymised blood samples and clinical monitoring data were obtained through the clozapine monitoring services, first in collaboration with Novartis and later through the Zaponex Treatment Access System (second wave 2013–15, third wave 2019–21), for Cardiff University&apos;s genetic studies of schizophrenia and clozapine metabolism.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22614287</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36804072</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11260</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>schizophrenia cases in the analysed CLOZUK GWAS sample (after QC), 2018</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5918692/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The final sample size was 11,260 cases and 24,542 controls (5,220 cases and 18,823 controls not in previous schizophrenia GWAS; Methods and Supplementary Figs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CLOZUK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90319690</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">483</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COL_Twin</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Colorado Longitidinal Twin Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Colorado Longitudinal Twin Sample</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LTS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Colorado Longitudinal Twin Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13333102/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>LTS participants, born between 1984 and 1990, were recruited in Colorado, and were followed from birth</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90319690</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Trans-ancestry meta-analysis of genome wide association studies of inhibitory control.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37500827</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10827666/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Colorado sample (COLORADO) includes same sex monozygotic (MZ) and dizygotic (DZ) twins recruited from the Colorado Longitudinal Twin Sample that was designed to investigate genetic and environmental influences on cognitive and emotional development.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23092589</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42223860</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">483</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>twin pairs (families) who have participated in the LTS (2012)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3854934/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus the number of families who have participated in LTS is 483 (male-male twin pairs: 240; female-female twin pairs: 243).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>COL_Twin</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LTS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9793"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90704646</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer&apos;s disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">181</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1292</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1473</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CSDC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Combined Small Datasets Collection</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9793">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9793"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CSDC is a harmonized collection of merged small datasets (comprising the existing datasets of BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2, and WASHU2) used in common variant analyses to deal with small case and control counts within the individual studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13263136/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CHAP (part of CSDC): CHAP is an on-going, community-based study of individuals from a geographically defined community of 3 neighborhoods in Chicago, Illinois (Morgan Park, Washington Heights, and Beverly), with 6,158 participants in the first phase of the study (78.7% overall; 80.5% of the blacks, 74.6% of the whites)53 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90704646</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Consensus meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies for Alzheimer&apos;s disease and related dementias.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42237039</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13263136/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we update descriptions of these studies, where applicable, and provide descriptions for ADC waves 8- 12, as well as the Combined Small Datasets Collection (CSDC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer&apos;s disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42237039</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">181</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AD cases and controls of the CSDC in the 2026 ADRD GWAS meta-analysis (raw N)</obo:IAO_0000116>
