    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90054778</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IBG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Institute for Behavioral Genetics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23092589+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Colorado Twin Registry (CTR) is a population-based registry housed at the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90054778</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Association Meta-analysis of Childhood and Adolescent Internalizing Symptoms.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35378236</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0890856722001794-mmc2.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Two cohort studies from the Institute for Behavioral Genetics (IBG) supplied information for this project: The Colorado Adoption Project (http://ibgwww.colorado.edu/cap/) and the Colorado Twin Registry (https://www.colorado.edu/ibg/research/human-research-studies/colorado-twin-registry)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23092589</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23158098</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35378236</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
