        <obo:IAO_0000116>HIV-1 infection</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV was established as a platform to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets obtained on HIV-1 infected individuals worldwide.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The AIDS clinical Trial Group (ACTG) in the USA</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001276"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10848312/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The AIDS Linked to the IntraVenous Experience (ALIVE) study is a natural history study following the incidence and progression of HIV infection among intravenous drug users (IDUs) in Baltimore, MD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology (CHAVI) in the USA</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10749428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GRIV cohort, which includes Long-Term Non-Progressors (LTNP) and Elite Controllers (ECs), is part of the ICGH consortium (9).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Hemophilia Growth and Development Study (HGDS) in the USA</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10848312/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study (MACS) DESCRIPTION: The Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study (MACS) is an ongoing prospective study of the natural and treated histories of HIV-1 infection in homosexual and bisexual men conducted by sites located in Baltimore, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10848312/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I) evaluated and prospectively followed patients with hemophilia or a related coagulation disorder.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001665"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10749428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The list of the ICGH cohorts/participants is as follows : 1. The AIDS clinical Trial Group (ACTG) in the USA 2. The AIDS Linked to the IntraVenous Experience (ALIVE) Cohort in Baltimore, USA 3. The Amsterdam Cohort Studies on HIV infection and AIDS (ACS) in the Netherlands 4. The ANRS CO18 in France 5. The ANRS PRIMO Cohort in France 6. The Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology (CHAVI) in the USA 7. The Danish HIV Cohort Study in Denmark</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10749428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The list of the ICGH cohorts/participants is as follows : 1. The AIDS clinical Trial Group (ACTG) in the USA 2. The AIDS Linked to the IntraVenous Experience (ALIVE) Cohort in Baltimore, USA 3. The Amsterdam Cohort Studies on HIV infection and AIDS (ACS) in the Netherlands 4. The ANRS CO18 in France 5. The ANRS PRIMO Cohort in France 6. The Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology (CHAVI) in the USA 7. The Danish HIV Cohort Study in Denmark 8. The Genetic and Immunological Studies of European and African HIV-1+ Long Term Non-Progressors (GISHEAL) Study, in France and Italy</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001895"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The IrsiCaixa Foundation Acute/Recent HIV-1 Infection cohort in Barcelona, Spain</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001903"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Hospital Clinic-IDIBAPS Acute/Recent HIV-1 Infection cohort in Barcelona, Spain</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001906"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Icona Foundation Study in Italy</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002074"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Modena Cohort in Modena, Italy</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Pumwani Sex Workers Cohort in Nairobi, Kenya, and Winnipeg, Canada</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002528"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The US military HIV Natural History Study (NHS)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002555"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The West Australian HIV cohort Study</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV was established as a platform to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets obtained on HIV-1 infected individuals worldwide. Patient material was collected at multiple clinical centers across North America, Europe, Australia and Africa (a list of contributing cohort studies and centers is given at the end of the paper).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90278200</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiancestry sex-stratified genomic associations with HIV viral load and controller status from the ICGH.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37097752</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37097752+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To address this, we performed a sex-stratified genome-wide association study using data from the ICGH.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23935489</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37097752</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9705</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HIV-1-infected participants with genotype and clinical data pooled in the ICGH viral-load analysis (2023)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37097752</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Although it is the largest collection of genomic data in HIV, this multiethnic sample of 9,705 people is 81.3% male.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ICGH</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid9996"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841381</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium of research groups studying the genetics of endometriosis, which pools genome-wide association data from studies in Europe, the United States, Australia and Japan, with cases identified by surgical confirmation, medical records or self-report, in meta-analyses of endometriosis risk.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">60674</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">701926</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">762600</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IEGC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International Endometriosis Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid9996">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005133"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841381</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry genome-wide association and integrated multi-omics analyses of endometriosis and its clinical manifestations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42056605</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC13195585</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The IEGC is a collaborative effort that aggregates data from multiple international studies to investigate the genetic factors of endometriosis4.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of research groups studying the genetics of endometriosis, which pools genome-wide association data from studies in Europe, the United States, Australia and Japan, with cases identified by surgical confirmation, medical records or self-report, in meta-analyses of endometriosis risk.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32423502</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36914876</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42056605</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">60674</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls in the 2023 IEGC GWAS meta-analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13195585/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The two most recent GWAS analyses of endometriosis, comprising 928,413 participants (including 44,125 cases; 30% non-European ancestry)7 and 762,600 participants of European descent (including 60,674 cases)4, identified up to 45 loci.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">701926</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls in the 2023 IEGC GWAS meta-analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13195585/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The two most recent GWAS analyses of endometriosis, comprising 928,413 participants (including 44,125 cases; 30% non-European ancestry)7 and 762,600 participants of European descent (including 60,674 cases)4, identified up to 45 loci.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">762600</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls in the 2023 IEGC GWAS meta-analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13195585/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The two most recent GWAS analyses of endometriosis, comprising 928,413 participants (including 44,125 cases; 30% non-European ancestry)7 and 762,600 participants of European descent (including 60,674 cases)4, identified up to 45 loci.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>IEGC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid9996"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>endometriosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC13195585</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The IEGC is a collaborative effort that aggregates data from multiple international studies to investigate the genetic factors of endometriosis4.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01323-z/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1323_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Oxford Endometriosis Gene Study (OXEGENE): Approved by the Oxford regional multi-center and local research ethics committees.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10042257/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a meta-analysis of 24 GWAS with a total effective sample size of 206,106 (60,674 cases and 701,926 controls) of European (98%: Europe, USA, Australia), and East Asian (2%: Japan) ancestry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
