        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.</obo:IAO_0000115>
