    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10118"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>age-related eye diseases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Montrachet (Maculopathy Optic Nerve nuTRition neurovAsCular and HEarT diseases) Study is a population‐based study designed to find associations between age‐related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly as a primary objective.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were recruited in Dijon (France), from the ongoing population‐based 3C Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants of the Montrachet Study were recruited from an ongoing population‐based study, the Three‐City (3C) Study, which examined the vascular risk factors for dementia (2003).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90559231</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>HTRA1/lncRNA HTRA1-AS1 dominates in age-related macular degeneration reticular pseudodrusen genetic risk with no complement involvement.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41361163</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685958/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Secondly, the EUGENDA cohort enrolled individuals from 55 years of age, while some other cohorts enrolled older individuals only (e.g. Montrachet ≥75 years, Alienor ≥77 years).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26466845</obo:IAO_0000119>
