    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10166"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>non-small-cell lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31326317+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To systematically identify genetic variants for NSCLC risk, we newly genotyped 19 546 samples from Chinese NSCLC cases and controls from the Nanjing Medical University Global Screening Array Project</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13348699/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifically, these included the NJMU Global Screening Array project (10,248 cases and 9,298 controls), with participants recruited from five major cities in China (Nanjing, Shanghai, Beijing, Tianjin, and Guangzhou); the NJMU GWAS dataset (2,126 cases and 3,077 controls) [17]; and the NJMU OncoArray dataset (953 cases and 953 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90482691</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide meta-analysis across East Asian and European populations provides insights into the molecular basis of lung cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42152146</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13348699/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Specifically, these included the NJMU Global Screening Array project (10,248 cases and 9,298 controls), with participants recruited from five major cities in China (Nanjing, Shanghai, Beijing, Tianjin, and Guangzhou); the NJMU GWAS dataset (2,126 cases and 3,077 controls) [17]; and the NJMU OncoArray dataset (953 cases and 953 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control sample of Chinese patients with histologically confirmed incident non-small cell lung cancer, untreated by chemotherapy or radiotherapy before diagnosis, and cancer-free controls from community screening for non-communicable diseases, frequency-matched on age, sex and region, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array by Nanjing Medical University, China; it combines three regional case-control studies, from Nanjing and Shanghai, from Beijing and Tianjin, and from Guangdong.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31326317</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42152146</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10248</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>NSCLC cases and controls genotyped on the Global Screening Array (2019)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7015703</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the present study, we newly performed genome-wide scan for 19,546 samples (NJMU GSA project: 10,248 cases and 9,298 controls) using Illumina Global Screening Array (GSA), which included three studies (Nanjing GSA study: 4,149 cases and 3,198 controls from Nanjing and Shanghai; Beijing GSA study: 2,155 cases and 2,035 controls from Beijing and Tianjin; and Guangzhou GSA study: 3,944 cases and 4,065 controls from Guangdong).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9298</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>NSCLC cases and controls genotyped on the Global Screening Array (2019)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7015703</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the present study, we newly performed genome-wide scan for 19,546 samples (NJMU GSA project: 10,248 cases and 9,298 controls) using Illumina Global Screening Array (GSA), which included three studies (Nanjing GSA study: 4,149 cases and 3,198 controls from Nanjing and Shanghai; Beijing GSA study: 2,155 cases and 2,035 controls from Beijing and Tianjin; and Guangzhou GSA study: 3,944 cases and 4,065 controls from Guangdong).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
