    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10262"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10264"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267392</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">781</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1859</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SMS AD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SMS_AD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Screening Markers for Colorectal Cancer Study (advanced adenomas)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Screening Markers for Colorectal Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10262">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10264">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0021392"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10262"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24875374+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a case-control study of the association between subsets of colorectal polyps, including adenomas and serrated polyps, and single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) related to colorectal cancer through prior genome-wide association studies (GWAS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10264"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal polyps</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24875374+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a case-control study of the association between subsets of colorectal polyps, including adenomas and serrated polyps, and single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) related to colorectal cancer through prior genome-wide association studies (GWAS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were enrollees in an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State (Kaiser Permanente Washington (formerly Group Health Cooperative, Seattle, Washington)) aged 24–79 years who underwent an index colonoscopy for any indication between 1998 and 2007 and donated a buccal-cell or blood sample for genotyping analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267392</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide Interaction Study with Smoking for Colorectal Cancer Risk Identifies Novel Genetic Loci Related to Tumor Suppression, Inflammation, and Immune Response.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36576985</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9992283/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SMS and REACH: This work was supported by the National Cancer Institute (grant P01 CA074184 to J.D. Potter and P.A. Newcomb, grants R01 CA097325, R03 CA153323, and K05 CA152715 to P.A. Newcomb, and the National Center for Advancing Translational Sciences at the National Institutes of Health (grant KL2 TR000421 to A.N. Burnett-Hartman)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24875374</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30510241</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">781</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants with genotyping data from both recruitment phases (genotyped subset), 2014</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4082340/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This resulted in 1,859 study participants (340 from phase 1 and 1,519 from phase 2) with genotyping data available, comprising 489 cases with adenomas only, 401 cases with serrated polyps only, 188 cases with synchronous adenomas and serrated polyps, and 781 polyp-free controls (Table 2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1859</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants with genotyping data from both recruitment phases (genotyped subset), 2014</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4082340/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This resulted in 1,859 study participants (340 from phase 1 and 1,519 from phase 2) with genotyping data available, comprising 489 cases with adenomas only, 401 cases with serrated polyps only, 188 cases with synchronous adenomas and serrated polyps, and 781 polyp-free controls (Table 2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122"/>
