        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SIGNET-REGARDS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10352"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000182"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90104085</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The Parkinson&apos;s disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson&apos;s Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson&apos;s disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2190</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5667</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EBI MERGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genome-wide association scan in Parkinson&apos;s disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 Parkinson&apos;s disease study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10352">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005180"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10352"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Parkinson&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21044948+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) in 1705 Parkinson&apos;s disease (PD) UK patients and 5175 UK controls, the largest sample size so far for a PD GWAS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>UK PD cases were randomly selected from population and hospital-based clinics with an emphasis on sporadic cases with no family history for this disease.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104085</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common X-Chromosome Variants Are Associated with Parkinson Disease Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33583074</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8601399/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PD cohorts include the International PD Genomics Consortium (IPDGC) NeuroX dataset, the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) PD dataset, the Autopsy-Confirmed PD GWAS Consortium (APDGC) dataset genotyped by the Center for Inherited Disease Research, the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (NGRC) dataset, the UK PD Consortium, and the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2, referred to here as EBI MERGE.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The Parkinson&apos;s disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson&apos;s Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson&apos;s disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21044948</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2190</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PD cases and WTCCC2 population controls before exclusions (2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21044948</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Prior to any exclusion, the full data set comprised 2190 individuals with idiopathic PD, and 5667 population controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5667</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PD cases and WTCCC2 population controls before exclusions (2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21044948</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Prior to any exclusion, the full data set comprised 2190 individuals with idiopathic PD, and 5667 population controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EBI MERGE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10360"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000022"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90026609</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">602</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cancer and Leukemia Group B 80303</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CALGB 80303</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10360">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009831"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10360"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>advanced pancreatic cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20606091+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These encouraging data led Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB) to conduct a double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized phase III trial of gemcitabine/bevacizumab versus gemcitabine/placebo in advanced pancreatic cancer patients.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The following institutions participated in this study: Delaware Christiana Care Community Clinical Oncology Program (CCOP) and Helen F. Graham Cancer Center, Wilmington, DE</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90026609</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Bevacizumab-induced hypertension and proteinuria: a genome-wide study of more than 1000 patients.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34616010</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8770703/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Two studies included only female patients (breast cancer, CALGB 40503 and 40502), one study included only male patients (prostate cancer, CALGB 90401), and one study included both female and male patients (pancreatic cancer, CALGB 80303).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20606091</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">602</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients enrolled and randomised 2004-2006</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20606091</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between June 2004 and April 2006, 602 patients were enrolled onto the study and 535 were treated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10366"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000022"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90026609</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1050</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CALGB (Alliance) 90401</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CALGB 90401</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10366">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004956"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10366"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22454414+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A randomized, placebo-controlled study based on preclinical and clinical data that supports the potential role of vascular endothelial growth factor in prostate cancer was performed to evaluate the addition of bevacizumab to standard docetaxel and prednisone therapy in patients with metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The following institutions (with supporting Grant No. in parentheses) participated in this study: Board of Regents of the University of Oklahoma, Oklahoma City, OK</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90026609</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Bevacizumab-induced hypertension and proteinuria: a genome-wide study of more than 1000 patients.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34616010</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8770703/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Two studies included only female patients (breast cancer, CALGB 40503 and 40502), one study included only male patients (prostate cancer, CALGB 90401), and one study included both female and male patients (pancreatic cancer, CALGB 80303).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22454414</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1050</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>men randomly assigned</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22454414</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 1,050 patients were randomly assigned.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10372"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90301397</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">100</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">50</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CLX</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COLONOMICS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Colonomics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10372">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0021063"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10372"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colon cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we present Colonomics (https://www.colonomics.org/), a multi-omics dataset that comprises 100 stage II colon cancer patients from which samples of tumoral tissue (T) and paired normal adjacent tissue (N) were obtained from the surgical specimen.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Colon cancer patients were retrospectively selected during 2012 from those that had received radical surgery in the Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) between January 1996 and December 2000, and had fresh frozen tumor samples in the hospital biobank.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90301397</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Germline genetic regulation of the colorectal tumor immune microenvironment.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38664626</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11046907/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three independent data sets were available for replication of our discovery phase findings: Colonomics (“CLX”, N = 99; clonality, abundance, TILs/hpf), the CRC Genetics Study (“CRCGEN”, N = 162; clonality, abundance), and the Nurses’ Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (N = 505; TILs).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36182938</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
