    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90255364</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-omics cohort of adult Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time. It combines whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2984</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>4D-SZ</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>4D-SZ study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">4D-SZ cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8648780/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 4D-SZ cohort (multi-omics, with more data to come, from Shenzhen, China) at present have high-depth whole-genome sequencing data from 2984 individuals</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90255364</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Sex differences in the oral microbiome, host traits, and their causal relationships.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36660475</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9843272/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 4D-SZ cohort is a well-designed multi-omics cohort,15,16,17,18 with shotgun data for the metagenome across multiple body sites and the host genome, as well as metabolic traits, detailed questionnaires, and clinical information.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-omics cohort of adult Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time. It combines whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33563976</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34118463</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34873157</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2984</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Shenzhen participants with high-depth whole-genome sequencing (as of 2021)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34873157</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 4D-SZ cohort (multi-omics, with more data to come, from Shenzhen, China) at present have high-depth whole-genome sequencing data from 2984 individuals (mean depth of 33×, ranging from 15× to 78×, Supplementary Table S1 and Fig.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>4D-SZ</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001141 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001141">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Obsoleted 2026-09-24. The Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study is the same cohort as the Sikh Diabetes Study, which its investigators write as AIDHS/SDS (&apos;the AIDHS (also named the SDS)&apos;, PMID:23300278); it was minted twice, once from each of the catalog tags AIDHS and SDS. COHO:0001116 (Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study/Sikh Diabetes Study) replaces it and carries all its names.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


