        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10401"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10403"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000905"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244057</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym AREDS also denotes Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2 (COHO:0001143); this term is Age-Related Eye Disease Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4757</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AREDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Age-Related Eye Disease Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10401">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004847"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10403">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005150"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10401"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>age-related cataract</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10588299+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Age-Related Eye Disease Study (AREDS) was initially conceived as a long-term multicenter, prospective study of the clinical course of age-related macular degeneration (AMD) and age-related cataract.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10403"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>age-related macular degeneration</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10588299+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Age-Related Eye Disease Study (AREDS) was initially conceived as a long-term multicenter, prospective study of the clinical course of age-related macular degeneration (AMD) and age-related cataract.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13157973/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, 4757 participants aged 55 to 80 years were recruited between 1992 and 1998 at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244057</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Rare variant analyses across multiethnic cohorts identify novel genes for refractive error.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36596879</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9810640/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the current analysis, 1562 participants aged 60 and older were included from the AREDS 1a, 1b and 1c population.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:10588299</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:11594942</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39826679</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4757</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants enrolled 1992-1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1473211/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 4757 participants were enrolled, 157 more than planned for by design.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AREDS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10410"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90559231</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym AREDS also denotes Age-Related Eye Disease Study (COHO:0001142); this term is Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4203</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AREDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AREDS2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10410">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005150"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10410"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>age-related macular degeneration</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23644932+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2 (AREDS2), a multicenter, randomized, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 study with a 2 × 2 factorial design, conducted in 2006-2012 and enrolling 4203 participants aged 50 to 85 years at risk for progression to advanced AMD with bilateral large drusen or large drusen in 1 eye and advanced AMD in the fellow eye.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22840421+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We enrolled 4203 participants at 82 clinical centers located in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90559231</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>HTRA1/lncRNA HTRA1-AS1 dominates in age-related macular degeneration reticular pseudodrusen genetic risk with no complement involvement.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41361163</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685958/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The AREDS2_OCT and NEI_research studies were supported by the intramural program funds and contracts from the National Eye Institute/National Institutes of Health (NEI/NIH), Department of Health and Human Services, Bethesda, MD</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22840421</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23644932</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4203</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants enrolled and randomised at 82 US centres</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22840421</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We enrolled 4203 participants at 82 clinical centers located in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AREDS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AREDS2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10418"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Southern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90399578</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3025</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ARK</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African Research Kidney Disease study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African Research into Kidney Diseases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>African Research on Kidney Disease Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">African Research on Kidney Disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10418">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005300"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10418"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>chronic kidney disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31941441+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The optimal methods to estimate glomerular filtration rate (GFR) and therefore to determine the presence of CKD in SSA are uncertain. We plan to measure iohexol excretion to accurately determine GFR in Malawi, South Africa and Uganda.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11134365/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The African Research Kidney Disease (ARK) study is a well characterised population-based cohort study of 2021 adults (20–80 years) of self-identified black ethnicity from Agincourt, (Mpumalanga, South Africa) with demographic data, health-related questionnaire data, and anthropometric measurements collected at enrolment (Fabian et al., 2022).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35839814+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We measured serum creatinine, cystatin C, and glomerular filtration rate (GFR) using the slope-intercept method for iohexol plasma clearance (mGFR) in population cohorts from Malawi, Uganda, and South Africa.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90399578</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic association and transferability for urinary albumin-creatinine ratio as a marker of kidney disease in four Sub-Saharan African populations and non-continental individuals of African ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38812969</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11134365/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The African Research Kidney Disease (ARK) study is a well characterised population-based cohort study of 2021 adults (20–80 years) of self-identified black ethnicity from Agincourt, (Mpumalanga, South Africa) with demographic data, health-related questionnaire data, and anthropometric measurements collected at enrolment (Fabian et al., 2022).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31941441</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35839814</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3025</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people who underwent measured GFR testing (Malawi 1020, South Africa 986, Uganda 1019), 2022</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35839814</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of 3025 people who underwent measured GFR testing (Malawi n=1020, South Africa n=986, and Uganda n=1019), we analysed data for 2578 participants who had complete data and adequate quality measurements.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ARK</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841377</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer&apos;s disease pathology.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BAC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BACS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Berkeley Aging Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Berkeley Aging Cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Berkeley aging cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Berkeley Aging Cohort Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10369372/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Berkeley Aging Cohort Study (BACS), a cohort of elderly individuals who had psychometrically normal cognition at baseline, residing in the community in the San Francisco Bay area</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841377</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large multi-ethnic genetic analyses of amyloid imaging identify new genes for Alzheimer disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37101235</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134547/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These cohorts included Memento [24], Mayo Clinic Study of Aging (MCSA) [25], Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer&apos;s Prevention (WRAP) [26], Berkeley Aging Cohort study (BACS) [27], Korean study [28], and MISSION-AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer&apos;s disease pathology.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29527500</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37502020</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38334195</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40441049</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
