        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10451"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16341085+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The National Cancer Institute Breast and Prostate Cancer Cohort Consortium--a pooled analysis of multiple large cohort studies with a total of more than 5,000 cases of breast cancer and 8,000 cases of prostate cancer--was therefore initiated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10453"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16341085+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The National Cancer Institute Breast and Prostate Cancer Cohort Consortium--a pooled analysis of multiple large cohort studies with a total of more than 5,000 cases of breast cancer and 8,000 cases of prostate cancer--was therefore initiated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3044744</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition, the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study (MCCS) established in 1990–1994 [42] recently joined the consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3921107/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>It consists of cases and controls selected from large cohorts assembled in Europe, Australia and the United States that have both biological samples and extensive questionnaire information collected prospectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01534-4/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1534_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention (ATBC) Study Nested case-control, Finland</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3044744/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition Cohort (EPIC – comprised of cohorts from Denmark, Great Britain, Germany, Greece, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain, and Sweden) in 1993</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90274713</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Characterizing prostate cancer risk through multi-ancestry genome-wide discovery of 187 novel risk variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37945903</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01534-4/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1534_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>8 study meta analysis (ELLIPSE OncoArray/BPC3/CAPS1/CAPS2/PRACTICAL iCOGS/Pegasus/UK GWAS1/UK GWAS2)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16341085</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18596909</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21390317</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23255287</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24523857</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10501</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer cases and controls genotyped in the 2011 pooled BPC3 analysis of 39 GWAS SNPs</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21390317</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We therefore genotyped 39 SNPs from regions identified by several prostate cancer GWAS in 10,501 prostate cancer cases and 10,831 controls from the NCI Breast and Prostate Cancer Cohort Consortium (BPC3).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10831</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer cases and controls genotyped in the 2011 pooled BPC3 analysis of 39 GWAS SNPs</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21390317</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We therefore genotyped 39 SNPs from regions identified by several prostate cancer GWAS in 10,501 prostate cancer cases and 10,831 controls from the NCI Breast and Prostate Cancer Cohort Consortium (BPC3).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BPC3</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10464"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90472771</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John&apos;s Institute of Dermatology, Guy&apos;s and St Thomas&apos; NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BSTOP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Biomarkers of Systemic Treatment Outcomes in Psoriasis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Biomarkers of Systemic Treatment Outcomes in Psoriasis study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UK Biomarkers of Systemic Treatment Outcomes in Psoriasis study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Biomarkers and Stratification To Optimise outcomes in Psoriasis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10464">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005083"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10464"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>psoriasis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12857016/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>BSTOP is an ongoing prospective observational study of patients with a primary diagnosis of moderate‒severe plaque psoriasis across &gt; 70 UK dermatology centres, which includes biological sample collection.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11871359/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases: BSTOP study, via UK hospital dermatology centres.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90472771</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>GWAS meta-analysis of psoriasis identifies new susceptibility alleles impacting disease mechanisms and therapeutic targets.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40021644</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11871359/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases: BSTOP study, via UK hospital dermatology centres.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John&apos;s Institute of Dermatology, Guy&apos;s and St Thomas&apos; NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40021644</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41408349</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants recruited so far (stated as over 10,000)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>BSTOP has so far recruited over 10,000 participants and collected more than 34,000 biological samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BSTOP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001483"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90461957</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses&apos; Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">59000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BWHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Black Womens Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Black Women&apos;s Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11885530/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Black Women’s Health Study (BWHS) is a U.S. prospective cohort study of 59,000 United States Black women who enrolled in the study in 1995 and have been followed by biennial questionnaires since then.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90461957</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide meta-analysis identifies novel risk loci for uterine fibroids within and across multiple ancestry groups.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40050615</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11885530/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Black Women’s Health Study (BWHS) is a U.S. prospective cohort study of 59,000 United States Black women who enrolled in the study in 1995 and have been followed by biennial questionnaires since then.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses&apos; Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40050615</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">59000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Black women enrolled in 1995</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BWHS is a “follow-up” study, following the 59,000 women who enrolled in 1995 over time.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BWHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10476"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10478"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90662913</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">652</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">764</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1416</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CACTI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Coronary Artery Calcification in T1D</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10476">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10478">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005311"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898750/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CACTI was designed to examine the prevalence of subclinical atherosclerosis in adults with type 1 diabetes and a comparable group of controls without any diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10478"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>subclinical atherosclerosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898750/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CACTI was designed to examine the prevalence of subclinical atherosclerosis in adults with type 1 diabetes and a comparable group of controls without any diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3687315/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study was performed at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes in Denver, Colorado, and at the Clinical Translational Research Center (CTRC) at the University of Colorado Hospital.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90662913</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetics of C-Peptide and Age at Diagnosis in Type 1 Diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39556808</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11755686/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a meta-GWAS of C-peptide that including four T1D studies: the Scottish Diabetes Research Network Type 1 Bioresource (SDRNT1BIO) (4,16), Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (DCCT) (17,18), Coronary Artery Calcification in T1D (CACTI) (19,20), and Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Diabetic Retinopathy (WESDR) (21).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:14578303</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23340891</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24130360</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30943964</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">652</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults enrolled at baseline (652 with type 1 diabetes, 764 non-diabetic controls), 2000-2002</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6448314/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study enrolled 1416 individuals between 19 and 56 years of age, with no known history of CHD: 652 subjects with type 1 diabetes and 764 nondiabetic control subjects.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">764</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults enrolled at baseline (652 with type 1 diabetes, 764 non-diabetic controls), 2000-2002</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6448314/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study enrolled 1416 individuals between 19 and 56 years of age, with no known history of CHD: 652 subjects with type 1 diabetes and 764 nondiabetic control subjects.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
