        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90129578</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CBC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cryptosporidiosis Birth Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh Birth Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10508">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015474"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10508"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cryptosporidiosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29897482+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cryptosporidiosis is a major cause of childhood diarrhea in low- and middle-income countries and has been linked to impairment of child growth. This study investigated the burden of cryptosporidiosis and its impact on child growth in both a rural and an urban site in Bangladesh.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bangladesh"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10960603/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify host genetic risk factors associated with astrovirus disease susceptibility that may explain disease mechanism and vaccine targets, we performed genome-wide association studies in children enrolled in 2 birth cohorts, the Performance of Rotavirus and Oral Polio Vaccines in Developing Countries (PROVIDE) study and the Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh Birth Cohort (CBC) study in Dhaka, Bangladesh [15, 16].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90129578</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Campylobacter-Positive Diarrhea Identifies Genes Involved in Toxin Processing and Inflammatory Response.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35420468</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9239263/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we aimed to identify genetic variants associated with host susceptibility to Campylobacter infection using two well-characterized birth cohorts: the Performance of Rotavirus and Oral Polio Vaccines in Developing Countries (PROVIDE) Study (19) and the Cryptosporidiosis Birth Cohort (CBC) (20).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29897482</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32019797</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40488529</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CBC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10514"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90267154</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">38000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CCSS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Childhood Cancer Survivor Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10514">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0006517"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10514"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>childhood cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19364948+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 1994, the US National Cancer Institute funded the Childhood Cancer Survivor Study, a multi-institutional research initiative designed to establish a large and extensively characterized cohort of more than 14,000 5-year survivors of childhood and adolescent cancer diagnosed between 1970 and 1986.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7190022/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Childhood Cancer Survivor Study is a multi-institutional retrospective cohort study with longitudinal follow-up of five year survivors of the most common childhood cancers (leukemia, central nervous system tumors, Hodgkin lymphoma, non-Hodgkin lymphoma, renal tumors, neuroblastoma, soft tissue sarcomas, and bone sarcomas) diagnosed before age 21 years at one of 27 participating institutions in the United States and Canada.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267154</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study Identifies ROBO2 as a Novel Susceptibility Gene for Anthracycline-Related Cardiomyopathy in Childhood Cancer Survivors.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36508697</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36508697+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We addressed this gap using the Childhood Cancer Survivor Study (discovery) and the Children&apos;s Oncology Group (COG) study COG-ALTE03N1 (replication).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19364948</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31941657</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">38000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>five-year survivors diagnosed 1970-1999 (stated as 38K+; siblings not included)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ccss.stjude.org/about-the-study.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>38K+ survivors diagnosed 1970-1999</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CCSS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10521"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hungary"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Latvia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lithuania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Romania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Serbia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90104613</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union&apos;s Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4509</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CENTER-TBI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research in TBI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative European Neurotrauma Effectiveness Research in TBI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Collaborative European Neurotrauma Effectiveness Research in Traumatic Brain Injury</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research in Traumatic Brain Injury</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10521">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0858950"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10521"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>traumatic brain injury</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25525693+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This multicenter, longitudinal, prospective, observational study in 22 countries across Europe and Israel will collect detailed data from 5400 consenting patients, presenting within 24 hours of injury, with a clinical diagnosis of TBI and an indication for computed tomography.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8486724/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research in TBI (CENTER-TBI, registered at clinicaltrials.gov NCT02210221) study is a prospective cohort study conducted in 63 centers from 18 countries across Europe and Israel between December 2014 and December 2017.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8486724/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We grouped countries into seven regions: Baltic States (Latvia, and Lithuania), Eastern Europe (Hungary, Romania, and Serbia), Israel, Northern Europe (Denmark, Finland, Norway, and Sweden), Southern Europe (Italy, and Spain), the United Kingdom, and Western Europe (Austria, Belgium, France, Germany, the Netherlands).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90104613</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study of outcome from traumatic brain injury.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35301180</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8927841/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CENTER-TBI study recruited patients who presented with a history of TBI and met local guidelines for CT imaging.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union&apos;s Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25525693</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31526754</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34351445</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4509</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients in the core study (analysed); registry counted separately (2014-2017)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31526754</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The core study was registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, number NCT02210221, and with Resource Identification Portal (RRID: SCR_015582).FindingsData from 4509 patients from 18 countries, collected between Dec 9, 2014, and Dec 17, 2017, were analysed in the core study and from 22 782 patients in the registry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CENTER-TBI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
