        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3677984/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three studies were from Germany: the Bavarian Breast Cancer Cases and Controls Collection (BBCC), the Gene Environment Interactions and Breast Cancer study (GENICA), and the Mammary Carcinoma Risk Factor Investigation (MARIE).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90129576</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide interaction analysis of menopausal hormone therapy use and breast cancer risk among 62,370 women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35418701</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9007944/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GENICA was funded by the Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF) Germany grants 01KW9975/5, 01KW9976/8, 01KW9977/0 and 01KW0114, the Robert Bosch Foundation, Stuttgart, Deutsches Krebsforschungszentrum (DKFZ), Heidelberg, the Institute for Prevention and Occupational Medicine of the German Social Accident Insurance, Institute of the Ruhr University Bochum (IPA), Bochum, as well as the Department of Internal Medicine, Evangelische Kliniken Bonn gGmbH, Johanniter Krankenhaus, Bonn, Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20039012</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23781229</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25229211</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1022</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls analysed in the 2014 GENICA circadian-gene study; no total stated</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25229211</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Associations between seven polymorphisms in circadian genes (CLOCK, NPAS2, ARTNL, PER2 and CRY2), genes of melatonin biosynthesis and signaling (AANAT and MTNR1B) and breast cancer were analyzed with conditional logistic regression models, adjusted for potential confounders for 1022 cases and 1014 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1014</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls analysed in the 2014 GENICA circadian-gene study; no total stated</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25229211</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Associations between seven polymorphisms in circadian genes (CLOCK, NPAS2, ARTNL, PER2 and CRY2), genes of melatonin biosynthesis and signaling (AANAT and MTNR1B) and breast cancer were analyzed with conditional logistic regression models, adjusted for potential confounders for 1022 cases and 1014 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GENICA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid10674"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90565134</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">760</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">995</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1755</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genizon</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genizon BioSciences</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genizon GWAS</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10674">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005083"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10674"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>psoriasis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11783861/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Currently published GWASs include eight Europe-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohorts, including CASP [7], Kiel [8], Genizon [8], PsA GWAS [9], WTCCC2 [10], Exomechip [11], PAGE [12], and GAPC [12], two South Asia-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohort including three batches [13], and one East Asia-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohort [14].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4423213/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Kiel sample included 471 cases and 1,129 controls, and the Genizon data from Canada included 1,755 samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90565134</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry genome-wide meta-analysis with 472,819 individuals identifies 32 novel risk loci for psoriasis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39885523</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11783861/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Currently published GWASs include eight Europe-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohorts, including CASP [7], Kiel [8], Genizon [8], PsA GWAS [9], WTCCC2 [10], Exomechip [11], PAGE [12], and GAPC [12], two South Asia-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohort including three batches [13], and one East Asia-originated psoriasis-associated GWAS cohort [14].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.</owl:annotatedTarget>
