        <owl:annotatedTarget>A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
