    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244787</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European and multi-ancestry genome-wide association meta-analysis of atopic dermatitis highlights importance of systemic immune regulation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37794016</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10550990/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Multicentre Allergy Study (MAS) is a German birth cohort which has been described in detail previously71,72 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25757221</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26011739</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29664587</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1314</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>newborns recruited in 1990</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4744942/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The German Multicentre Allergy Study began with the recruitment of 1314 newborns between January and December 1990 in maternity wards from university hospitals in 5 German cities – Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich – and has been described in detail elsewhere 19 including follow‐up methods 7.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>G.MAS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MAS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
