        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90558259</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children&apos;s hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CWRU also denotes Cleveland Clinic Foundation/Veteran Affairs Medical Center Cohort (COHO:0001641); this term is Genetic Modifier Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1203</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CWRU</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GMS Lung Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Gene Modifier Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UNC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>US extremes of phenotype study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>University of North Carolina/Case Western Reserve University Case-Control Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Modifier Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid10722">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009061"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10722"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cystic fibrosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3296486/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Genetic Modifier Study (GMS) consists of unrelated patients homozygous for the common CF allele F508del (HGVS nomenclature: p.Phe508del), recruited from extremes of lung function9.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2995003/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>(II) the University of North Carolina/Case Western Reserve University Case-Control Study, a sample ascertained on the phenotype of extremes of lung disease (7) (US extremes of phenotype study)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90558259</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic modifiers of body mass index in individuals with cystic fibrosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39260370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11480786/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Cystic Fibrosis Genome Project (CFGP) is comprised of individuals with CF recruited by the CF Twin and Sibling Study (TSS)15 and Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD) Study16 (Johns Hopkins University), Genetic Modifier Study (GMS)17,18,19 and GMS of Severe CF Liver Disease (GMS CFLD)20,21 (University of North Carolina), and Early Pseudomonas Infection Control Observational (EPIC Obs) Study22 (University of Washington and Seattle Children’s Hospital).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children&apos;s hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16207846</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20681990</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21602797</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26417704</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1203</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>unrelated F508del homozygotes at lung-function extremes genotyped for the first consortium GWAS (extremes arm only)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2995003/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The extremes of phenotype study collected and genotyped 1,203 unrelated CF patients who (a) were homozygous for F508del, the most common CFTR mutation and (b) had lung function at the extremes of the population distribution.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CWRU</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
