    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10767"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>acute appendicitis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33060696+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study aimed at characterizing immune responses towards a large variety of gut commensals and pathogens, and pattern recognition receptor (PRR) ligands, and investigating the course of systemic inflammation in a prospective cohort of acute appendicitis patients.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10769"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifestyle characteristics</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02391675</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a cohort of 300 patients and 300 controls, environmental factors as well as genetic make-up of the innate immune system, focusing mainly on pattern recognition, will be analyzed in order to gain insight in their relative importance in the pathology of appendicitis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10771"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>dietary habits</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02391675</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a cohort of 300 patients and 300 controls, environmental factors as well as genetic make-up of the innate immune system, focusing mainly on pattern recognition, will be analyzed in order to gain insight in their relative importance in the pathology of appendicitis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10773"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental factors</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02391675</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a cohort of 300 patients and 300 controls, environmental factors as well as genetic make-up of the innate immune system, focusing mainly on pattern recognition, will be analyzed in order to gain insight in their relative importance in the pathology of appendicitis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9174512/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 325 patients were prospectively recruited in the HAPPIEST population at Jessa Hospital, Hasselt, Belgium, between June 2012 and October 2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90132298</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Impact of Human Genetic Variation on C-Reactive Protein Concentrations and Acute Appendicitis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35693796</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9174512/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 325 patients were prospectively recruited in the HAPPIEST population at Jessa Hospital, Hasselt, Belgium, between June 2012 and October 2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of patients aged 5 to 85 who presented with acute appendicitis at the emergency department of Jessa Hospital in Hasselt, Belgium, and had an appendectomy, recruited from June 2012 to October 2016 in a study led by Hasselt University with Jessa Hospital and Radboud University Medical Center. Questionnaires on diet, lifestyle and environment were collected together with blood, appendix tissue and stool samples, to study how environmental factors, the innate immune system and its genetic make-up, and the gut microbiota influence the development and severity of acute appendicitis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33060696</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35693796</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02391675</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">325</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>appendicitis patients recruited at Jessa Hospital, June 2012 to October 2016</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9174512/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 325 patients were prospectively recruited in the HAPPIEST population at Jessa Hospital, Hasselt, Belgium, between June 2012 and October 2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001184"/>
