        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid10820"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19435955+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 275 patients aged &lt;16 years were followed from onset of type 1 diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2713624/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study was a multicenter longitudinal investigation in 18 pediatric departments representing 15 countries in Europe and Japan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fine-mapping, trans-ancestral and genomic analyses identify causal variants, cells, genes and drug targets for type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34127860</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8273124/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These studies include the Type 1 Diabetes Genetics Consortium (T1DGC), British 1958 Birth Cohort, Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID), Consortium for the Longitudinal Evaluation of African-Americans with Early Rheumatoid Arthritis (CLEAR), Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications (EDIC), Genetics of Kidneys and Diabetes Study (GoKinD), New York Cancer Project (NYCP), SEARCH for Diabetes in Youth study (SEARCH), Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet study (TrialNet), Tyypin 1 Diabetekseen Sairastuneita Perheenjäsenineen (IDDMGEN), Tyypin 1 Diabeteksen Genetiikka (T1DGEN), Northern Ireland GRID Collection, Northern Ireland Young Hearts Project, Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes (HSG), and International HapMap Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multinational longitudinal cohort of children and adolescents under 16 with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes, recruited from August 1999 to December 2000 at 18 paediatric departments in 15 countries of Europe and Japan by the Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes, an international group of paediatric diabetes centres, and followed through the first 12 months after diagnosis with meal-stimulated C-peptide tests, HbA1c, insulin doses, islet autoantibodies and HLA typing, to study residual beta-cell function and the partial remission period.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19435955</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19708904</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21429197</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33203694</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">275</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children and adolescents with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes enrolled 1999-2000</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2713624/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 275 children and adolescents aged &lt;16 years with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes presenting to the pediatric departments between August 1999 and December 2000 were included in the study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001190"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HSG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90271557</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The second survey of the HUNT Study, conducted in 1995–97, to which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag, Norway, aged 20 or over were invited for questionnaires, interviews, a clinical examination and biological sampling. Its participants have consented to linkage with Norwegian health and administrative registries, and many of them have been genotyped.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">65228</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HUNT 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HUNT2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HUNT2 survey</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Nord-Trøndelag Health Study 1995–97</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the HUNT Study, all residents aged ≥20 years in the Nord-Trøndelag region, Norway, have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984-86.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All current residents ≥20 years of age in Nord-Trøndelag have been invited to each survey wave: the HUNT1 (1984–86, 77 202 participants, 89.4% of invitees participated),1 HUNT2 (1995-97, 65 228 participants, 69.5%)2 and HUNT3 (2006-08, 50 800 participants, 54.1%)3 surveys (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90271557</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>GWAS of random glucose in 476,326 individuals provide insights into diabetes pathophysiology, complications and treatment stratification.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37679419</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01462-3/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1462_MOESM6_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HUNT: Nord-Trøndelag Health Study 1995-97 (HUNT 2):Objectives, contents, methods and participation.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The second survey of the HUNT Study, conducted in 1995–97, to which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag, Norway, aged 20 or over were invited for questionnaires, interviews, a clinical examination and biological sampling. Its participants have consented to linkage with Norwegian health and administrative registries, and many of them have been genotyped.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35578897</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001191"/>
