    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11034"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11036"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11038"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90841197</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized, double-blind primary prevention trial of the Cancer Institute of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and the US National Cancer Institute in Linxian, Henan province, China, a rural county with some of the world&apos;s highest rates of oesophageal and gastric cardia cancer, which in 1985 enrolled healthy adults aged 40–69 from four communes in northern Linxian and gave them daily combinations of vitamins and minerals or placebo in a fractional factorial design from March 1986 to May 1991. Its participants have since been followed as a prospective cohort for cancer incidence and cause-specific mortality.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29584</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Linxian Nutrition Intervention Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Linxian General Population Nutrition Intervention Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11034">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_2000123"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11036">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0003834"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11038">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007576"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>daily combined vitamin/mineral supplement</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11101236/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Finally, a total of 29,584 subjects were included in the NIT study in 1986 to receive daily combined vitamin/mineral supplement or placebo.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11036"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>gastric cardia cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7960367+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Rates of oesophageal/gastric cardia cancer in Linxian, a rural county in north central China, are among the world&apos;s highest, but the risk factors are not well understood.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11038"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>oesophageal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7960367+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Rates of oesophageal/gastric cardia cancer in Linxian, a rural county in north central China, are among the world&apos;s highest, but the risk factors are not well understood.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11101236/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the 1980s, a Nutritional Intervention Trial (NIT) was initiated in Linxian, Henan province of China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90841197</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome wide association analysis and association of genetic risk and lifestyle with upper gastrointestinal cancer among an endoscopy-screened cohort in China.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41963194</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S2095927326003270-mmc1.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, participants were drawn from multiple established studies, including the Shanxi Upper Gastrointestinal Cancer Genetics Project and the Linxian Nutrition Intervention Trial, as well as additional prospective cohort studies incorporating in the validation phase.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomized, double-blind primary prevention trial of the Cancer Institute of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences and the US National Cancer Institute in Linxian, Henan province, China, a rural county with some of the world&apos;s highest rates of oesophageal and gastric cardia cancer, which in 1985 enrolled healthy adults aged 40–69 from four communes in northern Linxian and gave them daily combinations of vitamins and minerals or placebo in a fractional factorial design from March 1986 to May 1991. Its participants have since been followed as a prospective cohort for cancer incidence and cause-specific mortality.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34022824</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35224031</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38282387</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:7960367</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29584</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults randomised to supplement combinations or placebo (1986)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8866236/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Finally, a total of 29,584 subjects were randomly assigned to one of eight intervention groups which received daily vitamin/mineral supplement combinations or placebo according to a one-half replicate of a 24 fractional factorial design.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001214"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NIT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001215 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001215">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
