    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11056"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90013445</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort and biorepository of racially and ethnically diverse adults aged 30 or older living in the New York tri-state area, enrolled from January 2000 to December 2002 by the Academic Medical Development Company (AMDeC) Foundation, a consortium of New York institutions, at medical centres, community hospitals and community health centres in all five boroughs of New York City and at New York Blood Center donor drives. Participants completed a baseline questionnaire and gave blood for DNA and plasma, to be followed by questionnaires and registry linkage for studies of cancer aetiology and of racial and ethnic disparities in cancer risk, prevention and outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18187</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NYCP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>New York Control Population</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">New York Cancer Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11056">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004992"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11056"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15136663+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A new cohort study was undertaken with several aims: (1) to provide a database and biorepository for studies of cancer etiology and pathogenesis, including host genetics;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15136663+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Showing the feasibility of constructing a cohort based in New York City, plans proceed for additional recruitment and analyses on the salient questions about cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fine-mapping, trans-ancestral and genomic analyses identify causal variants, cells, genes and drug targets for type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34127860</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8273124/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>P.K.G. provided samples for genotyping through the New York Cancer Project (NYCP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort and biorepository of racially and ethnically diverse adults aged 30 or older living in the New York tri-state area, enrolled from January 2000 to December 2002 by the Academic Medical Development Company (AMDeC) Foundation, a consortium of New York institutions, at medical centres, community hospitals and community health centres in all five boroughs of New York City and at New York Blood Center donor drives. Participants completed a baseline questionnaire and gave blood for DNA and plasma, to be followed by questionnaires and registry linkage for studies of cancer aetiology and of racial and ethnic disparities in cancer risk, prevention and outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15136663</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18187</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults aged 30+ recruited with baseline questionnaire and blood (2000-2002)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:15136663</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Using venue-based sampling with quotas, 18,187 adults aged 30 years or older were recruited over a year to undergo a baseline questionnaire, venipuncture, and contact information.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001216"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NYCP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90454537</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based biobank study established in 2016 in Okinawa Prefecture, Japan, through the Okinawa Bioinformation Bank Project promoted by the University of the Ryukyus and Okinawa Prefecture, whose participants, recruited on Okinawa&apos;s islands including the Miyako Islands, give blood or saliva for DNA and genome-wide genotyping together with health check-up results, lifestyle questionnaires and, for some, the birthplaces of their four grandparents. It aims to clarify the population history of the Ryukyu islanders and to find genetic factors in common and rare diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10285</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>OBi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Okinawa Bioinformation Bank Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Okinawa Bioinformation Bank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10615566/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The second one consisted of 6,613 participants who were recruited at Okinawa Prefecture through the OBi Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90454537</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association studies for pelvic organ prolapse in the Japanese population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39349682</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11443051/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a GWAS for POP in Japanese participants registered in the Okinawa Bioinformation Bank (OBi) and Biobank Japan (BBJ) (Supplementary Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based biobank study established in 2016 in Okinawa Prefecture, Japan, through the Okinawa Bioinformation Bank Project promoted by the University of the Ryukyus and Okinawa Prefecture, whose participants, recruited on Okinawa&apos;s islands including the Miyako Islands, give blood or saliva for DNA and genome-wide genotyping together with health check-up results, lifestyle questionnaires and, for some, the birthplaces of their four grandparents. It aims to clarify the population history of the Ryukyu islanders and to find genetic factors in common and rare diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33432348</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37903429</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39987337</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10285</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals registered in the OBi analysed by PCA (analysed subset), 2025</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11846991/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed 10,285 individuals registered in the OBi using principal component analysis (PCA), along with individuals in the 1KGP phase 3 reference panel (AFR, n = 661; AMR, n = 347; EAS, n = 504; EUR, n = 503; SAS, n = 489), and defined 10,136 individuals as the Japanese population (Supplementary Fig. 2b).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001217"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>OBi</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11068"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001663"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90100588</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5117</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8845</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13962</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PANSCAN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PCCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PanScan</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11068">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009831"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11068"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pancreatic cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25086665+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a multistage genome-wide association study including 7,683 individuals with pancreatic cancer and 14,397 controls of European descent.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4191666/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Controls of ≥80% European ancestry were drawn from ten of the studies included in PanScan III (Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Lung Cancer Prevention Study (ATBC), American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study-II Cohort (CPS-II), European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC), Health Professionals Follow-Up Study (HPFS)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001663"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8488877/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 3 PanScan GWAS included participants from 16 cohorts from the National Cancer Institute (NCI) Cohort Consortium, 9 case–control studies, and 1 case series (Gastrointestinal Cancer Clinic of Dana–Farber Cancer Institute)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The studies included in PanScan (PanScan II) from PanC4 are: PACIFIC Study of Group Health and Northern California Kaiser Permanente Johns Hopkins University Mayo Clinic SPORE in Pancreatic Cancer MD Anderson Cancer Center Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center University of California San Francisco University of Toronto Yale University</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4191666/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Geographic region was defined as REGION_US (United States): AgHealth, CPS-II, DFCI, HPFS, MEC, NHS, NYU-WHS, PHS, PLCO, SELECT, VITAL, WHI; REGION_CNE (Central and Northern Europe): ATBC, EPIC, PANDoRA-Heidelberg, MCCS (Melbourne); and REGION_SE (Southern Europe): SBCS (Spain controls), PANKRAS-II (cases).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Also included are 61 pancreatic cancer cases and 67 control subjects from PanScan I as well as 173 pancreatic cancer cases from PanScan III of Asian ancestry from the Shanghai Men&apos;s and Women&apos;s Health Study (Supplemental Table 10, Wolpin et al. (Nat Genet, 2014)).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition to the cases from cohorts, we also included cases from the Gastrointestinal Cancer Clinic of Dana-Farber Cancer Institute Study (DFCI-GCC); from the University Hospital in Heidelberg, Germany, which is part of a larger European clinical case-control study (PANDoRA); and from clinic-based cases from eastern Spain (PANKRAS-II).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90100588</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of Recessively Inherited Genetic Variants Potentially Linked to Pancreatic Cancer Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34926279</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8678088/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To discover recessively inherited pancreatic cancer risk loci, we performed a re-analysis of the largest pancreatic cancer GWAS, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium (PanScan) and the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4), including 8,769 cases and 7,055 controls of European ancestry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25086665</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/cancer-types/pancreas/panscan</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5117</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PDAC cases and controls of European ancestry in the PanScan I-III association summary statistics</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The dataset includes results from an association study of 5,117 individuals diagnosed with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) and 8,845 control individuals, or a total of 13,962 subjects of European ancestry (as compared to the genotype and phenotype information under this project that includes 9,437 individuals (PanScan I and II PDAC case and control individuals and PanScan III PDAC cases only).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8845</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PDAC cases and controls of European ancestry in the PanScan I-III association summary statistics</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The dataset includes results from an association study of 5,117 individuals diagnosed with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) and 8,845 control individuals, or a total of 13,962 subjects of European ancestry (as compared to the genotype and phenotype information under this project that includes 9,437 individuals (PanScan I and II PDAC case and control individuals and PanScan III PDAC cases only).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13962</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PDAC cases and controls of European ancestry in the PanScan I-III association summary statistics</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The dataset includes results from an association study of 5,117 individuals diagnosed with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) and 8,845 control individuals, or a total of 13,962 subjects of European ancestry (as compared to the genotype and phenotype information under this project that includes 9,437 individuals (PanScan I and II PDAC case and control individuals and PanScan III PDAC cases only).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PANSCAN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PCCC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218"/>
