    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11084"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000485"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90274713</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym PEGASUS also denotes Prevention of Cardiovascular Events in Patients With Prior Heart Attack Using Ticagrelor Compared to Placebo on a Background of Aspirin-Thrombolysis in Myocardial Infarction 54 (COHO:0002246); this term is Prostate Cancer Genome-wide Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility Loci.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4838</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3053</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCI Prostate Cancer Genome-Wide Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility Loci Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PEGASUS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PEGASUS_PCa</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PEGASUS_Pca</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ProstatE cancer Genetic Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility loci</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prostate cancer Genome-wide Association Study to Uncover Susceptibility loci</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prostate Cancer Genome-wide Association Study of Uncommon Susceptibility Loci</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11084">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11084"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4422072/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A new genome-wide association study was conducted in prostate cancer cases and controls of European ancestry from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4422072/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, 76,693 men were enrolled in the trial from 10 centers in the United States from 1993 to 2001 and randomized to receive annual screening with prostate-specific antigen (PSA) for six years and digital rectal exam for the four years or referred to their physician for routine care.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000485"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5290311/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For PEGASUS, non-cases between ages 55–74 years were selected between 1993 and 2001 from non-Hispanic white men in the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90274713</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Characterizing prostate cancer risk through multi-ancestry genome-wide discovery of 187 novel risk variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37945903</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01534-4/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1534_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>PEGASUS was supported by the Intramural Research Program, Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics, National Cancer Institute, National Institutes of Health.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25939597</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28139693</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30287866</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4838</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PLCO prostate cancer cases and matched controls of European ancestry selected for genotyping (2015)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4422072/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 4,838 prostate cancer cases and 3,053 controls of European ancestry, matched on age and year of randomization, were selected for stage 1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3053</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PLCO prostate cancer cases and matched controls of European ancestry selected for genotyping (2015)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4422072/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 4,838 prostate cancer cases and 3,053 controls of European ancestry, matched on age and year of randomization, were selected for stage 1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PEGASUS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PEGASUS_PCa</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
