        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8991589/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SBCGS was conducted in 5152 participants (2867 case participants and 2285 control participants) from the following four population-based studies conducted among Chinese women in urban Shanghai between 1996 and 2005: the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study [25], the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study [26], the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (contributing controls only) [27] and the Shanghai Women’s Health Study [28].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001229"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000799.v1.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study (SBCGS) includes data from four population-based studies conducted among Chinese women in urban Shanghai: the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), the Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study (SWHS), and the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (SECS, contributing controls only).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001229"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90090980</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of novel breast cancer susceptibility loci in meta-analyses conducted among Asian and European descendants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32139696</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7057957/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Chinese participants were drawn from Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study 4 (SBCGS), which consists of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), Shanghai 5 Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study 6 (SECS, contributed control data only), and the Shanghai Women’s Health Study 7 (SWHS), four large population-based studies in urban Shanghai.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001229"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
