        <rdfs:comment>A total of 3740 patients diagnosed between October 1, 1999, and August 30, 2002, with incident malignant lymphomas, including non-Hodgkin lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma, and 3187 population controls provided detailed information on history of UV exposure and skin cancer and information on other possible risk factors for lymphomas.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4411784/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, SCALE is a population-based case–control study of the etiology of malignant lymphomas conducted in Sweden and Denmark 1999 to 2002.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90267402</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Distinct germline genetic susceptibility profiles identified for common non-Hodgkin lymphoma subtypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36273105</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41375-022-01711-0/MediaObjects/41375_2022_1711_MOESM1_ESM.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology GWAS SCALE FL-376 791 Population-based case-control study, Scandinavia Patients with incident primary NHL diagnosed through rapid case-ascertainment network in Sweden and Denmark Frequency matched (age in 10-year intervals, sex and country) population controls prospectively identified every 6 months in nationwide population registers (incidence density sampling).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15687363</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21037568</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25294155</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3740</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lymphoma patients diagnosed 1999-2002 and population controls who provided interview data</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15687363+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We tested this hypothesis in a population-based case-control study in Denmark and Sweden.MethodsA total of 3740 patients diagnosed between October 1, 1999, and August 30, 2002, with incident malignant lymphomas, including non-Hodgkin lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma, and 3187 population controls provided detailed information on history of UV exposure and skin cancer and information on other possible risk factors for lymphomas.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3187</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lymphoma patients diagnosed 1999-2002 and population controls who provided interview data</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15687363+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We tested this hypothesis in a population-based case-control study in Denmark and Sweden.MethodsA total of 3740 patients diagnosed between October 1, 1999, and August 30, 2002, with incident malignant lymphomas, including non-Hodgkin lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma, and 3187 population controls provided detailed information on history of UV exposure and skin cancer and information on other possible risk factors for lymphomas.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230"/>
