        <dcterms:title>Africa-specific human genetic variation near CHD1L associates with HIV-1 load.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37532928</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10848312/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Swiss HIV Cohort Study (SHCS) is an ongoing multicentre research project dealing with adults infected with HIV aged 16 years or older residing in Switzerland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001235"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide prospective longitudinal cohort of people with HIV aged 16 or older in Switzerland, established in 1988 as a collaboration of the Swiss university hospitals, large cantonal hospitals, affiliated smaller hospitals and private physicians, who recruit and follow the participants, to improve the health of people with HIV through clinical, translational and basic research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37532928</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.shcs.ch/about-shcs/study-design/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001235"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">22282</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants ever enrolled since 1988, as of June 2025</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13566368/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>By June 2025, 22 282 participants had been enrolled from university and cantonal hospitals, and, since 1996, also from regional hospitals and private practitioners (Figure S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
