    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11224"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90281365</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10366</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SOF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Study of Osteoporotic Fractures</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11224">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11224"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>osteoporotic fractures</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5390547/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SOF is a NIH-funded prospective cohort study of older women initially designed to determine risk factors for fractures and falls but expanded to evaluate risk for other outcomes including all-cause and cause-specific mortality in older women.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10319806/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohort is comprised of 9,704 community-dwelling women 65 years 6 old or older recruited from populations-based listings in four U.S. areas: Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90281365</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The identification of distinct protective and susceptibility mechanisms for hip osteoarthritis: findings from a genome-wide association study meta-analysis of minimum joint space width and Mendelian randomisation cluster analyses.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37619450</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10470292/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GWAS cohorts comprised the UKB, The Rotterdam Study (RS) I&amp;II, Osteoporotic Fractures in Men (MrOS) Study and Study of Osteoporotic Fractures (SOF). mJSW was measured automatically in UKB and manually in RS, MrOS and SOF (see Supplementary Methods).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28465840</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37402774</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37619450</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10366</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women enrolled in total (9704 white women 1986-1988 plus 662 African-American women at Year 10), 1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5390547/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subsequently, at the Year 10 SOF examination conducted between 1997 and 1998, 662 African-American women were enrolled in the study increasing the total cohort enrollment to 10,366 women [11].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SOF</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90726344</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">25313</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>STAGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Screening Twin Adults: Genes and Environment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Swedish Twin Study of Adults: Genes and Environment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12859210/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The &apos;Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment’ (STAGE) is a cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry at the Karolinska Institute in Stockholm, of approximately 32,000 twin individuals, born between 1959 and 1985.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12859210/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The &apos;Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment’ (STAGE) is a cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry at the Karolinska Institute in Stockholm, of approximately 32,000 twin individuals, born between 1959 and 1985.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90726344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analyses identify distinct genetic architectures for early-onset and late-onset depression.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41233554</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12695632/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment (STAGE): This cohort consisted of those born between 1959 and 1985 from the Swedish Twin Registry10 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35580588</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38446452</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40425723</obo:IAO_0000119>
