    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90568440</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2960</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Swedisch Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Swedish Twin study of Child and Adolescent Development</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TCHAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Twin Study of Child and Adolescent Development</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Swedish Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6133086/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Six large population-based cohorts (NTR and GenR from the Netherlands, TEDS from the UK, CATSS and TCHAD from Sweden and FinnTwin12 from Finland) analysed the co-occurrence of aggression measures with other psychopathologies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000160"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5581816/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A population-based prospective cohort study including all twins from the Swedish Twin Registry who were born in Sweden 1985–1986 (N = 2960) [19] was conducted. These twins were invited to participate in a longitudinal Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development (TCHAD), see [20].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90568440</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis of childhood ADHD symptoms and diagnosis identifies new loci and potential effector genes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40962958</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02295-y/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2295_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Swedish Twin study of Child and Adolescent Development (TCHAD) was supported by the 658 Swedish Council for Working Life and the Swedish Research Council (Medicine and SIMSAM).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17539366</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28638965</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29845340</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37289452</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2960</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>twin children born May 1985-Dec 1986 in the cohort (1480 pairs), 1994</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10251215/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were originally included in a population-based longitudinal twin study, the Twin Study of Child and Adolescent Development (TCHAD), comprising all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986 (2960 children in total).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
