        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90013445</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">250000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TrialNet</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet Research Group</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet Study Group</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11264">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11264"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>TrialNet actively screens relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes, but other individuals who do not have a relative with the disease may join TN01 if they are found to have positive islet autoantibodies in an outside laboratory.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Currently, TrialNet includes 17 clinical centers located in the U.S., Canada, and Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90013445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fine-mapping, trans-ancestral and genomic analyses identify causal variants, cells, genes and drug targets for type 1 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34127860</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8273124/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We acknowledge the support of the Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet Study Group (https://www.trialnet.org), which identified study participants and provided samples and follow-up data for this study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40272284</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">250000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>relatives screened for islet autoantibodies in Pathway to Prevention (stated as more than 250,000), 2024</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The findings from TN01 have proven to be reproducible across multiple cohorts in different intervention studies.In TN01 (renamed Pathway to Prevention) &gt;250,000 relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes have been screened for autoantibodies (Fig. 1), and Pathway to Prevention remains the largest long-running cohort study of both children and adults at risk for disease with 8,937 individuals enrolled in monitoring.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TrialNet</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


