        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11424"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>primary open-angle glaucoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31688885+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A 2-stage GWAS with a discovery data set of 2320 individuals with primary open-angle glaucoma and 2121 control individuals without primary open-angle glaucoma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Peru"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31688885+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Study participants were recruited from Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru, and Mali from 2003 to 2018.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90455614</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A multi-cohort genome-wide association study in African ancestry individuals reveals risk loci for primary open-angle glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38242088</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11844349</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a mega-analysis in a discovery cohort that combined three African ancestry datasets: the ADAGES study (n = 1,999),36 the GGLAD consortium (n = 2,952),37 and the Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics (POAAGG) study (n = 6,324)38 (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women&apos;s Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31688885</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
