        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
