    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11553"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>melanoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19887461+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 2001 to 2005, the authors recruited 1,164 probands including 629 cases with histopathologically confirmed, first-primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed before age 40 years, 240 population-based controls frequency matched for age, and 295 spouse/friend controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11555"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>solar ultraviolet exposure</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19887461+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Discovering and understanding genetic risk factors for melanoma and their interactions with phenotype, sun exposure, and other risk factors could lead to new strategies for melanoma control.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11557"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifetime sun exposure</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19887461+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Discovering and understanding genetic risk factors for melanoma and their interactions with phenotype, sun exposure, and other risk factors could lead to new strategies for melanoma control.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6249137/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Recruitment of case (n = 629) and control (n = 535) participants was locally coordinated in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane, Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001266</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies a new melanoma susceptibility locus at 1q21.3.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21983785</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3227560/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Melanoma cases of European descent (n=2,168) were selected from the Queensland study of Melanoma: Environment and Genetic Associations (Q-MEGA)6 and the Australian Melanoma Family Study7 (AMFS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, population-based case-control-family study in Australia, recruiting people with early-onset first-primary cutaneous melanoma, population-based and spouse or friend controls, and their relatives, between 2001 and 2005, to investigate genetic and environmental influences on melanoma risk.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19887461</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">629</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>probands recruited 2001-2005 (629 cases, 240 population controls, 295 spouse/friend controls); relatives not counted</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19887461</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 2001 to 2005, the authors recruited 1,164 probands including 629 cases with histopathologically confirmed, first-primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed before age 40 years, 240 population-based controls frequency matched for age, and 295 spouse/friend controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1164</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>probands recruited 2001-2005 (629 cases, 240 population controls, 295 spouse/friend controls); relatives not counted</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19887461</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 2001 to 2005, the authors recruited 1,164 probands including 629 cases with histopathologically confirmed, first-primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed before age 40 years, 240 population-based controls frequency matched for age, and 295 spouse/friend controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001277"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AMFS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11565"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90446654</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ANGST</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Anxiety NeuroGenetics STudy (ANGST) Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Anxiety NeuroGenetics STudy Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anxiety NeuroGenetics STudy</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11565">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005618"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11565"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>anxiety disorders</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940340/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Nine samples containing AD phenotypes from seven independent studies participating in the Anxiety NeuroGenetics STudy (ANGST) Consortium were included in the meta-analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2015.197/MediaObjects/41380_2016_BFmp2015197_MOESM495_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The QIMR sample is an Australian twin/family sample by design from which we selected one representative member from each family for consistency of analysis with the other samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2015.197/MediaObjects/41380_2016_BFmp2015197_MOESM495_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SHIP and PsyCoLaus were psychiatric sub-studies of medical research cohorts ascertained in Germany and Switzerland, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2015.197/MediaObjects/41380_2016_BFmp2015197_MOESM495_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three cohorts come from the Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2015.197/MediaObjects/41380_2016_BFmp2015197_MOESM495_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>MGS is the control sample collected in the US for a schizophrenia case-control study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90446654</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide meta-analysis, functional genomics and integrative analyses implicate new risk genes and therapeutic targets for anxiety disorders.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37945807</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-023-01746-y</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The genome-wide summary statistics of ANGST were downloaded from https://figshare.com/ndownloader/articles/14842689/versions/1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26754954</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>unrelated individuals in the 2016 anxiety-disorder GWAS meta-analysis of nine samples (stated as &quot;over 18 000&quot;)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26754954</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Meta-analysis for each phenotype combined results across the nine samples for over 18 000 unrelated individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ANGST</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11575"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_Zealand"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST001595</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1955</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>AOGC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11575">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005298"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11575"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>osteoporosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080863/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify genes associated with osteoporosis, we have performed a genome-wide association study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080863/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The discovery sample population included 1128 Australian, 74 New Zealand and 753 British women, between 55–85 years of age, five or more years postmenopausal</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST001595</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>WNT16 influences bone mineral density, cortical bone thickness, bone strength, and osteoporotic fracture risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22792071</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium (AOGC) study collected unrelated individuals with extreme BMD phenotypes as a powerful strategy for gene discovery in quantitative traits [11], [52].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21533022</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22792071</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1955</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>postmenopausal women with extreme high or low hip BMD in the GWAS discovery sample</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080863/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In order to improve study power and to address the demographic group of highest risk from osteoporotic fracture, we have used a unique study design, studying 1,955 postmenopausal women with either extreme high or low hip bone mineral density.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>AOGC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11582"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624455</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">64</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>APRICOT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Anakinra for Pustular psoriasis: Response in a Controlled Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Anakinra for pustular psoriasis trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Anakinra for Pustular Psoriasis: Response in a Controlled Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11582">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015597"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11582"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>palmoplantar pustulosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34411292+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To determine whether anakinra (an IL-1 receptor antagonist) delivers therapeutic benefit in PPP.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9255857/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This was a randomized (1 : 1), double‐blind, two‐staged, adaptive, UK multicentre, placebo‐controlled trial</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624455</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide meta-analysis of palmoplantar pustulosis implicates TH2 responses and cigarette smoking in disease pathogenesis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38815935</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2024/01/17/2024.01.17.24301406.full.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UK dataset included 288 affected individuals of European descent, who were recruited in specialist dermatology centers as part of the APRICOT clinical trial</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30157880</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34411292</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">64</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants randomised October 2016 - January 2020 (31 anakinra, 33 placebo)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9255857/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From October 2016 to January 2020, 374 patients were screened and 64 eligible participants were enrolled; 33 were randomized to placebo and 31 to anakinra (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>APRICOT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281">
