        <obo:IAO_0000115>An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson&apos;s disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson&apos;s disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
