    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11705"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90245878</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">750</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CanSCAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CanSCAD Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CanSCAD Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian SCAD Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian SCAD Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian Spontaneous Coronary Artery Dissection Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian spontaneous coronary artery dissection study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>canSCAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Canadian Spontaneous Coronary Artery Dissection Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11705">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005010"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11705"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>spontaneous coronary artery dissection</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30698711+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a multicentre, prospective, observational study of patients with non-atherosclerotic SCAD presenting acutely from 22 centres in North America.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7474092/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients presenting with acute SCAD were prospectively enrolled from 22 sites throughout North America (20 sites in Canada and 2 in the United States).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90245878</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis of spontaneous coronary artery dissection identifies risk variants and genes related to artery integrity and tissue-mediated coagulation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37248441</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10260398/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CanSCAD genetic substudy (N=502) included SCAD patients from the prospective Canadian SCAD Cohort Study and the Non-Atherosclerotic Coronary Artery Disease (NACAD) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30698711</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32887874</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">750</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>SCAD patients enrolled in the first phase (Canadian SCAD Cohort Study), 2018</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30698711</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We prospectively enrolled 750 SCAD patients from June 2014 to June 2018.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CanSCAD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>canSCAD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11713"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11715"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90027158</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CCHS also denotes China Cardiovascular Health Study (COHO:0001579); this term is Copenhagen City Heart Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">14223</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CCHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Østerbroundersøgelsen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Copenhagen City Heart Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11713">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
