    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11750"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11752"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000456"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90451657</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses&apos; Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1172</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1157</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGEMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGEMS collaboration</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Cancer Institute Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Cancer Institute Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11750">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007254"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11752">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11750"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A new NCI initiative, Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility (CGEMS), is a three-year study designed to identify common genetic variations associated with risk for prostate and breast cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11752"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A new NCI initiative, Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility (CGEMS), is a three-year study designed to identify common genetic variations associated with risk for prostate and breast cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000456"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3493132/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We initially genotyped 1183 cases of postmenopausal invasive breast cancer and 1185 individually-matched controls from the Nurses’ Health Study (NHS) cohort, using the Illumina HumanHap500 array, as part of the National Cancer Institute CGEMS (Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility) Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3374121/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohort studies were: the Prostate, Lung Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO, subjects from continental USA) (Gohagan et al. 2000); the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II (CPS-II, from continental USA) (Calle et al. 2002) and the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study (ATBC, from Finland) (1994).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3374121/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case–control study was the French Prostate Case–Control Study (CeRePP, Centre de Recherche pour les Pathologies Prostatiques, from France) (Valeri et al. 2003).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90451657</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Deciphering the genetics and mechanisms of predisposition to multiple myeloma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39103364</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-50932-7/MediaObjects/41467_2024_50932_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses&apos; Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17529973</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22271044</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1172</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls in the first (prostate cancer) genome-wide scan, 2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17401363</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>While conducting a genome-wide association study in the Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility project with 550,000 SNPs in a nested case-control study (1,172 cases and 1,157 controls of European origin), we identified a new association at 8q24 with an independent effect on prostate cancer susceptibility.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1157</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls in the first (prostate cancer) genome-wide scan, 2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17401363</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>While conducting a genome-wide association study in the Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility project with 550,000 SNPs in a nested case-control study (1,172 cases and 1,157 controls of European origin), we identified a new association at 8q24 with an independent effect on prostate cancer susceptibility.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGEMS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11762"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90271928</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2441</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian CF Gene Modifier Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian CF Modifier Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian Consortium for Genetic Studies</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian Cystic fibrosis Gene Modifier Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Canadian Gene Modifier Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Canadian Cystic Fibrosis Gene Modifier Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11762">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009061"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11762"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cystic fibrosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589222/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CGS patients were recruited from the Canadian population of CF patients.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2248329/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CF patients and their family members were recruited from 37 specialized CF clinics across Canada (shown in Supplemental Table 5), during a period from 2003 to 2006, as participants in the Canadian CF Modifier Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90271928</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Modifiers of Cystic Fibrosis Lung Disease Severity: Whole-Genome Analysis of 7,840 Patients.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36921087</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC10595435</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CGS=Canadian CF Gene Modifier Study (population-based); FrGMS=French CF Gene Modifier Consortium (population-based); JHU=Johns Hopkins University (twin-siblings design); UNC=University of North Carolina (extremes of phenotype); UW=University of Washington (longitudinal study for effect of Pseudomonas aeruginosa acquisition on lung disease).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18292811</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23670970</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26417704</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30807572</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31697830</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2441</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients with CF recruited 2003-2006 (parents not included)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18292811</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Canadian CF Modifier Study population consists of 2,441 patients diagnosed with CF between 1951 and 2006 and 3,092 parents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGMS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11770"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90824165</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2554</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHAVI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIAID Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11770">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005109"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11770"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HIV-1 infection</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4138272/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed PBMC values from CHAVI cohorts of acutely HIV-infected (n = 1125), chronically HIV-infected (n = 626) and HIV-negative (n = 297) participants and found that initial PBMC viabilities, yield, and processing time were equivalent (all p-values &lt;0.001; data not shown) for all cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21160409+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) in a population of 1532 individuals from Malawi, a country with high prevalence of HIV-1 infection.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2791220/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients have been included from two sources (Text S1): [1] Euro-CHAVI, a Consortium of 8 European and 1 Australian Cohorts/Studies; and [2] MACS, the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study that enrolled homosexual and bisexual men in 4 US cities.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24910414+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Nine site-affiliated laboratories in Africa and the USA collected and processed PBMCs, and cryopreserved PBMC were shipped to CHAVI repositories in Africa and the USA for long-term storage.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90824165</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiancestry Genome-Wide Association Study Identifies Variants in a Zinc Finger Gene Cluster as Novel Regulators of HIV Control.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41640362</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20041166</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20205591</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21160409</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23935489</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24910414</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2554</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HIV-1-infected individuals genotyped in the Host Genetics Core&apos;s 2009 GWAS of HIV control (Euro-CHAVI and MACS)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20041166</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 2554 HIV-1 infected individuals of self-reported Caucasian ancestry were genotyped on Illumina whole-genome chips (Table S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHAVI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11779"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90837424</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients&apos; first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1114</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CKC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese Keratoconus Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese keratoconus cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chinese Keratoconus Cohort Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11779">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015486"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11779"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>keratoconus</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38703249+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CKC cohort is hospital-based and dynamic and was established in Zhengzhou, China; KC patients (n = 1114) from a large geographical area were enrolled from January 2019 to June 2023, with a mean age of 22.23 years (6‒57 years).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114610/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All subjects were from China and self-reported Chinese.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90837424</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of Novel Loci With Keratoconus Susceptibility in a Chinese Genome-Wide Association Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38767907</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114610/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 958 patients with KC from the Chinese keratoconus (CKC) cohort study and 7186 controls were included in the current study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients&apos; first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38703249</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39186261</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40642536</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1114</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>keratoconus patients enrolled January 2019 to June 2023</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38703249</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CKC cohort is hospital-based and dynamic and was established in Zhengzhou, China; KC patients (n = 1114) from a large geographical area were enrolled from January 2019 to June 2023, with a mean age of 22.23 years (6‒57 years).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
