    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11843"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Southern_Africa"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90328131</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks&apos; gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1137</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DCHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Drakenstein Child Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11843">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0024355"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11843"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lower respiratory tract infection</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5107608/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We describe a unique multidisciplinary South African birth cohort, the Drakenstein Child Health Study (DCHS), to investigate the incidence, risk factors, aetiology and long-term impact of early lower respiratory tract infection (LRTI) on child health.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5107608/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DCHS is a population-based birth cohort study in the Drakenstein area in Paarl, a peri-urban area, 60 km outside Cape Town, South Africa.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90328131</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry genome-wide association study of major depression aids locus discovery, fine mapping, gene prioritization and causal inference.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38177345</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10864182/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We had access to individual-level data for Army STARRS, UKB, Women’s Health Initiative (WHI), Intern Health Study (IHS), GERA, Jackson Heart Study (JHS), Drakenstein Child Health Study and the Detroit Neighborhood Health Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks&apos; gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25228292</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38177345</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1137</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pregnant women enrolled who gave birth (mothers; 1143 live-born children)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31751344</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Over 3 years, 1137 women (median age 25.8 years; 21% HIV-infected) gave birth to 1143 live babies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>DCHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11850"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90103973</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">552</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Dental SCORE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pittsburgh Dental SCORE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dental Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11850">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11850"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The fourth cohort (Dental SCORE, n = 548) is a subset of a larger project, Heart SCORE, which is an ongoing cardiovascular disease study of 2,000 middle aged White and African Americans in the Pittsburgh region of Pennsylvania [17].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The fourth cohort (Dental SCORE, n = 548) is a subset of a larger project, Heart SCORE, which is an ongoing cardiovascular disease study of 2,000 middle aged White and African Americans in the Pittsburgh region of Pennsylvania [17].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90103973</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic Analyses of Enamel Hypoplasia in Multiethnic Cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35172313</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The fourth cohort (Dental SCORE, n = 548) is a subset of a larger project, Heart SCORE, which is an ongoing cardiovascular disease study of 2,000 middle aged White and African Americans in the Pittsburgh region of Pennsylvania [17].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.</owl:annotatedTarget>
