    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid11935"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenya"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tanzania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uganda"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90652520</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">862</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2934</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EMBLEM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EMBLEM study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology of Burkitt Lymphoma in East-African Children and Minors</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology of Burkitt lymphoma in East African children and minors</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Epidemiology of Burkitt Lymphoma in East African Children and Minors</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid11935">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007243"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid11935"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Burkitt lymphoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://emblem.cancer.gov/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>EMBLEM is a case control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma (BL) designed to investigate risk factors of BL in malaria-endemic areas of Uganda, Tanzania, and Kenya.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tanzania"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12380610/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the EMBLEM study enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0-15 years from six neighboring rural geographical areas—two each in Uganda, Kenya, and Tanzania (Figure 1a) during 2010-2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90652520</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study identifies an African-specific locus on chromosome 21q22.12 associated with Burkitt lymphoma risk and survival.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40646133</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12380610/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the EMBLEM study enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0-15 years from six neighboring rural geographical areas—two each in Uganda, Kenya, and Tanzania (Figure 1a) during 2010-2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40646133</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://emblem.cancer.gov/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">862</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>suspected Burkitt lymphoma cases and population controls enrolled 2010-2016</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31054214</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We therefore conducted a population-based case-control study of eBL in children aged 0-15 years old in six regions in Northern Uganda, Northern Tanzania and Western Kenya, enrolling 862 suspected cases and 2,934 population controls (response rates 98.5-100%), and processing ~40,000 vials of samples using standardized protocols.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2934</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>suspected Burkitt lymphoma cases and population controls enrolled 2010-2016</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31054214</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We therefore conducted a population-based case-control study of eBL in children aged 0-15 years old in six regions in Northern Uganda, Northern Tanzania and Western Kenya, enrolling 862 suspected cases and 2,934 population controls (response rates 98.5-100%), and processing ~40,000 vials of samples using standardized protocols.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EMBLEM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


