        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The FARIVE study is a French multicentre case-control study carried out between 2003–2009, as previously described45.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001323"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A French multicentre case-control study of venous thromboembolism, run in 11 centres from 2003 to 2009, that enrolled consecutive adult inpatients and outpatients treated for a first objectively documented deep vein thrombosis and/or pulmonary embolism, without active cancer or malignancy in the previous 5 years, whose blood was mostly sampled in the week after diagnosis, and hospital controls matched for age, sex and centre with no history of venous or arterial thrombosis; the patients were also followed prospectively, to study risk factors for a first venous thromboembolism and for its recurrence.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19967159</obo:IAO_0000119>
