        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90103971</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission&apos;s Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members&apos; melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2981</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1982</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenoMEL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenoMEL Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GenoMEL consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>International Melanoma Genetics Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Melanoma Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12054">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005105"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12054"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>melanoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21983787+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our discovery phase included 2,981 individuals with melanoma and 1,982 study-specific control individuals of European ancestry, as well as an additional 6,426 control subjects from French or British populations, all of whom were genotyped for 317,000 or 610,000 single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0611-8/MediaObjects/41588_2020_611_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Additional clinically confirmed cutaneous melanoma cases and controls were available from two French cohorts contributing to GenoMEL Phase 1 and 2; MELARISK (535 cases)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2957428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The following geographic locales were defined across three continents: Europe—France (Paris), Italy (Emilia-Romagna and Genoa), the Netherlands (Leiden), Spain (Barcelona), Sweden (Lund, Stockholm), and United Kingdom (Glasgow, Leeds); North America—Boston, NCI, Philadelphia, and Toronto; Australia—Brisbane and Sydney.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2957428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The participants of GenoMEL in Toronto, Canada</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3251256/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>the analysis utilised 2,804 cases (2,692 European and 112 Israeli) and 1,835 controls from GenoMEL studies and 5,783 controls from France and the UK Wellcome Trust Case-Control Consortium (WTCCC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.959/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng959_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These regions were: Scandinavia (Lund, Stockholm and Norway)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.959/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng959_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>UK/Netherlands (Leeds, Leiden and Glasgow), France, Spain, Israel and Poland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335"/>
