        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90833065</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">489975</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1472094</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1962069</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GO</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GO Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Osteoarthritis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Osteoarthritis consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Osteoarthritis Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12088">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005178"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12088"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>osteoarthritis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34450027+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we conduct a genome-wide association study meta-analysis across 826,690 individuals (177,517 with osteoarthritis) and identify 100 independently associated risk variants across 11 osteoarthritis phenotypes, 52 of which have not been associated with the disease before.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Aged Study was conducted in 1993 as a multi-wave mailout to 4562 twins (2281 pairs) aged over 50 years old who were registered with the Australian Twin Registry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The China Kadoorie Biobank (CKB) is a prospective cohort of 512,000 adults aged 30-79 years, recruited from ten rural and urban areas of China during 2004-2008.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study is based on material from Copenhagen Hospital Biobank (CHB), a regional biobank containing leftover EDTA whole blood samples from type and screen analyses in patients admitted to hospitals in the Capital Region of Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Estonian Biobank cohort is a volunteer-based sample of the Estonian resident adult population (aged ≥18 years).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim is to get 500,000 Finns to participate in the study through donations of samples to biobanks.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The osteoarthritis participants’ recruitment was conducted in the city of Larissa, central Greece.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hong_Kong"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Volunteers of southern Chinese ancestry living in Hong Kong were recruited for assessment which included a questionnaire for low back pain and associated symptoms and sagittal T2-weighted fast spin-echo MRI of the spine.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Iceland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The deCODE genetics osteoarthritis study is an ongoing population based study in Iceland that was initiated in 1997.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japanese cohort of knee OA GWAS (disease cohort) consists of 900 cases and 3,400 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The RAAK study is aimed at the biobanking of joint materials as well as mesenchymal stem cells and primary chondrocytes from patients (paired preserved and OA affected cartilage samples) and controls in the Leiden University Medical Center and collaborating outpatient clinics in the Leiden area in The Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HUNT Study is a longitudinal, population-based health study, which has been conducted in the county of Nord-Trøndelag, Norway, since 1984.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Samples were collected in 2 stages from 10 United Kingdom locations (London, Nottingham, Oxford, Sheffield, Southampton, Edinburgh, Newcastle-Upon-Tyne, Sheffield, Wansbeck, and Worcester).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The United States Million Veteran Program (MVP) is a national research program to learn how genes, lifestyle, and military exposures affect health and illness.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90833065</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic study identifies novel genes in developmental dysplasia of the hip.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41912496</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13035913/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Since DDH is a strong risk factor of hip OA, to maximize statistical power to detect novel signals in hip OA, we used summary statistics of European hip OA in GO,25 international consortium of osteoarthritis, and meta-analyzed with Japanese DDH.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34450027</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">489975</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the 2025 GO 2.0 GWAS meta-analysis (osteoarthritis cases and controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-08771-z</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we conducted a large-scale GWAS meta-analysis across 1,962,069 individuals, achieving a 2.64-fold increase in effective sample size compared with the next largest GWAS3.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1472094</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the 2025 GO 2.0 GWAS meta-analysis (osteoarthritis cases and controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-08771-z</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we conducted a large-scale GWAS meta-analysis across 1,962,069 individuals, achieving a 2.64-fold increase in effective sample size compared with the next largest GWAS3.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1962069</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the 2025 GO 2.0 GWAS meta-analysis (osteoarthritis cases and controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-08771-z</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we conducted a large-scale GWAS meta-analysis across 1,962,069 individuals, achieving a 2.64-fold increase in effective sample size compared with the next largest GWAS3.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


