    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12258"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90101764</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1345</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ISP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International Stuttering Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12258">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0000723"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12258"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>developmental stuttering</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Formed in 2020, the ISP continues to collate global outbred populations of people who stutter, specifically to illuminate genetic etiology and broaden investigations of its diverse and variable phenotype.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8756529/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We greatly thank every individual who donated DNA to this project in Ireland, Australia, and the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90101764</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Phenome risk classification enables phenotypic imputation and gene discovery in developmental stuttering.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34861174</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8715184/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We validated these results by comparing the concordance of our GWAS summary statistics to the GWAS results obtained from an independent clinically ascertained stuttering sample set acquired through the International Stuttering Project (ISP) and the polygenic-risk-prediction scores in the clinically ascertained cases versus matched population-based controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34861174</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35047858</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1345</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>clinically ascertained people who stutter in the collection used for the 2022 GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35047858</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ISP comprises 1,345 clinically ascertained developmental stuttering cases collected from the Curtin Stuttering Treatment Clinic in Perth, Australia; the SpeechMatters Clinic and the Irish Stammering Association, in Dublin, Ireland; the National Stuttering Association, USA; online recruitment on reddit.com; and Dr.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
