    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12284"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>tuberculosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ITHGC includes 12 case–control GWAS from nine countries in Europe, Africa, and Asia (total of 14,153 pulmonary TB cases and 19,536 healthy controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition, all institutions involved in the ITHGC have ethics approval for their respective studies: China 1 and 2: The study protocol was approved by the Ethics Committee of the Beijing Chest Hospital, the 309 Hospital of the PLA, Shijiazhuang Fifth Hospital, the China PLA General Hospital, the Tongliao TB institute and the Center for Diseases Control and Prevention in Jalainuoer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Estonian Bioethics and Human Research Council (EBIN) approved the Estonian Genome Center study reported in this manuscript.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study protocol was approved by the ethics committee (EC) of the University of Luebeck, Germany (reference 07-125), and was adopted by other ethics committees covering all 18 participating centres</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ghana"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Ethics approval was granted by the Committee on Human Research, Publications and Ethics, School of Medical Sciences, Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology, Kumasi, Ghana, and the Ethics Committee of the Ghana Health Service, Accra, Ghana.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We would like to thank all the subjects and the members of the Rotary Club of Osaka-Midosuji District 2660 Rotary International in Japan who donated their DNA for this work.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Blood samples from all participants were collected and studied with written informed consent according to the Declaration of Helsinki and with approvals from the local ethics committees in Russia (St. Petersburg and Samara)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The RSA population is a five-way admixed South African population with genetic contributions from Bantu-speaking African, KhoeSan, European, and South and South East Asian populations</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359"/>
