        <rdfs:comment>Haemostasis Unit, Hôpital Cantonal Universitaire, Geneva, Switzerland</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8106967+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We studied human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) infection incidence over time in a 16-center cohort of hemophiliacs in the United States and Europe and estimated the most likely date of seroconversion for all seropositive subjects.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90269914</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Africa-specific human genetic variation near CHD1L associates with HIV-1 load.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37532928</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10848312/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I) evaluated and prospectively followed patients with hemophilia or a related coagulation disorder.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20337924</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37532928</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8106967</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1219</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>subjects in the first study (MHCS-I) only, as of 1989</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:2477702</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We evaluated a multicenter cohort of 1219 subjects with hemophilia or related disorders prospectively, focusing on 319 subjects with documented dates of seroconversion to human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MHCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12437"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90451657</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A UK open-label, randomised, phase 3 adaptive-design trial for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales and Scotland, recruiting from 2010, which assigned patients by age and fitness to intensive (transplantation) or non-intensive pathways and had three randomisation stages, including induction regimens and lenalidomide maintenance against observation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym MRC also denotes MRC Myeloma IX trial (COHO:0001375); this term is Myeloma XI trial.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4420</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MRC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MyXI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Myeloma XI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Myeloma-XI trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Myeloma XI trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
