        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.</owl:annotatedTarget>
