    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12519"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12521"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90565134</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Henschel Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NPF</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Psoriasis Foundation Victor Henschel Tissue Repository</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Psoriasis Victor Henschel Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Victor Henschel Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">National Psoriasis Victor Henschel BioBank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12519">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005083"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12521">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011849"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12519"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>psoriasis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Indeed, similar studies using the Henschel biobank reported the differences in the genes that contribute to the risk of psoriatic arthritis versus the more common skin presentations we think of as psoriasis [5].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12521"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>psoriatic arthritis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Indeed, similar studies using the Henschel biobank reported the differences in the genes that contribute to the risk of psoriatic arthritis versus the more common skin presentations we think of as psoriasis [5].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4423213/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We thank the National Psoriasis Foundation for provision of US replication samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90565134</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry genome-wide meta-analysis with 472,819 individuals identifies 32 novel risk loci for psoriasis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39885523</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11783861/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the PsA GWAS, 1,526 PsA case subjects and 1,508 unaffected control subjects North American (American and Canadian population) were recruited by four collection centers—Michigan, Toronto, Newfoundland, and the National Psoriasis Foundation.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26626624</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32725812</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NPF</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90671959</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China&apos;s National Science &amp; Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3557</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NSPT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Survey of Physical Traits Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Survey of Physical Traits Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">National Survey of Physical Traits</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10351707/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The National Survey of Physical Traits Study (NSPT) is part of the National Science &amp; Technology Basic Research Project, which contained four sub-cohorts collected from three different regions of China in different years: Taizhou, Jiangsu province in 2015 and 2019, Zhengzhou, Henan province in 2017, Nanning, Guangxi province in 2018.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90671959</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>GWASs Identify Genetic Loci Associated with Human Scalp Hair Whorl Direction.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37565938</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China&apos;s National Science &amp; Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34995520</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37459304</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40118068</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40938633</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
