        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12546"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pancreatic cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22104574+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed data from 12 case-control studies within the International Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4), including 6507 pancreatic cases and 12 890 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The studies included in PanScan (PanScan II) from PanC4 are: PACIFIC Study of Group Health and Northern California Kaiser Permanente Johns Hopkins University Mayo Clinic SPORE in Pancreatic Cancer MD Anderson Cancer Center Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center University of California San Francisco University of Toronto Yale University</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000648.v1.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The studies were drawn from the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control consortium and include case-control studies from the United States, Europe and Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3387822</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eight studies [7–14] (including the unpublished Louisiana State University study) were conducted in North America, two in Europe [15, 16], and one in China [17], and one was the International Agency for Research on Cancer- coordinated Surveillance of Environmental Aspects Related to Cancer in Humans (SEARCH) study from Canada, Europe, and Australia [18].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3139985</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Italian multicentric study [22] included 322 cases with incident pancreatic cancer (histologically, 55%, or imaging confirmed) identified between 1991 and 2008 in the major teaching and general hospitals in the provinces of Pordenone and Greater Milan and 652 hospital controls, frequency matched to cases by sex, age and area of residence.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3139985</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Surveillance of Environmental Aspects Related to Cancer in Humans (SEARCH) study [11] was a collaborative study of the International Agency for Research on Cancer including 810 cases and 1679 controls matched by age and sex collected in the 1980s in Toronto and Montreal, Canada, Utrecht, The Netherlands, Opole, Poland and Adelaide, Australia, based upon a random sample from the population at risk.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90554823</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Analysis to Assess if Heavy Alcohol Consumption Modifies the Association between SNPs and Pancreatic Cancer Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38869494</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11928872</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data from study participants in three previously conducted genome-wide association studies of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma in European ancestry populations, the PanScan I-II studies, and the PanC4 study (Figure 1) were used in these analyses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22104574</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26098869</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26646264</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4164</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls genotyped in the PanC4 GWAS after QC (9 member studies), 2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26098869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After quality control (Online Methods, Fig. 1, Supplementary Table 2), 7,956 individuals (4,164 cases and 3,792 controls) and 654,470 SNPs with call rates greater than 98% were analyzed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3792</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls genotyped in the PanC4 GWAS after QC (9 member studies), 2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26098869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After quality control (Online Methods, Fig. 1, Supplementary Table 2), 7,956 individuals (4,164 cases and 3,792 controls) and 654,470 SNPs with call rates greater than 98% were analyzed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7956</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls genotyped in the PanC4 GWAS after QC (9 member studies), 2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26098869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After quality control (Online Methods, Fig. 1, Supplementary Table 2), 7,956 individuals (4,164 cases and 3,792 controls) and 654,470 SNPs with call rates greater than 98% were analyzed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387"/>
