    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90277419</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Vascular endothelial growth factor-D plasma levels and VEGFD genetic variants are independently associated with outcomes in patients with cardiovascular disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36869765</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36869765+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Levels of VEGF biomarkers, including bFGF, Flt-1, KDR (VEGFR2), PlGF, Tie-2, VEGF-A, VEGF-C, and VEGF-D, were measured in the PLATO ACS cohort (n = 2091, discovery cohort).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19332184</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21685437</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36869765</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18624</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients with acute coronary syndrome randomised (2008)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19717846</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this multicenter, double-blind, randomized trial, we compared ticagrelor (180-mg loading dose, 90 mg twice daily thereafter) and clopidogrel (300-to-600-mg loading dose, 75 mg daily thereafter) for the prevention of cardiovascular events in 18,624 patients admitted to the hospital with an acute coronary syndrome, with or without ST-segment elevation.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PLATO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12633"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90624455</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A UK research study sponsored by Guy&apos;s and St Thomas&apos; NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients&apos; relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">161</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLUM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pustular psoriasis: eLucidating Underlying Mechanisms</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12633">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0022205"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12633"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pustular psoriasis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2024/01/17/2024.01.17.24301406.full.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UK dataset included 288 affected individuals of European descent, who were recruited in specialist dermatology centers as part of the APRICOT clinical trial4 and its sister study PLUM.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32936291+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A UK data set including 203 patients was obtained through the Anakinra in Pustular Psoriasis, Response in a Controlled Trial (2016-2019) and its sister research study Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms (2016-2020).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90624455</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide meta-analysis of palmoplantar pustulosis implicates TH2 responses and cigarette smoking in disease pathogenesis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38815935</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2024/01/17/2024.01.17.24301406.full.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UK dataset included 288 affected individuals of European descent, who were recruited in specialist dermatology centers as part of the APRICOT clinical trial4 and its sister study PLUM.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A UK research study sponsored by Guy&apos;s and St Thomas&apos; NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients&apos; relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30036598</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32936291</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">161</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients with palmoplantar pustulosis enrolled through PLUM 2016-2020 (analysed subset only)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32936291</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The remaining 161 patients were enrolled between 2016 and 2020 through the sister research study Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms (PLUM).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
