    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12640"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90455614</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania&apos;s Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10255</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>POAAGG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>primary open-angle African American glaucoma genetics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12640">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005338"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12640"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>primary open-angle glaucoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25576993+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 2520 African Americans recruited to the POAAGG study to date, 2067 (82.0%), including 807 controls and 1260 POAG cases, met all inclusion criteria and completed the detailed clinical ocular examination.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40782885+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were recruited from ophthalmology clinics in Philadelphia between July 2010 and August 2024.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90455614</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A multi-cohort genome-wide association study in African ancestry individuals reveals risk loci for primary open-angle glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38242088</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11844349</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, the POAAGG study population consists of self-identified Blacks (African American, African descent, or African Caribbean), aged 35 years or older, recruited from the Philadelphia area.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania&apos;s Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25576993</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28705151</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40782885</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10255</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals of African descent recruited (cases, controls and glaucoma suspects), 2024</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40782885</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics (POAAGG) study recruited 10,255 individuals of African descent from the Philadelphia area, representing the largest single-city study of POAG nationwide.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>POAAGG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12647"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002163"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Turkey"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90833053</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups&apos; ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8835</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2550</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11385</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project MinE ALS Sequencing Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project MinE ALS sequencing Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project MinE ALS sequencing consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project_MinE_ALS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Project MinE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12647">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004976"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12647"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>amyotrophic lateral sclerosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6138692/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Project MinE seeks to obtain sequencing data in 15,000 ALS patients and 7,500 matched controls with the aim of identifying new loci associated to ALS risk, fine-map known and novel loci, and provide a publicly-available summary-level dataset that will enable further genetic research of this and other diseases.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002163"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00762-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_762_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The control group consisted of a previously genotyped Dutch control population from project Mine (cohort NL4, as described in van Rheenen et al.5 ).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9799999/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Samples were from the international Project MinE whole genome sequencing consortium and derived from seven countries: the USA, Ireland, Belgium, the Netherlands, Spain, Turkey, and the United Kingdom (van Rheenen et al., 2018).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90833053</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale exome analyses reveal new rare variant contributions in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41917433</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13083253/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Case cohorts included the Project MinE ALS sequencing consortium (7,614 cases; 2,605 controls)47, the NYGC ALS Consortium (2,650 cases; 342 controls), the ALS Sequencing Consortium (2,851 cases)5, two cohorts from the FALS consortium (1,277 cases; phs001585), the National Institutes of Health (NIH) Exome Sequencing of FALS Project (194 cases; phs000101), two Australian cohorts described in ref. 48 (125 cases, 18 controls) and ref. 49 (568 cases), and a Chinese motor neurone disease (MND) cohort50 (583 cases, 182 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups&apos; ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29955173</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36589292</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://projectmine.com/about/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8835</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>DNA profiles (whole genomes) collected by Project MinE: ALS cases and controls (2026)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.projectmine.com/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>DNA Profiles Collected Project MinE data 11385 Cases 8,835 Controls 2,550</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
