    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12689"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000538"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90244057</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort&apos;s 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1344</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>REHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Raine eye health study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Western Australian Pregnancy (Raine) Cohort 20 year follow up Eye Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Western Australian Pregnancy Cohort (Raine) Eye Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Western Australian Pregnancy Cohort (Raine) Study: 20-year follow-up Eye Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Raine Eye Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12689">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005328"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12689"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>eye disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23301674+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Raine Eye Health Study (REHS) was conceived to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults, and to characterize ocular biometric parameters in a young adult cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24168726+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subject groups were participants in (1) the Avon Longitudinal Study of Parents and Children (ALSPAC; UK; age 15 years; N = 4401), (2) the Singapore Cohort Study of Risk Factors for Myopia (SCORM; Singapore; age 13 years; N = 1959), (3) the Raine Eye Health Study (REHS; Australia; age 20 years; N = 1344), and (4) Israeli Defense Force Pre-recruitment Candidates (IDFC; Israel; age 16-22 years; N = 888,277).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000538"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9810640/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These 14 cohorts were: Singapore Chinese Eye Study (SCES), Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES), Singapore Indian Eye Study (SINDI), Age Related Eye Study (AREDS), Rotterdam Study I (RSI), Erasmus Rucphen Family (ERF), Raine Eye Health Study (REHS) of the Raine Study, Beaver Dam Eye Study (BDES), Estonian Genome Center for the University of Tartu (EGCUT), Finnish Twin Study on Aging (FITSA), Ogliastra, Croatia-Korcula, TwinsUK, and EPIC-Norfolk.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90244057</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Rare variant analyses across multiethnic cohorts identify novel genes for refractive error.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36596879</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9810640/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These 14 cohorts were: Singapore Chinese Eye Study (SCES), Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES), Singapore Indian Eye Study (SINDI), Age Related Eye Study (AREDS), Rotterdam Study I (RSI), Erasmus Rucphen Family (ERF), Raine Eye Health Study (REHS) of the Raine Study, Beaver Dam Eye Study (BDES), Estonian Genome Center for the University of Tartu (EGCUT), Finnish Twin Study on Aging (FITSA), Ogliastra, Croatia-Korcula, TwinsUK, and EPIC-Norfolk.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort&apos;s 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23301674</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36596879</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Raine Study Generation 2 participants given the eye assessment at the 20-year follow-up</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23301674</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1344 participants (51.3% male) were assessed over a 24-month period.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>REHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12697"/>
