        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90897930</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">196</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SIT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SITT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Silent Cerebral Infarct Transfusion Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Silent Infarct Transfusion trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Silent Cerebral Infarct Multi-Center Clinical Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12745">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0002679"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12747">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011382"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12745"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>silent cerebral infarct</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25140956+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were between 5 and 15 years of age, with no history of stroke and with one or more silent cerebral infarcts on magnetic resonance imaging and a neurologic examination showing no abnormalities corresponding to these lesions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12747"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>sickle cell anemia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25140956+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were between 5 and 15 years of age, with no history of stroke and with one or more silent cerebral infarcts on magnetic resonance imaging and a neurologic examination showing no abnormalities corresponding to these lesions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11609527/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the multicenter, single-blind clinical trial for children with sickle cell anemia, each participant was randomly allocated to receive regular blood transfusion therapy (transfusion group) or standard care (observation group) in 29 centers in the United States, Canada, France, and the United Kingdom.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90897930</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>FLT1 and other candidate fetal haemoglobin modifying loci in sickle cell disease in African ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40025045</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11873275/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohorts included: Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease (CSSCD: n = 841), Multicenter Study of Hydroxyurea (MSH: n = 178), Pulmonary Hypertension and the Hypoxic Response in Sickle Cell Disease (PUSH) study (n = 73), Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers Collaborative Data (C-data) project (n = 127), Treatment of Pulmonary Hypertension and Sickle Cell Disease with Sildenafil Treatment (Walk-PHaSST) trial (n = 181), Duke University Outcome Modifying Genes study (n = 152), and Silent Infarct Transfusion (SIT) trial (SITT: n = 488).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25140956</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39293085</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">196</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children randomised to transfusion or observation (2013)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25140956</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 196 children (mean age, 10 years) were randomly assigned to the observation or transfusion group and were followed for a median of 3 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SIT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SITT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12755"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90672046</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1128</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SKIPOGH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Swiss Kidney Project On Genes in Hypertension</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Swiss Kidney Project on Genes in Hypertension</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12755">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005044"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12755"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>hypertension</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963885/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SKIPOGH (Swiss Kidney Project on Genes in Hypertension) is a family and population-based cross-sectional study that examines the genetic determinants of BP.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41695656+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Epidemiology and risk factors of urolithiasis: insights from SKIPOGH, a population-based cohort study in Switzerland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90672046</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic determinants of zinc homeostasis and its role in cardiometabolic diseases.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41325371</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12677789/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SKIPOGH study (Swiss Kidney Project on Genes in Hypertension) is a multicenter family-based population study aiming at exploring genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure and renal function as well as other health-related cardiometabolic outcomes [29,30].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24663506</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41325371</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41695656</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1128</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants recruited at baseline in Lausanne, Geneva and Bern (2012)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41695656</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Swiss Kidney Project on Genes in Hypertension (SKIPOGH) is a multicenter cohort including 1128 participants recruited from the general population of Lausanne, Geneva and Bern (2009-12).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SKIPOGH</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid12762"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90027445</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">350</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SLOVENIA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Slovenia study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SLOVENIA study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid12762">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004979"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid12762"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>asthma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8399629/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma from the SLOVENIA study were included in the GWAS of change in lung function after ICS treatment.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90027445</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of ROBO2 as a Potential Locus Associated with Inhaled Corticosteroid Response in Childhood Asthma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34442380</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34442380+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A genome-wide association study (GWAS) of the change in lung function after 6 weeks of ICS treatment was performed in 166 asthma patients from the SLOVENIA study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28639505</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34442380</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">350</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children and young people with asthma aged 5-19 in the study, as listed in the PiCA design paper (2017)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5967359/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Slovenia Slovenia Asthma cohort Tertiary care 350 5–19 162 (46) 89.9 (14.85) 193 † † 86 Peripheral blood</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SLOVENIA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
