        <obo:IAO_0000116>abdominal aortic aneurysm</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29405273+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were identified through the United Kingdom Aneurysm Growth Study (UKAGS), a nationwide prospective cohort study of men with an AAA of less than 55 mm diagnosed through voluntary participation in screening.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UK Aneurysm Growth Study (UKAGS) is a prospective study of men attending the NHS aneurysm screening programmes in the UK at reaching age 65.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90432152</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association meta-analysis identifies risk loci for abdominal aortic aneurysm and highlights PCSK9 as a therapeutic target.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37845353</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UK Aneurysm Growth Study (UKAGS) is a prospective study of men attending the NHS aneurysm screening programmes in the UK at reaching age 65.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A UK national prospective cohort of men recruited in 2011–2019 through the NHS abdominal aortic aneurysm screening programmes of England, Wales and Scotland, which invite men in the year of their 65th birthday: men with a small aneurysm detected at screening, together with screened men without an aneurysm as controls, followed with annual postal questionnaires and, for those with an aneurysm, ultrasound surveillance scans, to study the growth of small abdominal aortic aneurysms.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29405273</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38055889</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3670</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>men with AAA included in the 2023 growth analysis (analysed subset; controls not counted), 2011-2019</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38055889</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Some 3670 participants were included in the analyses, each with one or more completed questionnaire responses and two or more post-recruitment scans, with at least one scan &gt;= 30 mm in diameter (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>UKAGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


