    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid13013"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90026612</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6170</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Multi-centre National Population Health Examination Survey</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Multicenter National Health Survey II</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Multicentre National Population Health Examination Survey</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WOBASZ</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">WOBASZ II</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid13013">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid13013"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26620680+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The epidemiologic assessment of prevalence, control and treatment of CVD risk factors, and monitoring of healthy behaviour and morbidity due to diseases like coronary artery disease, hypertension and diabetes is very important for health policy planning. The WOBASZ II is the newest Polish population based survey, performed in 2013-2014 to evaluate prevalence, control, treatment, and morbidity.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26620680+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The WOBASZ II study was planned as a cross-sectional survey of a random sample of Polish residents aged over 20 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90026612</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic investigation of fibromuscular dysplasia identifies risk loci and shared genetics with common cardiovascular diseases.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34654805</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used 298 controls from a randomly ascertained sample from the WOBASZ II (Multicentre National Population Health Examination Survey) study, a population-based Polish cohort54.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26620680</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41144382</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6170</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>persons examined in 2013-2014</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26620680</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Out of eligible persons, 6170 (2760 men and 3410 women) were examined (the response rate 45.5%).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WOBASZ</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid13020"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid13022"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>GCST90000529</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">527</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ORPS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Oxford Regional Prospective Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Oxford Regional Prospective Study of Childhood Diabetes (ORPS)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Oxford regional prospective study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GWAS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Oxford Regional Prospective Study of Childhood Diabetes</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid13020">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0012594"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid13022">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid13020"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>microalbuminuria</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10097935+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1985 and 1996, 514 children (279 male) who developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 years (91% of those eligible from a region where ascertainment of new cases is 95%) were recruited for a longitudinal study with central annual assessment of HbAlc and albumin excretion (three urine samples).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid13022"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 1 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10097935+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1985 and 1996, 514 children (279 male) who developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 years (91% of those eligible from a region where ascertainment of new cases is 95%) were recruited for a longitudinal study with central annual assessment of HbAlc and albumin excretion (three urine samples).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10773897/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Multi-center regional (Oxford regional prospective study, the United Kingdom)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90000529</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Analysis of overlapping genetic association in type 1 and type 2 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33830302</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8099827/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Oxford Regional Prospective Study of Childhood Diabetes (ORPS)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:10097935</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18349042</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">527</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children recruited at diagnosis 1986-1997</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 1986 to 1997, 91% (n=527) of eligible children were recruited at a mean age 8.8 (SD 4.0) years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437"/>
