    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-02662-2/MediaObjects/41467_2017_2662_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>It represents a collaboration of more than 30 studies from the United Kingdom, United States, Canada, Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy, and Finland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90000618</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies 143 loci associated with 25 hydroxyvitamin D concentration.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32242144</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7118120/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The largest GWAS for 25OHD to date, from the SUNLIGHT consortium8, used BMI as a covariate, hence we also generated UKB results including BMI in the model and used those for meta-analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium, formed in 2008, of cohort studies from the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy and Finland that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results for circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D concentration in people of European descent, to identify genetic determinants of vitamin D status and insufficiency.</owl:annotatedTarget>
