        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20485516</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based sample of unrelated adults from Adelaide, Australia, with measured central corneal thickness, whose members in the thinnest and thickest fifths of the distribution had equal volumes of whole blood pooled before DNA extraction and genotyped as case and control pools in a genome-wide association study of central corneal thickness.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">106</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">105</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">530</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ABP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Adelaide Blood pool</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Adelaide population-based cohort in Blood pooling design</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Adelaide Blood Pools</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2869325/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The second cohort, based on a blood pooling design [26] was collected from Adelaide, Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20485516</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common genetic variants near the Brittle Cornea Syndrome locus ZNF469 influence the blinding disease risk factor central corneal thickness.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20485516</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2869325/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The four cohorts in comparison are the combined Australian twin cohorts (AU), the UK twin cohort (UK), the Blue Mountains population-based cohort in DNA pooling design (DNA), and the Adelaide population-based cohort in Blood pooling design (BLOOD).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based sample of unrelated adults from Adelaide, Australia, with measured central corneal thickness, whose members in the thinnest and thickest fifths of the distribution had equal volumes of whole blood pooled before DNA extraction and genotyped as case and control pools in a genome-wide association study of central corneal thickness.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20485516</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001462"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">106</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>unrelated individuals in the Adelaide sample (pools drawn from its thinnest and thickest fifths), 2010</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2869325/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study consisted of 530 unrelated individuals in total, with 106 individuals in the thin CCT group (covers 20% lower tail of the underlying CCT distribution) and 105 individuals in the thick CCT group (covers 20% upper tail).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
