        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29892016</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association analyses of more than 140,000 men identify 63 new prostate cancer susceptibility loci.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29892016</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>APCB = Acquired through the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource (APCB), where cases were recruited through local urologists at the time of diagnosis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22970239</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23846169</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29703916</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29892016</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37370825</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
