        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.</owl:annotatedTarget>
