        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20567021</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20567021+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Breast Cancer in Northern Israel Study is a population-based case-control study in northern Israel of patients with breast cancer and age-, clinic-, and ethnic-group matched controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20567021</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21952991</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29324747</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37451831</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11608</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>BCINIS participants (cases and controls) in a 2018 analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5764256/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data from two large prospective population-based case-control studies, the Molecular Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer (MECC, n = 8,383) and the Breast Cancer in Northern Israel Study (BCINIS, n = 11,608), were used to better understand the nature and temporality of a possible association between cancer diagnosis and AF events before and after cancer diagnosis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BCINIS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:27346685</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">746667</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BCX</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Blood Cell Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Blood-Cell Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5005441/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Platelet Function Exomechip Two BCX cohorts, GeneSTAR and the Framingham Heart Study (FHS), measured platelet aggregation in a subset of genotyped participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27346685</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Exome Genotyping Identifies Pleiotropic Variants Associated with Red Blood Cell Traits.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27346685</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5005438/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Blood-Cell Consortium (BCX) aims to identify novel common and rare variants associated with blood-cell traits using an exome array.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27346685</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27346686</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34925446</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">746667</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the second-phase (BCX2) trans-ethnic GWAS of blood-cell traits (2020)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34925446</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>BCX2 is a consortium comprising of trans-ethnic data of blood cell traits of 746,667 individuals from five different ancestries.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
