    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:11470126</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen&apos;s University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of &apos;elite&apos; octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">500</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BELFAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BELFAST</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BELFAST study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Belfast Elderly Longitudinal Free-living Ageing STudy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Belfast Elderly Longitudinal Free-living Aging STudy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Belfast Elderly Longitudinal Free-living Aging Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Belfast Elderly Longitudinal Free-living Ageing Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4552771/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the BELFAST study, 90 year old subjects, who were ‘very good’ for their age, also called ‘elite’ and met the Senieur protocol (Lightart et al. 1984), were recruited through their General Practitioners, from the Greater Belfast area.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
