        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies 32 novel breast cancer susceptibility loci from overall and subtype-specific analyses.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32424353</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Breast Cancer in Galway Genetic Study</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of breast cancer in the West of Ireland whose cases are unselected breast cancer patients recruited from University College Hospital Galway and surrounding hospitals in the West of Ireland since 2001, and whose controls are women over 60 years of age with no personal history of any cancer and no family history of breast or ovarian cancer, identified from retirement groups in the West of Ireland in 2001–2008; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23535729</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32424353</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">988</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls from the West of Ireland genotyped in the study&apos;s 2010 paper</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19390964</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In order to clarify whether TGFBR1*6A is associated with breast cancer risk, we have genotyped this polymorphism in 988 breast cancer cases and 1,016 controls from the West of Ireland and also performed a meta-analysis of previously published data (5,150 cases and 6,344 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1016</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls from the West of Ireland genotyped in the study&apos;s 2010 paper</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19390964</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In order to clarify whether TGFBR1*6A is associated with breast cancer risk, we have genotyped this polymorphism in 988 breast cancer cases and 1,016 controls from the West of Ireland and also performed a meta-analysis of previously published data (5,150 cases and 6,344 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BIGGS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid13862"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001749"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21249187</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium&apos;s eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2191</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1434</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BIGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BiGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIMH Bipolar Disorder Genome Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bipolar Genome Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid13862">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004985"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid13862"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21249187+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The second evaluation was program performance calling rare and common CNVs in the Bipolar Genome Study (BiGS) data set (1001 bipolar cases and 1033 controls, all of European ancestry) as measured by the Affymetrix SNP 6.0 array.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21595007+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants in the US Bipolar Genome Study (BIGS) were assessed on six items of concerns in the Questionnaire on Genetic Risk (QGR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21249187</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Accuracy of CNV Detection from GWAS Data.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21249187</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21249187+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The second evaluation was program performance calling rare and common CNVs in the Bipolar Genome Study (BiGS) data set (1001 bipolar cases and 1033 controls, all of European ancestry) as measured by the Affymetrix SNP 6.0 array.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium&apos;s eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19488044</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21738484</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2191</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>European-ancestry bipolar cases and controls genotyped in the GAIN and TGen stages combined (2011)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21738484</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We present new genotype data for 1,190 cases and 401 controls and perform a genome-wide association study including additional samples for a total of 2,191 cases and 1,434 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
