        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study identifies GRK5 and RASGRP1 as type 2 diabetes loci in Chinese Hans.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22961080</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3526061/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The stage 2 samples for replication testing of 96 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) consisted of 13,517 unrelated Chinese Hans (6,570 T2D case and 6,947 nondiabetic control subjects) from the Guizhou-Bijie Type 2 Diabetes Study (GBTDS), the Beijing Type 2 Diabetes Studies (BTDS), and the Hubei Type 2 Diabetes Studies (HTDS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001549"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of unrelated Han Chinese from Beijing, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, used in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and glycaemic traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22961080</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25993007</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001549"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BTDS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000744"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21655089</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins&apos; parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3957</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BTNS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Brisbane Twin Naevus Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TWin Mole study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Brisbane Twin Nevus Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13106845/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BTNS cohort has measurements for iris nevi in addition to the skin nevi used in the nevus GWAS meta-analysis. The cohort comprises a sample of predominantly adolescent twins (age 9–23 years) and their parents from Southeastern Queensland, Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000744"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5540428/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SPHERE-34 was administered as part of three main projects that make up the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study (BLTS; also known as the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study (BATS)) [8]. The first two waves of data were collected in the clinic, following an assessment of Melanocyte Naevi (moles) around the twelfth (TWin Mole study visit 1: TW1) and fourteenth birthday of the twins (TWin Mole study visit 2: TW2)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21655089</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiple common susceptibility variants near BMP pathway loci GREM1, BMP4, and BMP2 explain part of the missing heritability of colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21655089</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3107194/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 2,353 controls were derived from Queensland or Melbourne: for the former, the controls came from the Brisbane Twin Nevus Study [16]; for the latter, individuals were participants in the Genes in Myopia study [17].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins&apos; parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24949998</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28764680</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40576277</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41807453</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3957</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>12-year-old twins and nearest-age siblings examined 1992-2016</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40576277+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among 3957 participants (158 per year), we saw an approximate halving of naevus counts over the 25-year period, and examined multiple explanations for this trend.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BTNS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551">
