        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CAGE-Fukuoka</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000027"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24647736</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based prospective cohort at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine in Tokyo, Japan, whose participants, drawn from the hospital&apos;s clinical practice and annual medical check-ups, are enrolled for detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus to investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CAGE-NCGM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCGM Hospital-based Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Center for Global health and Medicine hospital-based cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hospital-based Cohort Study at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4673465/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subjects in the Tokyo district were selected from participants in the Hospital-based Cohort Study at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine (NCGM), Tokyo, to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility for lifestyle-related diseases.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24647736</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiple nonglycemic genomic loci are newly associated with blood level of glycated hemoglobin in East Asians.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24647736</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>National Center for Global health and Medicine hospital-based cohort study (CAGE-NCGM) aims to prospectively investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based prospective cohort at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine in Tokyo, Japan, whose participants, drawn from the hospital&apos;s clinical practice and annual medical check-ups, are enrolled for detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus to investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24647736</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26648100</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CAGE-NCGM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14090"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20614474</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1460</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CAIFOS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Calcium Intake Fracture Outcome study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Calcium intake fracture outcome study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LSAW</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Longitudinal Study of Aging in Women</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PLSAW</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Perth Longitudinal Study of Aging Women</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Calcium Intake Fracture Outcome Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14090">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14090"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>fracture</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240159/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 1998, the Calcium Intake Fracture Outcome Study (CAIFOS) began, which was a randomized controlled trial aimed at preventing fractures in women by providing them with daily calcium supplements for 5 yr.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12673806/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Ambulant, community-dwelling women aged ≥70 years were recruited from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, a citizenship requirement that covers &gt;98% of this age group.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20614474</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Calcium supplementation and the risks of atherosclerotic vascular disease in older women: results of a 5-year RCT and a 4.5-year follow-up.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20614474</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20614474+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study used data from a published 5-year randomized, double-blinded, placebo-controlled trial [Calcium Intake Fracture Outcome Study (CAIFOS)].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38477757</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41346785</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1460</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women randomised to calcium or placebo in 1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20614474+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The participants were 1460 women aged 75.1 ± 2.7 years at baseline (1998) recruited from the general population and randomized to receive 1200 mg of calcium carbonate daily or an identical placebo.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CAIFOS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LSAW</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PLSAW</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25279460</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">647</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CALEX family study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CALEX-FAM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Calex family study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Calex-family</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Calex-family study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CALEX-family study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4184839/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, 235 Finnish young women (mean age 18.3 yrs, range 16.1–21.4 yrs) participated in the laboratory tests in the year 2007–8.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25279460</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The associations of serum serotonin with bone traits are age- and gender-specific.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25279460</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4184839/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subjects were part of the CALEX-family study and comprised 235 young women, 121 premenopausal women, 124 postmenopausal women, and 168 men.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19171028</obo:IAO_0000119>
