    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14113"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000864"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20700438</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A lung cancer case–control study of ethnic Han Chinese, carried out from 1997 to 2008, in which cases were recruited from Beijing and surrounding provinces at the Cancer Hospital of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences in Beijing, China, and cancer-free controls from the same region and period were drawn from a community nutritional survey, to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer; its never-smoking women take part in the genome-wide association studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">642</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">334</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CAMSCH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14113">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008903"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14113"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2916850/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Replication of the strongest signal, rs2736100 was performed in the remaining subjects of the GELAC study [13] as well as six studies of never-smoking Asian women with lung adenocarcinoma in East Asia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20700438</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The 5p15.33 locus is associated with risk of lung adenocarcinoma in never-smoking females in Asia.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20700438</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2916850/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The additional replication studies included the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital study (CAMSCH) [16], Wuhan lung cancer study (WHLCS) [17], Seoul National University study (SNU) [18], Korea University Medical Center study (KUMC) [19], Kyungpook National University Hospital study (KNUH) [20] and Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Cohort Study (SWHS) [21], [22] (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A lung cancer case–control study of ethnic Han Chinese, carried out from 1997 to 2008, in which cases were recruited from Beijing and surrounding provinces at the Cancer Hospital of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences in Beijing, China, and cancer-free controls from the same region and period were drawn from a community nutritional survey, to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer; its never-smoking women take part in the genome-wide association studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20700438</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23143601</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
