    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14177"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>coronary heart disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4608367/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CARE was a secondary-prevention trial that investigated the clinical benefit of pravastatin 40 mg daily versus placebo in individuals with prior MI who had total cholesterol ≤240 mg/dL and LDL cholesterol between 115 and 174 mg/dL.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14179"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>myocardial infarction</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4608367/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CARE was a secondary-prevention trial that investigated the clinical benefit of pravastatin 40 mg daily versus placebo in individuals with prior MI who had total cholesterol ≤240 mg/dL and LDL cholesterol between 115 and 174 mg/dL.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9841599+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>80 hospitals and affiliates in the United States and Canada.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25748612</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic risk, coronary heart disease events, and the clinical benefit of statin therapy: an analysis of primary and secondary prevention trials.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25748612</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4608367/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CARE was a secondary-prevention trial that investigated the clinical benefit of pravastatin 40 mg daily versus placebo in individuals with prior MI who had total cholesterol ≤240 mg/dL and LDL cholesterol between 115 and 174 mg/dL.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16714328</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:1746424</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:7572695</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8801446</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9841599</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4159</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients randomised (3583 men, 576 women)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:8801446</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a double-blind trial lasting five years we administered either 40 mg of pravastatin per day or placebo to 4159 patients (3583 men and 576 women) with myocardial infarction who had plasma total cholesterol levels below 240 mg per deciliter (mean, 209) and low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol levels of 115 to 174 mg per deciliter (mean, 139).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARE_b</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14187"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22792082</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CARE also denotes Los Angeles component of The Womens Contraceptive and Reproductive Experiences Study (COHO:0000110), Canadian Airways Research Group (COHO:0000229), Cholesterol and Recurrent Events (COHO:0001569) and Candidate Gene Association Resource (COHO:0001586); this term is Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARE Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARE_c</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Asthma Research and Education</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Asthma Research and Education network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Childhood Asthma Research and Education program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14187">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004979"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14187"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>asthma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15157730+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In order to promote innovative research in asthma therapies, the National Heart, Lung and Blood Institute created the Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network in 1999.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742212/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CARE Network was next developed in 1999 and consisted of five clinical centers (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and one data coordinating center (Penn State University, Hershey).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22792082</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis in asthma subjects identifies SPATS2L as a novel bronchodilator response gene.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22792082</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390407/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The primary group of subjects consisted of 1,644 non-Hispanic white asthmatics from the following drug clinical trials: Childhood Asthma Management Program (CAMP) [33], Leukotriene Modifier or Corticosteroid Salmeterol study (LOCCS) [34], Effectiveness of Low Dose Theophylline as an Add-on Treatment in Asthma trial (LODO) [35], a medication trial conducted by Sepracor, Inc. [36], [37], and subsets of clinical trials within the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network [38], and the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN) [39] participating in the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) Asthma Resource project (SHARP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15157730</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17141853</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARE Network</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARE_c</owl:annotatedTarget>
