    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14293"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Romania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Russia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22113997</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC&apos;s lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies. Participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region&apos;s high kidney cancer rates.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1097</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1476</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEERCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEERCC case-control study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European Kidney Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European RCC case-control study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European Renal Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Central and Eastern European Renal Cell Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Central and Eastern European Renal Cell Carcinoma Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14293">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005086"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14293"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>renal cell carcinoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2737618/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the CEERCC study is a hospital-based case-control study of renal cell cancer conducted between 1999 and 2003 in seven centers in four Central and Eastern European countries (Moscow, Russia; Bucharest, Romania; Lodz, Poland; and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske-Budejovice, and Brno, Czech Republic).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2600689/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This hospital-based case–control study was conducted in seven centres (Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice, and Brno (Czech Republic)).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22113997</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The chromosome 2p21 region harbors a complex genetic architecture for association with risk for renal cell carcinoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22113997</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3277315/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We genotyped 59 tagged SNPs in 2278 RCC cases and 3719 controls from two nested case–control studies [the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial and the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention (ATBC) study in Finland], a hospital-based Central and Eastern European RCC (CEERCC) case–control study and Caucasians from the United States Kidney Cancer (USKC) population-based case–control study (see Materials and Methods and Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC&apos;s lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies. Participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region&apos;s high kidney cancer rates.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19034282</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19753122</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21540858</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22113997</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1097</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>incident renal cell carcinoma cases and hospital controls (1999-2003)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19034282</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a case-control study of kidney cancer in four central European countries, with 1097 incident cases and 1476 controls, we found an increased risk for self-reported hypertension and for obesity.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1476</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>incident renal cell carcinoma cases and hospital controls (1999-2003)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19034282</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a case-control study of kidney cancer in four central European countries, with 1097 incident cases and 1476 controls, we found an increased risk for self-reported hypertension and for obesity.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CEERCC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14301"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14303"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31792337</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">352</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">646</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CEFALO study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cefalo</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">CEFALO</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14301">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0021211"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14303">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_8000054"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14301"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>brain tumour</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23652309+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CEFALO is an interview-based case-control study in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, including children and adolescents aged 7-19 years with primary intracranial brain tumours diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and matched population controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14303"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mobile phone use</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3681020/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CEFALO study is a multinational case–control study conducted in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, with the primary aim to investigate the possible association between CABT risk and mobile phone use and other relevant exposures (Aydin et al, 2011).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6889151/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CEFALO is a population-based case-control study of brain tumors in children and adolescents aged 7–19 years conducted in Sweden, Denmark, Norway, and Switzerland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31792337</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Weighted Genetic Risk Score of Adult Glioma Susceptibility Loci Associated with Pediatric Brain Tumor Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31792337</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31792337+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GRS was calculated in CEFALO, a population-based case-control study of brain tumors in children and adolescents including saliva DNA of 245 cases and 489 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21795665</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23652309</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26014354</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31792337</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">352</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls interviewed (2004-2008)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21795665</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted interviews, in person, with 352 case patients (participation rate: 83%) and 646 control subjects (participation rate: 71%) and their parents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">646</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases and controls interviewed (2004-2008)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21795665</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted interviews, in person, with 352 case patients (participation rate: 83%) and 646 control subjects (participation rate: 71%) and their parents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14310"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32820175</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11502</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Color Genomics participants</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Color genomics study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Color Genomics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14310">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0003582"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14310"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndrome</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7441381/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Second, a breast cancer case-control study consisted of 19,264 women (1920 cases and 17,344 controls) who underwent clinical grade genetic testing for hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndrome at a commercial testing laboratory (Color Genomics; Burlingame, CA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32820175</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic background modifies penetrance of monogenic variants for tier 1 genomic conditions.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32820175</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7441381/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Second, a breast cancer case-control study consisted of 19,264 women (1920 cases and 17,344 controls) who underwent clinical grade genetic testing for hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndrome at a commercial testing laboratory (Color Genomics; Burlingame, CA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31771638</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32820175</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11502</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>clinical cohort sequenced by low-coverage WGS (analysed subset)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6880438/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The clinical cohort included DNA samples from 11,502 individuals whose healthcare provider had ordered a Color multi-gene panel test (Fig. 1b).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CG</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20400780</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym CARe also denotes Los Angeles component of The Womens Contraceptive and Reproductive Experiences Study (COHO:0000110), Canadian Airways Research Group (COHO:0000229), Cholesterol and Recurrent Events (COHO:0001569) and Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network (COHO:0001570); this term is Candidate Gene Association Resource.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">41000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CARe Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Candidate Gene Association Resource Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Candidate gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Candidate-gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI CARe Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI Candidate Gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI_CARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute Candidate Gene Association Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Candidate Gene Association Resource</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition, a genome wide association study using a 1,000K SNP Chip was conducted on approximately 8,900 African American participants drawn from five CARe cohorts: ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, JHS, and MESA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3048024/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>DNA samples and phenotypic information from the nine NHLBI cohorts—ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, CHS, CSSCD, FHS, JHS, MESA, and SHHS—were sent to the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard and deposited in the CARe Phenotype Database.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were recruited from six field centers across the United States: Wake Forest University, Columbia University, Johns Hopkins University, University of Minnesota, Northwestern University and University of California - Los Angeles.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20400780</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Candidate gene association resource (CARe): design, methods, and proof of concept.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20400780</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20400780+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute&apos;s Candidate Gene Association Resource (CARe), a planned cross-cohort analysis of genetic variation in cardiovascular, pulmonary, hematologic, and sleep-related traits, comprises &gt;40,000 participants representing 4 ethnic groups in 9 community-based cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20400780</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">41000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants of the nine cohorts in the CARe genotype-phenotype database (approximate)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A database of genotype and phenotype data was created that includes records for approximately 41,000 study participants with approximately 50,000 SNPs from more than 2,000 selected candidate genes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CARe</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGARe</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NHLBI_CARe</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28530674</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">160000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CGPS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Herlev/Østerbroundersøgelsen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Copenhagen General Population Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18523221+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three studies of white individuals from Copenhagen, Denmark, were used: the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS), a 31-year prospective general population study (n = 9022; 28 heterozygotes); the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS), a cross-sectional general population study (n = 31,241; 76 heterozygotes); and the Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study (CIHDS), a case-control study (n = 16,623; 44 heterozygotes).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28530674</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Fifteen new risk loci for coronary artery disease highlight arterial-wall-specific mechanisms.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28530674</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5555387/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, the European (EUR) studies comprised 16,093 CAD cases and 16,616 controls from EPIC-CVD (a case-cohort study embedded in the pan-European EPIC prospective study), the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS), the Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study (CIHDS) and the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS) all recruited within Copenhagen, Denmark.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36214322</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36852012</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36891075</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">160000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults enrolled since 2003 (approximate, enrolment ongoing), 2023</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9960719/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Copenhagen General Population Study Adults (≥20 years) from the Copenhagen area enrolled since 2003 (~160,000)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CGPS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14330"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35195259</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study&apos;s 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11480</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>China MUCA (1998)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>China MUCA 1998</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>China MUCA-1998</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ChinaMUCA-1998</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology 1998</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14330">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14330"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10249193/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>the China Multi‐Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (China MUCA‐1998), which employed a cluster random sampling method to select 11 clusters aged 35–59 years in nine provinces</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12302729/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These cohorts together covered 15 provinces and provided a good representation of residents across a wide range of geographical areas in China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35195259</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A polygenic risk score improves risk stratification of coronary artery disease: a large-scale prospective Chinese cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35195259</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The validation cohorts were derived from three cohorts in the China-PAR project, including the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA), the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (ChinaMUCA-1998), and Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China and Chinese Family Health Study (CIMIC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study&apos;s 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32433046</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34327424</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35195259</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37305106</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588"/>
