        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Consortium of Lithium Genetics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Consortium on Lithium Genetics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>International Consortium of Lithium Genetics</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International Consortium on Lithium Genetics</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14596">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004985"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14596"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11041653/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The discovery analysis consisted of ConLi+Gen data obtained from 2,367 bipolar patients of European ancestry who had undergone lithium treatment for at least six months.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3686769/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Japanese Collaborative Group on the Genetics of Lithium Response in Bipolar Disorder (Japan)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Taiwan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3686769/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Academia Sinica, Taipei (Taiwan)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11041653/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the current study, we analyzed the genome-wide genotype and clinical data of 2367 lithium-treated bipolar patients of European ancestry collected by 22 participating sites in 13 countries, including Australia (n = 122), Austria (n = 43), Czech Republic (n = 45), France (n = 210), Germany (n = 218), Italy (n = 255), Poland (n = 97), Romania (n = 152), Spain (n = 74), Sweden (n = 304), Switzerland (n = 57), Canada (n = 353) and the USA (n = 437)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26806518</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic variants associated with response to lithium treatment in bipolar disorder: a genome-wide association study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26806518</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4814312/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we report the results of a genome-wide association study of lithium response in 2,563 patients collected by 22 participating sites from the International Consortium on Lithium Genetics (ConLiGen); the largest attempted so far.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of lithium researchers, established in 2008 on the initiative of the International Group for the Study of Lithium-Treated Patients (IGSLI) and the Unit on the Genetic Basis of Mood and Anxiety Disorders of the US National Institute of Mental Health, whose participating sites in Europe, America, Asia and Australia pool genotyped patients with bipolar disorder treated with lithium, their long-term response rated retrospectively on the Alda scale, for genome-wide studies of the genetic basis of lithium response.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20453537</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26806518</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37433967</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001619"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2563</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lithium-treated bipolar patients from 22 sites in the 2016 GWAS of lithium response</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26806518</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we report the results of a genome-wide association study of lithium response in 2,563 patients collected by 22 participating sites from the International Consortium on Lithium Genetics (ConLiGen); the largest attempted so far.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
