    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33623038</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Norwegian multipurpose collection of health data and blood samples pooled from ten regional population-based health surveys conducted in 1994–2003, among them the fourth and fifth surveys of the Tromsø Study, the second Nord-Trøndelag Health Study (HUNT II), the Hordaland Health Study, the Oslo Health Study, the Oppland and Hedmark Health Study and the Troms and Finnmark Health Study. Participants, invited through the Population Registry of Norway, answered about 50 common core questions, had standardised examinations and gave non-fasting blood samples, and consented to linkage with national health registries; the collaboration is run by the Norwegian Institute of Public Health with the universities of Bergen, Oslo, Tromsø and Trondheim.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">173236</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CONOR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COhort of NORway</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cohort Norway</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Cohort of Adults in Norway</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>General Cohort of Adults in Norway</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cohort of Norway</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://husk-en.w.uib.no/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Hordaland Health Studies are part of the national research collaboration CONOR (COhort of NORway)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Norway"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2409050/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CONOR database has several strengths: it is population based including populations from various parts of Norway, both rural and urban.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33623038</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic hazard score is associated with prostate cancer in multi-ethnic populations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33623038</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902617/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The authors wish to acknowledge the services of CONOR, the contributing research centres delivering data to CONOR, and all the study participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Norwegian multipurpose collection of health data and blood samples pooled from ten regional population-based health surveys conducted in 1994–2003, among them the fourth and fifth surveys of the Tromsø Study, the second Nord-Trøndelag Health Study (HUNT II), the Hordaland Health Study, the Oslo Health Study, the Oppland and Hedmark Health Study and the Troms and Finnmark Health Study. Participants, invited through the Population Registry of Norway, answered about 50 common core questions, had standardised examinations and gave non-fasting blood samples, and consented to linkage with national health registries; the collaboration is run by the Norwegian Institute of Public Health with the universities of Bergen, Oslo, Tromsø and Trondheim.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17984119</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001620"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">173236</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals who took part in the ten CONOR surveys 1994-2003</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17984119</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus, the total number of individuals in the CONOR cohort is 173 236.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
