    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001642 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001642">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid14795"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21256834</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A series of independent cross-sectional surveys of cardiovascular risk factors in the Czech Republic that continued the country&apos;s WHO MONICA Project surveys: random 1% samples of residents aged 25–64 years, stratified by age and sex and drawn from health insurance registers, were examined in the same districts in 1997/98, 2000/01, 2007/08 and 2016/17 by investigators in Prague (the Institute for Clinical and Experimental Medicine, and Charles University and Thomayer Hospital). DNA from its participants has also served as general-population controls in genetic studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Czech Post-MONICA Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Czech post-MONICA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Czech post-MONICA Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Czech_post-MONICA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Czech post-MONICA study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid14795">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001642"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14795"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8382653/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Czech post-MONICA (the WHO Monitoring Trends and Determinants in Cardiovascular Disease) study was a cross-sectional survey investigating the determinants of cardiovascular risk factors in a 1% random sample of the general population in nine districts of the Czech Republic, stratified by age and sex [30].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001642"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40992627+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Individuals from the Czech post-MONICA study representing the general Czech population (n=2,621) were used as controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001642"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21256834</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Plasma HDL-cholesterol and triglyceride levels in familial hypercholesterolemia: data from the MedPed CZ database and the Czech population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21256834</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21256834+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The control group were 1995 individuals of the population sample of the Czech post-MONICA study (956 males and 1039 females).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
