        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide association sample of asthma from the north of the Netherlands, assembled by the Dutch Asthma Genetics Consortium in two phases that were genotyped separately and meta-analysed: a family-based phase whose asthmatic cases came from a trio and family study, with non-asthmatic spouses or the untransmitted alleles of the trios as controls, and a case–control phase whose asthmatics came from earlier clinical and genetic studies of the investigators&apos; research institute, with controls from COPACETIC, a population-based lung cancer screening study of male smokers. Cases had a physician&apos;s diagnosis of asthma, asthma symptoms and bronchial hyperresponsiveness; controls had no asthma, COPD or significant airway obstruction.</owl:annotatedTarget>
