        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5537566/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DeCC is a case–control study that recruited individuals from three UK sites (London, Cardiff and Birmingham).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001653"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:23164817</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The protective effect of the obesity-associated rs9939609 A variant in fat mass- and obesity-associated gene on depression.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23164817</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23164817+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As variation in the intron 1 of the fat mass- and obesity-associated (FTO) gene contributes to polygenic obesity, we assessed the possibility that FTO gene may contribute to depression in a cross-sectional multi-ethnic sample of 6561 depression cases and 21,932 controls selected from the EpiDREAM, INTERHEART, DeCC (depression case-control study) and Cohorte Lausannoise (CoLaus) studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001653"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control study of recurrent major depressive disorder in the United Kingdom, funded by the Medical Research Council, that recruited unrelated patients who had had at least two episodes of major depression of at least moderate severity, diagnosed with the Schedules for Clinical Assessment in Neuropsychiatry (SCAN) interview, at three UK sites (London, Cardiff and Birmingham), together with healthy controls; it is one of the three studies making up the RADIANT depression sample.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25903154</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26526099</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28187293</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28233563</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28642257</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001653"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1420</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>recurrent depression cases and controls of the study&apos;s own 2009 case-control sample</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19181679+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report the first study investigating this gene in a large, adequately powered, clinical depression case-control sample (n = 1420 cases, 1624 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001653"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1624</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>recurrent depression cases and controls of the study&apos;s own 2009 case-control sample</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19181679+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report the first study investigating this gene in a large, adequately powered, clinical depression case-control sample (n = 1420 cases, 1624 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
