    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid14922"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>insulin resistance syndrome</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subjects were men and women aged from 30 to 64 years who participated in a 9- year follow-up study that aims to clarify the development of the insulin resistance syndrome.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28597074+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The predictive performance of the machine learning models and marker panels was evaluated using repeated nested cross-validation, and replicated in an independent French cohort of 1044 individuals including 231 participants who progressed to type 2 diabetes during a 9 year follow-up period in the DESIR (Data from an Epidemiological Study on the Insulin Resistance Syndrome) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000737</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Predicting cardiac electrical response to sodium-channel blockade and Brugada syndrome using polygenic risk scores.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31504448</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:17293876</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A genome-wide association study identifies novel risk loci for type 2 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:17293876</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The control subjects were participants in the Data from an Epidemiological Study on the Insulin Resistance syndrome (DESIR) program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A French prospective cohort of men and women aged 30 to 64 years, volunteers insured by the French social security system who attended ten of its health examination centres in west-central France, followed for nine years to clarify the development of the insulin resistance syndrome.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17293876</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5153</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>DESIR participants with baseline data</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 5,153 subjects had data available at baseline (men/women ratio: 49.6/50.4%; age: 47.2 ± 10.0y., body mass index (BMI): 24.7 ± 3.8 kg/m²).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
