        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32424353</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre prospective cohort of women under 75 with grade I–III invasive primary breast cancer, recruited 9–15 months after diagnosis from 56 hospitals in the United Kingdom, who gave clinical, dietary, lifestyle, complementary-therapy and quality-of-life data and blood and urine samples every year for five years. Run from the University of Westminster, London, and funded by the charity Against Breast Cancer, it studies how dietary phytoestrogens and other diet and lifestyle factors relate to breast cancer recurrence and survival.</obo:IAO_0000115>
