    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15077"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>late-onset Alzheimer disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4000602/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A cohort of Caribbean Hispanics with familial LOAD was recruited in a different study at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer’s Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic as part of the EFIGA study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dominican_Republic"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5373783/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Similar to NIA-LOAD, this study recruited patients from families multiply affected by LOAD, but of Caribbean Hispanic ancestry from the Dominican Republic and New York.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000054</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk scores in familial Alzheimer disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28213371</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28213371</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk scores in familial Alzheimer disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28213371</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5373783</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Estudio Familiar de Influencia Genetica en Alzheimer (EFIGA) study was employed as a replication study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family study of Caribbean Hispanics from families multiply affected by late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease, recruited at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic, with follow-up of unaffected family members, to study the genetics of familial late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24425039</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28213371</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3324</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>EFIGA family members (65% affected) included in the 2017 polygenic risk score analysis (analysed set; no size of the whole study is stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5373783/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 3,324 participants were included from the EFIGA study, 65% affected; the age distribution in the EFIGA family significantly differed between cases and controls (78.2 vs 69.8, respectively, p &lt; 0.01).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EFIGA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15085"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21270820</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1738</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1099</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Emory GeneBank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Emory GeneBank Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Emory Genebank Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15085">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005010"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15085"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>coronary artery disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079521/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Emory Genebank Study was designed to investigate the relationship between biochemical and genetic factors with CAD in subjects undergoing cardiac catheterization.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Emory Genebank Study (Atlanta, Georgia, USA): Study participants were enrolled at the Emory University Hospital, Crawford Long Hospital, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital, all in Atlanta, Georgia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21270820</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A common variant in the CDKN2B gene on chromosome 9p21 protects against coronary artery disease in Americans of African ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21270820</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079521/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SNPs that met our stringent permutation-based criteria for association with incident CAD in the discovery GeneSTAR population were genotyped for replication in a total of 990 individuals (601 cases and 389 controls) using data from the Emory Genebank Study and CATHGEN cohorts.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21239051</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21270820</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
