        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000734</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21655089</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPICOLON Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPICOLON consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPICOLON project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPICOLON study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPICOLON</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15179">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15179"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22294762+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>It recruited consecutive, unselected, population-based colorectal cancer (CRC) cases and control subjects matched by age and gender without personal or familial history of cancer all over Spain with the main goal of gaining knowledge in Lynch syndrome and familial CRC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694"/>
