        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21655089</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiple common susceptibility variants near BMP pathway loci GREM1, BMP4, and BMP2 explain part of the missing heritability of colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21655089</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3107194/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>EPICOLON [19] included 1,410 cases matched with the same number of controls collected in a prospective fashion from centres in Spain.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20638935</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22294762</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30510241</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Approximate EPICOLON phase I/II cases and controls in its own 2012 review</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22294762+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This epidemiological, prospective and multicentre study collected extensive clinical data and biological samples from ∼2000 CRC cases and 2000 controls in Phases 1 and 2 involving 25 and 14 participating hospitals, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Approximate EPICOLON phase I/II cases and controls in its own 2012 review</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22294762+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This epidemiological, prospective and multicentre study collected extensive clinical data and biological samples from ∼2000 CRC cases and 2000 controls in Phases 1 and 2 involving 25 and 14 participating hospitals, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15187"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22956598</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6791</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPIFUND</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPIFUND study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPIdemiological study of FUNctional Disorders</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EpiFunD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epifund</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>epidemiology of functional disorders</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Epidemiology of Functional Disorders</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15187">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0012531"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15187"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pain</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.3899/jrheum.080541</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a 4-year prospective population-based study of pain in the North-West of England known as the Epidemiology of Functional Disorders (Epifund) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3691951/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The studies are from the UK (the British 1958 Birth Cohort (1958BC),23 36–38 the Chingford Study (CHINGFORD),39 40 the Dyne Steel DNA Bank for Aging and Cognition (DSDBAC),41 the EPIdemiological study of FUNctional Disorders (EPIFUND),20 and the Hertfordshire Cohort Study (HCS)42);</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22956598</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study meta-analysis of chronic widespread pain: evidence for involvement of the 5p15.2 region.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22956598</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3691951/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The stage 2b studies (CHINGFORD, EPIFUND and HCS) performed de novo genotyping, using both Sequenom iPLEX and TaqMan-based assays (supplementary methods).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19059720</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19369469</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19723618</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20400346</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6791</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults aged 25-65 who took part in the baseline postal survey (2001)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.3899/jrheum.080541</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 6791 baseline participants, 3985 and 2761 completed first and second followup surveys, respectively, as shown in Figure 1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EPIFUND</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EpiFunD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
