    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15206"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000558"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000617"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000217</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38965493</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">25444</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPIHEALTH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EpiHealth cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EpiHealth study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology for Health</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epidemiology for Health cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Epihealth</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EpiHealth</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15206">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000015"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15206"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifestyle factors</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In contrast, the study will well serve the postulated main aim, to investigate gene–lifestyle interactions in the causation of common diseases in the middle-aged and elderly, since this only requires sufficiently large ranges in the distributions of lifestyle factors and genetic variants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11225376/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For this purpose, we used data from the Swedish cohort study EpiHealth (www.epihealth.se) [32], a large population study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000217</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genomic and drug target evaluation of 90 cardiovascular proteins in 30,931 individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33067605</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38965493</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Bioelectrical impedance and lung function-associations with gender and central obesity: results of the EpiHealth study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38965493</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11225376/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study started in 2011 and included a questionnaire and a visit to a test centre located in Malmö or Uppsala, with the aim of studying the connections between lifestyle factors and genetic predisposition contributing to the development of the most common diseases, such as cardiovascular and respiratory [32].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23435790</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38965493</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
