    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15224"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15226"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15228"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS002291</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35414057</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1845</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2275</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPI-NPC-2005</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPI-NPC-2005 project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>EPI-NPC-2005 sample</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">EPI-NPC-2005 study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15224">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0015459"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15226">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_3000273"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15228">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ExO_0000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15224"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>nasopharyngeal carcinoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6712476/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, NPC patients were recruited from Sun Yat‐sun University Cancer Center (SYSUCC), Guangzhou, China, according to the following criteria: (a) pathologically confirmed NPC; (b) under 80 years of age; (c) residence in Guangdong Province for at least 5 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15226"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>EBV</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6712476/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The present hospital‐based case‐only study was conducted on the basis of a case‐control study named as EPI‐NPC‐2005 project conducted during October 2005 and October 2007, which was designed to assess the interaction between EBV, environmental factors and genetic determinants in the pathogenesis and progression of NPC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15228"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental factors</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6712476/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The present hospital‐based case‐only study was conducted on the basis of a case‐control study named as EPI‐NPC‐2005 project conducted during October 2005 and October 2007, which was designed to assess the interaction between EBV, environmental factors and genetic determinants in the pathogenesis and progression of NPC.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9005522/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the PRS construction, 4 GWAS populations were included from regions in southern China with the highest NPC incidence, including the EPI-NPC-2005 sample (1614 cases and 1819 controls)41,42, NPCGEE sample (1098 cases and 991 controls)43, SYSUNPC sample (1617 cases and 2610 controls)44,45 and Hong Kong sample (426 cases and 573 controls)46,47.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS002291</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The interaction and mediation effects between the host genetic factors and Epstein-Barr virus VCA-IgA in the risk of nasopharyngeal carcinoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37970759</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35414057</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A polygenic risk score for nasopharyngeal carcinoma shows potential for risk stratification and personalized screening.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35414057</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9005522/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the PRS construction, 4 GWAS populations were included from regions in southern China with the highest NPC incidence, including the EPI-NPC-2005 sample (1614 cases and 1819 controls)41,42, NPCGEE sample (1098 cases and 991 controls)43, SYSUNPC sample (1617 cases and 2610 controls)44,45 and Hong Kong sample (426 cases and 573 controls)46,47.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20727127</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29905022</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31241250</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35414057</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1845</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>nasopharyngeal carcinoma patients and physical-examination-centre controls who completed the study interview, October 2005 to October 2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6051183/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1948 patients were included and 1845 patients (94.7%) completed the interviews.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2275</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>nasopharyngeal carcinoma patients and physical-examination-centre controls who completed the study interview, October 2005 to October 2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6051183/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the same period, 2381 eligible controls were identified and 2275 (95.5%) interviews were finished.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>EPI-NPC-2005</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
