    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15273"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lymphoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080942/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ESCALE study is a national study conducted in 2003 and 2004 in mainland France (11 million children &lt; 15 years of age) to investigate the role of infectious, environmental, and genetic factors in four childhood neoplastic diseases (acute leukemia, lymphoma, neuroblastoma, and brain tumor) (Brosselin et al. 2009; Rudant et al. 2007, 2008, 2010).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
