        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of family-based genetic studies of isolated European populations, funded as a European Union Sixth Framework Programme project, whose samples (the Erasmus Rucphen Family study in the Netherlands, MICROS in South Tyrol, Italy, the Northern Swedish Population Health Study, the Orkney Complex Disease Study in Scotland and the Vis study in Croatia) were genotyped on a common platform and analysed together in genome-wide association studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
