        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2675</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>surviving Framingham Heart Study original-cohort members, aged 52-85, given eye examinations in 1973-1975</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:879158</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>During the period 1973--1975, 2675 out of 3977 still-living members of the Framingham, Massachusetts, study population, who have been under investigation for coronary disease risk factors since 1948 and who were in 1973--1975 aged 52 to 85, were given an eye examination stressing cataract, diabetic retinopathy, macular degeneration and glaucoma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
