    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15460"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000070"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38671483</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym FTC also denotes Finnish Twin Cohort Study (COHO:0000070) and NCI Familial Testicular Cancer Study (COHO:0000825); this term is Older Finnish Twin Cohort.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31145</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FTC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FinnTwinOld</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Older Twin Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Older Finnish Twin Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>older Finnish Twin Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>older Finnish Twin Cohort Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>older Finnish Twin Cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Older Finnish Twin Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15460">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000013"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15460"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>smoking</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.54</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Since its establishment, the FTC has been hosted by the University of Helsinki and the primary goal in the 1970s and early 1980s was to study twin-pairs discordant for smoking, as the causal evidence for smoking in major diseases was still lacking.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11046842/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The participants of this study were from the older Finnish Twin Cohort study, which is a longitudinal population-based study of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958 (N=13,888) [24, 25].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38671483</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Longitudinal leisure-time physical activity profiles throughout adulthood and related characteristics: a 36-year follow-up study of the older Finnish Twin Cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38671483</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11046842/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We included 2,778 females and 1,938 males from the population-based older Finnish Twin Cohort Study, who responded to health and behavior surveys at the mean ages of 24, 30, 40 and 60.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12537859</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23298696</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31462340</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38671483</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">31145</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals who replied to the 1975 baseline questionnaire (including 1,175 who said they were not biological twins)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2025.10025</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 36,922 individuals were invited in 1975, of which 31,145 replied (response rate of 84.6%).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FTC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FinnTwinOld</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


