    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15646"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21305692</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIN bipolar sample</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIN-BP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Association Information Network BD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Association Information Network Bipolar Sample</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIMH Bipolar Disorder Genetic Association Information Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIMH Genetic Association Information Network bipolar disorder project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Bipolar Disorder Genetic Association Information Network</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15646">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004985"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15646"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19488044+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify bipolar disorder (BD) genetic susceptibility factors, we conducted two genome-wide association (GWA) studies: one involving a sample of individuals of European ancestry (EA; n=1001 cases; n=1033 controls), and one involving a sample of individuals of African ancestry (AA; n=345 cases; n=670 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3178836/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Controls for both the GAIN-BP and BiGS samples were ascertained throughout the United States and genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array as part of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia II (MGS2) Collaboration (Sanders et al., 2008).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3035981/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The initial BiGS GWA study was funded through the Foundation for the National Institutes of Health Genetic Information Association Network (GAIN) initiative (http://www.genome.gov/19518664) and we report the results of this GWA study here.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21305692</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis of age at onset and psychotic symptoms in bipolar disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21305692</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21305692+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We combined data from three GWAS: NIMH Bipolar Disorder Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN-BP), NIMH Bipolar Disorder Genome Study (BiGS), and a German sample.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19488044</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21305692</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GAIN-BP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15653"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001749"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24081561</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1862</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1857</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIN-MDD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GAIN-MDD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Association Information Network-MDD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Association Information Network-MDD Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Major Depression Stage 1 Genomewide Association in Population-Based Samples Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Major Depression: Stage 1 Genomewide Association in Population-Based Samples</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
