        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0002009"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15653"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>major depressive disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/5201979</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Within these studies, 1862 participants with a diagnosis of MDD and 1857 controls at low liability for MDD have been selected for genome-wide genotyping by the US Foundation for the National Institutes of Health Genetic Association Information Network.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/5201979</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this paper, we briefly review linkage studies of MDD and then describe the large-scale nationwide biological sample collection in Dutch twin families from the Netherlands Twin Register (NTR) and in participants in the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety (NESDA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24081561</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic risk score analysis indicates migraine with and without comorbid depression are genetically different disorders.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24081561</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3947136/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The analyses in this paper are based on 2966 unrelated individuals from the GAIN-MDD study (Boomsma et al. 2008; Sullivan et al. 2008) with data on both migraine and MDD, who were genotyped on the Affymetrix Perlegen 5.0 platform.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18197199</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19065144</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
