        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31033776</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Determining population stratification and subgroup effects in association studies of rare genetic variants for nicotine dependence.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31033776</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6636808/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To evaluate the validity of the extended methods, we analyzed the Genetic Architecture of Smoking and Smoking Cessation database, which includes African Americans and European Americans genotyped on Illumina Human Omni2.5, and we compared the results with those obtained with the sequence kernel association test (SKAT) and its modification, SKAT-O that included population stratification and subgroup effect as covariates.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
