    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15696"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38062264</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nation-wide cohort of adults living with bipolar disorder in Australia, run by QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute, recruited from 2018 in three waves (a nation-wide media campaign, a Services Australia mail-out to people dispensed lithium carbonate, and a follow-up survey of the Australian Genetics of Depression Study) who completed an online survey and were asked for a saliva sample for genotyping and consent to linkage of their Pharmaceutical and Medicare Benefits Schedule records, to study the relationships between genetic risk, symptom severity, treatment response, medication side effects and health care usage in bipolar disorder.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6682</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Genetics of Bipolar Disorder</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Australian Genetics of Bipolar Disorder study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GBP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GBP Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Australian Genetics of Bipolar Disorder Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15696">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004985"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15696"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10619176/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To address these questions, we established a nation-wide cohort of 6682 adults living with BD in Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10619176/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To address these questions, we established a nation-wide cohort of 6682 adults living with BD in Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38062264</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multi-ancestry study of the genetics of problematic alcohol use in over 1 million individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38062264</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10719093/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>for example, the QIMR Berghofer Australian Genetics of Depression Study (AGDS) cohort has high major depression comorbidity, and the Australian Genetics of Bipolar Disorder Study (GBP) cohort has high bipolar disorder comorbidity.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nation-wide cohort of adults living with bipolar disorder in Australia, run by QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute, recruited from 2018 in three waves (a nation-wide media campaign, a Services Australia mail-out to people dispensed lithium carbonate, and a follow-up survey of the Australian Genetics of Depression Study) who completed an online survey and were asked for a saliva sample for genotyping and consent to linkage of their Pharmaceutical and Medicare Benefits Schedule records, to study the relationships between genetic risk, symptom severity, treatment response, medication side effects and health care usage in bipolar disorder.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37655588</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001757"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6682</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults living with bipolar disorder recruited in three waves and completing the survey (2021)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37655588</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 6682 participants (68.3% female; aged 44.8 ± 13.6 years [range = 18–90]) were recruited in three waves: a nation-wide media campaign, a mail-out based on prescriptions for lithium carbonate and through the Australian Genetics of Depression Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
