    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15830"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15832"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Turkey"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19165155</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GEMS also denotes Genes and Environment in Multiple Sclerosis (COHO:0000909); this term is Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1025</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1008</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GEMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GEMS Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15830">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003119"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15832">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011565"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15830"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>atherogenic dyslipidemia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eligible families consisted of a minimum of two siblings (an affected sib-pair) with atherogenic dyslipidemia (ADL), which was defined by the simultaneous presence of high triglyceride (≥75% percentile for age, sex, and country) and low HDL-cholesterol (HDL-C) (≤25% percentile for age, sex, and country) levels in plasma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15832"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>metabolic syndrome</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eligible families consisted of a minimum of two siblings (an affected sib-pair) with atherogenic dyslipidemia (ADL), which was defined by the simultaneous presence of high triglyceride (≥75% percentile for age, sex, and country) and low HDL-cholesterol (HDL-C) (≤25% percentile for age, sex, and country) levels in plasma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Families were recruited into the GEMS Study from six study sites, located in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland, and the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19165155</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide linkage and association analyses to identify genes influencing adiponectin levels: the GEMS Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19165155</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19165155+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify genes influencing variation in plasma adiponectin levels, we performed genome-wide linkage and association scans of adiponectin in two cohorts of subjects recruited in the Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15642551</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19165155</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25164947</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1025</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of the association arm; the family (linkage) arm phenotyped 3,069 subjects from 450 families, and no source states a total for the study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19165155</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
