        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004896</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31537649</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cross-sectional multicentre study of people with insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes and proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and so exposed to the risk of diabetic nephropathy, conducted from May 1994 to April 1995 in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium, in which participants were classified by the severity of their renal involvement, to study the genetic determinants of diabetic nephropathy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">494</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENEDIAB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GENEDIAB Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GEnétique de la NEphropathie DIABétique</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Diabetic Nephropathy</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetique de la Nephropathie Diabetique</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Génétique de la Néphropathie Diabétique</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15864">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001660"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15866">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005016"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15868">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005147"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15864"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>proliferative diabetic retinopathy</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9120002+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As angiotensin II increases glomerular pressure, we studied the relationship between genetic polymorphisms in the renin-angiotensin system-angiotensin I converting enzyme (ACE), angiotensinogen (AGT), and angiotensin II, subtype 1, receptor-and the renal involvement of insulin-dependent diabetic subjects with proliferative retinopathy: those exposed to the risk of nephropathy due to diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15866"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>diabetic nephropathy</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9120002+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As angiotensin II increases glomerular pressure, we studied the relationship between genetic polymorphisms in the renin-angiotensin system-angiotensin I converting enzyme (ACE), angiotensinogen (AGT), and angiotensin II, subtype 1, receptor-and the renal involvement of insulin-dependent diabetic subjects with proliferative retinopathy: those exposed to the risk of nephropathy due to diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15868"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>insulin-dependent diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9120002+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As angiotensin II increases glomerular pressure, we studied the relationship between genetic polymorphisms in the renin-angiotensin system-angiotensin I converting enzyme (ACE), angiotensinogen (AGT), and angiotensin II, subtype 1, receptor-and the renal involvement of insulin-dependent diabetic subjects with proliferative retinopathy: those exposed to the risk of nephropathy due to diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9120002+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of 494 subjects recruited in 17 centers in France and Belgium (GENEDIAB Study), 157 (32%) had no nephropathy, 104 (21%) incipient (microalbuminuria), 126 (25 %) established (proteinuria), and 107 (22%) advanced (plasma creatinine &gt; or = 150 micromol/liter or renal replacement therapy) nephropathy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004896</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Albuminuria-Related Genetic Biomarkers: Replication and Predictive Evaluation in Individuals with and without Diabetes from the UK Biobank.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37446387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31537649</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-Wide Association Study of Diabetic Kidney Disease Highlights Biology Involved in Glomerular Basement Membrane Collagen.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31537649</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>France-Belgium: The GENEDIAB (&apos;Génétique de la Néphropathie Diabétique, Genetics of Diabetic Nephropathy) and Genesis subjects were recruited in France, and in France- Belgium, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cross-sectional multicentre study of people with insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes and proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and so exposed to the risk of diabetic nephropathy, conducted from May 1994 to April 1995 in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium, in which participants were classified by the severity of their renal involvement, to study the genetic determinants of diabetic nephropathy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31537649</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9120002</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">494</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>insulin-dependent diabetic subjects with proliferative retinopathy recruited and kept in the study at 17 centres in France and Belgium (1995)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:9120002</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of 494 subjects recruited in 17 centers in France and Belgium (GENEDIAB Study), 157 (32%) had no nephropathy, 104 (21%) incipient (microalbuminuria), 126 (25 %) established (proteinuria), and 107 (22%) advanced (plasma creatinine &gt; or = 150 micromol/liter or renal replacement therapy) nephropathy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775"/>
