        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19536175</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2559</coho:numberOfParticipants>
