    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A European Community-funded research project that joined eight large twin registers (the national twin cohorts of Denmark, Finland, Italy, the Netherlands, Norway and Sweden, the UK TwinsUK cohort and an Australian twin cohort) with the multinational MORGAM population cohort, to identify genetic and lifestyle contributors to common diseases by linkage and association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:14624719</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">300000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>twins in the eight member twin cohorts (stated as a lower bound, &apos;over 300,000&apos;)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2687074/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Danish, Dutch, Finnish, Italian, Norwegian and Swedish national twin cohorts, together with St. Thomas’ twin cohort in Great Britain and an Australian twin cohort, form the basis of the GenomEUtwin project, a collection of over 300,000 twins.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


