        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:12707949</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collaborative study run at six sites in the United States with NIMH support that recruited people with recurrent DSM-IV major depressive disorder beginning before age 31 and a parent or sibling with recurrent major depression beginning before age 41, as a sample for molecular genetic studies of depression whose biological materials and clinical data are made available through the NIMH repository. Its first phase (GenRED I) recruited families with affected sibling pairs, with their parents and some unaffected siblings, for linkage studies, and its second (GenRED II) further probands for association studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1110</coho:numberOfParticipants>
