    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid15999"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000350</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22570617</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary&apos;s Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">485</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">344</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">829</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GEP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Etiologies of POAG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Etiologies of Primary-Open angle Glaucoma</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Etiology Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MEEI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary case control group</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Massachussetts Eye and Ear Infirmary</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetic Etiologies of Primary-Open angle Glaucoma Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid15999">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005338"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid15999"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>primary open-angle glaucoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GLAUGEN study contains POAG cases and controls derived from the Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma (GEP) study, the Nurses’ Health Study (NHS), and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS). The GEP is a clinical case-control study from Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary while the NHS and HPFS contain cases and controls nested within population-based cohorts at risk for POAG.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All cases and controls for both studies were residents of the continental United States and were of mainly European ancestry, which was confirmed by principal component analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000350</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of a Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Genetic Risk Score With Earlier Age at Diagnosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31436842</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22570617</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common variants at 9p21 and 8q22 are associated with increased susceptibility to optic nerve degeneration in glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22570617</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GEP is a clinic-based case-control set, and the NHS and HPFS are case-control sets nested within population-based studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary&apos;s Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22570617</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">485</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>MEEI (GEP) participants genotyped in GLAUGEN and analysed in the NEIGHBORHOOD meta-analysis (485 POAG cases, 344 controls), 2016 report</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3482/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3482_MOESM79_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All individuals had genotyping call rate &gt;99%, thus 485 POAG cases and 344 controls were analyzed at 495,160 SNPs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>MEEI (GEP) participants genotyped in GLAUGEN and analysed in the NEIGHBORHOOD meta-analysis (485 POAG cases, 344 controls), 2016 report</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3482/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3482_MOESM79_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All individuals had genotyping call rate &gt;99%, thus 485 POAG cases and 344 controls were analyzed at 495,160 SNPs.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
