        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
