        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Diagnosis of histologically confirmed, supratentorial, intracranial glioma</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16089"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental exposures</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With 4,545 cases and 4,173 controls, the GICC Study confers the opportunity to evaluate both environmental exposures and genetic variation while accounting for tumor subtype.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the GICC is an international consortium with 14 recruitment sites across five countries: Brigham and Women’s Hospital (MA, USA), Case Western Reserve University (Ohio, USA), Columbia University (NY, USA), Danish Cancer Society Research Centre (Copenhagen, Denmark), The Gertner Institute (Tel Hashomer, Israel)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Umeå University (Umeå, Sweden), University of California, San Francisco (CA, USA), University of Southern California (CA, USA) and The Institute of Cancer Research (London, United Kingdom).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000781</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Weighted Genetic Risk Score of Adult Glioma Susceptibility Loci Associated with Pediatric Brain Tumor Risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31792337</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28346443</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of glioma subtypes identifies specific differences in genetic susceptibility to glioblastoma and non-glioblastoma tumors.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28346443</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5558246/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed GWAS SNP data that passed quality control for 12,496 cases (6,191 classified as GBM and 5,819 classified as non-GBM tumors) and 18,190 controls from eight studies with individuals of European ancestry, a new GWAS of 4,572 cases and 3,286 controls performed by the Glioma International Case Control Consortium (GICC) (Supplementary Table 1), a new GWAS of 1,591 cases and 804 controls from the University of California, San Francisco (UCSF)-Mayo, and six previously reported GWAS totaling 6,405 cases and 14,100 controls (Supplementary Table 2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26656478</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30482874</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4545</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Original GICC case-control study recruited 2010–2013</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With 4,545 cases and 4,173 controls, the GICC Study confers the opportunity to evaluate both environmental exposures and genetic variation while accounting for tumor subtype.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
