        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000801</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21655089</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GEM also denotes Ginkgo Evaluation of Memory Study (COHO:0000682) and Genetic Epidemiology of Migraine Study (COHO:0001770); this term is Genes in Myopia Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1224</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GEM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GEnes in Myopia (GEM) study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GIMS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genes in Myopia study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genes in Myopia Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16112">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001384"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16112"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>myopia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16283990+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Genes in Myopia (GEM) Study aims to recruit probands with myopia and their family members to allow genetic analysis of myopia to be undertaken.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24265017+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 157 patients with KC were recruited from public and private clinics in Melbourne, Australia, and 673 individuals without KC were identified through the Genes in Myopia study from Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000801</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Colorectal cancer susceptibility variants and risk of conventional adenomas and serrated polyps: results from three cohort studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31038671</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21655089</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiple common susceptibility variants near BMP pathway loci GREM1, BMP4, and BMP2 explain part of the missing heritability of colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21655089</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3107194/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 2,353 controls were derived from Queensland or Melbourne: for the former, the controls came from the Brisbane Twin Nevus Study [16]; for the latter, individuals were participants in the Genes in Myopia study [17].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16283990</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18552384</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20576483</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1224</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>twins examined in the GEM twin study (612 pairs); the probands and relatives of the family study are not counted</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18552384+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 612 twin pairs (1224 twins) aged from 18 to 86 years were examined in the GEM twin study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GEM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
