        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses&apos; Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
