    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16157"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>glioma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3615132/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population comprised 841 glioma patients identified in 376 families (9797 individuals).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4296199/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Gliogene Consortium recruited 435 glioma families from 14 centers in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom, and Israel between 2007 and 2011 (7).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22037877</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide high-density SNP linkage search for glioma susceptibility loci: results from the Gliogene Consortium.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22037877</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3242820/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We have undertaken a genome-wide scan of 75 glioma families in the U.S. ascertained through GLIOGENE.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international family study of non-syndromic glioma run by the Gliogene Consortium (Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium) to find glioma susceptibility genes, first by genome-wide linkage analysis: between 2007 and 2011 its 14 centres in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom and Israel recruited families with at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas among first- to third-degree relatives, found by screening glioma patients in clinics, by review of medical records or through the internet, and collected questionnaires from probands and blood or saliva samples from living affected relatives.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17855690</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23290425</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25482530</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25652157</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
