    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16230"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16232"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:29380848</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5118</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GNHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16230">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_9001695"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16232">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005066"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16230"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>nutrition</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohort will provide data that will be influential in establishing the role of nutrition in metabolic diseases with multi-omics.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16232"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>metabolic diseases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2008, we launched the GNHS project, a cohort designed to provide evidence for the determinants of metabolic diseases in nutritional aspects, as well as other environmental and genetic factors, and explore possible biomarkers and mechanisms with multi-omics integration.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The population-based sample of adults in Guangzhou, China (baseline: 40–83 years old; n = 5,118) was followed up about every 3 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29380848</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Tea Consumption Is Associated with Increased Bone Strength in Middle-Aged and Elderly Chinese Women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29380848</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12876336/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The participants of this study were from the ongoing Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, a cohort study started in 2008 that was designed to assess the determinants of osteoporosis and cardiometabolic outcomes (19).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37813622</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5118</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants recruited at baseline in 2008-2015 (original GNHS and CCFH sub-cohorts)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After completing the baseline examination, a total of 5,118 participants were recruited during 2008–2015 in the GNHS project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GNHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31187567</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1911</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GOBS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Brain Structure</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Brain Structure and Function</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetics of Brain Structure and Function study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Genetics of Brain Structure and Function Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9531122/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To minimize selection bias, participants were drawn from extended pedigrees of Mexican American families recruited at random from the San Antonio, Texas community.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11702472/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were part of the genetics of brain structure and function study (GOBS) (McKay et al. 2014; Olvera et al. 2011), a subset of individuals from the San Antonio Family Heart Study (Mahaney et al. 1995; Mitchell et al. 1996) and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study (Puppala et al. 2006).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31187567</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Evidence for genetic correlation between human cerebral white matter microstructure and inflammation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31187567</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31187567+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted genetic correlation analyses of these traits using randomly ascertained extended pedigrees from the Genetics of Brain Structure and Function Study (N = 1862, 59% females, ages 18-97 years; 42 ± 15.7).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21557468</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22028680</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36204553</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1911</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals recruited into GOBS in three data-acquisition blocks over 15 years</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9531122/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, 1,911 individuals were recruited in three data acquisition blocks over the course of 15 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GOBS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16245"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
