        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in south-eastern Australia, in which women were randomly recruited from the general population in 1993–1997, with further women aged 20–29 years recruited at the 10-year follow-up, and a random age-stratified sample of men aged over 20 years was recruited from the Barwon Statistical Division through the Australian electoral roll in 2001–2006, followed with repeated assessments of bone mineral density, fractures and other musculoskeletal and general health outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
