        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
