    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16373"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>high salt diet</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18440328+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The measurements included blood pressure responses to the cold pressor stress test and to a high salt diet, triglyceride excursion in response to a high-fat challenge, and response in platelet aggregation to aspirin therapy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16375"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>high-fat challenge</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18440328+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The measurements included blood pressure responses to the cold pressor stress test and to a high salt diet, triglyceride excursion in response to a high-fat challenge, and response in platelet aggregation to aspirin therapy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16377"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18440328+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HAPI Heart Study was initiated in 2002 to measure the cardiovascular response to 4 short-term interventions affecting cardiovascular risk factors and to identify the genetic and environmental determinants of these responses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.nature.com/articles/s42003-022-03291-2</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Old Order Amish (OOA) population of Lancaster County, PA immigrated to the Colonies from Central Europe in the early 1700’s.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004864</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk score for predicting weight loss after bariatric surgery.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30185664</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:18440328</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The genetic response to short-term interventions affecting cardiovascular function: rationale and design of the Heredity and Phenotype Intervention (HAPI) Heart Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18440328</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18440328+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HAPI Heart Study was initiated in 2002 to measure the cardiovascular response to 4 short-term interventions affecting cardiovascular risk factors and to identify the genetic and environmental determinants of these responses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of relatively healthy adults, aged 20 or over and from large families, of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, initiated in 2002 to measure cardiovascular responses to four short-term interventions (a cold pressor stress test, a high-salt diet, a high-fat challenge and aspirin therapy) and to identify the genetic and environmental determinants of these responses.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18440328</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.nature.com/articles/s42003-022-03291-2</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">868</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HAPI participants remaining after refusal, ineligibility and pre-intervention withdrawal</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2443415/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Twelve eligible and consented individuals withdrew prior to completing any of the interventions, leaving a final sample size of 868 participants (Figure I).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001839"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HAPI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001840 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001840">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16385"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19198609</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction in King, Pierce and Snohomish counties, Washington, United States, whose cases were men under 50 and women under 60 with a first myocardial infarction diagnosed between 1991 and 2002, ascertained through medical record review at all acute care facilities in those counties, and whose controls, matched on age and sex and free of cardiovascular disease, were identified by random digit dialling in the same counties; it is one of the six studies of the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">505</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">559</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HARPS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Heart Attack Risk in Puget Sound</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16385">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005068"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001840"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16385"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>early-onset myocardial infarction</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>HARPS2 is a population-based case-control study of cases of early-onset MI and controls matched on age and sex.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001840"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases were ascertained through medical record review at all acute care facilities in King, Pierce, and Snohomish counties, Washington, US.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001840"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19198609</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association of early-onset myocardial infarction with single nucleotide polymorphisms and copy number variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19198609</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The six studies were: i) Italian Atherosclerosis Thrombosis and Vascular Biology (IATVB); ii) Heart Attack Risk in Puget Sound (HARPS); iii) Registre Gironi del COR (Gerona Heart Registry or REGICOR); iv) Massachusetts General Hospital Premature Coronary Artery Disease (MGH PCAD); v) FINRISK; and vi) Malmo Diet and Cancer Study (MDC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001840"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction in King, Pierce and Snohomish counties, Washington, United States, whose cases were men under 50 and women under 60 with a first myocardial infarction diagnosed between 1991 and 2002, ascertained through medical record review at all acute care facilities in those counties, and whose controls, matched on age and sex and free of cardiovascular disease, were identified by random digit dialling in the same counties; it is one of the six studies of the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19198609</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21239051</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
