        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES), set up by the Center for Genome Science of the Korea National Institute of Health, made up of community-based cohorts of adults aged 40–69 in five rural areas of South Korea (Wonju, Pyeongchang, Gangneung, Geumsan and Naju), and later counted as part of the KoGES Cardiovascular Disease Association Study (CAVAS). It served as a replication and case-control sample in Korean genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes, blood pressure, lipids and blood cell traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
