        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19700434+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A sample of 3428 adolescents (1845 girls) aged 12.5-17.49 years from 10 European cities in Austria, Belgium, France, Germany, Greece (an inland city and an island city), Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden was assessed in the Healthy Lifestyle in Europe by Nutrition in Adolescence study between 2006 and 2008.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001852"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37608495</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The body mass index increases the genetic risk scores&apos; ability to predict risk of hepatic damage in European adolescents: The HELENA study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37608495</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37608495+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 972 adolescents (51.3% females), aged 12.5-17.5 years, from the Healthy Lifestyle in Europe by Nutrition in Adolescence study were included in the analyses.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001852"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre cross-sectional study of adolescents aged 12.5 to 17.5 years in ten European cities (Stockholm, Athens, Heraklion, Rome, Zaragoza, Ghent, Lille, Dortmund, Vienna and Pecs), carried out from October 2006 to December 2007 within the European Union-funded HELENA project, which selected adolescents through randomly chosen schools by multi-stage random cluster sampling stratified by geographical location, age and socioeconomic status, and measured diet, physical activity, fitness and body composition with harmonised methods, with fasting blood samples from a randomly selected subsample, to describe the nutritional status and lifestyle of European adolescents.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17617932</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19011652</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23148760</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25609179</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
