        <owl:annotatedTarget>HerCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16507"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000558"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000758</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35995766</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">763</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HERITAGE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HERITAGE Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HEalth, RIsk factors, exercise Training And Genetics Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Health, Risk Factors, Exercise Training and Genetics Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Health, Risk Factors, Exercise Training, and Genetics Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Health, Risk Factors, Training and Genetics Family Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16507">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16507"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>aerobic exercise training</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7674877+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HERITAGE family study (HEalth, RIsk factors, exercise Training And GEnetics) will document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic, and hormonal responses to aerobic exercise training.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9395431/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>HERITAGE enrolled a combination of self-identified white and Black family units, totaling 763 sedentary participants (38% Black) between the ages of 17–65 years, in a 20-week, graded endurance exercise training study across four clinical centers in the US and Canada in 1995.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000758</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Polygenic Risk Score to Predict Future Adult Short Stature Among Children.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33788949</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35995766</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Whole Genome Association Study of the Plasma Metabolome Identifies Metabolites Linked to Cardiometabolic Disease in Black Individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35995766</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9395431/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To extend prior work, we performed a genome-wide association study integrating whole genome sequencing (WGS) of 2,291 metabolite peaks in 2466 participants from the Jackson Heart Study (JHS), a Black epidemiological cohort in Jackson, Mississippi, and validated findings in the Multi-Ethnic Study of Atherosclerosis (MESA; n = 995) and Health, Risk Factors, Exercise Training and Genetics Family Study (HERITAGE; n = 658).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35995766</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:7674877</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">763</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>sedentary white and Black family members aged 17-65 enrolled in the exercise training study (1995)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9395431/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>HERITAGE enrolled a combination of self-identified white and Black family units, totaling 763 sedentary participants (38% Black) between the ages of 17–65 years, in a 20-week, graded endurance exercise training study across four clinical centers in the US and Canada in 1995.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HERITAGE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16515"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16517"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000718</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33012170</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized controlled trial, funded by the US National Institutes of Health, that enrolled adult patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%) and NYHA class II-IV symptoms despite optimal therapy, at 82 centers in the United States, Canada and France from April 2003 to February 2007, comparing usual heart-failure care with usual care plus supervised and then home-based aerobic exercise training, and including a genetic sub-study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2331</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HF-ACTION</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Heart Failure - A Controlled Trial Investigating Outcomes of Exercise TraiNing</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Heart Failure: a Controlled Trial Investigating Outcomes of Exercise Training</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Heart Failure: A Controlled Trial Investigating Outcomes of Exercise Training</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16515">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0006993"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16517">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16515"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>heart failure and reduced ejection fraction</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2916661/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Multicenter, randomized controlled trial among 2331 medically stable outpatients with heart failure and reduced ejection fraction.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16517"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>regular structured exercise training</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2916661/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our primary hypothesis was that in patients with stable heart failure, regular structured exercise training, when added to usual, evidence-based care in accordance with published guidelines, would significantly reduce the incidence of a combined end point of all-cause mortality or all-cause hospitalization.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19351941+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants in Heart Failure: A Controlled Trial Investigating Outcomes of Exercise Training (HF-ACTION) were randomized from April 2003 through February 2007 at 82 centers within the United States, Canada, and France; median follow-up was 30 months.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000718</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic Score for β-Blocker Survival Benefit in European Ancestry Patients With Reduced Ejection Fraction Heart Failure.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33012170</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33012170</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic Score for β-Blocker Survival Benefit in European Ancestry Patients With Reduced Ejection Fraction Heart Failure.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33012170</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7738407/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three datasets were used: the Henry Ford Heart Failure Pharmacogenomic registry (HFPGR); the Trial of Intensified vs Standard Medical Therapy in Elderly Patients With Congestive Heart Failure (TIME-CHF); and Heart Failure: A Controlled Trial Investigating Outcomes of Exercise Training (HF-ACTION).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomized controlled trial, funded by the US National Institutes of Health, that enrolled adult patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%) and NYHA class II-IV symptoms despite optimal therapy, at 82 centers in the United States, Canada and France from April 2003 to February 2007, comparing usual heart-failure care with usual care plus supervised and then home-based aerobic exercise training, and including a genetic sub-study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19351941</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33012170</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2331</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HF-ACTION randomized heart-failure patients (2007)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2916661/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 2331 patients were enrolled at 82 participating centers in the United States, Canada, and France.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HF-ACTION</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002034"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24860199</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia&apos;s vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4119</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HHO</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Health Habits and Opinions study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>United States Health Habits and Opinions study (HHO) 1990</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002034"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The sample is a follow up of the 1988 MATR study above.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24860199</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Influence of Major Life Events on Economic Attitudes in a World of Gene-Environment Interplay.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24860199</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4031194/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This Health Habits and Opinions study (HHO) assessed many of the same political attitudes in the HLQ.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia&apos;s vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24569950</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24860199</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4119</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>twins aged 40-93 who took part in the follow-up survey about two years after the Health and Life Styles questionnaire (1990)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4031194/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In addition, 4,119 of the twins, comprised of 744 female MZ twin pairs, 421 female DZ twin pairs, 195 male MZ pairs, 93 male DZ pairs, and 339 female-male twin pairs, aged 40–93 (μ=64, σ=7.9), took part in a follow-up two years later.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HHO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001859 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001859">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. HIHG is the Hussman Institute for Human Genomics of the University of Miami (formerly the Miami Institute for Human Genomics). In the PGS Catalog&apos;s source paper the id labels the institute&apos;s Parkinson&apos;s disease GWAS sample, a genotyping set of unrelated cases gathered by the 13 ascertainment centres of the PD Genetics Collaboration and the Udall Parkinson Disease Center of Excellence core, with spouse and friend controls (PMID:20070850, PMC2853717). It is a GWAS sample assembled from those collections under the institute&apos;s name, not a collection with a name of its own. If a term is ever wanted, the named collection behind it would be the PD Genetics Collaboration (Scott et al. 2001) or the Udall center&apos;s collection, not HIHG. No COHO term or review name matches; the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (COHO:0001108) and the Ashkenazi Jewish Dataset (COHO:0001283) are separate datasets of the same meta-analysis. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Hussman Institute of Human Genomics</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000729"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000739"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chile"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Colombia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mexico"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Peru"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS005102</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35399580</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">59771</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HISLA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Hispanic/Latino Anthropometry Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>First, HISLA stage 1 includes 17 studies and one consortium (Consortium for the Analysis of the Diversity and Evolution of Latin America [CANDELA]17) collectively representing up to 59,771 adults, depending on the trait, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru, or the US with self-reported heritage from across Spanish-speaking Latin America, or Native American heritage, primarily Pima and Zuni25 (Table S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Given the unique patterns of admixture and ancestry represented by the Brazilian or Native American samples, we conducted sensitivity analyses in stage 1 studies (i.e., comparing the inclusion and exclusion of the Baependi Heart Study, the 1982 Pelotas Birth Cohort Study, and the Family Investigation of Nephropathy and Diabetes substudy of individuals of Pima and Zuni heritage) to assess the influence of these three studies on the meta-analysis results.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000729"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Given the unique patterns of admixture and ancestry represented by the Brazilian or Native American samples, we conducted sensitivity analyses in stage 1 studies (i.e., comparing the inclusion and exclusion of the Baependi Heart Study, the 1982 Pelotas Birth Cohort Study, and the Family Investigation of Nephropathy and Diabetes substudy of individuals of Pima and Zuni heritage) to assess the influence of these three studies on the meta-analysis results.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000739"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Given the unique patterns of admixture and ancestry represented by the Brazilian or Native American samples, we conducted sensitivity analyses in stage 1 studies (i.e., comparing the inclusion and exclusion of the Baependi Heart Study, the 1982 Pelotas Birth Cohort Study, and the Family Investigation of Nephropathy and Diabetes substudy of individuals of Pima and Zuni heritage) to assess the influence of these three studies on the meta-analysis results.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Only one family-based study in stage 1 and two non-family-based studies in stage 2 (Genetics of Latinos Diabetic Retinopathy, 0.3% &lt;18 years; and Mapping the Genes for Hypertension, Insulin Resistance, and Salt Sensitivity Study, 3.9%) included a small subset of adolescents aged 15–17 years, each less than 5% of the total sample.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>First, HISLA stage 1 includes 17 studies and one consortium (Consortium for the Analysis of the Diversity and Evolution of Latin America [CANDELA]17) collectively representing up to 59,771 adults, depending on the trait, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru, or the US with self-reported heritage from across Spanish-speaking Latin America, or Native American heritage, primarily Pima and Zuni25 (Table S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005102</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Metabolic polygenic risk scores for prediction of obesity, type 2 diabetes, and related morbidities.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41844147</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35399580</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Ancestral diversity improves discovery and fine-mapping of genetic loci for anthropometric traits-The Hispanic/Latino Anthropometry Consortium.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35399580</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Hispanic/Latino Anthropometry (HISLA) Consortium is comprised of 27 studies/consortia of adult participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35399580</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">59771</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults with BMI data in the stage 1 (discovery) meta-analysis of the 2022 HISLA GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Stage 1 included a total sample of 59,771 individuals with data on BMI, 56,161 with height, and 42,455 with WHRadjBMI.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HISLA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861">
