        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004921</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:26343387</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Finnish forensic autopsy series of men aged 35 to 69 who died out of hospital, combining consecutive autopsies in Helsinki in 1991-1992 (the Helsinki Sudden Death Study) and in Tampere in 2001-2004 (the Tampere Coronary Study), in which coronary artery disease was assessed at autopsy from coronary stenosis of 50% or more, old or acute myocardial infarction, or sudden cardiac death from plaque rupture and thrombosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">206</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">258</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>HSDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Helsinki Sudden Death Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Helsinki Sudden Death Study/Tampere Coronary Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16649">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005010"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16649"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>coronary artery disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Coronary artery disease was defined as coronary artery stenosis 50 % or greater, old or acute myocardial infarction, or sudden cardiac death caused by plaque rupture and thrombosis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Helsinki Sudden Death Study (HSDS) and Tampere Coronary Study (TCS) are a series of consecutive forensic autopsies of men aged 35-69 who died out of hospital in Helsinki between 1991 and 1992 (HSDS) or in Tampere between 2001 and 2004 (TCS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874"/>
