    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32665703</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk scores and breast and epithelial ovarian cancer risks for carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32665703</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7521995/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The BBCC included data from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study (IBCCS), Breast Cancer Family Registry (BCFR), and the Kathleen Cunningham Foundation Consortium for Research into Familial Breast Cancer (kConFab) (details in Supplementary material).2 Only women of European ancestry were included in the analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31948486</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32665703</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1593</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>IBCCS retrospective BRCA1/2-carrier sample in the 2007 oral-contraceptive analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&amp;id=17635951&amp;retmode=xml</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort study (IBCCS), a retrospective cohort of 1,593 BRCA1/2 mutation carriers was analyzed with a weighted Cox regression analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
