    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001901 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001901">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. ICO is the Institut Català d&apos;Oncologia (Catalan Institute of Oncology), a cancer centre in Catalonia, Spain. In the PGS Catalog it labels unnamed site samples: in every CIMBA paper (PMID:28448241, 32665703, 34320204 and the source GWAS PMID:28346442, 29058716) it is the ICO Hereditary Cancer Program&apos;s BRCA1/2 pathogenic-variant carriers contributed to CIMBA (COHO:0000901), and in PMID:37321833 it is the ICO&apos;s series of Lynch syndrome carriers plus Spanish controls (&apos;Patients were recruited based on the fulfilment of Bethesda or Amsterdam criteria or via an EC and CRC-based LS screening programme (since 2016 at the ICO).&apos;). Neither sample has a study name of its own. This follows the review&apos;s decisions for other institution-named CIMBA sites (MSKCC, UPENN, BRICOH, Chicago, FCCC, OUH): not a cohort. Not the HVH, PBCS, kConFab or deCODE terms the automatic matching suggested (those are other CIMBA/BCAC ids in the same tables). The ICO Breast Cancer Cohort (PMID:40282542) is a separate clinical cohort that the PGS Catalog does not record. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Institut Català d&apos;Oncologia</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16855"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Barbados"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cameroon"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Central_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jamaica"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Latin_America_and_the_Caribbean"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nigeria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saint_Lucia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Western_Africa"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41908051</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based survey of blood pressure, hypertension and associated risk factors such as obesity among adults of West African origin living in societies at different stages of social and economic development, which examined age-stratified samples at seven sites in Nigeria, Cameroon, Jamaica, St. Lucia, Barbados and metropolitan Chicago in the United States under a standardized protocol with centrally trained field staff; its Nigerian base sample, recruited in Ibadan and Igbo-Ora in Oyo State, later provided the sampling frame for genotyped cohorts.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10014</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ICSHIB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International Collaborative Study on Hypertension in Blacks</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16855">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005044"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16855"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>hypertension</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9103091+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study was undertaken to describe the distribution of blood pressures, hypertension prevalence, and associated risk factors among seven populations of West African origin.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9103091+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The rates of hypertension in West Africa (Nigeria and Cameroon), the Caribbean (Jamaica, St. Lucia, Barbados), and the United States (metropolitan Chicago, Illinois) were compared on the basis of a highly standardized collaborative protocol.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41908051</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pathway-specific polygenic risk scores for blood pressure traits in a West African cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41908051</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41908051+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All participants were recruited from the International Collaborative Study on Hypertension in Blacks.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based survey of blood pressure, hypertension and associated risk factors such as obesity among adults of West African origin living in societies at different stages of social and economic development, which examined age-stratified samples at seven sites in Nigeria, Cameroon, Jamaica, St. Lucia, Barbados and metropolitan Chicago in the United States under a standardized protocol with centrally trained field staff; its Nigerian base sample, recruited in Ibadan and Igbo-Ora in Oyo State, later provided the sampling frame for genotyped cohorts.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41908051</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8581794</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8793366</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9103091</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10014</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Adults examined at seven sites in the original ICSHIB hypertension survey</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9103091+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After researchers were given central training in survey methods, population-based samples of 800 to 2500 adults over the age of 25 were examined in seven sites, yielding a total sample of 10014.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001902"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ICSHIB</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001903 -->

