    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001917 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001917">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. INCa is the Institut national du cancer (French National Cancer Institute), France&apos;s national cancer agency, which funds, coordinates and publishes cancer data but is not itself a recruited study sample (&apos;The pilot program IMPULSION, launched by the French National Cancer Institute (INCa)...&apos;, PMID:41820119, E542.16). The PGS Catalog lists the id among its cohorts but links it to no score or sample set, so there is no paper in which it denotes a sample; nothing names an &apos;INCa&apos; cohort. Not a cohort. If the Catalog later links it to a sample, it will most likely be an INCa-funded study that should be identified by its own name. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete French National Cancer Institute</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001918 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001918">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000099"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Indiana cohort is how multi-cohort GWAS (PMID:20541252, PMID:28724990) name the Indiana University sample of premenopausal sister pairs, the Indiana Sisters Study. Replaced by COHO:0000099 (Indiana Sisters Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Indiana cohort</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16924"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid16926"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/India"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Asia"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000558"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS005204</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:40691366</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India&apos;s two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2087</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1927</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INDICO</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INdian DIabetes COnsortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Indian Diabetes Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16924">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16926">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000015"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16924"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11568-011-9157-2/MediaObjects/11568_2011_9157_MOESM1_ESM.doc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the total CURES participants, 2,087 individuals diagnosed with T2D and 1,927 non-diabetic control subjects were included as a part of this consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16926"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifestyle</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1007/s11568-011-9157-2</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This gives us an unprecedented opportunity to probe the correlation, if any, between genetic and epigenetic changes in the genome and rapid changes in lifestyle.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/India"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3238020/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus, we initiated a nation-wide collaborative effort by establishing the INdian DIabetes COnsortium (INDICO) for the systematic, comprehensive, and large-scale studies towards the understanding of T2D in India.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005204</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40691366</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:40691366</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40691366</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41591-025-03827-z/MediaObjects/41591_2025_3827_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The INDICO gratefully acknowledges the contributions of the participants and the study staff.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India&apos;s two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23205164</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2087</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>INDICO Dravidian component sampled from CURES in the biorepository profile</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11568-011-9157-2/MediaObjects/11568_2011_9157_MOESM1_ESM.doc</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the total CURES participants, 2,087 individuals diagnosed with T2D and 1,927 non-diabetic control subjects were included as a part of this consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
