        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:29273806</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1227</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>INDUSTRIAL</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Industrial Cohorts Research Group</rdfs:label>
