        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15838</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>InterASIA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid16987">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid16987"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15132212+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The overall objective of the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA) was to estimate the prevalence and distribution of cardiovascular disease risk factors, including hypertension, hypercholesterolemia, diabetes, obesity, cigarette smoking, and physical inactivity, in the general population of both China and Thailand.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Thailand"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15132212+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A multistage cluster sampling method was used to select a nationally representative sample of 15,838 adults, aged 35-74 years, in China, and 5,350 similarly aged adults in Thailand.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS002259</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Integrating polygenic and clinical risks to improve stroke risk stratification in prospective Chinese cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36881318</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35195259</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A polygenic risk score improves risk stratification of coronary artery disease: a large-scale prospective Chinese cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35195259</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The validation cohorts were derived from three cohorts in the China-PAR project, including the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA), the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (ChinaMUCA-1998), and Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China and Chinese Family Health Study (CIMIC).</rdfs:comment>
