        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
