        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28346443</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of glioma subtypes identifies specific differences in genetic susceptibility to glioblastoma and non-glioblastoma tumors.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28346443</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5558246/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, the UK GWAS was based on 636 cases (401 males; mean age 46 years) who were ascertained through the INTERPHONE study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17636416</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34648614</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6311</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>intracranial tumour cases and controls recruited (parotid cases not included)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34648614</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Interphone study recruited 6311 cases with intracerebral tumours and 7658 controls from 13 countries (Denmark, Finland, Norway, Sweden, Germany, United Kingdom, France, Italy, Israel, Japan, Canada, Australia and New Zealand).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927"/>
