    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001931 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001931">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. IPM is the Charles Bronfman Institute for Personalized Medicine at Mount Sinai, and the PGS id denotes its BioMe Biobank (the catalog&apos;s long name is the IPM BioBank GWAS), which COHO already has as COHO:0000424 BioMe Biobank (it already carries the synonyms &apos;IPM Biobank&apos; and &apos;Institute for Personalized Medicine (IPM) BioMe Biobank Project&apos;). Add the PGS id IPM as an acronym and the catalog&apos;s full name as a synonym; no other COHO term uses the acronym IPM. The placeholder COHO:0001931 is a duplicate. The CARDIoGRAMplusC4D sub-sample tags IPM-EurAmer, IPM-AfrAmer, IPM-HispAmer (and IPM_EA, IPM_AA, IPM_HA) are ancestry subsets of the same biobank; they could be added as synonyms if the curator wants every tag, but neither catalog uses them as ids. Replaced by COHO:0000424 (BioMe Biobank), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Charles R Bronfman Institute for Personalized Medicine - IPM / BioBank Genome Wide Association Study of Cardiovascular, Renal and Metabolic Phenotypes</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


