    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17097"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17099"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17101"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000791</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33910586</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">867</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">774</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1641</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ItGxE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Italian Gene-Environment Interactions in Lymphoma Etiology study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Italian GxE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Italian_GxE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Multicenter Italian study on gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology: translational aspects</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Italian Gene-Environment Interactions in Lymphoma Etiology</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17097">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005062"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17099">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0009693"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17101">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_9002138"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17097"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lymphoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used unconditional logistic regression models to assess risk of lymphoma (all subtypes), the NHL and BCL groups, HL, and the major BCL subtypes, including diffuse large B cell lymphoma (DLBCL), chronic lymphocytic leukaemia (CLL), follicular lymphoma (FL), and multiple myeloma (MM), associated with ever exposure (including all categories of confidence, intensity, frequency and duration of exposure), and with categories of confidence, duration, intensity, and frequency of exposure to glyphosate, as well as with cumulative exposure to glyphosate.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17099"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>multiple myeloma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used unconditional logistic regression models to assess risk of lymphoma (all subtypes), the NHL and BCL groups, HL, and the major BCL subtypes, including diffuse large B cell lymphoma (DLBCL), chronic lymphocytic leukaemia (CLL), follicular lymphoma (FL), and multiple myeloma (MM), associated with ever exposure (including all categories of confidence, intensity, frequency and duration of exposure), and with categories of confidence, duration, intensity, and frequency of exposure to glyphosate, as well as with cumulative exposure to glyphosate.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17101"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>occupational exposure to glyphosate</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We inquired into the association between occupational exposure to glyphosate and risk of lymphoma subtypes in a multicenter case-control study conducted in Italy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The “Gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology” (ItGxE) multicentre case-control study took place in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres, namely Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000791</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pan-cancer analysis demonstrates that integrating polygenic risk scores with modifiable risk factors improves risk prediction.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33247094</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33910586</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Occupational exposure to glyphosate and risk of lymphoma:results of an Italian multicenter case-control study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33910586</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The “Gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology” (ItGxE) multicentre case-control study took place in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres, namely Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
