    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001943 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001943">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001013"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog records no score or paper for this id (its REST record is empty); the name is copied from Todd et al. 2007 (PMID:17554260). The PGS Catalog name is the source of the id: Todd et al. 2007 calls the case sample &apos;the JDRF/WT Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory&apos;s JDRF/WT British case collection (Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes)&apos;, so the JDRF/WT British case collection is GRID, already in COHO as COHO:0001013 (whose definition already says it was assembled by the JDRF/WT Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory). Add JDRF/WT as an acronym and the collection names as synonyms, and obsolete the placeholder COHO:0001943 in favour of COHO:0001013. Replaced by COHO:0001013 (Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Juvenile Diabetes Research Foundation/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratorys British case collection</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17128"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:23565137</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer&apos;s Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer&apos;s disease in the Japanese population.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1656</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1656</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3312</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>JGSCAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Japanese Genetic Consortium for Alzheimer Disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for AD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Japanese Genetic Study Consortium of Alzheimer’s Disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer&apos;s Disease</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17128">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17128"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2986257/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Blood samples were collected by the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for AD (JGSCAD): the members are listed in our recent publications.10, 11 The LOAD patients were clinically validated, and satisfied the criteria of the National Institute of Neurological and Communicative Disorders and Stroke-Alzheimer&apos;s Disease and Related Disorders Association for a diagnosis of probable AD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:23565137</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>SORL1 is genetically associated with late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease in Japanese, Koreans and Caucasians.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23565137</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23565137+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To discover susceptibility genes of late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease (LOAD), we conducted a 3-stage genome-wide association study (GWAS) using three populations: Japanese from the Japanese Genetic Consortium for Alzheimer Disease (JGSCAD), Koreans, and Caucasians from the Alzheimer Disease Genetic Consortium (ADGC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer&apos;s Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer&apos;s disease in the Japanese population.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18854865</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23565137</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39428694</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1656</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>LOAD patients and controls collected by JGSCAD and genotyped in the 2009 GAB2 study (one paper&apos;s sample)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18854865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The total sample size is 1656 LOAD patients (female, 71.6%) and 1656 controls (female, 58.7%), which is large enough to detect risk alleles assuming OR&gt;1.3 (range of risk allele frequency=0.1–0.9, α=0.05, power=80%).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1656</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>LOAD patients and controls collected by JGSCAD and genotyped in the 2009 GAB2 study (one paper&apos;s sample)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18854865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The total sample size is 1656 LOAD patients (female, 71.6%) and 1656 controls (female, 58.7%), which is large enough to detect risk alleles assuming OR&gt;1.3 (range of risk allele frequency=0.1–0.9, α=0.05, power=80%).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3312</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>LOAD patients and controls collected by JGSCAD and genotyped in the 2009 GAB2 study (one paper&apos;s sample)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18854865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To determine whether the GAB2 association can be replicated in Japanese or not, we analyzed the 10 SNPs using a total of 3312 clinical subjects for genotyping (see Supplementary Figure 2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>JGSCAD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


