    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33627073</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1026</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KAWP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kawasaki Aging and Wellbeing Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This cross-sectional study used data from the Kawasaki Aging and Wellbeing Project (KAWP) conducted in Kawasaki city (Kanagawa Prefecture, Japan)(21).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33627073</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Behavioral changes and hygiene practices of older adults in Japan during the first wave of COVID-19 emergency.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33627073</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33627073+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A cross-sectional telephonic survey was conducted with the participants of the Kawasaki Aging and Wellbeing Project (KAWP), an on-going longitudinal cohort study of older adults aged 85 or older.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1026</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>community-dwelling adults aged 85-89 enrolled at baseline (2017-2018)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between March 2017 and December 2018, a total of 1026 independent seniors were enrolled in the KAWP and a comprehensive baseline assessment, including assessment of physical, mental, and cognitive function as well as social participation was conducted (Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KAWP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001957 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001957">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: KBA is strictly the name of a genotyping array and project; the sample it denotes is KoGES participants genotyped on it, not a separately recruited cohort. In PMID:32499647 KBA and KARE (Ansan and Ansung Study, COHO:0000530, a KoGES cohort genotyped earlier on another array) appear as separate study groups, so &apos;KBA&apos; there is the KBA-genotyped part of KoGES; KoGES (COHO:0000411) is still the term it belongs to. If the curator prefers not to attach an array&apos;s name to a cohort, the alternative verdict is &apos;not a cohort&apos; (a genotyping project on KoGES samples). The PGS name is a garbled fragment of the sentence &apos;The Korea National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array (KBA) project in 2014&apos; (PMID:36333282). The KBA is the Korean genotyping array used on the KoGES cohorts&apos; samples held at the National Biobank of Korea, and PMID:40778152 calls the sample &apos;Korean Biobank Array from the Korean Genome and Epidemiology (KoGES) Consortium (KBA)&apos;. So the id denotes KoGES participants genotyped on the KBA: the existing aggregation KoGES (COHO:0000411). Add KBA as an acronym and the array/project names (including the catalog&apos;s name) as synonyms; obsolete placeholder COHO:0001957 in favour of COHO:0000411. Replaced by COHO:0000411 (Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array project</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17213"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17215"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33436035</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer&apos;s disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer&apos;s disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KBASE-V</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of AD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Validation Cohort of Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of AD</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17213">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0002039"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17215">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17213"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mild cognitive impairment</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We recruited 71 cognitively normal (CN) participants, 96 with subjective cognitive decline (SCD), 72 with mild cognitive impairment (MCI), and 56 with AD dementia (ADD).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17215"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>AD dementia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We recruited 71 cognitively normal (CN) participants, 96 with subjective cognitive decline (SCD), 72 with mild cognitive impairment (MCI), and 56 with AD dementia (ADD).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We have recruited 71 CN participants, 96 SCD, 72 MCI, and 56 ADD in nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33436035</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Alzheimer&apos;s cerebrospinal biomarkers from Lumipulse fully automated immunoassay: concordance with amyloid-beta PET and manual immunoassay in Koreans : CSF AD biomarkers measured by Lumipulse in Koreans.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33436035</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Herein, we analyzed CSF samples from a validation cohort in the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer’s Disease (KBASE-V study) using a fully automated immunoassay Lumipulse G and two manual immunoassay platforms: xMAP-Luminex INNOBIA-AlzBio3 multiplex assay (Luminex) and ELISA with INNOTEST kit (INNOTEST) for Aβ42, Aβ40 (only for INNOTEST and Lumipulse G), t-tau, or p-tau.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer&apos;s disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer&apos;s disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
