        <rdfs:comment>Our study was set in Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30033078</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Human candidate gene polymorphisms and risk of severe malaria in children in Kilifi, Kenya: a case-control association study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30033078</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We did a case-control study in Kilifi County, Kenya.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network&apos;s multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN&apos;s candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23717212</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25261933</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26686045</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30033078</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31844061</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2244</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>severe malaria cases and community infant controls (1995-2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between June 11, 1995, and June 12, 2008, 2244 children with severe malaria were recruited to the study, and 3949 infants were included as controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3949</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>severe malaria cases and community infant controls (1995-2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between June 11, 1995, and June 12, 2008, 2244 children with severe malaria were recruited to the study, and 3949 infants were included as controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6193</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>severe malaria cases and community infant controls (1995-2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We report the results of a large case-control study (n=6193) of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria, undertaken in a carefully phenotyped population.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KEMRI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17256"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saudi_Arabia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS005331</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41844147</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6416</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KFSH&amp;RC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KFSH&amp;RC cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17256">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005267"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17256"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiac disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC13092120</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center (KFSH&amp;RC) cohort consists of indigenous Arabs from Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care at KFSH&amp;RC, a tertiary care hospital recognized throughout Saudi Arabia and the Middle East, for work-up of cardiac disease from all over the country.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saudi_Arabia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC13092120</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center cohort: The King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center (KFSH&amp;RC) cohort consists of indigenous Arabs from Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care at KFSH&amp;RC, a tertiary care hospital recognized throughout Saudi Arabia and the Middle East, for work-up of cardiac disease from all over the country.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005331</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Metabolic polygenic risk scores for prediction of obesity, type 2 diabetes, and related morbidities.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41844147</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41844147</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Metabolic polygenic risk scores for prediction of obesity, type 2 diabetes, and related morbidities.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41844147</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC13092120</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We validated the MetPRS in three external multiethnic cohorts: All of Us (n = 245,394), Mass General Brigham Biobank (MGBB, n = 53,306), and the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center [KFSH&amp;RC] cohort (n = 6,566) (Figure 4; Table S6).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37852978</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41844147</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6416</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>genotyped samples passing QC: 5399 cardiology patients and 1017 population reference individuals (2023)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37852978</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Out of 6566 samples, quality control excluded 150 samples due to variant calling missingness &gt; 5%, heterozygosity rate &gt; 5 standard deviations above the mean, and mismatch between genotypically-determined and self-reported sex, resulting in 6416 samples consisting of 5399 patients and 1017 reference samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KFSH&amp;RC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17264"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17266"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004922</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28921760</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial (NCT00666978), conducted from December 2007 to May 2010 at an urban community-based clinic in Kansas City, Missouri, of sustained-release bupropion combined with health education counselling for smoking cessation in African American light smokers (10 or fewer cigarettes per day) aged 18 or older; the third of the Kick It at Swope trials.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">540</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KIS-III</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KIS3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kick It at Swope 3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kick-it-at-Swope (KIS)-3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kick-it-at-Swope-3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Kick It at Swope III</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17264">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_with_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000038"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17266">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17264"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>light smoking (≤10 cigarettes per day)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3283533/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All participants were African American light smokers (≤10 CPD), aged 18 years or older.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17266"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>nicotine dependence</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3283533/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>KIS-III was a randomized, double-blind placebo-controlled study with the primary aim of evaluating the efficacy of bupropion SR in combination with HE counseling for smoking cessation among African American light smokers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3283533/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This KIS-III study was the third in a series of clinical trials of African American smokers conducted at an urban community-based clinic in Kansas City (MO) that serves predominantly low-income African American patients.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004922</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Transferability of Ancestry-Specific and Cross-Ancestry CYP2A6 Activity Genetic Risk Scores in African and European Populations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33300144</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28921760</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of a nicotine metabolism biomarker in African American smokers: impact of chromosome 19 genetic influences.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28921760</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28921760+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>AA smokers from two clinical trials: Pharmacogenetics of Nicotine Addiction Treatment (PNAT)-2 (NCT01314001; n = 504) and Kick-it-at-Swope (KIS)-3 (NCT00666978; n = 450).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial (NCT00666978), conducted from December 2007 to May 2010 at an urban community-based clinic in Kansas City, Missouri, of sustained-release bupropion combined with health education counselling for smoking cessation in African American light smokers (10 or fewer cigarettes per day) aged 18 or older; the third of the Kick It at Swope trials.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22282543</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">540</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>African American light smokers randomised (270 bupropion SR, 270 placebo), 2007-2009</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3283533/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 540 participants, recruited from December 27, 2007, to October 27, 2009, were randomly assigned to receive a 7-week supply of active bupropion SR or placebo.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KIS-III</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001965"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KIS3</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001966 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001966">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. KLCRI is the Kentucky Lung Cancer Research Initiative, the population-based case-control study of lung cancer in Appalachian Kentucky that the lung cancer OncoArray study table lists as LCRI-DOD (PMID:28604730); a 2019 paper gives the id with the name (PMID:30059977). Replaced by COHO:0001992 (LCRI-DOD), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Kentucky Lung Cancer Research Initiative</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001967 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001967">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000486"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The Korean Metabolic Syndrome Research Initiative is the programme under which the Korean Cancer Prevention Study-II Biobank recruited its health examinees; papers use the two names for the same people (PMID:25113383, PMID:27632197). Replaced by COHO:0000486 (Korean Cancer Prevention Study-II Biobank), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Korean Metabolic Syndrome Research Initiative</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001968 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001968">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Korean National Health Insurance is South Korea&apos;s national health insurance programme and its claims database, a data source used by many unrelated studies, not a study sample; no score in the PGS Catalog uses the id. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Korean National Health Insurance</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17275"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ghana"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Western_Africa"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25261933</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital&apos;s labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1923</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2326</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KNUST</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in Kumasi, Ghana</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17275">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005136"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17275"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>severe malaria</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases consist of children (aged 3 months - 12 years) with severe malaria.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969"/>
