    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17297"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17299"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:36789760</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">246</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">345</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ko-EVE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ko-Eve</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Korean epithelial ovarian cancer study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Korean Epithelial Ovarian Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17297">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0000646"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17299">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005140"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17297"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This case-control study covers incident epithelial ovarian cancers and benign neoplasms, four major centers participating in enrolling incident cases and 3 hospitals enrolling healthy controls among health examinees.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17299"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>epithelial ovarian cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This case-control study covers incident epithelial ovarian cancers and benign neoplasms, four major centers participating in enrolling incident cases and 3 hospitals enrolling healthy controls among health examinees.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this database, patients with EOC were enrolled from 2008 to 2015 from seven general hospitals located in Seoul and Gyeonggi‐do, Korea, namely Seoul National University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Asan Medical Center, National Cancer Center, Gangnam Severance Hospital, Kyung Hee University Hospital at Gangdong, and Cheil General Hospital.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36789760</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Stratifying the risk of ovarian cancer incidence by histologic subtypes in the Korean Epithelial Ovarian Cancer Study (Ko-EVE).</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36789760</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36789760+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this matched case-control study derived from the Korean epithelial ovarian cancer study (Ko-EVE), we calculated the risk of OC subtypes using odds ratios (ORs) and 95% confidence intervals (95% CIs) in a logistic regression model.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23098463</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">246</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Ko-EVE malignant epithelial ovarian cancer cases and healthy controls recruited in 2010-2011</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The total number recruited in 2010-2011 was 246 epithelial ovarian cancer cases, 362 benign epithelial tumors and 345 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">345</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Ko-EVE malignant epithelial ovarian cancer cases and healthy controls recruited in 2010-2011</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The total number recruited in 2010-2011 was 246 epithelial ovarian cancer cases, 362 benign epithelial tumors and 345 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ko-EVE</owl:annotatedTarget>
