    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17308"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17310"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000020"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000344</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32737321</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3144</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KOHBRA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KOHBRA Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Korean Hereditary Breast Cancer study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Korean Hereditary Breast Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17308">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007254"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17310">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ExO_0000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17308"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The following individuals were eligible for inclusion in the KOHBRA Study: 1) patients with breast cancer and a family history of breast or ovarian cancer; 2) patients with breast cancer without a family history of breast or ovarian cancer who were ≤40 years of age at diagnosis, diagnosed with bilateral breast cancer or another primary malignancy related to BRCA mutations, or male; and 3) family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers [10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17310"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental modifiers</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between June 2010 and May 2013, the second phase of the KOHBRA Study was conducted to identify the clinicopathological characteristics and prognostic factors of BRCA-related breast cancer and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA mutations and to develop a Korean BRCA risk prediction model and nationwide genetic counseling network for HBC in Korea.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Korea"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In May 2007, the Korean Hereditary Breast Cancer (KOHBRA) Study, a large, prospective, nationwide study, was established to acquire evidence for the accurate risk assessment and management of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer (HBOC) in the Korean population.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European polygenic risk score for prediction of breast cancer shows similar performance in Asian women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32737321</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32737321</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European polygenic risk score for prediction of breast cancer shows similar performance in Asian women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32737321</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-020-17680-w/MediaObjects/41467_2020_17680_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We thank all investigators of the KOHBRA (Korean Hereditary Breast Cancer) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24155753</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3144</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients and family members at high risk for hereditary breast and ovarian cancer recruited May 2007-April 2013</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The KOHBRA Study recruited 3,144 patients and family members at high risk for HBOC from 40 centers between May 2007 and April 2013 and plans to report the comprehensive prevalence table for BRCA mutations using this larger sample size.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KOHBRA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001977"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004864</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25583993</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The ten-year follow-up examination of the KORA S3 survey, conducted in 2004/05, which re-examined participants of the 1994/95 S3 survey, a population-based random sample of residents aged 25–74 of the city of Augsburg and surrounding counties in southern Germany, within the KORA research platform.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3006</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KORA F3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MONICA/KORA F3</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cooperative Health Research in the Region of Augsburg F3</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The third KORA survey (KORA S3, n=3,996) is a population-based sample from the general population of the South-German city of Augsburg and surrounding counties from 1994/1995.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001977"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>3,006 participants from KORA S3 were reexamined in a 10-year follow- up (KORA F3) in the years 2004/05.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004864</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk score for predicting weight loss after bariatric surgery.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30185664</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25583993</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>DNA methylation of lipid-related genes affects blood lipid levels.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25583993</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25583993+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eight associations were confirmed by replication in the Cooperative Health Research in the Region of Augsburg F3 study (n=499) and in the Invecchiare in Chianti, Aging in the Chianti Area study (n=472).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The ten-year follow-up examination of the KORA S3 survey, conducted in 2004/05, which re-examined participants of the 1994/95 S3 survey, a population-based random sample of residents aged 25–74 of the city of Augsburg and surrounding counties in southern Germany, within the KORA research platform.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3006</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>KORA S3 participants re-examined at the 10-year follow-up in 2004/05</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>3,006 participants from KORA S3 were reexamined in a 10-year follow- up (KORA F3) in the years 2004/05.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>KORA F3</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MONICA/KORA F3</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001975 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001975">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001978"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004864</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:27019061</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The follow-up examination of the KORA S4 survey, conducted in 2006–2008, which re-examined participants of the 1999–2001 S4 survey, a population-based sample of residents aged 25–74 of the city of Augsburg and two adjacent counties in southern Germany, within the KORA research platform; its participants were examined again seven years later in the FF4 follow-up.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3080</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>KORA F4</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cooperative Health Research in the Region of Augsburg F4</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001975"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41483755+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data were drawn from 1700 adults (52.3 % women; mean age = 49.6 ± 9.4 years) participating in the KORA F4 study and its 7-year follow-up (FF4) in Augsburg, Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001975"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001978"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01314-0/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1314_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>KORA F4 including 3,080 individuals was conducted from 2006-2008 as a follow-up study to KORA S4 (1999-2001).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001975"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004864</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic risk score for predicting weight loss after bariatric surgery.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30185664</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001975"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27019061</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association between DNA Methylation in Whole Blood and Measures of Glucose Metabolism: KORA F4 Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27019061</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27019061+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Therefore, we performed an epigenome-wide association study for measures of glucose metabolism in whole blood samples of the population-based Cooperative Health Research in the Region of Augsburg F4 study using the Illumina HumanMethylation 450 BeadChip.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
