        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:40212049</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association between socioeconomic position and lung cancer incidence in 16 countries: a prospective cohort consortium study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40212049</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985077/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this international prospective cohort consortium study, we used data from the Lung Cancer Cohort Consortium (LC3), which includes 20 prospective population cohorts from 16 countries in North America, Europe, Asia, and Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts&apos; participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36404465</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36653422</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39179310</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40212049</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
