    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001994"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24880342</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Rare variants of large effect in BRCA2 and CHEK2 affect risk of lung cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24880342</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4074058/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The IARC-GWAS2 comprised 3,062 lung cancer cases and 4,455 controls derived from five case-control studies: (i) Carotene and Retinol Efficacy Trial (CARET) cohort38; (ii) The Central Europe multicenter hospital-based case-control39,40; (iii) The hospital-based case-control study from France40; (iv) The hospital based case-control lung cancer study from Estonia41,42; and (v) The population-based HUNT2/Tromsø IV lung cancer studies43.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001994"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Estonia, whose cases were lung cancer patients enrolled in Estonian hospitals between 2002 and 2006 and whose controls were randomly selected from the population-based cohort of the Estonian Genome Project; genotyped genome-wide with support from the University of Tartu, it was one of the five case–control studies of the IARC lung cancer genome-wide association study and was pooled in the lung cancer meta-analyses of the TRICL consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
