    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17511"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17513"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS001800</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32649918</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5887</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>US Lung Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lung Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17511">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_with_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000038"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17513">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0006536"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17511"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cigarette smoking</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2048803+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Lung Health Study is a randomized clinical trial designed to determine whether a smoking intervention program and prescription of an inhaled bronchodilator can reduce the annual rate of decline of FEV1 (FEV1 slope) in cigarette smokers with mild to moderate airflow limitation.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17513"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mild to moderate airflow limitation</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2048803+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Lung Health Study is a randomized clinical trial designed to determine whether a smoking intervention program and prescription of an inhaled bronchodilator can reduce the annual rate of decline of FEV1 (FEV1 slope) in cigarette smokers with mild to moderate airflow limitation.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41527371+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The updated analysis excludes 608 participants from the one Canadian clinic and their baseline smoking characteristics differed from the US participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41164942+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed data from 5279 participants from the United States from the Lung Health Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS001800</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and related phenotypes: polygenic risk scores in population-based and case-control cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32649918</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32649918</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and related phenotypes: polygenic risk scores in population-based and case-control cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32649918</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7429152/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Case-control studies included COPDGene (non-Hispanic white and African American participants),23 ECLIPSE,24 NETT25 and Normative Aging Study (NAS),26 SPIROMICS,27, 28 and the Lung Health Study (LHS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:2048803</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41527371</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5887</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Lung Health Study cigarette smokers with mild-to-moderate airflow limitation assessed in recruitment</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2048803+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>During the recruitment period, spirometry measurements were obtained during three screening visits from 5,887 cigarette smokers 35 to 60 yr of age.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
