        <obo:IAO_0000115>A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
