    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:12206514</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Long Island Breast Cancer Study Project: description of a multi-institutional collaboration to identify environmental risk factors for breast cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:12206514</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12206514+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Long Island Breast Cancer Study Project is a federally mandated, population-based case-control study to determine whether breast cancer risk among women in the counties of Nassau and Suffolk, NY, is associated with selected environmental exposures, assessed by blood samples, self-reports, and environmental home samples.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12206514</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35010632</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1508</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>interviewed breast cancer cases and population controls; no total stated (1996-1997)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1023/A:1016387020854.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main questionnaire was completed by 1,508 (82.1%) of eligible case women (n=235 with in situ and 1,273 with invasive breast cancer) and 1,556 (62.7%) of eligible control women (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1556</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>interviewed breast cancer cases and population controls; no total stated (1996-1997)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1023/A:1016387020854.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main questionnaire was completed by 1,508 (82.1%) of eligible case women (n=235 with in situ and 1,273 with invasive breast cancer) and 1,556 (62.7%) of eligible control women (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
