        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000906</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic Risk Score of Longevity Predicts Longer Survival Across an Age Continuum.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33216869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30642433</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genomics of 1 million parent lifespans implicates novel pathways and common diseases and distinguishes survival chances.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30642433</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6333444/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>LifeGen – A consortium of 26 population cohorts of European Ancestry, with UK Biobank lives removed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of population studies, mainly from Europe, Australia and North America and of European or African ancestry, that ran a common protocol relating their genotyped participants&apos; genomes to the survival of those participants&apos; parents, and meta-analysed the results with UK Biobank in a genome-wide association study of human longevity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29030599</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30642433</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">606059</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>parents&apos; lifespans (parents of the genotyped participants) analysed in the 2017 LifeGen genome-wide meta-analysis, UK Biobank included</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5715013/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 606,059 parental lifespans were available for analysis, of which 334,974 were already complete (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LifeGen</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002003 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002003">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. LIKAR is the Limburg Cancer Registry of Belgium, which is not a study; its only genetic use is as the source of the cases of the Belgian case-control study on bladder cancer risk (PMID:21750109), so the id goes on that study and the registry&apos;s name is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0001547 (Belgian case-control study on bladder cancer risk), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Limburg Cancer Registry</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17578"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22199011</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls without atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">487</coho:numberOfCases>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LIPAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Linz Peripheral Arterial Disease (LIPAD) Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Linz Peripheral Arterial Disease study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Linz Peripheral Arterial Disease Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17578">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005386"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17578"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>peripheral arterial disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From April 2000 to April 2002 we consecutively enrolled all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic PAD admitted to a single tertiary care hospital in Austria (Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder, Linz).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Austria"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From April 2000 to April 2002 we consecutively enrolled all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic PAD admitted to a single tertiary care hospital in Austria (Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder, Linz).3–5 PAD was diagnosed by the vascular surgeon attending during index hospitalization.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22199011</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association between chromosome 9p21 variants and the ankle-brachial index identified by a meta-analysis of 21 genome-wide association studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22199011</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3303225/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The replication studies included 5 population-based studies and 3 clinically-based studies including a total of over 16,000 participants: the Bruneck Study (n=786), the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS, n=5,330), the Multi-Ethnic Study of Atherosclerosis (MESA, n=2,611), the National Health and Nutrition Examination Surveys (NHANES 1999–2002, n=2,335), Prevention of Renal and Vascular End-stage disease (PREVEND, n=3,691) cohort, Cardiovascular Disease in Intermittent Claudication (CAVASIC, n=443) Study, Genetic Determinants of Peripheral Arterial Disease (GenePAD, n=850), and the Linz Peripheral Arterial Disease (LIPAD, n=671) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls without atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18325332</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">487</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>consecutive patients with symptomatic lower extremity PAD enrolled April 2000 to April 2002 (the whole LIPAD patient cohort); the matched controls are not counted</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The entire LIPAD cohort included 487 consecutive patients with symptomatic lower extremity PAD as described previously.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LIPAD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


