    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17647"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:29036523</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Greek study of healthy young male army conscripts, randomly selected and recruited from June 2008 in waves at the Greek Army Training Camp in Heraklion, Crete, within their first two months of service and screened to exclude mental and physical illness, who were assessed on schizophrenia-related intermediate phenotypes (prepulse inhibition of the startle reflex, cognition, personality and schizotypal traits) and gave DNA, to study the genetics of the schizophrenia spectrum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1540</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LOGOS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LOGOS cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LOGOS project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Learning On Genetics Of Schizophrenia Spectrum</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Learning on Genetics of Schizophrenia</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Learning on Genetics of Schizophrenia Spectrum study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Learning on Genetics of Schizophrenia Spectrum</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17647">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005090"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17647"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>schizophrenia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3138651/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LOGOS cohort provides a comprehensive endophenotypic assessment of schizophrenia-related intermediate phenotypes in a demographically and genetically homogeneous population of healthy, young, Greek males.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5814832/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LOGOS acquired the same recruitment procedures as the ASPIS, assessing Caucasian healthy male conscripts (N = 690; mean age: 22.3 ± 3.7) on multiple cognitive and psychometric phenotypes, at the Greek Army Training Camp in Heraklion, Crete, Greece.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29036523</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Stress-Dependent Association Between Polygenic Risk for Schizophrenia and Schizotypal Traits in Young Army Recruits.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29036523</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29036523+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we sought to investigate the contribution of common genetic risk variation for SZ on self-reported schizotypy in 2 ethnically homogeneous cohorts of healthy young males during compulsory military service, enrolled in the Athens Study of Proneness and Incidence of Schizophrenia (ASPIS, N = 875) and the Learning on Genetics of Schizophrenia Spectrum study (LOGOS, N = 690).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Greek study of healthy young male army conscripts, randomly selected and recruited from June 2008 in waves at the Greek Army Training Camp in Heraklion, Crete, within their first two months of service and screened to exclude mental and physical illness, who were assessed on schizophrenia-related intermediate phenotypes (prepulse inhibition of the startle reflex, cognition, personality and schizotypal traits) and gave DNA, to study the genetics of the schizophrenia spectrum.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21471957</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27336024</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29036523</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1540</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>young male Greek Army conscripts recruited June 2008 to July 2011 (2008-2011)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2016.244/MediaObjects/41380_2017_BFmp2016244_MOESM471_ESM.docx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LOGOS project recruited 1540 randomly selected young male conscripts from the Greek Army (mean age 22.13; range 18–44) between June 2008 and July 2011 at the Military Training Camp of Candidate, Supply Army officers (SEAP) in Heraklion, Crete.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002013"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LOGOS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002014 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002014">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000561"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24997018</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A longitudinal cohort study at the Institute for Aging Research of the Albert Einstein College of Medicine in the Bronx, New York, which from 2008 enrolled Ashkenazi Jewish adults aged 65 or older from the New York City area without significant cognitive, visual or hearing impairment, comparing offspring of parents with exceptional longevity (at least one parent surviving to 95) with offspring of parents with usual survival, and follows them until death with biomarkers, genotyping, proteomics and cognitive and frailty assessments to study healthy ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1066</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LonGenity</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LonGenity Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LonGenity cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Longenity study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">LonGenity study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002014"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13519853/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 2008 through 2024, the study enrolled Ashkenazi Jewish individuals from the New York City area, aged 65 years or older, and free of significant cognitive, visual, or hearing impairments.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002014"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24997018</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of exceptional parental longevity and physical function in aging.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24997018</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24997018+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LonGenity study recruited a relatively genetically homogenous cohort of Ashkenazi Jewish (AJ) adults age 65 and older, who were defined as either OPEL (having at least one parent who lived to age 95 or older) or OPUS (neither parent survived to age 95).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002014"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A longitudinal cohort study at the Institute for Aging Research of the Albert Einstein College of Medicine in the Bronx, New York, which from 2008 enrolled Ashkenazi Jewish adults aged 65 or older from the New York City area without significant cognitive, visual or hearing impairment, comparing offspring of parents with exceptional longevity (at least one parent surviving to 95) with offspring of parents with usual survival, and follows them until death with biomarkers, genotyping, proteomics and cognitive and frailty assessments to study healthy ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24997018</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41529745</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42646838</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002014"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1066</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants enrolled 2008-2024 in all parental-longevity groups of the 2026 analysis (those whose parents died of unnatural causes excluded)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13519853/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LonGenity total participant count (n = 1066) includes intermediate parental longevity cohorts, which are summarized in eTable 2 in Supplement 1.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
