    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17691"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>COPD</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5669789/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Enrollment in the LSC started in 2001 with the goal to conduct longitudinal studies on biomarkers of respiratory diseases, including COPD and lung cancer in biospecimens from smokers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17693"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5669789/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Enrollment in the LSC started in 2001 with the goal to conduct longitudinal studies on biomarkers of respiratory diseases, including COPD and lung cancer in biospecimens from smokers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17695"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>smoking</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5669789/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Enrollment was restricted to current and former smokers aged 40–74 years with a minimum of 10 pack-years of smoking.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10533946/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LSC recruited 2273 individuals from the Albuquerque area (NM, USA) aged 40–75 years with ≥15 pack-years of smoking from 2001 to 2015.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22139380</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic determinants for promoter hypermethylation in the lungs of smokers: a candidate gene-based study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22139380</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22139380+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A two-stage approach involving discovery and replication was used to assess the association between promoter hypermethylation of a 12-gene panel and common variation in 40 genes involved in carcinogen metabolism, regulation of methylation, and DNA damage response in members of the Lovelace Smokers Cohort (N = 1,434).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A community-based volunteer cohort of current and former smokers aged 40 to 75 from the greater Albuquerque area of New Mexico, established in 2001 at the Lovelace Respiratory Research Institute to study sputum and blood biomarkers for lung cancer risk and the development of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, with repeated spirometry and questionnaires and follow-up for lung cancer incidence and death.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29133979</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36076291</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37678951</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2511</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>unique cohort members with spirometry data by the end of active enrolment in summer 2017 (2001-2017)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9454202/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Active enrollment and on-site follow-up ended in the summer of 2017. Spirometry data were collected from 2511 unique subjects for a total of 11,328 person-visits.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002019"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LSC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid17702"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000560"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:18433484</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">847</coho:numberOfCases>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LUCY</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LUCY-study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LUng Cancer in the Young</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LUng Cancer in the Young study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lung Cancer in the Young study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid17702">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008903"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17702"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The LUCY-study provides access to a nationwide, population based family and a case-control sample (control population KORA, described below) of lung cancer patients aged 50 years or younger at diagnosis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>LUCY (LUng Cancer in the Young) is a multicenter study with 31 recruiting hospitals in Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:18433484</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Early onset lung cancer, cigarette smoking and the SNP309 of the murine double minute-2 (MDM2) gene.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18433484</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2377274/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>472 cases were from the LUCY (LUng Cancer in the Young) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18433484</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24704916</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25644374</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">847</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>young lung cancer patients whose phenotype data were collected (their 5524 relatives not counted)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Phenotype data of 847 young patients with primary lung cancer and 5524 relatives have been collected.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LUCY</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002021 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002021">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. LUHR is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for Landspitali University Hospital, Reykjavik, as a contributing site: the Icelandic BRCA1/BRCA2 carriers it contributed to CIMBA (called ILUH, &apos;Iceland Landspitali - University Hospital&apos;, in CIMBA&apos;s own lists; PMID:32665703, 28346442) and the hospital&apos;s ovarian cancer material in the deCODE BRIP1 study (PMID:21964575). None of these papers gives the sample a study name or a recruitment of its own beyond the hospital, so it is a site, not a named cohort. Note that the PGS Catalog&apos;s own id ILUH is a different thing (Infanta Leonor University Hospital, Madrid), so this is not a duplicate of E535. The Icelandic cohorts COHO already has (deCODE genetics Icelandic cohort COHO:0000428, Icelandic Cancer Registry COHO:0000096) are not this sample. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Landspitali University Hospital, Reykjavik</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


