        <rdfs:comment>Alt Fq denotes alternative allele frequency, CI confidence interval, and Ref reference allele. † The nominal gene was taken from the Illumina SNP database. ‡ Position is based on the number of base pairs from the start of the chromosome. § The rs3771166 SNP was imputed in the MRC Asthma and United Kingdom Control panel (MRCA-UKC) and in the Multicenter Asthma Genetics in Childhood Study (MAGICS) panel.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002029"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An observational study of children with physician-diagnosed asthma recruited from secondary and tertiary care centres in Germany and Austria for the genetics of childhood asthma, whose cases have been compared in genome-wide association studies with controls from the German arm of the International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood Phase II, and whose participants were re-examined as adolescents and young adults in a follow-up stage, followMAGICS.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20860503</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25930191</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8503671/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002029"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">655</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>asthmatic children from MAGICS in the case-control dataset of the first asthma GWAS, reused by GABRIEL and TAGC (analysed subset)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>MAGICS consists of 655 asthmatic children (asthma diagnosed by a pulmonologist) were derived from the Multicenter Asthma Genetics In Childhood Study with a further 73 asthmatics and 694 unaffected individuals (randomly selected) from Phase One of the International Study of Asthma and Allergy in Childhood (ISAAC)78,79 .</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002029"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MAGICS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002030 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002030">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog id has no score, development sample or evaluation sample set in the Catalog today (REST /cohort/MAHI and the full cohort list return nothing; it appears only in the Catalog&apos;s cohort table), so the paper that gave rise to it cannot be identified from the Catalog. MAHI is the Mid-America Heart Institute (Saint Luke&apos;s Health System, Kansas City), a cardiovascular hospital (E660.14). The PGS Catalog records no sample for the id. Where the name labels a genetic study sample (MIGen, PMID:19198609), it is a case-control set assembled at the institute: acute coronary syndrome survivors drawn from the institute&apos;s &apos;successive prospective cohort studies&apos; plus outpatient controls, with no study name of its own. The underlying outcome registries have their own names in their own papers, but nothing ties the PGS id to any one of them, so the id denotes the site, not a named cohort. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Mid-America Heart Institute</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


