        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Danish population-based case-control study of the Danish Cancer Society, in which women aged 35 to 79 diagnosed in 1994 to 1999 with ovarian cancer or a borderline ovarian tumour in the municipalities of Copenhagen and Frederiksberg and the surrounding counties, and controls drawn at random from the female population of the same area through the Central Population Register, gave questionnaire data, blood and tumour tissue, to identify risk factors and prognostic factors for ovarian cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
