        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008903"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid17776"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2945218/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the Mayo genome-wide association study, patients with lung cancer who were classed as never smokers were identified and recruited between January, 1997, and September, 2008.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:20304703%20AND%20SRC:MED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>First, a genome-wide association study of single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) was done with 754 never smokers (377 matched case-control pairs at Mayo Clinic, Rochester, MN, USA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000740</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Assessing Lung Cancer Absolute Risk Trajectory Based on a Polygenic Risk Model.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33472890</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26363033</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of lung cancer histology-specific variants applying Bayesian framework variant prioritization approaches within the TRICL and ILCCO consortia.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26363033</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4635669</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>cancer study (21); the Helmholtz-Gemeinschaft Deutscher Forschungszentren lung cancer GWAS (22); the lung cancer study from Canada (Lunenfeld- Tanenbaum Research Institute (LTRI) and University of Toronto) (23); the Harvard lung cancer study (24); NCI lung cancer GWAS including the Environment and Genetics in Lung Cancer Etiology (EAGLE) GWAS (25), the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study (ATBC) GWAS (26), the Prostate, Lung, Colon, Ovary Screening Trial (PLCO) (27), lung cancer GWAS and the Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort (CPS-II) GWAS (28); the IARC lung cancer GWAS (29); the Memorial Sloan Kettering Lung Cancer GWAS (30) and the Mayo lung cancer GWAS (31).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control sample of lung cancer patients who had never smoked, identified and recruited at Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, between 1997 and 2008, and never-smoking community residents matched to them by age, sex and ethnic background, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer in never smokers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20304703</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002036"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">754</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>never smokers in 377 matched lung cancer case-control pairs genotyped in the GWAS (2010)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20304703</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>First, a genome-wide association study of single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) was done with 754 never smokers (377 matched case-control pairs at Mayo Clinic, Rochester, MN, USA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
