        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:23805179</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cross-sectional study of schizophrenia conducted by the Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute (now the Mind Research Network) at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital and the University of Iowa, which collected clinical, cognitive, structural, functional and diffusion MRI and genetic data under a common protocol from people with schizophrenia, recruited where possible early in their illness, and sex- and age-matched controls, to identify neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">188</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">190</coho:numberOfControls>
