        <rdfs:comment>Samples were provided by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR, Australia), The Netherlands Study of Anxiety and Depression (NESDA), The Netherlands Twin Registry (NTR), the University of Edinburgh (UK), and the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study (controls only, US).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21042317</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder: new results, meta-analysis, and lessons learned.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21042317</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we present the largest GWAS for MDD to date, the MDD2000+ study comprising 2431 cases and 3673 screened controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21042317</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
