    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002065 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002065">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. MGS_nonGAIN is the second genotyping phase of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia case-control sample (&apos;The remainder of the sample (called “nonGAIN” here) was genotyped in the same laboratory several months later&apos;, PMID:19571809). The Catalog&apos;s name describes only that phase and is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0000116 (Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia Collaboration), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia - nonGAIN Sample</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002066 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002066">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000734"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. MHC is the Mexican Hypertriglyceridemia study (MexHTG) of the BMI GWAS of PMID:40691366, funded by the grant of the Mexican Hypertriglyceride Study (HL-095056). Replaced by COHO:0000734 (Mexican Hypertriglyceride Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Mexican Hypertriglyceridemia cohort</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002067 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002067">
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Identity resolved 2026-09-28: the PGS tag MIAMI-WFPCS denotes the Wake Forest University Prostate Cancer Study (COHO:0002564), as named in the prostate consortium cohort tables. The former institutional expansion is not carried as a cohort name. This deprecated term now has its biological replacement.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002564"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. The University of Miami – Sylvester Comprehensive Cancer Center (MIAMI-WFPCS) is an institution: the PGS Catalog cohort id is the PRACTICAL consortium’s site label for prostate cancer samples of the Sylvester Comprehensive Cancer Center in its African-ancestry analyses, not a named cohort. Found by the review of 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete The University of Miami – Sylvester Comprehensive Cancer Center</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20593021</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A general population study of families in the towns of Renfrew and Paisley in the west of Scotland, in which the locally resident adult offspring, aged 30 to 59, of couples who had taken part in the Renfrew and Paisley general population survey of 1972 to 1976 were surveyed in 1996 by questionnaire, clinical examination, spirometry and blood samples and then followed up for cardiovascular disease and death, to study familial and intergenerational influences on cardiovascular and respiratory health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2338</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MIDSPAN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MIDSPAN Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MIDSPAN family study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Midspan family study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Renfrew-Paisley (Midspan) family study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Midspan Family Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4636631/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Midspan Family Study is a general population survey of 1477 Caucasian families in Renfrew and Paisley (Scotland), which included 15 402 participants in the first, parental, generation (aged 45–64 years) surveyed between 1972 and 1976.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20593021</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Which circulating antioxidant vitamins are confounded by socioeconomic deprivation? The MIDSPAN family study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20593021</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20593021+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Socioeconomic and lifestyle measures were available in 1040 men and 1298 women from the MIDSPAN Family Study (30-59 years at baseline) together with circulating levels of vitamins A, C, E, and carotenoids (alpha-carotene, beta-carotene, lutein and lycopene).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A general population study of families in the towns of Renfrew and Paisley in the west of Scotland, in which the locally resident adult offspring, aged 30 to 59, of couples who had taken part in the Renfrew and Paisley general population survey of 1972 to 1976 were surveyed in 1996 by questionnaire, clinical examination, spirometry and blood samples and then followed up for cardiovascular disease and death, to study familial and intergenerational influences on cardiovascular and respiratory health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:10884260</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12540691</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23071162</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26525718</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2338</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adult offspring aged 30-59 surveyed in 1996</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4636631/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the second generation, 2338 offspring (1040 sons and 1298 daughters) aged 30–59 years were surveyed in 1996 from an eligible population of 3202 offspring aged 30–59 years who lived locally.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002068"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MIDSPAN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


