        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000745"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000012</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:27655226</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease case-control studies, formed for a genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction (men aged 50 or younger, women 60 or younger) and age- and sex-matched controls from sites in Boston and Seattle in the United States, Sweden, Finland, Spain and Italy, and later extended with further case-control cohorts for exome and gene sequencing studies of coronary artery disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10138</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12395</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">22533</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MI Genetics Consortium Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MIGen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18039">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005010"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18039"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>coronary artery disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5664181/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Gene sequencing of LPL was performed in 22,533 participants of the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium, including 12,395 controls and 10,138 cases with CAD (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000071"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The six studies were: i) Italian Atherosclerosis Thrombosis and Vascular Biology (IATVB); ii) Heart Attack Risk in Puget Sound (HARPS); iii) Registre Gironi del COR (Gerona Heart Registry or REGICOR); iv) Massachusetts General Hospital Premature Coronary Artery Disease (MGH PCAD); v) FINRISK; and vi) Malmo Diet and Cancer Study (MDC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000142"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5664181/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Studies included the Italian Atherosclerosis Thrombosis and Vascular Biology (ATVB) study,6 the Exome Sequencing Project Early-Onset Myocardial Infarction (ESP-EOMI) study,7 a nested case-control of the Jackson Heart Study (JHS),8 the South German Myocardial Infarction study,9 the Ottawa Heart Study (OHS),10 the Precocious Coronary Artery Disease Study (PROCARDIS),11 the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study (PROMIS),12 the Registre Gironi del COR (Gerona Heart Registry or REGICOR) study,13 the Leicester Myocardial Infarction study,14 and the North German Myocardial Infarction study.15 Clinical data was assessed in each study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000169"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5664181/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Studies included the Italian Atherosclerosis Thrombosis and Vascular Biology (ATVB) study,6 the Exome Sequencing Project Early-Onset Myocardial Infarction (ESP-EOMI) study,7 a nested case-control of the Jackson Heart Study (JHS),8 the South German Myocardial Infarction study,9 the Ottawa Heart Study (OHS),10 the Precocious Coronary Artery Disease Study (PROCARDIS),11 the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study (PROMIS),12 the Registre Gironi del COR (Gerona Heart Registry or REGICOR) study,13 the Leicester Myocardial Infarction study,14 and the North German Myocardial Infarction study.15 Clinical data was assessed in each study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
