    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002071 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002071">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The evidence is a table row (Band et al. 2013 Table S1, https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&amp;id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1003509.s020, a .docx): &apos;Malawi | Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme, Blantyre | University of Malawi, college of Medicine | CoM REC | Illumina 1.2M&apos;. The PGS Catalog id has no score or sample set in the Catalog today (it is only in the Catalog&apos;s cohort table). MLWCRP is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the site name that Band et al. 2013 (PMID:23717212) give for their Malawi sample: the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme in Blantyre, the research programme that runs the Malawi severe malaria case-control study. The sample itself is the MalariaGEN partner study already in COHO as &apos;Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in Malawi&apos; (COHO:0001536), which was minted from the PGS id &apos;Blantyre&apos; taken from the same paper. So this placeholder is a duplicate of COHO:0001536: add MLWCRP as an acronym and the catalog name as a synonym there, and retire the placeholder (COHO:0002071). Replaced by COHO:0001536 (Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in Malawi), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme, Blantyre</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


