    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18151"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000327</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30804558</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">318</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MONBOS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MonBos</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MonBos Collection</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Montreal Boston Collection</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Montreal/Boston (MonBos) Collection</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Montreal/Boston Collection</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18151">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005258"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18151"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>autism spectrum disorders</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subjects diagnosed with autism spectrum disorders with both of their parents were recruited from clinics specializing in the diagnosis of Pervasive Developmental Disorders (PDD), readaptation centers, and specialized schools in the Montreal and Quebec City regions, Canada, as described 31.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subjects diagnosed with autism spectrum disorders with both of their parents were recruited from clinics specializing in the diagnosis of Pervasive Developmental Disorders (PDD), readaptation centers, and specialized schools in the Montreal and Quebec City regions, Canada, as described 31.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Recruitment took place in Massachusetts and surrounding states through contacts with parent support and patient advocacy groups, brochures, newsletters, and the study web site.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000327</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of common genetic risk variants for autism spectrum disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30804558</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30804558</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of common genetic risk variants for autism spectrum disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30804558</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6454898/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, five cohorts provided genotypes to the sample (N denoting the number of trios for which genotypes were available): The Geschwind Autism Center of Excellence (ACE; N = 391), the Autism Genome Project (AGP; N = 2,272), the Autism Genetic Resource Exchange (AGRE; N = 974), the NIMH Repository, the Montreal/Boston Collection (MONBOS; N = 1,396, and the Simons Simplex Collection(SSC; N = 2,231).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19812673</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28540026</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30804558</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">318</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>parent-offspring trios (families, not individuals) collected by Autism Consortium investigators and in Montreal with genome-wide data, 2009</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>First, we utilized additional autism family samples (318 trios collected by investigators of the Autism Consortium and in Montreal) with genome-wide Affymetrix 5.0/500K array data also genotyped at the Genetic Analysis Platform of the Broad Institute using the same conditions, QC, and analysis pipelines (Methods).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MONBOS</owl:annotatedTarget>
