    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18161"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we generate new and so far unpublished genome-wide SNP data from 2,266 clinically well-characterized patients with BD (∼76% BD type I) and 5,028 ethnically matched controls, derived from the MooDS (Systematic Investigation of the Molecular Causes of Major Mood Disorders and Schizophrenia) consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18163"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>schizophrenia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we generate new and so far unpublished genome-wide SNP data from 2,266 clinically well-characterized patients with BD (∼76% BD type I) and 5,028 ethnically matched controls, derived from the MooDS (Systematic Investigation of the Molecular Causes of Major Mood Disorders and Schizophrenia) consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric in-patient units at the University Hospital Würzburg (Germany II), at the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim and other collaborating psychiatric hospitals in Germany (Germany III), at the Mood Disorder Unit, Prince of Wales Hospital in Sydney (Australia), at the Department of Psychiatry, Poznan University of Medical Sciences (Poland), at specialty mood disorders clinics in Halifax and Ottawa (Canada), at the Russian State Medical University, Moscow (Russia), and at the Civil Hospital Carlos Haya, Málaga (Spain).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6432650/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These German samples were collected by separate groups within the MooDS Consortium in Mannheim, Bonn, Munich and Jena.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24618891</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study reveals two new risk loci for bipolar disorder.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24618891</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we generate new and so far unpublished genome-wide SNP data from 2,266 clinically well-characterized patients with BD (∼76% BD type I) and 5,028 ethnically matched controls, derived from the MooDS (Systematic Investigation of the Molecular Causes of Major Mood Disorders and Schizophrenia) consortium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A German research consortium, the Integrated Genome Research Network MooDS of the National Genome Research Network plus (NGFNplus), funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, whose groups collected and genotyped case-control samples for genome-wide association studies of schizophrenia in Germany and of bipolar disorder in Germany and in partner centres in Poland, Russia, Spain, Canada and Australia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24618891</obo:IAO_0000119>
