    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18197"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>diabetes mellitus</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7083427/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These subjects were randomly selected from groups defined by glucometabolic status: normal fasting plasma glucose (FPG) (≤6.0 mmol/L); impaired FPG; new‐onset Type 2 diabetes mellitus; and prevalent diabetes mellitus.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18199"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Type 2 diabetes mellitus</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7083427/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These subjects were randomly selected from groups defined by glucometabolic status: normal fasting plasma glucose (FPG) (≤6.0 mmol/L); impaired FPG; new‐onset Type 2 diabetes mellitus; and prevalent diabetes mellitus.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7083427/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1974 and 1992, birth cohorts (men born in 1921, 1926–42, 1944, 1946, and 1948‐49; women born in 1926, 1928, 1930–36, 1938, 1941–42, and 1949) of inhabitants residing in Malmö, Sweden, were invited to participate in a large cohort study The Malmö Preventive Project (MPP) with a total of 33 346 participants (67% men, attendance rate 71%, mean age 46 ± 7 years).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000787"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7083427/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Hence, our aim in this observational study was to investigate SNPs with documented association with diabetes and their further association with one of the earliest signs of left ventricular dysfunction (i.e. diastolic dysfunction) in two independent Swedish population UCG cohorts: the population‐based Malmö Preventive Project‐Re‐examination Study UCG (MPP‐RES UCG) and the VARA UCG.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005203</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40691366</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:40691366</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40691366</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41591-025-03827-z/MediaObjects/41591_2025_3827_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Broad Bayer MPP-echo | The Malmö Preventive Project echo study | EUR</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An echocardiography study within the 2002-2006 re-examination of the Malmö Preventive Project in Malmö, Sweden, in which a subsample of re-examined participants, randomly selected from groups defined by glucometabolic status with impaired fasting glucose and diabetes oversampled, underwent echocardiography.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31860786</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
