        <owl:annotatedTarget>MAS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MyOvCa</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:42341622</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1042</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>N85PLUS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Newcastle 85+ cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Newcastle 85+ Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797051/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The sampling frame comprised all people born in 1921 who were permanently registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside primary care trusts in the UK.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:42341622</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Exploring the relationship between cognitive impairment, frailty and mortality in the oldest old: findings from the Newcastle 85+ cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42341622</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42341622+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We utilised data from the Newcastle 85+ Study, a prospective longitudinal cohort of individuals aged 85 at baseline (n = 695).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17594470</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20028777</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1042</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people born in 1921 who took part at baseline (851 health assessment plus record review, 188 record review only, 3 health assessment only), 2006-2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797051/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 1453 people eligible to participate—that is, registered with a participating general practice and still alive—1042 (71.7%) participated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>N85PLUS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18315"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18317"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000558"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS005203</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:40691366</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control study of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease run by Harokopio University of Athens in Greek adults without secondary liver disease or excessive alcohol intake, recruited between 2012 and 2015 at the outpatient clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine, Laiko General Hospital, Athens, and classified as cases or controls by degree of hepatic steatosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">134</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">217</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">351</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NAFLD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NAFLD BioResource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NAFLD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Greek NAFLD study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18315">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0013209"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18317">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000021"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18315"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>non-alcoholic fatty liver disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29574608+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The sample consisted of 134 patients with NAFLD and 217 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18317"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>dietary habits</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00394-018-1675-4</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aims of the present study were to evaluate the effect of PNPLA3, TM6SF2, and GCKR genetic variants on a NAFLD case–control Greek cohort, to assess the impact of dietary habits and to further explore the interaction of these three single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) with dietary factors and their effect on NAFLD.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this regard, available data from 351 individuals in a Greek case–control NAFLD study were also used during following stages of our analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005203</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40691366</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:40691366</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
