        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.</owl:annotatedTarget>
