        <dcterms:title>Polygenic Risk Score of Longevity Predicts Longer Survival Across an Age Continuum.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33216869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33216869</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic Risk Score of Longevity Predicts Longer Survival Across an Age Continuum.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33216869</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8087277/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As controls, we used (a) a sample of 1779 Dutch older adults from the Longitudinal Aging Study of Amsterdam (24), (b) a sample of 1206 older adults with subjective cognitive decline who visited the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam and SCIENCe project, who were labeled cognitively normal after the extensive examination (25), (c) a sample of 40 healthy controls from the Netherlands Brain Bank (26), (d) a sample of 201 individuals from the twin study (27), and (e) a sample of 86 older adults from the 100-plus Study (partners of centenarian’s children).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A brain bank established at the end of 1985 at the Netherlands Institute for Brain Research, in collaboration with nursing homes in and around Amsterdam, the Netherlands, which performs rapid autopsies of donors who gave informed consent during life for the research use of their brain tissue and medical files, originally to supply post-mortem brain tissue from Alzheimer&apos;s disease patients and controls.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:1480765</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29496148</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8360654</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002115"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4003</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>brain donors collected by the NBB from 1989 to 2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7098103/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Clinical records of all donors (n = 4003) collected by the NBB in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, from 1989 to 2015 were screened for inclusion in this study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002115"/>
