        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22238607</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The US National Cancer Institute&apos;s genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3532</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5120</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genome-wide association study for Bladder Cancer Risk</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCI bladder cancer GWAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCI-GWAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCI-GWAS1</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NCI-GWAS2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">NCI Bladder Cancer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18437">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001187"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18437"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bladder cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3251580/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We applied our analyses to primary scan data of 591,637 SNPs from NCI&apos;s bladder cancer GWAS containing 3,532 cases and 5,120 controls of European ancestry from five studies (Spanish Bladder Cancer Study [SBCS], New England, Maine and Vermont Bladder Cancer Study [NEBCS-ME/VT], Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study [ATBC], the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort [CPS-II], and the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial [PLCO]) [22].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000065"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3919005/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We genotyped cases and used existing control data for four cohort studies already subjected to rigorous quality control metrics: the European Prospective Investigation Into Cancer and Nutrition Study (EPIC), Women&apos;s Health Initiative (WHI), Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS) and Nurses&apos; Health Study I and II (NHS I and II), which have been a part of Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility (CGEMS) (Supplementary Material, Table S1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3919005/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For LABCS, CeRePP, FBCS and BBCS studies where we genotyped cases only, we created in silico study groups based on comparable geographic/demographic parameters, which resulted in three new ‘study groups’, specifically, Europe (which comprises data from EPIC, CeRePP, and FBCS), Multiethnic Cohort (MEC)/LA (which comprises cases from LABCS and controls from the MEC) and Italy (which comprises cases from BBCS and controls from the EAGLE).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123"/>
