        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22238607</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale pathway-based analysis of bladder cancer genome-wide association data from five studies of European background.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22238607</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3251580/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We applied our analyses to primary scan data of 591,637 SNPs from NCI&apos;s bladder cancer GWAS containing 3,532 cases and 5,120 controls of European ancestry from five studies (Spanish Bladder Cancer Study [SBCS], New England, Maine and Vermont Bladder Cancer Study [NEBCS-ME/VT], Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study [ATBC], the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort [CPS-II], and the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial [PLCO]) [22].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The US National Cancer Institute&apos;s genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22238607</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24163127</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
