        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the overall NEIGHBORHOOD (NBH), the summary value for the population cohorts (POP; NHS/HPFS/WGHS) are presented separately from the case/control cohorts (CC; Iowa, OHTS (Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study), Marshfield, MEEI, NEIGHBOR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the overall NEIGHBORHOOD (NBH), the summary value for the population cohorts (POP; NHS/HPFS/WGHS) are presented separately from the case/control cohorts (CC; Iowa, OHTS (Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study), Marshfield, MEEI, NEIGHBOR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the overall NEIGHBORHOOD (NBH), the summary value for the population cohorts (POP; NHS/HPFS/WGHS) are presented separately from the case/control cohorts (CC; Iowa, OHTS (Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study), Marshfield, MEEI, NEIGHBOR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the overall NEIGHBORHOOD (NBH), the summary value for the population cohorts (POP; NHS/HPFS/WGHS) are presented separately from the case/control cohorts (CC; Iowa, OHTS (Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study), Marshfield, MEEI, NEIGHBOR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For all 8 NEIGHBORHOOD studies cases were primarily defined as at least 1 reliable visual field showing loss consistent with glaucoma, without a secondary cause, or CDR (cup-to-disc ratio) ≥ 0.7 or CDR asymmetry ≥ 0.2 or documented progression of optic nerve degeneration (in the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study [OHTS]).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5266624/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The national eye institute glaucoma human collaboration heritable overall operational database (NEIGHBORHOOD) dataset represents a genome-wide meta-analysis summary dataset from eight independent studies, including the Nurses’ Health Study, with a total of 3,853 POAG cases and 33,480 controls of European ancestry from the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27760082</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Age at natural menopause genetic risk score in relation to age at natural menopause and primary open-angle glaucoma in a US-based sample.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27760082</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27760082+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subsequently, to assess the relation with POAG, we used data from 2,160 female POAG cases and 29,110 controls in the National Eye Institute Glaucoma Human Genetics Collaboration Heritable Overall Operational Database (NEIGHBORHOOD), which consists of 8 datasets with imputed genotypes to 5.6+ million markers.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide meta-analysis resource for primary open-angle glaucoma that combines summary data from eight independent case-control and population-based datasets of European ancestry from the United States: the NEIGHBOR study, the Nurses&apos; Health Study, the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, the Women&apos;s Genome Health Study, the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study, and collections from Iowa, Marshfield and the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary. Cases in all datasets were defined by a harmonised glaucoma definition.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26752265</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27760082</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3853</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>POAG cases and controls in the 8-dataset discovery meta-analysis (2016)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify new susceptibility loci, we meta-analyzed GWAS results from 8 independent studies from the United States (3,853 cases and 33,480 controls) and investigated the most significant SNPs in two Australian studies (1,252 cases and 2,592 controls), 3 European studies (875 cases and 4,107 controls) and a Singaporean Chinese study (1,037 cases and 2,543 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">33480</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>POAG cases and controls in the 8-dataset discovery meta-analysis (2016)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To identify new susceptibility loci, we meta-analyzed GWAS results from 8 independent studies from the United States (3,853 cases and 33,480 controls) and investigated the most significant SNPs in two Australian studies (1,252 cases and 2,592 controls), 3 European studies (875 cases and 4,107 controls) and a Singaporean Chinese study (1,037 cases and 2,543 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NBH</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NEIGHBORHOOD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18548"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18550"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000560"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000740</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28604730</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of lung cancer, based at Dartmouth College, among residents of northern and central New Hampshire counties and the bordering region of Vermont, United States, in which cases of histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 through the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center Tumor Registry, and controls identified from a commercial database were matched to them on five-year age group, sex and county.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">277</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">251</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">528</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NELCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">New England Lung Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18548">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008903"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18550">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_0080000"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18548"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lung cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases with histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 using the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center (DHMC) Tumor Registry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18550"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>arsenic in drinking water</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2801179/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we used toenail arsenic concentration as a biomarker of exposure to examine the risk of lung cancer among persons in the U.S. population who had been exposed to low levels of arsenic in drinking water.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>NELCS New England Lung Cancer Study Dartmouth College A. Andrew USA Pop. CC 2005-2007</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000740</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Assessing Lung Cancer Absolute Risk Trajectory Based on a Polygenic Risk Model.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33472890</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28604730</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Large-scale association analysis identifies new lung cancer susceptibility loci and heterogeneity in genetic susceptibility across histological subtypes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28604730</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>NELCS is a population-based case-control study of lung cancer among residents of Northern and Central New Hampshire counties and the bordering region of Vermont.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of lung cancer, based at Dartmouth College, among residents of northern and central New Hampshire counties and the bordering region of Vermont, United States, in which cases of histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 through the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center Tumor Registry, and controls identified from a commercial database were matched to them on five-year age group, sex and county.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28604730</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">277</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>NELCS participants who completed interviews before toenail and data exclusions, 2005-2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2801179/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 454 eligible cases, 24 (5%) could not be reached because of an inaccurate address or phone number, 52 (11%) were too ill to be interviewed, and 101 (22%) refused to participate, which yielded 277 subjects and a 61% participation rate.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">251</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>NELCS participants who completed interviews before toenail and data exclusions, 2005-2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2801179/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 251 controls completed the interview for a 46% participation rate.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">528</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>NELCS participants who completed interviews before toenail and data exclusions, 2005-2007</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2801179/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Of the 528 participants, we excluded from the analysis 62 who did not provide a toenail sample and 2 (&lt; 1%) whose toenail selenium could not be analyzed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NELCS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18560"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35913550</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A psychiatric epidemiological population study of non-institutionalised Dutch adults, conducted by the Trimbos Institute in Utrecht, that interviews representative samples drawn by multistage, stratified random sampling (NEMESIS-1 from 1996 and NEMESIS-2 from 2007, aged 18-64, the latter with DNA from saliva, and NEMESIS-3 from 2019, aged 18-75) with the Composite International Diagnostic Interview and follows them up to determine the prevalence, incidence, course and consequences of mental disorders.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6646</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NEMESIS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NEMESIS-Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Netherlands Mental Health Survey and Incidence Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18560">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005084"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18560"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mental disorders</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6878518/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main objectives of the new study are to provide up‐to‐date figures on the prevalence, incidence, course and consequences of mental disorders, and to study trends in mental disorders and service use, with the use of a new sample.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9555131+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A representative sample of 7076 adults (18-64 years) in the Netherlands&apos; population were interviewed in 1996 to determine the prevalence of mental disorders ever, in the previous 12 months and in the previous month.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35913550</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Age- and sex-specific associations between risk scores for schizophrenia and self-reported health in the general population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35913550</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9845157/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were from the population-based Netherlands Mental Health Survey and Incidence Study–2 (NEMESIS-2).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A psychiatric epidemiological population study of non-institutionalised Dutch adults, conducted by the Trimbos Institute in Utrecht, that interviews representative samples drawn by multistage, stratified random sampling (NEMESIS-1 from 1996 and NEMESIS-2 from 2007, aged 18-64, the latter with DNA from saliva, and NEMESIS-3 from 2019, aged 18-75) with the Composite International Diagnostic Interview and follows them up to determine the prevalence, incidence, course and consequences of mental disorders.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20641046</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35913550</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42687372</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9555130</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9857790</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6646</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>respondents at the 2007-2009 baseline of NEMESIS-2, the second of the study&apos;s three independent samples</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6878518/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Its baseline wave included 6646 subjects.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NEMESIS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


