        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000456"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NHS-Hu is the label the age-at-menopause GWAS of PMID:22267201 gives the Nurses&apos; Health Study&apos;s type 2 diabetes GWAS set. Replaced by COHO:0000456 (Nurses&apos; Health Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete NHS-Hu</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002147 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002147">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. NIA is the PGS Catalog&apos;s name for the US National Institute on Aging, an NIH research funding institute, and no PGS Catalog score or sample set uses the id, so no study sample stands behind it. Every Europe PMC hit is about the institute (grant mechanisms, workshops), not a cohort. Cohorts the institute sponsors already have their own terms (the NIA Late Onset Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Family Study COHO:0000669, the NIA Long Life Family Study in COHO:0000513), but nothing links this id to either one. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete National Institute on Aging</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


