    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002151 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002151">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. NICR is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for 23 childhood B-cell precursor acute lymphoblastic leukaemia cases, with no study name, from the Northern Institute for Cancer Research (Leukaemia Research Group, Newcastle University, UK). They were included in the UK-GWAS of PMID:27694927 (&apos;23 cases from the Northern Institute for Cancer Research (16 males)&apos;). This is an institute&apos;s unnamed handful of cases, not a named cohort. The other UK-GWAS samples already have COHO terms or are other catalog ids: UK Childhood Cancer Study COHO:0000178, 1958 British Birth Cohort COHO:0000207, WTCCC COHO:0000182. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Northern Institute for Cancer Research</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002152 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002152">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The PGS Catalog id Nigerian (Nigerian cohort) names only a nationality: no score uses it, and every paper found by the name uses the phrase for an unrelated, unnamed sample. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Nigerian cohort</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18619"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41751589</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1199</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Norfolk Island Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Norfolk Island Health study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Norfolk Island cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Norfolk Island Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18619">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18619"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular diseases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8484585/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>However, because the initial aim of the Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS) was to study cardiovascular diseases, only serum biomarkers were collected.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4667444/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Located in the Pacific Ocean between Australia and New Zealand, the unique population isolate of Norfolk Island has been shown to exhibit increased prevalence of metabolic disorders (type-2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease) compared to mainland Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41751589</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>An &lt;i&gt;ACOT4&lt;/i&gt; Multi-Nucleotide Variant Is Associated with Cardiovascular Risk in Norfolk Island and UK Biobank Cohorts.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41751589</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41751589+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We leveraged the population genetic features of the Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS, n = 601), to identify candidate functional variants which were analysed for association with CVD and metabolic syndrome traits.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26628212</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41751589</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1199</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Norfolk Islanders with data and samples collected by 2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4667444/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To date the Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS) has collected data and samples for 1199 Norfolk Islanders, 52 % (N = 624) of whom were found to have direct links to the original founders.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NIC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NIHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002154 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002154">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Nijmegen is a city: the PGS Catalog cohort id Nijmegen is a prostate cancer sample listed by city (alongside the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, NBS, as its controls) in the deCODE replication sets behind PGS000082 and PGS000793, with no study name. Found by the review of 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Nijmegen</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002155 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002155">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The NIMH Intramural Research Program is the in-house research division of the US National Institute of Mental Health, which papers name as an affiliation, a funder or the host of several distinct collections; no score in the PGS Catalog uses the id. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete NIMH Intramural Research Program</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18627"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19416921</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1177</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">772</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIMH RGR Bipolar Study 2 (Pritzker)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIMH/Pritzker</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PNDRC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18627">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001866"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18627"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar I disorder</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the NIMH/Pritzker GWAS, 1,177 BP I cases (473 sibling pairs and 231 unrelated individuals) from the NIMH and Prechter Repositories and 772 controls from the NIMH Repository (Table 1) were genotyped on the Illumina HumanHap 550K chip; 512,844 autosomal SNPs passed QC (see Methods) and had minor allele frequency (MAF)≥1%.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6432650/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>19416921 [PGC1] | Michigan, USA (Pritzker and NIMH) | bip_mich_eur</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19416921</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association and meta-analysis of bipolar disorder in individuals of European ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19416921</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We analyzed the NIMH/Pritzker and GSK GWAS samples separately and performed a 2-study meta-analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19416921</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21926972</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29906448</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1177</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar I cases and NIMH repository controls genotyped for the sample&apos;s own GWAS (2009)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the NIMH/Pritzker GWAS, 1,177 BP I cases (473 sibling pairs and 231 unrelated individuals) from the NIMH and Prechter Repositories and 772 controls from the NIMH Repository (Table 1) were genotyped on the Illumina HumanHap 550K chip; 512,844 autosomal SNPs passed QC (see Methods) and had minor allele frequency (MAF)≥1%.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">772</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar I cases and NIMH repository controls genotyped for the sample&apos;s own GWAS (2009)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the NIMH/Pritzker GWAS, 1,177 BP I cases (473 sibling pairs and 231 unrelated individuals) from the NIMH and Prechter Repositories and 772 controls from the NIMH Repository (Table 1) were genotyped on the Illumina HumanHap 550K chip; 512,844 autosomal SNPs passed QC (see Methods) and had minor allele frequency (MAF)≥1%.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NIMH/Pritzker</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PNDRC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002157 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002157">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NINCDS-ADRDA is a set of diagnostic criteria for Alzheimer&apos;s disease, which studies cite for how their cases were diagnosed, not a sample. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Disorders and Stroke and the Alzheimers Disease and Related Disorders Association</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18636"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18638"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001813"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22886559</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver&apos;s licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants&apos; DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">798</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1175</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1973</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIOSH Upper Midwest Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIOSH-UMHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NIOSH_AGCC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health Upper Midwest Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UMHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Upper Midwest Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18636">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0021042"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18638">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_0000530"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18636"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>glioma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3406961/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study included 798 histologically confirmed primary intracranial glioma cases (45 % with proxy respondents) and 1,175 population-based controls, all adult (age 18–80) non-metropolitan residents of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota, and Wisconsin.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18638"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pesticides</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3406961/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The primary objective of the UMHS was to determine if pesticides were associated with an increased risk of glioma, the most common type of brain tumor in adults [13].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2270/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2270_MOESM14_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health Upper Mid-west Health Study 60 NIOSH- UMHS Case-control Hospital- based 298 525 Blood Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota, Wisconsin, USA</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22886559</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of glioma and meta-analysis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22886559</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1007/s00439-012-1212-0</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The mean age of cases ranged from 48.7 years in the NIOSH Upper Midwest Health Study to 73.5 years in the Multi-Ethnic Cohort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver&apos;s licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants&apos; DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15866761</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17131948</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22561519</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22691464</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22715102</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22886559</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">798</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Consenting participants in the original Upper Midwest Health Study; cases diagnosed January1995–January1997 and interviews conducted1995–1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4530494/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among eligible potential participants, 70.4% of 1,669 controls and 91.5% of 872 cases (or their next-of-kin) agreed to participate, resulting in a study population of 1,175 controls and 798 cases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1175</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Consenting participants in the original Upper Midwest Health Study; cases diagnosed January1995–January1997 and interviews conducted1995–1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4530494/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among eligible potential participants, 70.4% of 1,669 controls and 91.5% of 872 cases (or their next-of-kin) agreed to participate, resulting in a study population of 1,175 controls and 798 cases</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1973</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Consenting participants in the original Upper Midwest Health Study; cases diagnosed January1995–January1997 and interviews conducted1995–1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4530494/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The jobs dataset contained 12,145 records (participant-jobs) for 1,967 of the 1,973 participants (6 participants were 16 years of age in 1993 with no jobs recorded), including over 4,000 records of gaps in the work histories.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NIOSH-UMHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
