        <rdfs:comment>In this biomarker sub-study of the Nashville Men&apos;s Health Study (NMHS), we included 494 NMHS participants, consisting of 98 high-grade (Gleason≥7) and 100 low-grade cancer cases, 133 prostate intraepithelial neoplasia (PIN) cases, and 163 controls without cancer or PIN at biopsy.</rdfs:comment>
