    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002168 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002168">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The catalog name &apos;Navrongo Memorial Institute&apos; is not the name of any institution or study found anywhere: Europe PMC has no article containing the phrase. Ghana has a Navrongo Health Research Centre (Navrongo) and a Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research (Accra), which are listed next to each other in MalariaGEN author lists (PMC6914791, PMC4629224), so the name looks like a conflation of the two; this is a guess and cannot be confirmed without the paper the Catalog took it from. NMI is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for &apos;Navrongo Memorial Institute&apos;, an institution name (apparently a garbled one: Ghana&apos;s Navrongo Health Research Centre and Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research are real, a &apos;Navrongo Memorial Institute&apos; is not). The Catalog lists the id in its cohort table but attaches it to no score or sample set, so there is no sample for it to denote, and no paper found by name uses a study sample called NMI. It is an institution name, not a cohort. Named Ghanaian samples COHO already has (AWI-Gen COHO:0000006, whose Ghanaian site is Navrongo; Ghana Prostate Study COHO:0000086; Ghana Breast Health Study COHO:0001333; MalariaGEN COHO:0000294) cannot be tied to the id, so it should not become a synonym of any of them. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Navrongo Memorial Institute</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002169 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002169">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. NNPIO is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the N.N. Petrov Institute of Oncology, St Petersburg, Russia, as a contributing centre of CIMBA: the BRCA1/BRCA2 pathogenic-variant carriers it ascertained and sent to the consortium (PMID:32665703, 28346442). CIMBA&apos;s own lists call the contribution only by the institute&apos;s name, and no paper gives it a study name or a recruitment of its own beyond the institute, so it is a site, not a named cohort (the same judgement as LUHR, E651). Its data are covered by CIMBA (COHO:0000901). It is not the Polish Breast Cancer Study or any other COHO term the triage matched. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete N.N. Petrov Institute of Oncology</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


