        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2249/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2249_MOESM26_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>NOSOS is a population‐based osteoporosis screening programme of postmenopausal females aged 60‐82 years of age at baseline.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002175"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2249/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2249_MOESM26_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>NOSOS North of Scotland Osteoporosis Study Cohort Population‐based UK Aberdeen, Dingwall North‐western European 1,293 NOSOS is a population‐based osteoporosis screening programme of postmenopausal females aged 60‐82 years of age at baseline.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002175"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20966103</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The functional ACTN3 577X variant increases the risk of falling in older females: results from two large independent cohort studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20966103</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20966103+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Case-control analysis was conducted using two large cohorts of Caucasian postmenopausal women--the North of Scotland Osteoporosis Study (n = 1,245) and the Aberdeen Prospective Osteoporosis Screening Study (n = 2,918)--for whom self-reported falls status and DNA samples were available.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002175"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based osteoporosis screening programme of postmenopausal women aged 60-82 at baseline, recruited at centres in Aberdeen and Dingwall in the north of Scotland, who underwent bone mineral density measurement in 2001-2003 and gave questionnaire data and DNA samples.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18633668</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20966103</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2249/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2249_MOESM26_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002175"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1847</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women aged 60-82 screened at baseline, 2001-2003</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1007/s00198-008-0681-4</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The current participants were subjects from the North of Scotland Osteoporosis Study (NOSOS), which is a population-based screening programme for osteoporotic fracture that involved 1,847 women aged 60–82 years at baseline (2001–2003).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002175"/>
