        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.</owl:annotatedTarget>
