        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists&apos; skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.</owl:annotatedTarget>
