    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002199 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002199">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. ODZH is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the Spanish case-control material that deCODE genetics&apos; multi-population cancer GWAS used as a replication group: cancer patients (lung, ovarian and thyroid cancer in the papers read) recruited from the Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital, with controls who attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for other conditions (PMID:21303977, 28195142, 21964575). The papers call it only &apos;the Spanish study population&apos; or &apos;Zaragoza, Spain&apos;, with case recruitment differing by cancer; it has no study name and no design of its own beyond the hospital, so the id denotes a site, not a named cohort (like LUHR, E651, the Landspitali material in the same deCODE papers). No COHO term covers it. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18907"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001615"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000547"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000734</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:11007659</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based familial colorectal cancer registry in Ontario, Canada, one of the sites of the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Colon Cancer Family Registry, which recruited people aged 20 to 74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed from July 1997 to June 2000, identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly sampled from Ontario residents and frequency-matched to the cases by sex and five-year age group, who completed family-history, epidemiologic and food questionnaires and gave blood samples.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1395</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>OFCCR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ontario Familial Colon Cancer Registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ontario Registry for Studies of Familial Colorectal Cancer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ontario Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18907">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18907"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11007659+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ontario Familial Colon Cancer Registry (OFCCR) is a novel registry that collects family history information, epidemiologic data, blood samples and tumour specimens from a population-based sample of colorectal cancer patients and their families.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng2089/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng2089_MOESM20_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The population-based Ontario Cancer Registry (OCR) was used to identify and recruit colorectal cancer cases, aged 20-74 and diagnosed between July 1, 1997 and June 30, 2000.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000547"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng2089/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng2089_MOESM20_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The OFCCR is one of six international sites participating in the Cooperative Familial Registry for Colorectal Studies established by the US National Cancer Institute (http://epi.grants.cancer.gov/CFR/).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000734</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Cumulative Burden of Colorectal Cancer-Associated Genetic Variants Is More Strongly Associated With Early-Onset vs Late-Onset Cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31866242</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:11007659</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Discovery of common and rare genetic risk variants for colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:11007659</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11007659+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ontario Familial Colon Cancer Registry (OFCCR) is a novel registry that collects family history information, epidemiologic data, blood samples and tumour specimens from a population-based sample of colorectal cancer patients and their families.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based familial colorectal cancer registry in Ontario, Canada, one of the sites of the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Colon Cancer Family Registry, which recruited people aged 20 to 74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed from July 1997 to June 2000, identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly sampled from Ontario residents and frequency-matched to the cases by sex and five-year age group, who completed family-history, epidemiologic and food questionnaires and gave blood samples.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17618283</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1395</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Participating OFCCR probands in its first recruitment year</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11007659+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The first-year response rate was 61%, resulting in 1,395 participating probands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200"/>
