    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002203 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002203">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The Columbus-area HNPCC study, one of the named studies behind this id, has no COHO term and no PGS Catalog id of its own; the curator may want to consider it separately if a catalog or resource names it. Ohio_SU is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the Ohio State University&apos;s combined contribution to the colorectal cancer GWAS of Huyghe et al. 2019 (PMID:30510241): cases from two separate named studies, the Columbus-area HNPCC study and the Ohio Colorectal Cancer Prevention Initiative, matched to controls from the OSUMC Human Genetics Sample Bank (Columbus Area Controls Sample Bank). The id names the university, not a study; the combined set has no name or design of its own, and its parts are distinct studies that the Catalog also lists separately (OCCPI, E836, COHO:0002196; OSUMC, E857, judged not a cohort; OSU, E855, the Stefanie Spielman Breast Bank and the Columbus Area Control Sample Bank). So it is not a cohort, and it should not be a synonym of any of those. None of the COHO terms the triage matched (BioVU, TGEN2, York, CRC, etc.) is related. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Ohio State University</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002204 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002204">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002202"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The Ottawa Heart Study of PMID:28209224 cites the design paper of the Ottawa Heart Genomics Study (PMID:17478681) and has its design. Replaced by COHO:0002202 (Ottawa Heart Genomics Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Ottawa Heart Study</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18932"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000350</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:26752265</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre randomised clinical trial at 22 clinical centres in the United States that from 1994 to 1996 enrolled people aged 40 to 80 with ocular hypertension and no evidence of glaucomatous damage, randomised them to topical ocular hypotensive medication or close observation, and followed them for the onset of primary open-angle glaucoma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1637</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>OHTS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18932">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005338"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18932"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>primary open angle glaucoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10326953+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study (OHTS) seeks to evaluate the safety and efficacy of topical ocular hypotensive medication in preventing or delaying the onset of visual field loss and/or optic nerve damage in subjects with ocular hypertension at moderate risk for developing primary open angle glaucoma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11437927/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The OHTS was a prospective, multicenter investigation conducted at 22 centers across the United States, aimed at preventing or delaying the onset of VF loss in individuals with ocular hypertension (OHT).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000350</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of a Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Genetic Risk Score With Earlier Age at Diagnosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31436842</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26752265</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis identifies TXNRD2, ATXN2 and FOXC1 as susceptibility loci for primary open-angle glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26752265</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For all 8 NEIGHBORHOOD studies cases were primarily defined as at least 1 reliable visual field showing loss consistent with glaucoma, without a secondary cause, or CDR (cup-to-disc ratio) ≥ 0.7 or CDR asymmetry ≥ 0.2 or documented progression of optic nerve degeneration (in the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study [OHTS]).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre randomised clinical trial at 22 clinical centres in the United States that from 1994 to 1996 enrolled people aged 40 to 80 with ocular hypertension and no evidence of glaucomatous damage, randomised them to topical ocular hypotensive medication or close observation, and followed them for the onset of primary open-angle glaucoma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:10326953</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:12049574</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39346574</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1637</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people with ocular hypertension randomized at 22 clinical centres, 28 February 1994 to 31 October 1996 (1994-1996)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10326953+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We describe the baseline characteristics of 1637 subjects randomized between February 28, 1994, and October 31, 1996.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002205"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>OHTS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


