    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid18955"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000770</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24064335</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits in randomly recruited, healthy adult Caucasians living in Omaha, Nebraska, United States, and its surrounding areas, screened by exclusion criteria for chronic and metabolic diseases, with bone mineral density and body composition measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Its unrelated genotyped members formed genome-wide association samples for obesity-related traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1879</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>OOS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Omaha osteoporosis study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Omaha Osteoporosis Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid18955">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005298"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18955"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>osteoporosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6707235/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study used 11,315 randomly recruited Caucasian subjects, from three cross-sectional study cohorts: 5,939 from the Louisiana Osteoporosis Study (LOS, New Orleans and Baton Rouge area, Coordinates: ~30oN~90–91oW)39, 3,497 from the Kansas City Osteoporosis Study (KCOS, Kansas City area, Coordinates: ~39oN~94oW)40, and 1,879 from the Omaha Osteoporosis Study (OOS, Omaha area, Coordinates: ~41oN~96oW)41.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2900891/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All of the chosen subjects were US Caucasians of Northern European origin living in Omaha, NE, USA, and its surrounding areas.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000770</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Challenge of Stratifying Obesity: Attempts in the Quebec Family Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31649740</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24064335</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Meta-analysis of genome-wide association data identifies novel susceptibility loci for obesity.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24064335</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3888264/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The three in-house samples included those from the Omaha Osteoporosis Study (OOS, with 998 unrelated Caucasian subjects), Kansas-City Osteoporosis Study (KCOS, with 2283 unrelated Caucasian subjects) and China Osteoporosis Study (COS, with 1624 unrelated Chinese Han subjects).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits in randomly recruited, healthy adult Caucasians living in Omaha, Nebraska, United States, and its surrounding areas, screened by exclusion criteria for chronic and metabolic diseases, with bone mineral density and body composition measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Its unrelated genotyped members formed genome-wide association samples for obesity-related traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18325910</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31444391</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1879</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>randomly recruited Caucasian adults of the OOS in a 2019 analysis of the group&apos;s three osteoporosis cohorts</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6707235/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study used 11,315 randomly recruited Caucasian subjects, from three cross-sectional study cohorts: 5,939 from the Louisiana Osteoporosis Study (LOS, New Orleans and Baton Rouge area, Coordinates: ~30oN~90–91oW)39, 3,497 from the Kansas City Osteoporosis Study (KCOS, Kansas City area, Coordinates: ~39oN~94oW)40, and 1,879 from the Omaha Osteoporosis Study (OOS, Omaha area, Coordinates: ~41oN~96oW)41.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>OOS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


