        <obo:IAO_0000116>fallopian tube cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle (OPAL) study is a national prospective cohort of Australian women aged 21-79 years diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal, or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18965"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>epithelial ovarian cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle (OPAL) study is a national prospective cohort of Australian women aged 21-79 years diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal, or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18967"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>primary peritoneal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle (OPAL) study is a national prospective cohort of Australian women aged 21-79 years diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal, or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid18969"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifestyle</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33144284+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the prospective Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle (OPAL) study, diet-quality scores were calculated using data from food frequency questionnaires completed pre-diagnosis (n = 650) and 12 months&apos; post-diagnosis (n = 503).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33034053+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We investigated the potential survival benefit of statins in women with ovarian cancer using data from the Ovarian cancer Prognosis and Lifestyle study, a prospective study of Australian women aged 18 to 79 years, diagnosed with ovarian cancer from 2012 to 2015 and followed for 5 to 8 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36744914</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common analgesics and ovarian cancer survival: the Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle (OPAL) Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36744914</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle (OPAL) study is a national prospective cohort of Australian women aged 21-79 years diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal, or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national prospective population-based cohort of Australian women diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015, run from QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, who completed questionnaires at recruitment and repeatedly during follow-up and whose medical records were abstracted, to study how lifestyle factors relate to outcomes after an ovarian cancer diagnosis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33034053</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36744914</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40118516</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">958</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>OPAL women who consented to participate following diagnoses in 2012-2015</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Overall, 958 women (78% of those approached) consented to participate (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>OPAL</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
