    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19169"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19171"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19173"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS004611</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37188791</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4505</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pathways</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pathways study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pathways Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19169">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0006256"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19171">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000021"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19173">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000039"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19169"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>invasive breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eligibility includes any woman diagnosed with invasive breast cancer within KPNC, no previous diagnosis of other invasive cancer, age 21 years or older, and ability to speak English, Spanish, Cantonese, or Mandarin.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19171"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>diet</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim of one such study, the Pathways Study, is to examine the effect on recurrence and survival of 1) lifestyle factors such as diet, physical activity, quality of life, and use of complementary and alternative medicine (CAM) and 2) molecular factors such as genetic polymorphisms involved in metabolism of chemotherapeutic agents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19173"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>physical activity</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim of one such study, the Pathways Study, is to examine the effect on recurrence and survival of 1) lifestyle factors such as diet, physical activity, quality of life, and use of complementary and alternative medicine (CAM) and 2) molecular factors such as genetic polymorphisms involved in metabolism of chemotherapeutic agents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10185660/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Whereas UK Biobank is a population-wide biobanking initiative, Pathways is a breast cancer-specific study that recruited consecutive cases from a single healthcare system in the U.S.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004611</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Development and testing of a polygenic risk score for breast cancer aggressiveness.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37188791</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37188791</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Development and testing of a polygenic risk score for breast cancer aggressiveness.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37188791</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10185660/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Pathways Study is a longitudinal cohort of women diagnosed with breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18478338</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4505</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer enrolled 2006-2013</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10799916/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Pathways Study is a prospective cohort of 4,505 women newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer enrolled between 2006 and 2013 in Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Pathways</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
