    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19209"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000752"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000733</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37264206</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18882</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PCPT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SWOG-PCPT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19209">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19209"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3058741/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The foundation of this risk-modeling program, the PCPT, was designed to establish whether finasteride, a 5α-reductase type II inhibitor, prevents prostate cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3058741/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1994 and 1997, 18,882 men from 210 study sites located throughout the United States and Canada were randomized in the PCPT to either the finasteride or placebo arm and followed yearly with a digital rectal exam (DRE) and PSA determination.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000733</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>African-specific improvement of a polygenic hazard score for age at diagnosis of prostate cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32930425</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37264206</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetically adjusted PSA levels for prostate cancer screening.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37264206</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10287565/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PCPT is a completed phase 3 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of finasteride for prostate cancer prevention that began in 1993 (ref. 8).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21149329</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21667068</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22810146</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18882</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>men randomized in PCPT (1994–1997)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3058741/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1994 and 1997, 18,882 men from 210 study sites located throughout the United States and Canada were randomized in the PCPT to either the finasteride or placebo arm and followed yearly with a digital rectal exam (DRE) and PSA determination.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PCPT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
