    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19241"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24096698</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and giving blood samples.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">551</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1925</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PECS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Polish Endometrial Cancer study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Polish Endometrial Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19241">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011962"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19241"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>endometrial cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Eligible cases were diagnosed with incident pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our study subjects were derived from the Polish Endometrial Cancer Study, a large, population-based, endometrial case-control study (18) conducted among women residing in two Polish cities, Warsaw and Lodz, from 2001 to 2003.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24096698</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of endometrial cancer in E2C2.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24096698</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898362/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Seven participating studies, including four cohort [California Teacher’s Study (CTS), Nurses’ Health Study (NHS), Multiethnic Cohort (MEC), Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO)] and three case–control studies [Connecticut Endometrial Cancer (CONN), Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center (FHCRC), Polish Endometrial Cancer Study (PECS)], were genotyped in Stage 1 (2,695 cases, 2,777 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute&apos;s Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and giving blood samples.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22730518</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24096698</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41094331</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">551</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PECS cases and controls interviewed in the original 2001-2003 study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 551 of 695 eligible cases (79.3%) and 1925 of 2843 eligible controls (67.7%) were interviewed about demographic factors, reproductive history, exogenous hormone use, lifetime body size and physical activity, and medical history.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1925</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PECS cases and controls interviewed in the original 2001-2003 study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 551 of 695 eligible cases (79.3%) and 1925 of 2843 eligible controls (67.7%) were interviewed about demographic factors, reproductive history, exogenous hormone use, lifetime body size and physical activity, and medical history.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245"/>
