    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19299"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000558"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000539"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000758</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21977987</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial&apos;s participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union&apos;s Seventh Framework Programme.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5244</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PHASE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PHArmacogenetic study of Statin in the Elderly at risk</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PHArmacogenomic study of Statins in the Elderly at risk for CHD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PHArmacogenomic study of Statins in the Elderly at risk for cardiovascular disease</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROSPER/PHASE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PHArmacogenetic study of Statins in the Elderly at risk</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19299">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005385"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19299"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>vascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Men and women aged 70-82 years were recruited if they had pre-existing vascular disease or were at increased risk of such disease because of smoking, hypertension, or diabetes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between December 1997 and May 1999, we screened and enrolled subjects in Scotland, Ireland, and the Netherlands.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000539"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PHArmacogenetic study of Statins in the Elderly at risk (PHASE) is a genome wide association study in the PROspective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at risk for vascular disease (PROSPER) that investigates the genetic variation responsible for the individual variation in drug response to pravastatin.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000758</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A Polygenic Risk Score to Predict Future Adult Short Stature Among Children.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33788949</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21977987</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Replication of LDL GWAs hits in PROSPER/PHASE as validation for future (pharmaco)genetic analyses.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21977987</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With the GWAS in the PROSPER/PHASE study we confirm the previously found genetic associations with LDL-cholesterol levels.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial&apos;s participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union&apos;s Seventh Framework Programme.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21977987</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5244</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PROSPER participants with genome-wide genotypes passing quality control</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After a stringent quality control 557,192 SNPs in 5,244 subjects were available for analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PHASE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PROSPER/PHASE</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002253 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002253">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000383"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. PHBB is the Mass General Brigham Biobank&apos;s contribution to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative, drawn from the biobank&apos;s own participants (PMID:36013271). The Catalog&apos;s name is that of the COVID-19 analysis and is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0000383 (Mass General Brigham Biobank), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Mass General Brigham - Host Vulnerability to COVID-19</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002254 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002254">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Pirkanmaa Hospital District (PHD) is the Finnish health-care district around Tampere, not a study. The PGS Catalog id is its label for 2283 clinically diagnosed prostate cancer cases from the district&apos;s hospital (Tampere University Hospital) in PMID:33051487 (E895.4, Table 1 &apos;Clinical cases (Pirkanmaa Hospital)&apos;), used with FinRSPC cases and controls in a PRS evaluation; the paper gives the case series no study name or recruitment design of its own. The FinRSPC part is a separate id. Other papers found by the name use the district only as a place. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Pirkanmaa Hospital District</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


