    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002269">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Poland is a country: the PGS Catalog cohort id Poland is the PRACTICAL consortium’s label for a prostate cancer case-control sample from the University Hospital in Szczecin (The Poland Group) and, in a breast cancer score, another Polish sample, neither a cohort with a name of its own. Found by the review of 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Poland</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002270 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002270">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002170"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. POLYGENE is the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium&apos;s Nijmegen study NTH (&apos;Nijmegen Polygene Study &amp; Nijmegen Biomedical Study POLYGENE NTH Netherlands&apos;, PMID:21639959), which the consortium&apos;s later tables call the Nijmegen Ovarian Cancer Study. Replaced by COHO:0002170 (Nijmegen Ovarian Cancer Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Nijmegen Polygene Study &amp; Nijmegen Biomedical Study</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19401"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000020"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000344</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32424353</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort of women in the United Kingdom diagnosed with a first primary breast cancer at age 40 or younger, recruited between June 2001 and December 2007 (with an additional category of BRCA1 or BRCA2 carriers diagnosed at 41 to 50), with family history, epidemiological and clinical data and blood collected and annual follow-up, to establish whether genetic status influences breast cancer prognosis independently of known prognostic factors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3021</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3021</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>POSH</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>POSH study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Study of Outcomes in Sporadic Versus Hereditary Breast Cancer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Study of Outcomes in Sporadic Versus Hereditary Breast Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Study of Outcomes in Sporadic and Hereditary Breast Cancer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Study of Outcomes in Sporadic versus Hereditary Breast Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prospective study of Outcomes in Sporadic versus Hereditary breast cancer</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19401">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007254"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19401"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5805863/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients were eligible if they were diagnosed with invasive breast cancer aged 40 years or younger.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3632836/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Three thousand nine hundred and sixty breast cancer cases were used in stage 1, of which 3,652 were from cancer genetics clinics in the UK recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study (FBCS) and 308 were from oncology clinics in the UK recruited through the Prospective study of Outcomes in Sporadic versus Hereditary breast cancer (POSH) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European polygenic risk score for prediction of breast cancer shows similar performance in Asian women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32737321</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32424353</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies 32 novel breast cancer susceptibility loci from overall and subtype-specific analyses.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32424353</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7808397/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>BCAC DACC approval is required to access data from the ABCFS, ABCS, ABCTB, BBCC, BBCS, BCEES, BCFR-NY, BCFR-PA, BCFR-UT, BCINIS, BSUCH, CBCS, CECILE, CGPS, CTS, DIETCOMPLYF, ESTHER, GC-HBOC, GENICA, GEPARSIXTO, GESBC, HABCS, HCSC, HEBCS, HMBCS, HUBCS, KARBAC, KBCP, LMBC, MABCS, MARIE, MBCSG, MCBCS, MISS, MMHS, MTLGEBCS, NC-BCFR, OFBCR, ORIGO, pKARMA, POSH, PREFACE, RBCS, SKKDKFZS, SUCCESSB, SUCCESSC, SZBCS, TNBCC, UCIBCS, UKBGS and UKOPS studies (Supplementary Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort of women in the United Kingdom diagnosed with a first primary breast cancer at age 40 or younger, recruited between June 2001 and December 2007 (with an additional category of BRCA1 or BRCA2 carriers diagnosed at 41 to 50), with family history, epidemiological and clinical data and blood collected and annual follow-up, to establish whether genetic status influences breast cancer prognosis independently of known prognostic factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17697367</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20453838</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3021</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>eligible POSH women aged 40 or younger recruited January 2000-January 2008</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5805863/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between Jan 24, 2000, and Jan 24, 2008, we recruited 3021 eligible women, of whom 2733 (91%) were included in the analysis population, and 288 (9%) were excluded (figure 1; appendix p 11).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
