    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002273 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002273">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001188"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog id PoWHDR is not attached to any score or sample set in the Catalog&apos;s current data (REST /cohort/PoWHDR returns nothing; absent from cohort_papers.json), and Europe PMC has no paper with the exact phrase, so the PGS paper that used it could not be read; the identification rests on the name. The Prince of Wales Hospital (Shatin, the teaching hospital of the Chinese University of Hong Kong) runs one diabetes registry: the Hong Kong Diabetes Register/Registry (HKDR), &apos;established as a quality improvement program at the Prince of Wales Hospital since 1995&apos; (PMID:24376643). &apos;Prince of Wales Hospital Diabetes Registry&apos; is the Catalog&apos;s name for that register, which COHO already has as COHO:0001188 (whose definition already names the Prince of Wales Hospital). Add PoWHDR and the Catalog name to it; retire the placeholder. Replaced by COHO:0001188 (Hong Kong Diabetes Register), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Prince of Wales Hospital Diabetes Registry</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


