        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19480"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>training load</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11062611/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These international multicenter prospective trials aimed to investigate the effect of training load and genotype on the variability of structural, functional, and electrical exercise-induced cardiac remodeling in elite competitive endurance athletes, and the full study protocol has been detailed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19482"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>arrhythmias</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12305178/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ProAFHeart study is a multicentre prospective trial aiming to determine the prevalence and 2-year incidence of arrhythmias and athletic remodeling in endurance athletes 16–80 years of age.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11062611/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The athletes were enrolled to undergo the study investigations at 1 of 5 medical research facilities: (1) Baker Heart and Diabetes Institute, Melbourne, Australia; (2) Royal Adelaide Hospital, Adelaide, Australia; (3) Gasthuisberg University Hospital, Leuven, Belgium; (4) Jessa Ziekenhuis, Hasselt, Belgium; and (5) Universitair Ziekenhuis Antwerpen, Antwerp, Belgium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000666</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Reduced Ejection Fraction in Elite Endurance Athletes: Clinical and Genetic Overlap With Dilated Cardiomyopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38109351</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38109351</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Reduced Ejection Fraction in Elite Endurance Athletes: Clinical and Genetic Overlap With Dilated Cardiomyopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38109351</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11062611/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study cohort consisted of elite competitive endurance athletes from the Pro@Heart (Prospective Athletic Heart) and ProAFHeart (Prospective Atrial Fibrillation Athletic Heart) studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40273982</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ProAFHeart</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ProAFheart</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19490"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000742</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33623038</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5779</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROCAP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROCAP study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROgression in CAncer of the Prostate</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROgression in Cancer of the Prostate</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Progression in Cancer of the Prostate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19490">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19490"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>localized prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, study participants were derived from a retrospective nationwide cohort study of men with localized prostate cancer, the National Prostate Cancer Register (NPCR) of Sweden Follow-up Study (Stattin et al., 2008).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Men in the NPCR of Sweden Follow-up Study who were still alive in 2007 (n = 7075) were eligible for and invited to participate in the PROCAP study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7012357/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Men in the NPCR of Sweden Follow-up Study who were still alive in 2007 (n = 7075) were eligible for and invited to participate in the PROCAP study. In total, 5779 (82%) men agreed to participate in PROCAP.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000742</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Additional SNPs improve risk stratification of a polygenic hazard score for prostate cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33420416</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33623038</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic hazard score is associated with prostate cancer in multi-ethnic populations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33623038</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We thank and acknowledge all of the participants in the PROCAP study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31343436</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5779</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>PROCAP men who agreed to participate in 2007–2008</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 5779 (82%) men agreed to participate in PROCAP.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
