    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19499"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000103"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:23785401</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1002</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGEMUS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGEMUS Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGEMUS Group</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGEMUS study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROgnostic GEnetic factors in MUltiple Sclerosis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prognostic Genetic factors in Multiple Sclerosis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19499">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005301"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19499"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>multiple sclerosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681825/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1347 consecutive Italian MS patients diagnosed according to McDonald criteria [4], were ascertained by two Italian consortia, PROGEMUS (N = 1002), and PROGRESSO (N = 345).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Patients were collected from Continental Italy (excluding Sardinia) as part of the PROGEMUS (PROgnostic GEnetic factors in MUltiple Sclerosis) project, 87% of cases were collected in North-West Italy (Novara, Torino, Milano, Pavia) and 13% in Central Italy (Rome).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:23785401</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of genetic markers with CSF oligoclonal bands in multiple sclerosis patients.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23785401</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681825/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1347 consecutive Italian MS patients diagnosed according to McDonald criteria [4], were ascertained by two Italian consortia, PROGEMUS (N = 1002), and PROGRESSO (N = 345).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21833088</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23785401</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29587799</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38927672</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1002</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>consecutive MS patients ascertained by PROGEMUS in the example study (PMID:23785401)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681825/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1347 consecutive Italian MS patients diagnosed according to McDonald criteria [4], were ascertained by two Italian consortia, PROGEMUS (N = 1002), and PROGRESSO (N = 345).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PROGEMUS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19506"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:19279319</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genetic study of familial Parkinson&apos;s disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson&apos;s disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson&apos;s disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1497</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGENI</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGENI Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGENI study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Parkinson&apos;s Research: The Organized GENetics Initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Parkinsons Research: The Organized Genetics Initiative</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Parkinson&apos;s Research: The Organized Genetics Initiative</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19506">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005180"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19506"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Parkinson disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2690967/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As part of an ongoing study designed to identify genes contributing to PD susceptibility (PROGENI Study), subjects with PD were recruited through the Parkinson Study Group (PSG), a network of 65 participating clinical centers located throughout North America.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4946647/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The setting was among individuals with familial PD enrolled from academic movement disorder specialty clinics across the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19279319</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Variation in GIGYF2 is not associated with Parkinson disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19279319</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2690967/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As part of an ongoing study designed to identify genes contributing to PD susceptibility (PROGENI Study), subjects with PD were recruited through the Parkinson Study Group (PSG), a network of 65 participating clinical centers located throughout North America.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genetic study of familial Parkinson&apos;s disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson&apos;s disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson&apos;s disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18987351</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19279319</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26595808</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1497</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>members of the 566 multiplex PD families in the study&apos;s entire sample (1,324 reported to have PD), 2009</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2690967/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our entire sample of 566 multiplex PD families, consisting of 1,497 members, including 1,324 reported to have PD, were genotyped for the seven GIGYF2 point mutations previously reported12 as well as the three novel missense variants we identified through sequencing.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PROGENI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


