        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000137</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:36355370</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGRESSA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROGRESSA study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Progression Risk Of Glaucoma: RElevant SNPs with Significant Association</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Progression Risk Of Glaucoma; RElevant SNPs with Significant Association</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Progression Risk of Glaucoma: RElevant SNPs with Significant Association</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Progression Risk of Glaucoma: Relevant SNPs with Significant Association</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Progression Risk of Glaucoma: Relevant SNPs With Significant Association</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19525">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005338"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19525"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>primary open angle glaucoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35970205+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study combined a retrospective longitudinal analysis of suspect and early manifest primary open angle glaucoma cases from the Progression Risk of Glaucoma: RElevant SNPs with Significant Association (PROGRESSA) study with 2 replication cohorts from the UK Biobank and the Canadian Longitudinal Study of Ageing (CLSA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559075/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PROGRESSA study is a longitudinal, prospective, multicenter observational cohort study of patients with early glaucoma and patients with suspected glaucoma in Australia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000137</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of High Polygenic Risk With Visual Field Worsening Despite Treatment in Early Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36355370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36355370</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of High Polygenic Risk With Visual Field Worsening Despite Treatment in Early Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36355370</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36355370+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This cohort study used clinical and genetic data obtained from a longitudinal cohort study, Progression Risk of Glaucoma: Relevant SNPs With Significant Association (PROGRESSA).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30517101</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36246177</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36249683</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals with suspect or early manifest glaucoma (stated as a lower bound, &apos;&gt;2000&apos;), 2022</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9560531/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PROGRESSA study is a prospective longitudinal cohort study of &gt;2000 individuals with suspect or early manifest glaucoma that was designed to investigate genetic and clinical associations with glaucoma progression (as previously described).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PROGRESSA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
