    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002286 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002286">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002284"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-28. same cohort as review name E926. Same Santiago de Compostela, Spain prostate-cancer study as E926 (both PGS Catalog ids trace to the same PROGReSS entry in the same OncoArray consortium supplementary tables); see E926&apos;s note for the identity and naming caveat. Checked 2026-09-25: None: PROGReSS_PrCa is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the Santiago de Compostela prostate cancer study PROGReSS, the same study as E926 (PROGRESS). Both ids are recorded in papers on the prostate cancer OncoArray data, where the only PROGReSS is the hospital-based study at the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago de Compostela. The Catalog&apos;s name for this id, &apos;Prostate Cancer Group, Santiago, Spain&apos;, is the study-group name the PGS000742 paper&apos;s table gives PROGReSS (PMID:33420416 supplement) and is kept as a synonym on E926. Same as E926; merge this placeholder (COHO:0002286) into E926&apos;s term (COHO:0002284), whose acronyms include PROGReSS_PrCa. Curated 2026-09-28: Merged into COHO:0002284 after confirming the same Spanish prostate study in the OncoArray source; both PGS ids and the source-attested study-group name are retained on the survivor. Replaced by COHO:0002284 (PROGReSS study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by the checks of the placeholders&apos; names against their sources recorded in the pipeline repository, completed 2026-09-28.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Prostate Cancer Group, Santiago, Spain</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19533"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000666</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38109351</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PROspective ATHletic Heart study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pro@Heart</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pro@Heart study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Athlete’s Heart study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Athletic Heart</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Prospective Athletic Heart study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Prospective Athletic Heart Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19533">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19533"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>training load</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11062611/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These international multicenter prospective trials aimed to investigate the effect of training load and genotype on the variability of structural, functional, and electrical exercise-induced cardiac remodeling in elite competitive endurance athletes, and the full study protocol has been detailed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Pro@Heart (Prospective Athlete’s Heart) study is an international multicentre prospective cohort trial with collaborators in Australia (Baker Heart and Diabetes Institute Melbourne, St Vincent’s Hospital Melbourne, University of Adelaide, Royal Adelaide Hospital, Royal Melbourne Hospital and Victor Chang Cardiac Research Institute) and Belgium (University Hospitals Leuven, University Hospital Antwerp and Jessa Hospital Hasselt).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000666</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Reduced Ejection Fraction in Elite Endurance Athletes: Clinical and Genetic Overlap With Dilated Cardiomyopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38109351</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38109351</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Reduced Ejection Fraction in Elite Endurance Athletes: Clinical and Genetic Overlap With Dilated Cardiomyopathy.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38109351</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11062611/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study cohort consisted of elite competitive endurance athletes from the Pro@Heart (Prospective Athletic Heart) and ProAFHeart (Prospective Atrial Fibrillation Athletic Heart) studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35368514</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Pro@Heart</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19540"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:18835935</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1321</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project SuGAR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project SuGAR registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project Sugar</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Project_SuGAR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>project SuGAR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19540">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19540"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes mellitus</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4215639/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Project SuGAR enlisted medical clinics, churches, and established organizations on the Sea Islands to aid in identifying patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus who belonged to families with multiple affected biological members.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25279862+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1995 and 2003, 1321 Gullah African Americans with a high prevalence of diabetes mellitus from the South Carolina Sea Islands consented to and enrolled in the Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry (Project SuGAR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:18835935</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide linkage scan in Gullah-speaking African American families with type 2 diabetes: the Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry (Project SuGAR).</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18835935</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2606883/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Affected relative pairs with type 2 diabetes were recruited through the Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry (Project SuGAR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:18835935</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19783527</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25279862</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1321</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Gullah African Americans enrolled 1995-2003</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25279862</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1995 and 2003, 1321 Gullah African Americans with a high prevalence of diabetes mellitus from the South Carolina Sea Islands consented to and enrolled in the Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry (Project SuGAR).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
