    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19577"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The final sample for analysis consisted of 3,897 subjects, i.e., 1,916 prostate cancer cases and 1,985 population controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19579"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental and lifestyle factors</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Prostate Cancer &amp; Environment Study (PROtEuS), described previously (Blanc-Lapierre et al., 2015), is a population-based case-control study conducted in Montreal, Canada, to assess the role of environmental and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer risk.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24655933+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>PROtEuS (Prostate Cancer and Environment Study), a population-based case-control study set amongst the mainly French-speaking population in Montréal, Canada, was used to address study objectives.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000733</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>African-specific improvement of a polygenic hazard score for age at diagnosis of prostate cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32930425</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32930425</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>African-specific improvement of a polygenic hazard score for age at diagnosis of prostate cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32930425</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8135907/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>PROtEuS was supported financially through grants from the Canadian Cancer Society [13149, 19500, 19864, 19865] and the Cancer Research Society, in partnership with the Ministère de l&apos;enseignement supérieur, de la recherche, de la science et de la technologie du Québec, and the Fonds de la recherche du Québec - Santé.PROtEuS would like to thank its collaborators and research personnel, and the urologists involved in subjects recruitment.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal&apos;s French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24655933</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30233396</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
