        <owl:annotatedTarget>A double-blind randomised trial in patients hospitalised for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days that compared standard statin therapy (pravastatin 40 mg daily) with intensive statin therapy (atorvastatin 80 mg daily), and long-term treatment with the antibiotic gatifloxacin with placebo, for the prevention of death and major cardiovascular events.</owl:annotatedTarget>
