        <owl:annotatedTarget>PSC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002296 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002296">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog id PSEU is not attached to any score or sample set in the Catalog&apos;s current data (REST /cohort/PSEU returns nothing; absent from cohort_papers.json), so the Catalog paper that used it could not be read; the identification of the sample rests on the name, which matches the restless legs syndrome sample of Emory University&apos;s Department of Neurology and Program in Sleep. The Program in Sleep at Emory University is a clinical sleep programme in Atlanta (United States), not a study. The only sample of that name found is the restless legs syndrome case-control collection of the Department of Neurology and Program in Sleep, which the RLS GWAS PMID:33239738 calls just &apos;Emory cohort&apos; / &apos;US Emory&apos; (1417 subjects, 696 RLS cases): a clinic&apos;s sample with no study name of its own, like the other place-named samples judged not to be cohorts (e.g. KULEUVEN, Toronto). The Catalog id presumably denotes that collection in an RLS polygenic score paper that could not be identified. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Program in Sleep at Emory University</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002297 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002297">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The Perlegen Sciences genotyped discovery samples are the discovery sample of the psoriasis GWAS of the Collaborative Association Study of Psoriasis (&apos;Perlegen Sciences (Mountain View, CA, USA) genotyped discovery samples&apos;, PMID:19169254). The Catalog&apos;s name describes that sample and is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0001152 (Collaborative Association Study of Psoriasis), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Perlegen Sciences Genotyped Discovery Samples</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19616"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19618"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kenya"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22915813</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PSWC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pumwani Sex Worker Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pumwani cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pumwani sex worker Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pumwani sex worker cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Pumwani sex workers cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
