    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19652"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19654"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000339</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:32716505</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases&apos; relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2118</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15907</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>QFMP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Queensland familial melanoma project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Queensland Familial Melanoma Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19652">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005012"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19654">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_0000006"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19652"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cutaneous melanoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8791274+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After obtaining doctor&apos;s consent, a brief family history questionnaire was mailed to all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19654"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>solar ultraviolet radiation</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8791274+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Queensland Familial Melanoma Project was undertaken to investigate (a) the role of genetic susceptibility as indicated by skin type, pigmentation and the prevalence of naevi and (b) exposure to solar ultraviolet radiation, and their interaction in the aetiology of familial melanoma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4065098/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Samples were ascertained as part of the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project (QFMP), a population based study of melanoma in Queensland, Australia [26].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000339</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiplex melanoma families are enriched for polygenic risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32716505</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:32716505</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Multiplex melanoma families are enriched for polygenic risk.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32716505</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7566496/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Family members with melanoma from the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project (QFMP) had significantly higher scores compared to both unrelated melanoma cases and healthy controls (Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases&apos; relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8791274</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2118</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>QFMP family-study persons and melanoma index cases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8791274+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The final sample comprises 15,907 persons in the 1,912 families of 2,118 melanoma cases, including 509 families in which there are two or more individuals with confirmed melanoma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">15907</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>QFMP family-study persons and melanoma index cases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8791274+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The final sample comprises 15,907 persons in the 1,912 families of 2,118 melanoma cases, including 509 families in which there are two or more individuals with confirmed melanoma.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>QFMP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19663"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000558"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000770</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31649740</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1650</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>QFS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Québec Family Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Quebec Family Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19663">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011122"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19663"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>obesity</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24533236+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The cohort is a mixture of random sampling and ascertainment through obese individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Canada"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Quebec Family Study (QFS) was an observational study with three cycles of data collection between 1979 and 2002 in Quebec City, Canada.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000770</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Challenge of Stratifying Obesity: Attempts in the Quebec Family Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31649740</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31649740</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Challenge of Stratifying Obesity: Attempts in the Quebec Family Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31649740</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31649740+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 231 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNP) significantly associated to body mass index (BMI) from 21 genome-wide association studies were genotyped or imputed in 881 subjects from the Quebec Family Study (QFS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24533236</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1650</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals from 375 families recruited in phase 1 (1979-1982); obesity-ascertained families added in later phases are not counted</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24533236</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In phase 1 of the study (1979 to 1982), a total of 1650 individuals from 375 families (nuclear families with biological or adopted offspring and uncle/aunt when available) were recruited and assessed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>QFS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304 -->

