        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union&apos;s Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
