        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.</owl:annotatedTarget>
