    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19839"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid19841"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:39968102</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3040</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ROAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ROAD study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Research on Osteoarthritis Against Disability</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Research on Osteoarthritis Against Disability study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Research on Osteoarthritis/Osteoporosis Against Disability study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Research on Osteoarthritis/Osteoporosis Against Disability</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19839">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005178"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid19841">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005298"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19839"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>osteoarthritis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2005, we established a large-scale population-based OA cohort study called the Research on Osteoarthritis/Osteoporosis Against Disability (ROAD) with the goal of establishing epidemiologic indices to evaluate clinical evidence for the development of a disease-modifying treatment for skeletal diseases [6,7].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid19841"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>osteoporosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2005, we established a large-scale population-based OA cohort study called the Research on Osteoarthritis/Osteoporosis Against Disability (ROAD) with the goal of establishing epidemiologic indices to evaluate clinical evidence for the development of a disease-modifying treatment for skeletal diseases [6,7].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ROAD study was a prospective investigation of OA conducted among population-based cohorts in various cities across Japan.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:39968102</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Trends in knee osteoarthritis prevalence over a 10-year period in Japan: The ROAD study 2005-2015.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39968102</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study aimed to reveal trends in the prevalence and distribution of knee OA and symptomatic knee OA using cohorts from the ROAD study at the baseline survey and the fourth survey, which was conducted 10 years after the initial survey.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19410032</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39968102</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3040</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>residents enrolled at the baseline survey in three communities (2005-2007)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We initially enrolled 3040 participants (1061 men and 1979 women; mean age 70.3 years; range 23–95 years) during the baseline period and have since conducted multiple follow-up surveys since 2005.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ROAD</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


