    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20047"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>myopia</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1772924/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Children aged 7–9 years from three Singapore schools were invited to participate in the SCORM (Singapore Cohort study Of the Risk factors for Myopia) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Singapore"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7726587/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SCORM study was initiated in three schools in Singapore from 1999 to 2001.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27780307</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The contribution of recently identified adult BMI risk loci to paediatric obesity in a Singaporean Chinese childhood dataset.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27780307</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27780307+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We evaluated for paediatric obesity associations at these risk loci utilizing genome-wide data from Chinese childhood subjects in the Singapore Cohort study Of the Risk factors for Myopia study (N = 1006).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16234459</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33344056</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1979</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children aged 7-9 who agreed to participate at baseline (1999-2001)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1772924/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>There were 1979 children who agreed to participate (participation rate = 70.2%): 665 myopic (spherical equivalent (SE) at least −0.5 dioptres) children and 1314 non-myopic children at baseline.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SCORM</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20054"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20056"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000752"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000733</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:29117387</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">416</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">429</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">845</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SCPCS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">South Carolina Prostate Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20054">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20056">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000015"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20054"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This population-based case–control study of prostate cancer among men aged 65–79 years was conducted between 2000 and 2002 in South Carolina.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20056"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>lifestyle</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We investigated the association between lifestyle and prostate cancer risk among Caucasian and African– American men, separately.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16912087+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This population-based case-control study had information on farming-related activities for 405 incident prostate cancer cases and 392 controls matched for age, race and region in South Carolina, USA, from 1999 to 2001.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000733</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>African-specific improvement of a polygenic hazard score for age at diagnosis of prostate cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32930425</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29117387</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Two Novel Susceptibility Loci for Prostate Cancer in Men of African Ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29117387</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5448553/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SCPCS: SCPCS is funded by CDC grant S1135-19/19, and SCPCS sample preparation was conducted at the Epidemiology Biospecimen Core Lab that is supported in part by the Vanderbilt-Ingram Cancer Center (P30 CA68485).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15150583</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15280622</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16912087</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29117387</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">416</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>eligible final case-control study sample after recruitment exclusions (2000–2002)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After eliminating 59 subjects (7 cases and 52 controls) who had prevalent prostate cancer and three subjects (2 cases and 1 control) who completed fewer than five questions, the final sample size was 845 subjects (416 cases, 429 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">429</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>eligible final case-control study sample after recruitment exclusions (2000–2002)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>After eliminating 59 subjects (7 cases and 52 controls) who had prevalent prostate cancer and three subjects (2 cases and 1 control) who completed fewer than five questions, the final sample size was 845 subjects (416 cases, 429 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">845</owl:annotatedTarget>
