    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20066"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22158537</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1019</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1710</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2729</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SDGS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Diabetes GWAS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Diabetes Genetics Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Diabetes Genome-Wide Association Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Shanghai Diabetes Genetic Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20066">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20066"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 590,887 SNPs genotyped in 1,019 T2D cases and 1,710 controls selected from Chinese women in Shanghai, we selected the top 2,100 SNPs that were not in linkage disequilibrium (r2&lt;0.2) with known T2D loci for in silico replication in three T2D GWAS conducted among European Americans, Koreans, and Singapore Chinese.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3600840/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This analysis included a total of 6929 women from Shanghai, China who are participants of three ongoing GWAS: (i) the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study (SBCGS) (Zheng et al., 2009), (ii) the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Genetics Study (SECGS) (Delahanty et al., 2011; Long et al., 2012) and (iii) the Shanghai Diabetes Genetics Study (SDGS) (Shu et al., 2010).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22158537</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies identifies eight new loci for type 2 diabetes in east Asians.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22158537</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3582398/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These eight studies included 6,952 T2D cases and 11,865 controls from the Korea Association Resource Study (KARE), the Singapore Diabetes Cohort Study (SDCS), the Singapore Prospective Study Program (SP2), the Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES), the Japan Cardiometabolic Genome Epidemiology Network(CAGE), the Shanghai Diabetes Genetic Study (SDGS), the Taiwan T2D Study (TDS), and the Cebu Longitudinal Health and Nutritional Survey (CLHNS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20862305</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22158264</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23406970</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
