        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4168820/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participating studies (grant support) in the Shanghai Genome-Wide Association Studies (SGWAS) are as follows: Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study (R37CA070867 to W.Z.), Shanghai Men′s Health Study (R01CA082729 to X.-O.S.), Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (R01CA064277 to X.-O.S.) and Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (R01CA092585 to X.-O.S.).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000795"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Shanghai genome-wide association studies include participants of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (SECS), Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002347"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Shanghai genome-wide association studies include participants of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (SECS), Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Shanghai genome-wide association studies include participants of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (SECS), Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5146840/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>data from 11 participating case–control studies from three sources: 12,893 women (6269 cases and 6624 controls) of East Asian origin participating in nine studies in the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) that were conducted in China, Japan, South Korea, Thailand, and Malaysia; 5152 Chinese women (2867 cases and 2285 controls) from the Shanghai Genome-Wide Association Studies (SGWAS) who were participants in the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) (the SBCS is a population-based case–control study, and the SBCSS and SWHS are ongoing population-based, prospective cohort studies—all</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000050</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Prediction of breast cancer risk based on common genetic variants in women of East Asian ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27931260</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27931260</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Prediction of breast cancer risk based on common genetic variants in women of East Asian ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27931260</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5146840/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>data from 11 participating case–control studies from three sources: 12,893 women (6269 cases and 6624 controls) of East Asian origin participating in nine studies in the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) that were conducted in China, Japan, South Korea, Thailand, and Malaysia; 5152 Chinese women (2867 cases and 2285 controls) from the Shanghai Genome-Wide Association Studies (SGWAS) who were participants in the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) (the SBCS is a population-based case–control study, and the SBCSS and SWHS are ongoing population-based, prospective cohort studies—all</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study and the Shanghai Men&apos;s Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22344219</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24861553</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27931260</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2311</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women included in the Shanghai genome-wide association studies as described for the 2012 East Asian BMI GWAS: breast cancer, endometrial cancer and diabetes case groups and a common control group</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The control group included 2,311 women (2,081 controls from the SBCS and 230 women from the SWHS) and served as the common control for three disease groups.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6936</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women included in the Shanghai genome-wide association studies as described for the 2012 East Asian BMI GWAS: breast cancer, endometrial cancer and diabetes case groups and a common control group</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus, a total of 6,936 women were included in the Shanghai genome-wide association studies, of whom 6,918 women with BMI measurement are included in the current analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SGWAS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20193"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000769</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22792082</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genome-wide genotyping project of the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) that collects children and adults with asthma who took part in NHLBI asthma clinical trials: children of the Childhood Asthma Management Program and of trials of the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, most of them with their parents as parent-child trios, and adults of trials of the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN), for genetic studies of asthma and of response to asthma treatment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym SHARe also denotes WHI SNP Health Association Resource (COHO:0000604), Sinai-Helmsley Alliance for Research Excellence (COHO:0000725) and Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe (COHO:0002644); this term is SNP Health Association Asthma Resource Project.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) Asthma Resource project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SHARP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SHARe</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SHARe Asthma Resource project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SNP Health Associated Resource</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) Asthma Resource project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SNP Health Association Resource Asthma Resource Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Single-nucleotide polymorphism Health association-Asthma Resource Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SNP Health Association Asthma Resource Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20193">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004979"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20193"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>asthma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8073919/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>subsets of clinical trials within the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network including individuals with mild to moderate asthma [21], and the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN) participating in the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) Asthma Resource project (SHARP), which included individuals with a range of asthma severity (mild to severely persistent) [22].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
