        <obo:IAO_0000116>hypertension cases and normotensive controls in the GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Shanghai Institute of Hypertension (SIH) GWAS (N=901)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SIH</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002380 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002380">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Sikh GWAS is the Punjabi Sikh type 2 diabetes GWAS sample of PMID:23300278, drawn from the Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study, which the paper says is also named the Sikh Diabetes Study. The Catalog&apos;s name describes that analysis and is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0001116 (Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study/Sikh Diabetes Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Sikh GWAS</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Armenia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Azerbaijan"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kazakhstan"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tajikistan"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uzbekistan"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Georgia_(country)"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS005204</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:26188009</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of genetic and phenotypic data, gathered in 2010 by the scientific expedition Marco Polo (Marcopolo 2010), from healthy people in communities of the Terra Madre network along the Silk Road in Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan and Tajikistan (rural communities, and also cities in Uzbekistan and Kazakhstan), with ethics approval from the IRCCS Burlo Garofolo hospital in Trieste, Italy. It was used to study the genetics of the senses, such as taste, food preferences, hearing and vision, in these isolated populations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym SR also denotes Stroke Registry (COHO:0002407); this term is Silk Road.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">496</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SR cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Silk Road cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Silk Road</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tajikistan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4267745/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With the aim of studying the genetics of several phenotypes (e.g. food preferences, hearing and taste [9-12]), the Marco Polo scientific campaign, collected in 2010 genetic and phenotypic information of 411 individuals from six countries dwelling along the Silk Road (Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan and Tajikistan).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005204</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polygenic prediction of body mass index and obesity through the life course and across ancestries.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40691366</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:26188009</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis on normal hearing function identifies PCDH20 and SLC28A3 as candidates for hearing function and loss.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:26188009</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4572074/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>These 223 SNPs were further analyzed by combining data from a completely independent cohort of isolated communities (Silk Road cohort, N = 481), resulting in a total sample size of 2636.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of genetic and phenotypic data, gathered in 2010 by the scientific expedition Marco Polo (Marcopolo 2010), from healthy people in communities of the Terra Madre network along the Silk Road in Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan and Tajikistan (rural communities, and also cities in Uzbekistan and Kazakhstan), with ethics approval from the IRCCS Burlo Garofolo hospital in Trieste, Italy. It was used to study the genetics of the senses, such as taste, food preferences, hearing and vision, in these isolated populations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24626196</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25476266</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:26188009</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">496</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people who took part in the Marco Polo 2010 expedition study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24626196</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 496 subjects participated in the study (206 males and 290 females), coming from 20 different communities of six countries in the Caucasus and Central Asia: Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan and Tajikistan (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002381"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002382 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002382">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000660"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The PGS Catalog id Sisters is the NIEHS Sister Study: the ovarian cancer GWAS the id comes from (PMID:28346442) lists it as the OCAC study SIS, funded by the Sister Study&apos;s intramural grant Z01 ES044005. Replaced by COHO:0000660 (Sister Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Sisters Study</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002383 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002383">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The id is used for two different St. Jude samples: ALL patients on its Total Therapy trials (source GWAS) and SJLIFE survivors (sample set PSS003603). SJCRH is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for St. Jude Children&apos;s Research Hospital (Memphis, Tennessee) as an institution. In the source GWAS of PGS000077/PGS000788 (PMID:19684603) it denotes the children with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia treated on St. Jude&apos;s Total Therapy XIIIB and XV trial protocols. That is a clinical-trial patient series with no cohort name of its own, and the supplement expands the tag only to the hospital&apos;s name. In the evaluation sample PSS003603 (PMID:34465587) the same id denotes survivors from the St. Jude Lifetime Cohort Study, which COHO has as COHO:0001120 (SJLIFE). Because the id means the hospital and covers two unrelated samples, it is not a cohort and should not be merged into SJLIFE wholesale. The curator may still add SJCRH as an acronym of COHO:0001120, since the PGS Catalog uses it for SJLIFE in PSS003603. If so, no shared-acronym note is needed, as no other COHO term carries SJCRH. The Children&apos;s Oncology Group patients in the same GWAS are tagged COG (COHO:0000771). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete St. Jude Childrens Research Hospital</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002384 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002384">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. The PGS Catalog&apos;s id SJTU is only the name of Shanghai Jiao Tong University; the Catalog links it to no score or sample set, and the name-search papers are unrelated. In the East Asian diabetes GWAS where the abbreviation appears, SJTU is the contributing institution, not a sample: Hwang et al. 2015 (PMID:25187374) glosses &apos;SJTU, Shanghai Jiao Tong University; SJTUDS, Shanghai Jiao Tong University Diabetes Study&apos;, and the AGEN-T2D supplement (PMID:22158537) lists &apos;SJTU SJTUDS Chinese 190 198 388 Case-control&apos; and &apos;SJTU SDIID/SDS&apos; under the institution column. The id therefore names an institution with no study sample of its own. The named sample from there is SJTUDS (E1034 in this batch); the SDIID and SDS samples are separate review names (SDIID is placeholder COHO:0002358; note that the review mapped PGS &apos;SDS&apos; &quot;Shanghai Diabetes Study&quot; to COHO:0001116, the Sikh Diabetes Study, which should be checked). COHO:0000153 &apos;Shanghai Study&apos; (gallbladder carcinoma) is unrelated. Recommend obsoleting placeholder COHO:0002384. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Shanghai Jiao Tong University</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002385 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002385">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20240"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
