    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20350"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000127.v2.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study utilized samples from Irish patients with sporadic ALS and Irish control individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000127.v2.p1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>All 221 cases were diagnosed by a Consultant neurologist in Ireland.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20719408</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>No association between DNA repair gene XRCC1 and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20719408</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3005140/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We examined the association between ALS risk and single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in the gene x-ray repair complementing defective repair in Chinese hamster cells 1 (XRCC1) utilizing data from a case-control study and two genome-wide association studies (the Study of Irish Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis and the NINDS genome-wide study in Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis and Neurologically Normal Controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case–control collection of Irish patients with sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, diagnosed by consultant neurologists by the El Escorial criteria and drawn from across the island of Ireland, and unrelated neurologically normal controls, all reporting Irish ancestry for at least three generations, assembled in Dublin (Beaumont Hospital, Trinity College and University College Dublin) for a genome-wide association study of susceptibility to sporadic ALS in the Irish population, and later used for whole-genome sequencing of an Irish control.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20719408</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000127.v2.p1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002398"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">221</owl:annotatedTarget>
