    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002403 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002403">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000585"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The paper&apos;s supplement (the likely source of the Catalog&apos;s full name) could not be downloaded, even through the watcher; the identification rests on the hospitals named, the paper&apos;s acknowledgement and the Catalog&apos;s cohort list. The PGS Catalog&apos;s &apos;Spain&apos; (&apos;The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon)&apos;) is the colorectal cancer case-control study that COHO already has as CRCGEN (COHO:0000585, Colorectal Cancer Genetics &amp; Genomics). CRCGEN&apos;s own paper (PMC8574048) says its second component &apos;was conducted in parallel in the University Hospital of Bellvitge and in the Hospital of León, León, during 2007–2015&apos;, exactly the two hospitals the Catalog names, and the PGS Catalog paper PMID:31866242 acknowledges &apos;CRCGEN: Colorectal Cancer Genetics &amp; Genomics, Spanish study&apos; (COHO:0000585 already carries that phrase as a synonym). The other Spanish sample in that score (EPICOLON, Hospital Clínic Barcelona) has its own Catalog id. Add the Catalog name as a synonym and &apos;Spain&apos; as an acronym of COHO:0000585 (no other COHO term uses &apos;Spain&apos; as an acronym, so no editor note is needed); obsolete placeholder COHO:0002403 in its favour. Replaced by COHO:0000585 (Colorectal Cancer Genetics &amp; Genomics), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon)</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20397"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000238"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35933486</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">473</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">101</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SPGRX</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SPGRX cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SPGRX study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Determining the Molecular Pathways and Genetic Predisposition of the Acute Inflammatory Process Caused by SARS-CoV-2</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20397">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100096"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20397"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>COVID-19</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Whole blood samples from SARS-CoV-2 RT-PCR negative (101) and positive lab tested individuals (473) were obtained from two clinical centers (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid, discovery cohort and Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga, replication cohort).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10847137/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we included a total of 3904 European COVID-19 patients recruited in Italy (GEN-COVID and, in part, Hostage series), Spain (Hostage and SPGRX), Sweden (SWECOVID) and Belgium (BelCovid) (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35933486</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Whole blood DNA methylation analysis reveals respiratory environmental traits involved in COVID-19 severity following SARS-CoV-2 infection.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35933486</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The genotype data generated (SPGRX cohort) in this study have been deposited in the European Genome-phenome Archive (EGA) database under accession code EGAS00001005304.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33846372</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34237774</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35933486</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
