        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34319387+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PRS was generated from the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia genomewide association study (n = 542,934) and the Strabismus, Amblyopia, and Refractive Error in Singapore children Study (n = 500).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.</owl:annotatedTarget>
