    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002414 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002414">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. STOLLERY_CC is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the pilot clinical sample of PMID:32790217: about 128 children referred to the coeliac clinic of the Stollery Children&apos;s Hospital (Edmonton, Alberta, Canada) with suspected coeliac disease, plus paediatric gastroenterology controls, used once to evaluate a coeliac genetic risk score (PSS000381). The paper and the Catalog describe it only as a &apos;pilot clinical cohort&apos; at a tertiary paediatric clinic; it has no study name, design or recruitment beyond that one paper, so it is a clinic&apos;s patient sample, not a cohort. No COHO term matches. Recommend obsoleting placeholder COHO:0002414. If the curator prefers to keep one-paper clinical samples, reading the closed full text would be needed for recruitment dates. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Stollery Children’s Hospital Coeliac Clinic</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20482"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20484"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002703"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:42448324</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised controlled trial in Turku, Finland, that enrolled infants and their parents at well-baby clinics between 1989 and 1992 and gave the intervention group individualised dietary counselling from age 7 months to 20 years, aimed at improving dietary fat quality to prevent cardiovascular disease, while the control group received routine care; participants have been followed into adulthood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym STRIP also denotes Special Turku Coronary Risk Factor Intervention Project, Parents (COHO:0002703); this term is Special Turku Coronary Risk Factor Intervention Project.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1062</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>STRIP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>STRIP study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Special Turku coronary Risk factor Intervention Project for babies</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Special Turku Coronary Risk Factor Intervention Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20482">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000021"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20484">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20482"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>diet</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13092225/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The intervention is unique in that it began in infancy and continued for 20 years, with personalized dietary counseling provided to children and their parents in the intervention group.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20484"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13092225/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>It aimed at improving fat quality and promoting healthy foods to prevent cardiovascular diseases.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13092225/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The STRIP study was a prospective randomized controlled trial (RCT) conducted in Turku, Finland, starting in 1990.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:42448324</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Effect of dietary counselling on educational disparities in cardiometabolic health from childhood to adulthood.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42448324</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42448324+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study comprised 839 participants from the Special Turku Coronary Risk Factor Intervention Project (STRIP), in which the intervention group (n=417) received individualized dietary counselling during 20 years, while the control group (n=422) received routine care.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised controlled trial in Turku, Finland, that enrolled infants and their parents at well-baby clinics between 1989 and 1992 and gave the intervention group individualised dietary counselling from age 7 months to 20 years, aimed at improving dietary fat quality to prevent cardiovascular disease, while the control group received routine care; participants have been followed into adulthood.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16250721</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:42011282</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1062</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Infants enrolled with their parents in the STRIP randomized trial</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13092225/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1062 7‐month‐old infants and their parents were enrolled in the trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002415"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>STRIP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002416 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002416">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20491"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000020"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000344</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38098086</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An open-label, multicentre, randomised phase III trial in Germany that enrolled patients with HER2-positive, intermediate-to-high-risk early breast cancer between 2008 and 2011 and compared adjuvant chemotherapy of three cycles of fluorouracil, epirubicin and cyclophosphamide followed by three cycles of docetaxel with the same followed by three cycles of gemcitabine and docetaxel, all patients then receiving trastuzumab for a year.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">793</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUCCESS B</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUCCESS B study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUCCESS B trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUCCESSB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Simultaneous Study of Gemcitabine-Docetaxel Combination adjuvant treatment</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SuccessB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Simultaneous Study of Gemcitabine-Docetaxel Combination adjuvant treatment, as well as Biological Targeted Treatment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20491">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0006244"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002416"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20491"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HER2-positive breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10722735/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SUCCESS B was another open-label, multicenter, 1:1 randomized phase III study that enrolled 793 intermediate-to-high-risk breast cancer patients between June 2008 and September 2011. Study participants were positive for human epidermal growth factor receptors (HER2neu) and received the same adjuvant CHT as in the SUCCESS A study (i.e., FEC-Doc vs FEC-DocG).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002416"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature24284/MediaObjects/41586_2017_BFnature24284_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>SuccessB Simultaneous Study of Gemcitabine-Docetaxel Combination adjuvant treatment Multicenter, prospective, randomized, open-label phase III study Germany</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002416"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
