    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20501"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>HER2neu negative early breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10722735/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SUCCESS C trial was a multicenter, prospective randomized phase III study comprising 3643 patients with primary HER2neu negative early breast cancer that were enrolled between February 2009 and August 2011 at 231 German study sites.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20503"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>dietary changes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10722735/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The individualized lifestyle intervention program comprised a two-year standardized and structured telephone intervention aimed at moderate weight loss through dietary changes and physical activity, supported by educational materials and patient diary.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20505"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>physical activity</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10722735/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The individualized lifestyle intervention program comprised a two-year standardized and structured telephone intervention aimed at moderate weight loss through dietary changes and physical activity, supported by educational materials and patient diary.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10722735/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SUCCESS C trial was a multicenter, prospective randomized phase III study comprising 3643 patients with primary HER2neu negative early breast cancer that were enrolled between February 2009 and August 2011 at 231 German study sites.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000344</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European polygenic risk score for prediction of breast cancer shows similar performance in Asian women.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32737321</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:28190761</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Prevalence of Circulating Tumor Cells After Adjuvant Chemotherapy With or Without Anthracyclines in Patients With HER2-negative, Hormone Receptor-positive Early Breast Cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:28190761</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28190761+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Based on data suggesting a limited benefit of anthracyclines in human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2)-negative patients, the Simultaneous Study of Docetaxel Based Anthracycline Free Adjuvant Treatment Evaluation, as well as Life Style Intervention Strategies (SUCCESS) C study randomized patients to either anthracycline-containing or anthracycline-free chemotherapy.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An open-label, multicentre, randomised phase III trial at study sites in Germany that enrolled patients with HER2-negative early breast cancer between 2009 and 2011 and compared anthracycline-containing with anthracycline-free (docetaxel and cyclophosphamide) adjuvant chemotherapy, with a second randomisation of patients with a body mass index of 24 to 40 kg/m2 to an individualised two-year telephone lifestyle intervention aiming at moderate weight loss or to general lifestyle recommendations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38098086</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41711956</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3643</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>SUCCESS C enrolled trial patients (2009–2011)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10722735/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SUCCESS C trial was a multicenter, prospective randomized phase III study comprising 3643 patients with primary HER2neu negative early breast cancer that were enrolled between February 2009 and August 2011 at 231 German study sites.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002417"/>
