    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20515"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:10577996</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7814</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Suita</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>suita study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Suita Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20515">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20515"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As described elsewhere [20, 21], the Suita Study is a population-based study with a prospective cohort design, aimed at investigating CVD risk factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japan"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12358252/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We, therefore, used data from the Suita Study, a population-based prospective cohort study investigating people residing in an urban city in Osaka, Japan, to explore this association.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:10577996</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Human prostacyclin synthase gene and hypertension : the Suita Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:10577996</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10577996+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We then investigated the possible association of this repeat polymorphism with blood pressure in a large population-based sample (the Suita Study), which consisted of 4971 Japanese participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40383629</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40898037</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9056605</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7814</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants of the Suita Study&apos;s two randomly selected cohorts, recruited 1989-1998; a volunteer group of 546 (1992-2006) is stated separately and no total is given</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12358252/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Suita Study population (two randomly selected cohorts including 7,814 participants recruited from 1989 to 1998 and a volunteer group including 546 participants recruited from 1992 to 2006)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Suita</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000617"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000781</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:28346443</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary-prevention trial in the general adult population of France, which in 1994 enrolled women aged 35 to 60 and men aged 45 to 60 and followed them for eight years to test whether daily supplementation with antioxidant vitamins (vitamin C, vitamin E and beta-carotene) and minerals (selenium and zinc) at nutritional doses reduces cancers and cardiovascular diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">13017</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SU.VI.MAX</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SU.VI.MAX study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUVIMAX</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUVIMAX study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SUpplémentation en VItamines et Minéraux AntioXydants</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Supplementation en Vitamines et Mineraux Antioxydants</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Supplementation en Vitamines et Mineraux Antioxydants Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">SUpplementation en VItamines et Minéraux AntioXydants</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9503043+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study involves 12,735 eligible subjects (women aged 35 to 60 years; men aged 45 to 60 years) included in 1994 in France.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419"/>
