    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20536"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:23263487</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A colorectal cancer case-control study nested in two population-based cohorts in urban Shanghai, China, the Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study and the Shanghai Men&apos;s Health Study, whose cases were colorectal cancer patients identified among the cohorts&apos; participants and whose controls were cancer-free participants of the same cohorts frequency-matched to the cases by age and sex. Its samples, with additional community controls from the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, were genotyped as the Shanghai-1 and Shanghai-2 sets of the discovery stage of the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium&apos;s genome-wide association study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">777</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">758</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SVCRCGP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai-Vanderbilt Colorectal Cancer Genetics Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Shanghai-Vanderbilt Colorectal Cancer Genetic Project</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20536">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20536"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Colorectal cancer (CRC) cases for the project were derived from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) and the Shanghai Men’s Health Study (SMHS), both population-based cohort studies which are being conducted in urban Shanghai, China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Colorectal cancer (CRC) cases for the project were derived from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) and the Shanghai Men’s Health Study (SMHS), both population-based cohort studies which are being conducted in urban Shanghai, China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included 2,368 cases and 8,219 controls from three case- control collections, Shanghai-1, Shanghai-2 and Shanghai-3.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:23263487</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analyses in East Asians identify new susceptibility loci for colorectal cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23263487</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3679924/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>W.Z. conceived and directed the consortium as well as the Shanghai-Vanderbilt Colorectal Cancer Genetics Project.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A colorectal cancer case-control study nested in two population-based cohorts in urban Shanghai, China, the Shanghai Women&apos;s Health Study and the Shanghai Men&apos;s Health Study, whose cases were colorectal cancer patients identified among the cohorts&apos; participants and whose controls were cancer-free participants of the same cohorts frequency-matched to the cases by age and sex. Its samples, with additional community controls from the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, were genotyped as the Shanghai-1 and Shanghai-2 sets of the discovery stage of the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium&apos;s genome-wide association study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23263487</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">777</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>SVCRCGP cases and matched controls from SWHS/SMHS in the 2013 profile</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 777 CRC cases with DNA available were identified in participants of the SWHS and SMHS and included in this study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">758</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>SVCRCGP cases and matched controls from SWHS/SMHS in the 2013 profile</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 758 cancer-free controls were derived from the SWHS/SMHS and frequency- matched to CRC cases by age and sex.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
