    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002426 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002426">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The PGS Catalog id SWOG-SELECT denotes the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial, genotyped for prostate and colorectal cancer GWAS (PMID:29892016, PMID:30510241); the Catalog&apos;s name for it is the trial&apos;s name, misspelt. Replaced by COHO:0000693 (Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Selenium and Vitmain E Cancer Prevention Trial</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002427 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002427">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20571"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37794016</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective mother-offspring cohort of non-pregnant women aged 20 to 34 years from the general population of Southampton, UK, recruited through their general practitioners between 1998 and 2002 and characterised before pregnancy; the women who later became pregnant were followed through pregnancy, and their children through infancy and childhood, to study how maternal characteristics and the children&apos;s prenatal and postnatal growth affect their development and their risk factors for chronic diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">12579</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SWS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Southampton Womens Survey</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Southampton Women&apos;s Survey</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20571">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_6000021"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20571"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>mother&apos;s diet before and during pregnancy</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4579566/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The objectives of the Southampton Women’s Survey are: a)to characterise the influence of the mother’s own fetal growth and of her diet, body composition and endocrine profile before and during pregnancy on: 1) the early trajectory of fetal growth; 2) the maintenance of this growth trajectory in late gestation;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9542867/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, 12,583 non-pregnant women aged 20-34 years were recruited to the SWS between 1998 and 2002 from the general population of Southampton, UK, with no other exclusion criteria.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37794016</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>European and multi-ancestry genome-wide association meta-analysis of atopic dermatitis highlights importance of systemic immune regulation.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37794016</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-023-41180-2/MediaObjects/41467_2023_41180_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Between 1998 and 2002 the Southampton Women’s Survey team interviewed 12,583 Southampton women aged 20 to 34 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002427"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective mother-offspring cohort of non-pregnant women aged 20 to 34 years from the general population of Southampton, UK, recruited through their general practitioners between 1998 and 2002 and characterised before pregnancy; the women who later became pregnant were followed through pregnancy, and their children through infancy and childhood, to study how maternal characteristics and the children&apos;s prenatal and postnatal growth affect their development and their risk factors for chronic diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16195252</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35689423</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
