    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GCST90492734</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genetic drivers of heterogeneity in type 2 diabetes pathophysiology.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38374256</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10937372/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Through the newly established Type 2 Diabetes Global Genomics Initiative, we present findings from a very large meta-analysis of T2D GWAS data, comprising more than 2.5 million individuals of diverse ancestry—an increase of nearly threefold in the effective sample size compared with previous efforts8,9.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS012530</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Improving Genetic Risk Prediction of CAD in Chinese by Multi-ancestry and Multi-trait GWAS Integration.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42152175</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international initiative that assembled genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes from studies in six ancestry groups (African American, East Asian, European, Hispanic, South African and South Asian), among them the DIAMANTE Consortium and the Million Veteran Program, and meta-analysed them to characterise the genetic contribution to type 2 diabetes and its aetiological heterogeneity across populations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:38374256</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">428452</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the GWAS assembled for the 2024 multi-ancestry meta-analysis (T2D cases and controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10937372/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We assembled GWAS data, including 428,452 cases of T2D and 2,107,149 controls</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2107149</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the GWAS assembled for the 2024 multi-ancestry meta-analysis (T2D cases and controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10937372/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We assembled GWAS data, including 428,452 cases of T2D and 2,107,149 controls</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2535601</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals in the GWAS assembled for the 2024 multi-ancestry meta-analysis (T2D cases and controls)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10937372/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, to characterize the genetic contribution to these processes across ancestry groups, we aggregate genome-wide association study data from 2,535,601 individuals (39.7% not of European ancestry), including 428,452 cases of T2D.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>T2D-GGI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002430"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>T2DGGI</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


