    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20776"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS005402</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41851747</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19582</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TARGET-C</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TARGET-C colorectal cancer screening trial (China)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TARGET-C study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TARGET-C trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TARGETC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Comparative Evaluation of Novel Screening Strategies for Colorectal Cancer Screening</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20776">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20776"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12642085/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a comprehensive multicenter RCT in China, the Comparative Evaluation of Novel Screening Strategies for Colorectal Cancer Screening (TARGET-C), to assess the feasibility, adherence, diagnostic yield, and costs associated with colonoscopy, fecal immunochemical testing (FIT), and a risk-adapted screening approach [10].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13123215/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The TARGET-C study (Comparative Evaluation of Novel Screening Strategies for Colorectal Cancer Screening) is a multicenter randomized controlled trial conducted in six study centers across five provinces in China (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan, and Yunnan).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS005402</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Optimizing colorectal cancer screening through polygenic risk score-based risk stratification: evidence from a population-based cohort and screening trial.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41851747</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41851747</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Optimizing colorectal cancer screening through polygenic risk score-based risk stratification: evidence from a population-based cohort and screening trial.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41851747</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13123215/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 2,821 participants were included from a population-based CRC screening trial (TARGET-C)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41851747</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">19582</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Participants enrolled in TARGET-C</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12642085/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The TARGET-C trial enrolled 19,582 participants aged 50–74 years from 6 centers in China, randomized in a 1:2:2 ratio into 3 groups.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TARGET-C</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>TARGETC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002438 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002438">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:27325353</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based longitudinal cohort of community-dwelling people aged 60 to 85 randomly selected from the Southern Tasmanian electoral roll in Australia, examined in three phases between 2005 and 2012 with questionnaires, objective gait, cognitive and sensorimotor testing and brain magnetic resonance imaging, to study gait, cognition and brain structure in older people.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">431</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TASCOG</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TasCog</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Tasmanian study of cognition and gait</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Tasmanian Study of Cognition and Gait</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002438"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9434440/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Tasmanian Study of Cognition and Gait (TASCOG) is a population-based longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling older individuals aged between 60 and 85 years who were randomly recruited from the Southern Tasmanian Electoral Roll, Australia between 2005 and 2012.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002438"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:27325353</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>GWAS analysis of handgrip and lower body strength in older adults in the CHARGE consortium.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27325353</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5013019/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The discovery phase of this GWAS was conducted on 27 581 subjects from the following 14 participating studies of the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium (CHARGE); the Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility Study (AGES); the Cardiovascular Health Study (CHS); the Framingham Heart Study (FHS); the Health, Aging, and Body Composition (Health ABC) Study; the Health and Retirement Study (HRS); the InCHIANTI Study; the Lothian Birth Cohort Studies (1921 and 1936); the Osteoporotic Fractures in Men Study (MrOS); Religious Order Study, Memory and Aging Project (MAP/ROS); the Study of Health in Pomerania (SHIP); the Study of Osteoporotic Fractures (SOF); the Tasmanian Study of Cognition and Gait (TasCog); and the Twins UK Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
