        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33436325</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39001544</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1963</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals of the full Australian familial and case-control resources genotyped</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39001544</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Rare DDR gene variants (predicted to be damaging and present in two or more family members) were identified and subsequently genotyped in 1963 individuals (700 familial and 459 sporadic PrCa cases, 482 unaffected relatives, and 322 screened controls), and association analyses accounting for relatedness (MQLS) undertaken.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
