        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym TCGS also denotes Tehran Cardiometabolic Genetic Study (COHO:0002445); this term is Transcontinental COPD Genetics Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
