    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid20883"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000350</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25173106</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>TEST</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Twin Eye Study in Tasmania</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Twins Eye Study Tasmania</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Twins eye study in Tasmania</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Twins Eye Study in Tasmania</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid20883">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005328"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid20883"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>eye diseases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19803772+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Unravelling the mechanisms underpinning important blinding diseases could allow preventative or curative steps to be implemented. Twin siblings provide a unique opportunity in biology to discover genes associated with numerous eye diseases and ocular biometry.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0127-7/MediaObjects/41588_2018_127_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>TEST Australia population based twin study 267 46.10(12.25) 50.3 -0.54(1.99)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000350</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Association of a Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Genetic Risk Score With Earlier Age at Diagnosis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31436842</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25173106</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide analysis of multi-ancestry cohorts identifies new loci influencing intraocular pressure and susceptibility to glaucoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25173106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4177225/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The discovery cohorts included 27,558 individuals of European ancestry from 14 studies (ALIENOR, BATS, BMES,29,30 ERF,31,32 Framingham Family Study,33 GHS1, GHS2, ORCADES,34 RAINE, 35-37 RS-I, RS-II, RS-III,38 TEST39 and TwinsUK40).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19803772</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
