    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002468 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002468">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. TOR is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id (PGS000030 evaluation, sample set PSS000041) for the PRACTICAL/OncoArray prostate cancer study that the Schumacher 2018 supplement lists only as &apos;Toronto&apos;: men undergoing prostate biopsy at the Princess Margaret Cancer Centre (University Health Network), Toronto, Canada, cases with positive biopsies and controls with negative biopsies, described as &apos;Prospective hospital-based biopsy cohort&apos; (41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf, Supplementary Table 1). Its only design paper (PMID:24568896, Eur Urol 2014) calls it &apos;a large prostate biopsy cohort (in Toronto, Canada)&apos;. The sample has no name of its own beyond the city and institution, so, like HZ and Poland, it is not a cohort. No COHO term or review row names a Toronto prostate biopsy cohort (checked coho_names.tsv and catalog_cohorts_review.tsv for Toronto, Princess Margaret, UHN). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete University Health Network, Toronto, Canada</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


