    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002475 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002475">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UBNS (&apos;University of Bergen Norway Study&apos;) is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for OCAC&apos;s contributing study NOR: ovarian cancer cases and controls recruited in Norway in 2001–2010 at Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen. OCAC papers name it only by its institutions: &apos;The University of Bergen, Haukeland University Hospital, Norway study (NOR)&apos; (PMID:29029385, PMC5630285, funding statement). No design paper or name of its own was found (Europe PMC and web searches for an OCAC NOR study description; the OCAC website did not respond). Like HZ and Poland, it is a site sample labelled by institution, so it is not a cohort. No COHO term matches (coho_names.tsv searched for Bergen, Haukeland and Norw*; the Hordaland Health Study COHO:0001351 and GenKOLS COHO:0001009 are other Bergen samples and unrelated). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete University of Bergen Norway Study</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002476 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002476">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21030"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:25420145</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection at University Hospital, Salt Lake City, Utah, United States, one of the centres collaborating with the CADISP consortium that recruited patients of European origin, applying the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, for the second sample (CADISP-2) of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">26</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UCADC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Utah cervical artery dissection collection</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Utah Cervical Artery Dissection Collection</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21030">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0006061"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002476"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21030"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cervical artery dissection</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To increase the sample size for genetic analyses, an independent sample of 501 CeAD patients of European origin was recruited between 2008 and 2010, in some CADISP centers and additional 12 centers in 7 European countries and the United States (Supplementary Fig. 2), applying the same inclusion criteria as for the CADISP study (Supplementary Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002476"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CADISP-2: recruiting centers collaborating with the CADISP consortium for the genetics project, i.e. France, Nantes, Paris; Germany, Münster; Italy, Milan; Netherlands, Rotterdam; Spain, Barcelona; Switzerland, Lausanne; UK, London; USA, Salt Lake City - UT, Charlottesville – VA</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002476"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25420145</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common variation in PHACTR1 is associated with susceptibility to cervical artery dissection.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25420145</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Utah cervical artery dissection collection is supported by Award Number UL1TR000105-05 from the National Center for Research Resources by the Public Health Services (University Hospital, Salt Lake City, Utah).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002476"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection at University Hospital, Salt Lake City, Utah, United States, one of the centres collaborating with the CADISP consortium that recruited patients of European origin, applying the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, for the second sample (CADISP-2) of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:25420145</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
