        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31748521</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre case-control study in the Netherlands, started in 2011 as a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles and University Medical Center Utrecht with other Dutch mental health care institutes, that collects genetic and phenotypic information on patients with bipolar I disorder, their first-degree relatives and controls, recruited through clinicians, the Dutch bipolar disorder patients&apos; association, pharmacies, advertisements and earlier research studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1396</coho:numberOfCases>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DB Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>DBC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Dutch Bipolar (DB) Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Dutch Bipolar cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UCLA_NL_BP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Dutch Bipolar Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21054">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0001866"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21054"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>bipolar disorder type I</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9542330/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>DBC investigates genetic and phenotypic information of patients with bipolar disorder type I (BD‐I), their first‐degree relatives, and controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6868237/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The DB Cohort study, started in 2011, is a multicenter case–control study in the Netherlands, investigating genetic and phenotypic information of patients with BD type I, first-degree relatives, and controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31748521</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The association between antibodies to neurotropic pathogens and bipolar disorder : A study in the Dutch Bipolar (DB) Cohort and meta-analysis.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31748521</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6868237/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We, therefore, analyzed the seroprevalence and titer levels of IgG antibodies against several herpesviruses and Toxoplasma gondii (T. gondii) in plasma of 760 patients with a bipolar disorder, 144 first-degree matched relatives and 132 controls of the Dutch Bipolar (DB) Cohort using ELISA.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre case-control study in the Netherlands, started in 2011 as a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles and University Medical Center Utrecht with other Dutch mental health care institutes, that collects genetic and phenotypic information on patients with bipolar I disorder, their first-degree relatives and controls, recruited through clinicians, the Dutch bipolar disorder patients&apos; association, pharmacies, advertisements and earlier research studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31748521</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34821429</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1396</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>patients with bipolar I disorder in the cohort; its first-degree relatives and controls are not counted and no total is stated</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31449716+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the Dutch Bipolar Cohort, stages according to models A and B were assigned to all patients with bipolar-I-disorder (BD-I; N = 1396).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
