    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002485">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002256"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. same cohort as review name E897. UDP (&apos;Universita di Pisa&apos;) is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the CIMBA consortium&apos;s Pisa study of BRCA1/BRCA2 mutation carriers, which the Phelan 2017 ovarian cancer GWAS names only by its university (study code PBCS, &apos;Università di Pisa&apos; in its Supplementary Table 1). The same CIMBA study appears in Barnes et al. 2020 (PMID:32665703) as &apos;Pisa Breast Cancer Study (PBCS)&apos;, run under the Azienda Ospedaliera Pisana ethics committee and funded by AIRC and the Tuscany Institute for Tumors (&apos;PBCS: Italian Association of Cancer Research (AIRC) [IG 2013 N.14477] and Tuscany Institute for Tumors (ITT) grant 2014-2015-2016.&apos;, PMC7521995 supplementary files). The PGS Catalog gives that paper&apos;s sample the id PiBCS, which is review row E897 (placeholder COHO:0002256, &apos;Pisa Breast Cancer Study&apos;). So UDP and PiBCS are two PGS ids for one study. Whoever curates E897 should add UDP as an acronym. &apos;Università di Pisa&apos; is added as a synonym only because the GWAS&apos;s study-name column uses it; drop it if an institution name is unwanted. Do not add the acronym PBCS without an editor note: it is also the Polish Breast Cancer Study&apos;s (COHO:0000930). Replaced by COHO:0002256 (Pisa Breast Cancer Study), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Universita di Pisa</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


