        <rdfs:comment>Cases for discovery analysis were primarily from the Breast Cancer Now Male Breast Cancer Study, a population-based case-control study of MBC in England and Wales (UK-BCN-MBCS, n = 1210).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales, set up at the Institute of Cancer Research, London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men, whose cases are men resident in England and Wales diagnosed with invasive or in situ breast cancer at ages 18–79 from 2005 onwards, found through regional cancer registries and consultants, and whose controls are male non-blood relatives of cases and male spouses of women in the Generations Study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32785646</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
