        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1210</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>UK-BCN-MBCS native male cases and controls in the 2020 discovery analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases for discovery analysis were primarily from the Breast Cancer Now Male Breast Cancer Study, a population-based case-control study of MBC in England and Wales (UK-BCN-MBCS, n = 1210).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">264</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>UK-BCN-MBCS native male cases and controls in the 2020 discovery analysis</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To estimate autosomal SNP genotype frequencies from the general population, we used male and female controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort (UK-58BC, n = 2663), male controls from the UK-BCN-MBCS (n = 264), and female controls from the UK Generations Study (UK-GS, n = 698) (Supplementary Table 1, available online) (8).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
