    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21186"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Estonia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Portugal"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24795349</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2952</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">UKCVD</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21186">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005068"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21186"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>myocardial infarction</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4106467/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For Stage 2 replication, we directly genotyped 3 lead SNPs representing 2 top novel independent (r2&lt;0.25) association signals (CSNK2A2 and FER) in a UK CVD cohort available with RTL measures on 2,952 MI patients and healthy controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HIFMECH study comprises Caucasian male survivors of a first MI aged &lt;60 years (excluding patients with FH and insulin‐dependent diabetes mellitus) and population‐based individuals of the same age and region recruited from four centres in Europe: Stockholm, Sweden and London, England for the North and Marseille, France and San Giovanni Retondo, Italy representing the South</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The subjects were recruited from 14 European university student populations from 11 European countries, which were divided into 4 regions: Baltic (Estonia and Finland); United Kingdom; Middle Europe (Belgium, Denmark, Germany, and Switzerland); and South Europe (Greece, Italy, Portugal and Spain).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Simon Broome study is a cross‐sectional study comprising 410 Caucasian patients with treated heterozygous FH aged 18 years recruited from 6 lipid clinics in the UK.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24795349</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study identifies variants in casein kinase II (CSNK2A2) to be associated with leukocyte telomere length in a Punjabi Sikh diabetic cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24795349</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4106467/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Combined AIDHS/SDS and UKCVD meta-analysis revealed rs74019828 (CSNK2A2) and rs112020835 (FER) to be significantly associated with RTL (Figure 6, Supplementary Table 11).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24795349</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2952</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people of European ancestry (myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls) pooled as the Stage 2 replication sample of the 2014 telomere length GWAS</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4106467/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We further tested 3 top variants by genotyping in UKCVD (Caucasians n=2,952) for Stage 2.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


