        <obo:IAO_0000115>The patients with Graves&apos; disease of the United Kingdom&apos;s national DNA collection for autoimmune thyroid disease (the AITD National Collection), a multicentre collection of Caucasian patients with Graves&apos; disease or Hashimoto&apos;s thyroiditis and their family members, recruited at hospitals across the United Kingdom with clinical and biochemical data collected prospectively under a common protocol and funded by the Wellcome Trust. Its Graves&apos; disease patients have served as cases in genetic association studies of Graves&apos; disease, analysed against British 1958 Birth Cohort controls.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2478</coho:numberOfParticipants>
