    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002518 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002518">
        <obo:IAO_0100001 rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The id is ambiguous in PGS005391: there the Catalog lists UM among ADGC datasets (next to UPITT, NIA-LOAD, TARCC, GENADA), and the source paper (PMID:42237039) uses &apos;UM&apos; only for the University of Miami (&apos;the University of Miami (UM)/Case Western Reserve University (CWRU)/Mt. Sinai School of Medicine (MSSM)&apos;). That paper&apos;s own Munich sample is called &apos;The PAGES study&apos;, never UM. So in PGS005391 UM may be the Catalog&apos;s reuse of its Munich id for PAGES, or a mis-tag of UM/CWRU/MSSM (placeholder COHO:0002521). This could not be settled from the paper. UM (&apos;University of Munich&apos;) is not the university but, in PGS000823&apos;s source GWAS (Jonsson et al. 2013, TREM2), the Munich sample of Alzheimer&apos;s disease patients from the memory clinic of the Department of Psychiatry, University of Munich (LMU), with population controls randomly selected from Munich. The 2026 consensus meta-analysis supplement describes exactly this sample, in the same sentences, as &apos;The PAGES study&apos;. COHO already has PAGES as COHO:0000720 &apos;Phenomics and Genomics Sample&apos;, whose definition already includes &apos;Alzheimer&apos;s disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic&apos; and Munich controls. So UM should become an acronym of COHO:0000720. &apos;University of Munich&apos; is not added as a synonym: it is the institution&apos;s name. No other COHO term carries the acronym UM. PAGES is already shared with COHO:0000721 (Paediatric Asthma Gene Environment Study), which is unaffected. See problems for the PGS005391 ambiguity: if the curator reads that use as the University of Miami datasets, the UM tag there belongs with UM/VU/MSSM (COHO:0002521), with a shared-acronym note on both terms. Replaced by COHO:0000720 (Phenomics and Genomics Sample), which now carries this term&apos;s names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete University of Munich</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002519 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002519">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UMC (&apos;University Medical Center Utrecht&apos;) is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for samples that came from UMC Utrecht without a study name, and it covers at least two different sets. In the bladder cancer GWAS it is a pooled Dutch control group: companions of neurology outpatients and controls from a schizophrenia GWAS. In the intracranial aneurysm scores it is the Utrecht intracranial aneurysm patients (UMC Utrecht biobank data). Neither is a cohort with a name or recruitment of its own; the id is the hospital, so it is not a cohort. None of the COHO matches in the evidence is this sample: ALS Utrecht (COHO:0000506) is a 158-person MRI sample, and the Nijmegen Biomedical Study (COHO:0000128, acronym NBS) is the other Dutch control set in the bladder GWAS, which the UMC controls extended but are not part of. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete University Medical Center Utrecht</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002520 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002520">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UMN is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for the systemic lupus erythematosus cases and controls that the University of Minnesota contributed to the multi-ancestry LLAS2 sample of PMID:22523428. The paper&apos;s Supplementary Table S1 gives the source only as &quot;UMN (University of Minnesota, USA)&quot; (https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S000349672418630X-mmc1.pdf), with no study name, design or recruitment of its own; it is one institution among some twenty sample sources. The two Europe PMC hits for &apos;University of Minnesota study&apos; (a 1978 surgical follow-up and the Colon Cancer Control Study) have nothing to do with the id. Not a cohort; no COHO term matches. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete University of Minnesota study</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21297"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000823</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21460841</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A case-control collection of late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease, whose cases met NINCDS-ADRDA criteria for probable or definite Alzheimer&apos;s disease with onset after age 60 and whose controls are cognitively healthy, unrelated people from the same catchment areas frequency-matched by age and sex, ascertained at the University of Miami, Vanderbilt University (later Case Western Reserve University) and Mount Sinai School of Medicine, including autopsy-confirmed cases and controls mainly from Mount Sinai; it is one of the datasets of the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1177</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1126</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UM/CWRU/MSSM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UM/VU/MSSM</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>UMVUMSS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>University of Miami Hussman Institute for Human Genomics/Vanderbilt University Center for Human Genetics Research/Mount Sinai School of Medicine</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">University of Miami/Vanderbilt University/Mt. Sinai School of Medicine</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21297">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004975"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21297"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Alzheimer&apos;s disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Each affected individual met NINCDS-ADRDA criteria for probably or definite Alzheimer’s disease (G. McKhann et al., 1984; G. M. McKhann et al., 2011) with age at onset greater than 60 years</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UM/VU/MSSM dataset contains 1,186 cases and 1,135 CNEs (new and previously published) [15, 16, 17, 18] ascertained at the University of Miami, Vanderbilt University and Mt. Sinai School of Medicine, including 409 autopsy-confirmed cases and 136 controls, primarily from the Mt. Sinai School of Medicine [19].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000823</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The effect of APOE and other common genetic variants on the onset of Alzheimer&apos;s disease and dementia: a community-based cohort study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29555425</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21460841</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Common variants at MS4A4/MS4A6E, CD2AP, CD33 and EPHA1 are associated with late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21460841</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.801/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng801_MOESM5_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>University of Miami/Vanderbilt University/Mt. Sinai School of Medicine (UM/VU/MSSM): The UM/VU/MSSM dataset contains 1,186 cases and 1,135 CNEs (new and previously published)15-18 ascertained at the University of Miami, Vanderbilt University and Mt. Sinai School of Medicine, including 409 autopsy-confirmed cases and 136 controls, primarily from the Mt. Sinai School of Medicine</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A case-control collection of late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease, whose cases met NINCDS-ADRDA criteria for probable or definite Alzheimer&apos;s disease with onset after age 60 and whose controls are cognitively healthy, unrelated people from the same catchment areas frequency-matched by age and sex, ascertained at the University of Miami, Vanderbilt University (later Case Western Reserve University) and Mount Sinai School of Medicine, including autopsy-confirmed cases and controls mainly from Mount Sinai; it is one of the datasets of the Alzheimer&apos;s Disease Genetics Consortium.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1177</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease cases and cognitively normal elderly controls of the dataset, as the ADGC described it in 2024 (no total stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UM/CWRU/MSSM dataset (formerly UM/VU/MSSM (Beecham et al., 2009; Edwards et al., 2010; Najet al.,2010; Scott etal., 2001)⁠) contains 1,177 cases and 1,126 CNEs ascertained at the University of Miami, Case Western Reserve University and Mt. Sinai School of Medicine, including 409 autopsy-confirmed cases and 136 controls, primarily from the Mt. Sinai School of Medicine</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002521"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1126</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>late-onset Alzheimer&apos;s disease cases and cognitively normal elderly controls of the dataset, as the ADGC described it in 2024 (no total stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The UM/CWRU/MSSM dataset (formerly UM/VU/MSSM (Beecham et al., 2009; Edwards et al., 2010; Najet al.,2010; Scott etal., 2001)⁠) contains 1,177 cases and 1,126 CNEs ascertained at the University of Miami, Case Western Reserve University and Mt. Sinai School of Medicine, including 409 autopsy-confirmed cases and 136 controls, primarily from the Mt. Sinai School of Medicine</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
