    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21349"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000722</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22113997</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based case-control study of renal cell carcinoma run by the US National Cancer Institute in the Chicago (Cook County) and Detroit (Wayne, Macomb and Oakland counties) metropolitan areas, chosen for their high proportion of African American residents. Cases were residents aged 20 to 79 newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma between 2002 and 2007; controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Medicare records and frequency-matched to the cases by age, race and sex, and participants were interviewed about their medical history, tobacco use, occupation, diet, family history of cancer and other factors.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1217</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1235</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Cancer Institue U.S. Kidney Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Cancer Institute United States Kidney Cancer Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>USKC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>United States Kidney Cancer</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">US Kidney Cancer Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21349">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005086"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21349"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>renal cell carcinoma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2883149/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a population-based case–control study, unconditional logistic regression was used to calculate the association between RCC risk and a family history of cancer among 1217 RCC cases and 1235 controls.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>National Cancer Institute United States Kidney Cancer Study (USKC) This population-based case-control study of RCC was conducted in the metropolitan areas of Chicago (Cook County) and Detroit (Wayne, Macomb and Oakland counties), two areas of the United States with a high proportion of African American residents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000722</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Evaluating the Utility of Polygenic Risk Scores in Identifying High-Risk Individuals for Eight Common Cancers.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32596635</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:22113997</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The chromosome 2p21 region harbors a complex genetic architecture for association with risk for renal cell carcinoma.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:22113997</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3277315</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We genotyped 59 tagged SNPs in 2278 RCC cases and 3719 controls from two nested case–control studies [the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial and the Alpha- Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention (ATBC) study in Finland], a hospital-based Central and Eastern European RCC (CEERCC) case–control study and Caucasians from the United States Kidney Cancer (USKC) population-based case–control study (see Materials and Methods and Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based case-control study of renal cell carcinoma run by the US National Cancer Institute in the Chicago (Cook County) and Detroit (Wayne, Macomb and Oakland counties) metropolitan areas, chosen for their high proportion of African American residents. Cases were residents aged 20 to 79 newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma between 2002 and 2007; controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Medicare records and frequency-matched to the cases by age, race and sex, and participants were interviewed about their medical history, tobacco use, occupation, diet, family history of cancer and other factors.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3277315</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1217</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Participants recruited to the US Kidney Cancer Study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2883149/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus, 1217 cases (77.5% of those we attempted to recruit) participated in the study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1235</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Participants recruited to the US Kidney Cancer Study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2883149/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Thus, 1235 eligible controls (54.4% of those we attempted to recruit) participated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002529"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>USKC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


