        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.</obo:IAO_0000115>
