    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21509"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20520574</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based observational study of middle-aged residents of Vobarno, a small town between Brescia and Lake Garda in northern Italy, randomly selected from the electoral rolls and examined with clinic and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure measurement, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, aortic stiffness and blood sampling for biochemistry and DNA extraction, to relate cardiac and vascular structure and function to blood pressure; participants were followed for about 25 years for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">600</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vobarno</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Vobarno Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21509">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21509"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33988330+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Vobarno Study represents the first observational study aimed to assess in a general population sample the relationship between parameters of cardiac and vascular structure (and function) and blood pressure values, measured in the clinic and during the 24 hours.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33988330+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the frame of The Vobarno Study blood samples for hematochemistry and DNA extraction, clinic and 24-hour blood pressure measurements, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, and aortic stiffness were measured in all subjects, living in a small town (Vobarno) between Brescia and the Garda Lake (Italy), and randomly selected from electoral roles.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20520574</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Pulse wave velocity and cardiovascular risk stratification in a general population: the Vobarno study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20520574</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20520574+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Pulse wave velocity and cardiovascular risk stratification in a general population: the Vobarno study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based observational study of middle-aged residents of Vobarno, a small town between Brescia and Lake Garda in northern Italy, randomly selected from the electoral rolls and examined with clinic and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure measurement, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, aortic stiffness and blood sampling for biochemistry and DNA extraction, to relate cardiac and vascular structure and function to blood pressure; participants were followed for about 25 years for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33988330</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:8621195</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">600</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>about 600 individuals, the Vobarno Study population as a 2009 congress abstract gives it (approximate)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7101653/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We have examined about 600 individuals (Vobarno Study population), who have been characterized for traditional cardiovascular risk factors, including cigarette smoking.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Vobarno</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21516"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:30845926</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8465</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>VVC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vlagtwedde/Vlaardingen Cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Vlagtwedde/Vlaardingen cohort study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Vlagtwedde/Vlaardingen study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21516">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005275"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21516"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pulmonary diseases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4824471/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen study is a general population based study on the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in a general population of exclusively white individuals of Dutch descent [18,19].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5362243/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Controls were derived from Vlagtwedde/Vlaardingen cohort study, a population-based cohort of adult subjects of European ancestry in the Netherlands, recruited from 1965 with a follow-up of over 25 years.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:30845926</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Limited overlap in significant hits between genome-wide association studies on two airflow obstruction definitions in the same population.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:30845926</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6407273/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To study the overlap between the two airflow obstruction definitions, all subjects with available genotypic data were included from the Dutch LifeLines Cohort Study (discovery sample) and the Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen study (replication sample) [17–19].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23054033</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:27055053</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28073367</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28273074</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:30845926</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8465</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>all subjects of the Vlagtwedde/Vlaardingen study, 1965-1990, whose vital status was assessed in 2008</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23054033+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Vital status of all 8,465 subjects on December 31st, 2008 was assessed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>VVC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21523"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000020</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:16753056</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1520</coho:numberOfCases>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Diabetes UK Warren 2 repository</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>W2C</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WARREN 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WARREN2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Warren 2</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Warren 2 Cases</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Warren 2 Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Warren 2 Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Diabetes UK Warren 2 Repository</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21523">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21523"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2873325/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case-control dataset included 1520 cases from the Diabetes UK Warren 2 Sib Pair Repository (61.5% males) and 2570 control samples from the 1958 British birth cohort (n = 2027, 50.6% males) [29], and the HRC control collection (n = 543, 49.9% males) derived from UK blood donors and available from the European Centre for Cell Culture (ECACC, CAMR, Salisbury, UK).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1534014/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Subjects for the family-based analysis were recruited as part of a Warren 2 cohort from across the UK and were independent of subjects in the case-control analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000020</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Personalized risk prediction for type 2 diabetes: the potential of genetic risk scores.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:27513194</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:16753056</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The functional &quot;KL-VS&quot; variant of KLOTHO is not associated with type 2 diabetes in 5028 UK Caucasians.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:16753056</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1534014/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cases were recruited from three sources, as described previously [10,11]: a collection of young-onset subjects (YT2D; age at diagnosis 18–45 years; n = 256); probands from type 2 diabetic sibships from the Diabetes UK Warren 2 repository (W2SP; n = 499) [12,13]; and a more recent collection of cases with type 2 diabetes from the Diabetes UK Warren 2 repository (W2C; age at diagnosis 35–65 years; not selected for having a family history of diabetes; n = 1038).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:16753056</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19672314</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20459604</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1520</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Diabetes UK repository cases analysed in the 2010 TNF/LTA study</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2873325/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case-control dataset included 1520 cases from the Diabetes UK Warren 2 Sib Pair Repository (61.5% males) and 2570 control samples from the 1958 British birth cohort (n = 2027, 50.6% males) [29], and the HRC control collection (n = 543, 49.9% males) derived from UK blood donors and available from the European Centre for Cell Culture (ECACC, CAMR, Salisbury, UK).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>W2C</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WARREN2</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21532"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:21738491</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8171</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WACS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Antioxidant Cardiovascular Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Antioxidant Cardiovascular Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21532">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_at_risk_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21532"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, women were eligible if they were aged 40 years or older, postmenopausal or had no intention of becoming pregnant, had a self-reported history of CVD, or had at least three cardiac risk factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15006283+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In a factorial design, 8171 U.S. female health professionals aged &gt;or=40 years were randomized to vitamin E, vitamin C, beta-carotene, or placebos.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:21738491</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of a sudden cardiac death susceptibility locus at 2q24.2 through genome-wide association in European ancestry individuals.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21738491</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128111/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The SCD cases from the Physicians&apos; Health Study (PHS I and II), the Nurses&apos; Health Study (NHS), the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS), and the Women&apos;s Antioxidant Cardiovascular Study (WACS) were included in the present analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15006283</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17698683</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8171</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>WACS randomized women at increased cardiovascular risk (1996)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>8,171 women were willing and eligible, were compliant during a 12-week run-in, and were randomized into the trial from June, 1995, through October, 1996 (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WACS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


