    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21545"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000989"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000004</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:34101481</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1751</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1673</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WCHS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Circle of Health Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Circle of Health Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21545">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007254"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21545"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7505987/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Study participants were breast cancer cases based on the Women’s Circle of Health Study (WCHS), a multi-site case-control study in New York City and New Jersey designed to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive breast cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766507/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Because of the large, racially mixed population of women in metropolitan New York City (NYC) and eastern New Jersey (NJ), we are currently conducting a case-control study, the Women&apos;s Circle of Health Study (WCHS), with the goal of accruing 1200 AA and 1200 EA women with breast cancer and an equal number of controls, to specifically address these questions.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000004</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Evaluating Polygenic Risk Scores for Breast Cancer in Women of African Ancestry.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33769540</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:34101481</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Risk of Breast Cancer Among Carriers of Pathogenic Variants in Breast Cancer Predisposition Genes Varies by Polygenic Risk Score.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34101481</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8330969/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The two population-based case-control studies are the Women&apos;s Circle of Health Study</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19865486</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24113797</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29073238</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33024820</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1751</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls who had completed the interview by the time of the 2013 analysis, African American and European American women (no total stated; enrolment continued afterwards)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3886722/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1,751 cases (979 AA and 772 EA) and 1,673 controls (958 AA and 715 EA) completed the interview.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1673</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls who had completed the interview by the time of the 2013 analysis, African American and European American women (no total stated; enrolment continued afterwards)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3886722/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1,751 cases (979 AA and 772 EA) and 1,673 controls (958 AA and 715 EA) completed the interview.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WCHS</owl:annotatedTarget>
