    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002557 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002557">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. WCPSOCCI is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for OCAC&apos;s study LAX: ovarian cancer patients of the Women&apos;s Cancer Program at the Samuel Oschin Comprehensive Cancer Institute, Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, collected since 1989 with data taken from medical records (PMC5625672 Table 1; PMID:28346442). OCAC names it only by the programme and the acronym LAX. It has no study name, design or defined recruitment of its own beyond being the programme&apos;s patients, so it is an unnamed institutional collection. Not a cohort. The CIMBA group from the same programme is E1212 (WCRI). Cedars-Sinai&apos;s MIRIAD IBD biobank (COHO:0000716) is unrelated. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Womens Cancer Program at the Samuel Oschin Comprehensive Cancer Institute</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002558 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002558">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Obsoleted 2026-09-24. WCRI is the PGS Catalog&apos;s id for CIMBA&apos;s group WCP: BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers from the Women&apos;s Cancer Program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles (PMID:32665703 supplement; PMID:28346442; PMID:29058716). CIMBA names the group only by the clinical programme, with no study name or recruitment protocol of its own. That matches how other CIMBA institution groups in this review were decided (UPENN, UCSF, MSKCC, FCCC, KUMC and OUH are all &apos;not a cohort&apos;). Not a cohort. The same programme&apos;s OCAC contribution is E1211 (WCPSOCCI). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">obsolete Womens Cancer Research Institute - Cedars-Sinai Medical Center</rdfs:label>
        <owl:deprecated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</owl:deprecated>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21554"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20862305</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1063</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1408</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2471</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WDS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Wuhan Diabetes Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21554">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005148"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21554"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>type 2 diabetes</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&amp;id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study includes 2,471 participants, 1,063 newly diagnosed T2D patients and 1,408 normal glucose tolerance (NGT) individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Four of these SNPs (rs10906115, rs1359790, rs10751301, and rs1436955) were selected for the final stage of de novo genotyping replication in two independent Chinese studies, the Wuhan Diabetes Study (WDS; 1,063 cases and 1,408 controls) and the Nutrition and Health of Aging Population in China (NHAPC) study (424 cases and 1,908 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20862305</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification of new genetic risk variants for type 2 diabetes.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20862305</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Four of these SNPs (rs10906115, rs1359790, rs10751301, and rs1436955) were selected for the final stage of de novo genotyping replication in two independent Chinese studies, the Wuhan Diabetes Study (WDS; 1,063 cases and 1,408 controls) and the Nutrition and Health of Aging Population in China (NHAPC) study (424 cases and 1,908 controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20862305</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22109280</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&amp;id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559"/>
