        <owl:annotatedTarget>A UK family-based collection of white families recruited from the Southampton area, each with at least two biological siblings aged 5 to 21 years with a current physician&apos;s diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication regularly, originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough for the study that identified ADAM33 as an asthma gene, and later used to test asthma genetic associations by transmission disequilibrium tests.</owl:annotatedTarget>
