        <obo:IAO_0000115>The randomised clinical trial component of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">68132</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI CT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI Clinical Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI-CT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Women&apos;s Health Initiative Clinical Trials</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Health Initiative - randomized clinical trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Health Initiative Clinical Trial</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21614">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_2000121"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21614"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>low-fat eating pattern</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The CT is designed to allow randomized controlled evaluation of three distinct interventions: a low-fat eating pattern, hypothesized to prevent breast cancer and colorectal cancer and, secondarily, coronary heart disease;</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9933300/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Women Health Initiative (WHI) study is the US nationwide, long-term health study in postmenopausal women, with fragility fracture as one of the major outcomes.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9933300/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 1993 to 1998, the WHI enrolled 161,808 women aged 50 to 79 in randomized clinical trials (CT) or an observational study (OS).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36797788</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide polygenic risk score for major osteoporotic fractures in postmenopausal women using associated single nucleotide polymorphisms.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36797788</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9933300/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>WHI CT examined the effects of menopausal hormone therapy (HT) vs. placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation vs. placebo, and low-fat eating patterns vs. usual eating patterns.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The randomised clinical trial component of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36797788</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:9492970</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">68132</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women enrolled and randomised in the WHI Clinical Trial, 1993-1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2608/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2608_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>There are two major components of WHI: (1) a Clinical Trial (CT) that enrolled and randomized 68,132 women ages 50 – 79 into at least one of three placebo-control clinical trials (hormone therapy, dietary modification, and calcium/vitamin D); and (2) an Observational Study (OS) that enrolled 93,676 women of the same age range into a parallel prospective cohort study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WHI CT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WHI-CT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002567 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002567">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21623"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:22504420</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A genetic study of hip fracture and bone mineral density within the Women&apos;s Health Initiative in the United States, made up of a case-control sample in which all hip fractures in the WHI Clinical Trial and Observational Study up to August 2007 were matched to controls, and a subsample of the WHI bone mineral density cohort, measured at three of the 40 WHI clinical centres, in which women with the best or worst hip bone density Z-scores and physical functioning scores were selected.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2166</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2490</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4656</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>GeCHIP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Components of HIP Fracture</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Genetic Components of Hip Fracture</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI GeCHIP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI-GeCHIP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Women&apos;s Health Initiative Genetic Components of HIP Fracture (GeCHIP) Consortium</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Health Initiative GeCHIP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Health Initiative Genetic Components of HIP Fracture Consortium</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
