    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000505"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000043</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31676865</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The hormone therapy component of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">27347</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI Hormone Therapy Trials</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI-HT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI-HT trials</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Women&apos;s Health Initiative Hormone Therapy study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Health Initiative Hormone Therapy Trial</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Health Initiative Hormone Therapy Trials</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3059994/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we examined the association between PM and VTE and interaction between PM and hormone therapy in a randomized, placebo-controlled trial of estrogen (E) or estrogen plus progestin (E + P) among a large geographically and ethnically diverse population of postmenopausal women living in the United States.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12171572/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The WHI Clinical Trials (CT; N=68,132) includes three overlapping components, each a randomized controlled comparison: the Hormone Therapy Trials (HT), Dietary Modification Trial, and Calcium and Vitamin D Trial.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000043</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis of venous thromboembolism identifies new risk loci and genetic overlap with arterial vascular disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31676865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31676865</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis of venous thromboembolism identifies new risk loci and genetic overlap with arterial vascular disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31676865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6858581/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, among 10,975 European women prospectively followed for up to 25 years in the WHI-HT, 690 incident VTE events were identified among participants with genetic data.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The hormone therapy component of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21036692</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31676865</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">27347</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>postmenopausal women randomized in the two hormone therapy trials (estrogen plus progestin, estrogen alone), 1993-1998</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6858581/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The WHI-HT initially comprised 27,347 postmenopausal women who were randomized to receive either estrogen plus progestin or estrogen alone versus placebo until the trials were stopped early in July 2002 and March 2004, respectively.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WHI-HT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000043</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31676865</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An ancillary study of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym LLS also denotes Leiden Longevity Study (COHO:0000107); this term is Women&apos;s Health Initiative Long Life Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7875</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>LLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Long Life Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI LLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI Long Life Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHI-LLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Womens Health Initiative Long Life Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Women&apos;s Health Initiative Long Life Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9434234/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, multiethnic postmenopausal women aged 50–79 years were recruited in 40 clinical centers nationwide between 1993 and 1998.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9434234/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population consisted of 7,875 women over 70 years old who enrolled in the WHI-LLS, an ancillary study to the WHI.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000043</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis of venous thromboembolism identifies new risk loci and genetic overlap with arterial vascular disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31676865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31676865</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association analysis of venous thromboembolism identifies new risk loci and genetic overlap with arterial vascular disease.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31676865</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6858581/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data used in this analysis included genetic data from WHI-HT participants derived from three separate GWAS sub-studies: 1) the WHI Genomics and Randomized Trials Network study (WHI-GARNET, 457 incident VTE events among 4,233 participants), (2) the WHI Memory Study (WHIMS, 180 incident VTE events among 5,637 participants), and (3) the WHI Long Life Study (WHI-LLS, 53 incident VTE events among 1,105 participants).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An ancillary study of the Women&apos;s Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32680817</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35522983</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7875</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women aged 63 to 99 who provided measures at the 2012-2013 home visit</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7566285/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 7,875 women between the ages of 63 and 99 years provided measures for the WHI-LLS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>LLS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WHI LLS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WHI-LLS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21651"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid21653"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000867</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:29047167</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2996</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHISTLER</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHeezing-Illnesses-STudy-LEidsche-Rijn</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Wheezing-Illnesses-Study-Leidsche-Rijn</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Wheezing Illnesses Study Leidsche Rijn</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21651">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_9000215"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21653">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0030828"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21651"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>endotoxin exposure</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15499901+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In particular, WHISTLER will provide a well-balanced view on the prognostic power of neonatal lung function and genetic and environmental factors (including viral infections and endotoxin exposure) to predict wheezing illnesses from birth to young adulthood and beyond.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21653"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>wheezing illnesses</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15499901+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aims of WHISTLER are to investigate determinants for wheezing illnesses (including neonatal lung function, viral infections, asthma-susceptibility genes and endotoxin exposure) and to derive a comprehensive risk score, that is appropriate for use in primary health care and allows for efficient planning of early preventive strategies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10503770/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study population live in a residential area near the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands, and include those from diverse social, cultural and socioeconomic backgrounds.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15499901+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Based on actual neonatal care practice and embedded in a larger epidemiological study, the Utrecht Health Project, WHISTLER will provide an unique framework to address issues in childhood respiratory disease that are currently insufficiently understood.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000867</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The association between a genetic risk score for allergy and the risk of developing allergies in childhood-Results of the WHISTLER cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29047167</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:29047167</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The association between a genetic risk score for allergy and the risk of developing allergies in childhood-Results of the WHISTLER cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29047167</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29047167+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GRS was tested in children who participated in a population-based newborn cohort (WHISTLER) and were followed from birth to school age.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:15499901</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37713433</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2996</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>healthy newborns enrolled in the birth cohort from 2001 (2023)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10503770/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study was part of the WHeezing-Illnesses-STudy-LEidsche-Rijn (WHISTLER) prospective birth cohort of 2996 healthy newborns that commenced in 2001.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>WHISTLER</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000617"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS000814</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:23433573</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10308</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>WHII</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Whitehall</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Whitehall II</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Whitehall II study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Whitehall Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Whitehall II Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3281313/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Setting Civil service departments in London, United Kingdom.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS000814</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Use of low-density lipoprotein cholesterol gene score to distinguish patients with polygenic and monogenic familial hypercholesterolaemia: a case-control study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23433573</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:23433573</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Use of low-density lipoprotein cholesterol gene score to distinguish patients with polygenic and monogenic familial hypercholesterolaemia: a case-control study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23433573</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23433573+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In November, 2011, we assembled a sample of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia from three UK-based sources and compared them with a healthy control sample from the UK Whitehall II (WHII) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22223828</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23843750</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28642251</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10308</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>civil servants aged 35-55 recruited at phase 1 (1985-1988)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5480222/unicode</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 10 308 people (6895 men and 3413 women, aged 35-55) were recruited over the years 1985 to 1988.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
