        <obo:IAO_0000115>A collection of Tibetans recruited at two sites about 4,100 m above sea level on the Tibetan Plateau in Sichuan, western China: at Seda, among people studying or working at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute who came from diverse regions of the plateau, and at Litang, among nomadic people who had lived in the area for generations; their blood DNA was genotyped on the Illumina CoreExome array for a study of high-altitude adaptation, and the genotype and phenotype data are held by the Wenzhou Medical University biobank.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3008</coho:numberOfParticipants>
