    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A series of population-based case–control studies of breast cancer run at the University of Wisconsin, whose cases are Wisconsin women with incident breast cancer reported to the statewide cancer registry and whose controls are women without breast cancer randomly selected from lists of licensed drivers and, for women aged 65 or over until 2003, of Medicare beneficiaries, all interviewed by telephone about reproductive history, family cancer history and lifestyle, to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for breast cancer; it is the Wisconsin part of the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study, which recruited Wisconsin cases from 1988 to 2008.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22490319</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24647890</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29439783</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16076</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls of the five case-control studies enrolled 1988-2004 (no total stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35772615+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We develop a method to identify geographic patterns of breast cancer odds using the Wisconsin Women&apos;s Health Study, a series of 5 population-based case-control studies of female Wisconsin residents aged 20-79 enrolled in 1988-2004 (cases=16,076, controls=16,795).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">16795</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer cases and controls of the five case-control studies enrolled 1988-2004 (no total stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35772615+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We develop a method to identify geographic patterns of breast cancer odds using the Wisconsin Women&apos;s Health Study, a series of 5 population-based case-control studies of female Wisconsin residents aged 20-79 enrolled in 1988-2004 (cases=16,076, controls=16,795).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586"/>
