        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:38872215</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A Chinese genetic sample for colorectal neoplasia drawn from the population-based colorectal cancer screening programme of Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, made up of a one-to-one matched case-control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 and a cross-sectional colonoscopy screening study performed in 2014, whose participants were genotyped on the Illumina Asian Screening Array.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1814</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1814</coho:numberOfControls>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5980</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ZJCRC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Zhejiang Colorectal Cancer set</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Zhejiang colorectal cancer set</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid21826">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005335"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid21826"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>advanced colorectal neoplasm</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11170922/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 1814 patients with advanced colorectal neoplasm (including 1622 advanced adenoma and 192 cancer cases) and 1814 lesion-free controls were finally included in this study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11170922/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Participants were recruited from a one-to-one matched case–control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 based on an ongoing population-based CRC screening program running in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS004912</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Developing an optimal stratification model for colorectal cancer screening and reducing racial disparities in multi-center population-based studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38872215</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:38872215</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Developing an optimal stratification model for colorectal cancer screening and reducing racial disparities in multi-center population-based studies.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:38872215</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38872215+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Then, the performance of each PRS was assessed and validated in two independent cross-sectional screening sets, including 4600 patients with advanced colorectal neoplasm, 4495 patients with non-advanced adenoma, and 21,199 normal individuals from the ZJCRC (Zhejiang colorectal cancer set; EAS) and PLCO (the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial; European, EUR) studies.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
