        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:25874636</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>CMPF does not associate with impaired glucose metabolism in individuals with features of metabolic syndrome.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:25874636</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4398480/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this Sysdimet study, 106 men and women were randomized into three groups</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:21870174</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24587337</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">131</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals randomised to the three diets</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:21870174</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Altogether, 131 individuals were assigned to either the Healthy Diet (n = 44), a whole-grain-enriched diet (WGED) (n = 42) or a control (n = 45) diet, and 104 participants (mean ± SD: age 59 ± 7 years; BMI 31.1 ± 3.5 kg/m(2)) who had completed the study, were analysed (Healthy Diet n = 36, WGED n = 34 and control diet n = 34).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SYSDIMET</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Sysdimet</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37196097</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the first-trimester serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>FMC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Finnish Maternity Cohort Serum Bank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>MAT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Maternity cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Finnish Maternity Cohort</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://esis.fi/description/"/>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://www.ppshp.fi/Tutkimus-ja-opetus/Biopankki/Pages/default.aspx"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Finland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5727241/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Because the FMC is nationwide and contains samples from 94% of all Finnish pregnant women 11, very large‐scale over‐generation studies can be designed by linking the identities of the mothers to their offspring and/or relatives 13.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37196097</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Sexually Transmitted Infections and Risk of Epithelial Ovarian Cancer: Results From the Finnish Maternity Cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37196097</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10681868/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We measured antibodies (Abs) to CT, MG, HSV-2, and HPV-16/18 in serum samples in a nested case-control study in the Finnish Maternity Cohort (N = 484 cases 1:1 matched to controls).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the first-trimester serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:29071810</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women with stored serum samples (about 1 million; 2.0 million samples), 2016</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:29071810</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>At the end of 2016 the FMC comprised 2.0 million serum samples from about 1 million women.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>FMC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Finnish Maternity Cohort Serum Bank</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
