        <owl:annotatedTarget>The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.</owl:annotatedTarget>
