        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.</obo:IAO_0000115>
