    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22165"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:42051041</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1080</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BiSC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>BiSC Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Barcelona Life Study Cohort</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22165">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ExO_0000002"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22165"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>socio-environmental exposome during pregnancy and childhood</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Barcelona Life Study Cohort (BiSC) is an exposome cohort, aiming to comprehensively evaluate the socio-environmental and genetic determinants (i) of foetal and child health, growth, and development towards adult life and (ii) of maternal mental and physical health and wellbeing during pregnancy and afterwards, while shedding light on the underlying biological mechanisms.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The enrolment of the BiSC participants (n=1080) was carried out between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain, including Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau, and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona, and their corresponding primary healthcare centres.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:42051041</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Maternal Chrono-Nutrition and Placental DNA Methylation: The BiSC Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42051041</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42051041+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Data came from 389 pregnant women in the Barcelona Life Study Cohort (BiSC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1080</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pregnant women enrolled 2018-2021</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The enrolment of the BiSC participants (n=1080) was carried out between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain, including Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau, and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona, and their corresponding primary healthcare centres.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>BiSC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22172"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22174"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:36601007</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">191</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PUBMEP</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PUBMEP</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>PUBMEP study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Puberty and metabolic risk in obese children. Epigenetic alterations and pathophysiological and diagnostic implications</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22172">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011122"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22174">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0011565"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22172"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>obesity</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PUBMEP</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Children were allocated into five experimental groups according to their obesity and insulin resistance (IR) status before and after the onset of puberty.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22174"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>metabolic syndrome</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PUBMEP</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Children were allocated into five experimental groups according to their obesity and insulin resistance (IR) status before and after the onset of puberty.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Hence, the PUBMEP study aimed to evaluate the prevalence of MetS and the progression of cardiometabolic risk factors related to it from prepuberty to puberty in a cohort of Spanish children.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PUBMEP is a longitudinal study based on the follow-up of a cohort of children who had previously participated in the GENOBOX study (22–29).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36601007</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Progression of metabolic syndrome and associated cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty in children: The PUBMEP study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36601007</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Hence, the PUBMEP study aimed to evaluate the prevalence of MetS and the progression of cardiometabolic risk factors related to it from prepuberty to puberty in a cohort of Spanish children.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36601007</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">191</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>children followed from prepuberty to puberty</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36601007</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Longitudinal study based on the follow-up until puberty of a cohort of 191 prepubertal Spanish boys and girls without congenital, chronic, or inflammatory diseases: undernutrition: or intake of any drug that could alter blood glucose, blood pressure, or lipid metabolism.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PUBMEP</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22182"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22184"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22186"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ecuador"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:40777557</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">746</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ESPINA</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ESPINA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
