    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:40777557</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Urinary pesticide biomarkers from adolescence to young adulthood in an agricultural setting in Ecuador: Study of secondary exposure to pesticides among children, adolescents, and adults (ESPINA) 2016 and 2022 examination data.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40777557</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329275/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This article presents urinary pesticide metabolite concentrations for 665 participants in the “Study of Secondary Exposure to Pesticides among Children, Adolescents, and Adults” (ESPINA)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40777557</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://espina.ucsd.edu/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">746</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>analysed subset: participants with AChE measured at eight exams over 16 years (2024)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41904267</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We measured AChE activity in fresh fingerstick blood from 746 participants ages 4 to 26 years who resided in an agricultural county in Ecuador, totaling 3119 observations.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ESPINA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35641005</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2000000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ROLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>RoLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Rome longitudinal study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Rome Longitudinal Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37944432+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We enrolled 1,739,277 individuals 30 + years from the 2011 census in Rome, Italy, and followed them up until 2019.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35641005</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Differences in mortality between temporary and permanent workers: results from the Rome Longitudinal Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35641005</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9157355/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We used the Rome Longitudinal Study, the administrative cohort of residents in Rome who filled in the 2001 population census.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35641005</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37944432</obo:IAO_0000119>
