    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22207"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>alcohol</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17049075+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main hypotheses of the HAPIEE study relate to the role of alcohol, nutrition and psychosocial factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22209"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>nutrition</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17049075+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main hypotheses of the HAPIEE study relate to the role of alcohol, nutrition and psychosocial factors.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1626086/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HAPIEE (Health, Alcohol and Psychosocial factors In Eastern Europe) study consists of three cohorts in Novosibirsk (Russia), Krakow (Poland) and six centres in the Czech Republic (Havirov/Karvina, Hradec Kralove, Jihlava, Kromeriz, Liberec and Usti nad Labem).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000265"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1626086/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The HAPIEE (Health, Alcohol and Psychosocial factors In Eastern Europe) study consists of three cohorts in Novosibirsk (Russia), Krakow (Poland) and six centres in the Czech Republic (Havirov/Karvina, Hradec Kralove, Jihlava, Kromeriz, Liberec and Usti nad Labem).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:23113606</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Lack of an association between left-handedness and APOE polymorphism in a large sample of adults: results of the Czech HAPIEE study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23113606</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23113606+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Lack of an association between left-handedness and APOE polymorphism in a large sample of adults: results of the Czech HAPIEE study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:17049075</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8856</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>men and women aged 45-69 at baseline 2002-2005</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Four representative urban cohorts of middle-aged men and women were established in the Czech Republic (n = 8,856), Poland (n = 10,727), Lithuania (n = 10,940), and Russia (n = 9,363) in the early 2000s.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>HAPIEE-CZ</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22217"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22219"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22221"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Malawi"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41775864</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The participants of a randomised, single-blind controlled trial in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project: pregnant women enrolled from 2011, and later their infants. The women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation, and the infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1391</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>International Lipid‑Based Nutrient Supplements Project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>iLINS-DYAD-M</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>iLiNS DOSE iLiNS DYAD</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>iLiNS-DYAD-M</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>iLiNS-DYAD-Malawi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements Project-DYAD-Malawi</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
