        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Romania"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Slovakia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Slovenia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20731877</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym SHARE also denotes WHI SNP Health Association Resource (COHO:0000604), Sinai-Helmsley Alliance for Research Excellence (COHO:0000725) and SNP Health Association Asthma Resource Project (COHO:0002374); this term is Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">140000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SHARE</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SHARE</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Croatia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-6</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Additionally, Croatia participated in SHARE Wave 6 for the first time.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cyprus"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2017, the main data collection of Wave 7 took place in 28 countries - full coverage of the EU was achieved by including 8 new countries in SHARE: Finland, Lithuania, Latvia, Slovakia, Romania, Bulgaria, Malta and Cyprus.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Greece"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>They constitute a balanced representation of the various regions in Europe, ranging from Scandinavia (Denmark and Sweden) through Central Europe (Austria, France, Germany, Switzerland, Belgium, and the Netherlands) to the Mediterranean (Spain, Italy and Greece).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Israel"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Israel joined the SHARE framework in late 2004, being the first country in the Middle East to initiate a systematic study of its aging population.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Luxembourg"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-5</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The following countries collected data and are part of the scientific release: Austria, Belgium, Switzerland, Czech Republic, Germany, Denmark, Estonia, Spain, France, Israel, Italy, Luxembourg, Netherlands, Sweden, and Slovenia.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Republic_of_Ireland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-2</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Two &apos;new&apos; EU member states - the Czech Republic and Poland - as well as Ireland joined SHARE in 2006 and participated in the second wave of data collection in 2006-07.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Slovenia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-4</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2010, Estonia, Hungary, Portugal and Slovenia joined SHARE Wave 4, which is the third regular panel wave of the survey following the SHARELIFE life history questionnaire.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20731877</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>A frailty instrument for primary care: findings from the Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe (SHARE).</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20731877</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2939541/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A Frailty Instrument for primary care: findings from the Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe (SHARE)</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23778574</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">140000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people aged 50+ interviewed since 2004 (all waves, 28 countries and Israel)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From 2004 until today, 530,000 in-depth interviews with 140,000 people aged 50 or older from 28 European countries and Israel have been conducted.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644"/>
