        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40838581</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12497661/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>LASI-DAD is a representative subsample of LASI that has a focus on cognitive aging and dementia among persons aged 60 and over in India, with an oversampling of those at a higher risk of cognitive impairment.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationally representative in-depth study of late-life cognition and dementia in India, led from the University of Southern California with Indian partners, that recruited a sub-sample of Longitudinal Aging Study in India (LASI) respondents aged 60 and older, oversampling those at high risk of cognitive impairment, from 18 states and union territories in 2017–2019 and 22 in 2022–2024, and assessed them with the Harmonized Cognitive Assessment Protocol, informant interviews, geriatric assessments, blood biomarkers, neuroimaging, genomics and environmental exposure measures.</owl:annotatedTarget>
