        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005271"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22273"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>infant nutritional intervention</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GINIplus (German Infant Nutritional Intervention plus environmental and genetic influences on allergy development) and LISA (Influence of Lifestyle factors on the development of the Immune System and Allergies) studies are prospective population-based birth cohorts from East and West Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22275"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental and lifestyle influences on allergy development</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GINIplus (German Infant Nutritional Intervention plus environmental and genetic influences on allergy development) and LISA (Influence of Lifestyle factors on the development of the Immune System and Allergies) studies are prospective population-based birth cohorts from East and West Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22277"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>allergy</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The GINIplus (German Infant Nutritional Intervention plus environmental and genetic influences on allergy development) and LISA (Influence of Lifestyle factors on the development of the Immune System and Allergies) studies are prospective population-based birth cohorts from East and West Germany.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Germany"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4112441/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>GINI/LISA North covers the rural area near the industrial Ruhr area in Germany</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24862831</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Greenness and allergies: evidence of differential associations in two areas in Germany.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24862831</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4112441/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Longitudinal associations were assessed per study area (GINI/LISA South and GINI/LISA North) using generalised estimation equations adjusted for host and environmental covariates.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24149084</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24862831</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
