        <rdfs:comment>The Infants’ Environmental Health Study [Infantes y Salud Ambiental (ISA)] is a prospective community-based birth cohort study in Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, aimed at examining possible effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children’s growth and neurodevelopment.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652"/>
