        <obo:IAO_0000115>A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer&apos;s disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">5834</coho:numberOfParticipants>
