        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:37838044</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">792</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SPRINT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SPRINT project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Sustainable Plant Protection Transition</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Sustainable Plant-Protection Transition</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sustainable plant protection transition: a global health approach</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22347">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_participants_with_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_0000530"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22347"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>pesticide mixtures (plant protection products) among farmers, neighbours of agricultural fields and consumers</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Cross-sectional study performed in 2021 to assess differences in exposure of farmers (organic and non-organic practises), neighbours (people living close to agricultural fields) and controls (&apos;consumers&apos; living away from agricultural fields) to pesticides.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Argentina"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8592492/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>An additional study site in Argentina will inform the impact of PPP use on growing soybean which is an important European protein-source in animal feed.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Croatia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/cshr</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case study area is located on the largest peninsula of the Republic of Croatia in the northern part of the Adriatic coast, Istria (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Czech_Republic"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/cscz</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case study is realised in the Czech Republic located in the Central Europe (see Fig. 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Denmark"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/csdk</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The farms within the Case study area in Denmark are located in North and Central Jutland, in the western part of Denmark (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/France"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/csfr</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case study is located in Southwestern France, near the Atlantic Coast, in the Nouvelle Aquitaine Region (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Italy"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/csit</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Po Valley is the largest plain of southern Europe, with an extension of around 650 km from the Western Alps to the Adriatic Sea; it is located in Northern Italy</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Netherlands"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/csnl</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study site is located in the northern part of The Netherlands, enclosed by the Waddensea in the north (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Portugal"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/cspt</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The case study is located in the central littoral of Portugal</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Slovenia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/cssi</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Case study of Central Slovenia (2.555 km2) is located in the central part of Slovenia (300 m - 2.400 m altitude).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spain"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/cses</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Campo de Cartagena basin is located in the southeast of Spain (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Switzerland"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://sprint-h2020.eu/case-studies/csch</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>CSS4 is located in Canton Bern close to the university of Bern.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37838044</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Occurrence of pesticide residues in indoor dust of farmworker households across Europe and Argentina.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37838044</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37838044+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the present study, part of the Horizon 2020 funded SPRINT project, the presence of 198 pesticide residues was assessed in 128 indoor dust samples from both conventional and organic farmworker households across Europe, and in Argentina.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119> https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34780516 </obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
