    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22384"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Argentina"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Central_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chile"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Costa_Rica"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cuba"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dominican_Republic"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Latin_America_and_the_Caribbean"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mexico"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Peru"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Puerto_Rico"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Uruguay"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Venezuela"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:42724639</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">174180</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CC-LAC</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CC-LAC</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>The Cohorts Consortium of Latin America and the Caribbean (CC-LAC)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Cohorts Consortium of Latin America and the Caribbean</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22384">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004995"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22384"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>cardiovascular disease</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main aim of the CC-LAC is to start a collaborative cohort data pooling in LAC to examine the association between cardio-metabolic risk factors (e.g. blood pressure, glucose and lipids) and non-fatal and fatal cardiovascular outcomes (e.g. stroke or myocardial infarction).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/article/PMC/PMC7746413</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aforementioned 7 cohorts that have not been pooled because cardiovascular outcomes are not yet available include: CRONICAS Cohort Study (Peru), 27 Mexican Health &amp; Aging Study (Mexico), 28 Puerto Rican Elderly Health Conditions (Puerto Rico), 29 Costa Rican Longevity and Healthy Aging Study (CRELES) 1945–1955 Retirement Cohort (Costa Rica), 30 Influence of Biopsychosocial Factors on the Survival of the Elderly in Northeast Brazil—A Prospective Study (Brazil), 31 Baependi Heart Study (Brazil) 32 and MONICA-VITÓRIA study (Brazil).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aforementioned 7 cohorts that have not been pooled because cardiovascular outcomes are not yet available include: CRONICAS Cohort Study (Peru),27 Mexican Health &amp; Aging Study (Mexico),28 Puerto Rican Elderly Health Conditions (Puerto Rico),29 Costa Rican Longevity and Healthy Aging Study (CRELES) 1945–1955 Retirement Cohort (Costa Rica),30 Influence of Biopsychosocial Factors on the Survival of the Elderly in Northeast Brazil—A Prospective Study (Brazil),31 Baependi Heart Study (Brazil)32 and MONICA-VITÓRIA study (Brazil).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Puerto_Rico"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Among those cohorts we currently have pooled, there are two multi-country studies: Centro de Excelencia en Salud Cardiovascular para América del Sur (CESCAS) Cohort (Argentina, Chile and Uruguay)24 and the 10/66 Study (Cuba, Dominican Republic, Peru, Venezuela, Mexico and Puerto Rico),25,26 whereas the other cohort studies were based in only one country.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:42724639</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Visceral adipose tissue and incident cardiovascular disease among individuals without diabetes: an analysis of 15 prospective cohorts from 7 countries in Latin America.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42724639</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42724639+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here, we evaluated the association between estimated VAT (eVAT) and incident CVD among individuals without diabetes and estimated its population-attributable fraction (PAF) using data from the Cohorts Consortium of Latin America and the Caribbean (CC-LAC).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32888015</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39687239</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">174180</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals pooled from 32 cohorts at the first datalock (29 March 2020)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:32888015</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>At the time of the first datalock, data from 174 180 individuals have been pooled: 171 937 (98.7%) have complete follow-up or were censored (e.g. lost-to follow-up or death by other causes), 578 (0.3%) have had a first non-fatal cardiovascular event and 1665 (1.0%) have experienced a fatal cardiovascular event (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CC-LAC</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22393"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22395"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22397"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22399"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ecuador"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:24587469</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George&apos;s, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2404</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ECUAVIDA</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECUAVIDA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECUAVIDA birth cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>ECUAVIDA cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Ecuador Life study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ecuador Life</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22393">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_designed_to_study_exposure"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECTO_3000000"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22395">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004979"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22397">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005202"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22399">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005271"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22393"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>early-life microbial exposures</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>soil-transmitted helminth (STH) parasites</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4681103/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The ECUAVIDA birth cohort is studying the impact of exposures to soil-transmitted helminth (STH) parasites and early-life microbial exposures on the development of atopy, allergic diseases and immune responses in childhood.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22395"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>asthma</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ECUAVIDA</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>What for -The main goal is to investigate the origins of allergic diseases, asthma, and atopy in low- and middle-income tropical settings.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22397"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>atopy</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ECUAVIDA</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>What for -The main goal is to investigate the origins of allergic diseases, asthma, and atopy in low- and middle-income tropical settings.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22399"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>allergic diseases</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ECUAVIDA</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>What for -The main goal is to investigate the origins of allergic diseases, asthma, and atopy in low- and middle-income tropical settings.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ecuador"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4681103/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 2404 newborns were recruited between 2006 and 2009 in a public hospital serving the rural district of Quininde, Esmeraldas Province, in a tropical region of coastal Ecuador.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:24587469</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Risk factors for soil-transmitted helminth infections during the first 3 years of life in the tropics; findings from a birth cohort.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24587469</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24587469+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>To investigate risk factors for infection in early childhood, we analysed data prospectively collected in the ECUAVIDA birth cohort in Ecuador.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George&apos;s, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24990475</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2404</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>newborns recruited 2006-2009</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:24990475</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A total of 2404 newborns were recruited between 2006 and 2009 in a public hospital serving the rural district of Quininde, Esmeraldas Province, in a tropical region of coastal Ecuador.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>ECUAVIDA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


