    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:31816882</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17708</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CHARLS</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>CHARLS</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">China Health and Retirement Longitudinal Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23243115+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The China Health and Retirement Longitudinal Study (CHARLS) is a nationally representative longitudinal survey of persons in China 45 years of age or older and their spouses, including assessments of social, economic, and health circumstances of community-residents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31816882</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Public Health Insurance, Non-Farm Labor Supply, and Farmers&apos; Income: Evidence from New Rural Cooperative Medical Scheme.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31816882</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31816882+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Our dataset comprised of 8273 people, aged 45 or above, from the China Health and Retirement Longitudinal Study (CHARLS) conducted in 2011 and 2013.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23243115</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17708</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>respondents in the 2011-2012 national baseline</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:23243115</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The national baseline survey for the study was conducted between June 2011 and March 2012 and involved 17 708 respondents.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>CHARLS</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22418"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:41159539</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples of people aged 5 years and older, drawn from National Health Service general practice registers, SARS-CoV-2 swab tests (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3000000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/REACT</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>REACT</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>REACT Cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>REACT Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>REACT programme</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Real-time Assessment of Community Transmission</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Real-time Assessment of Community Transmission (REACT) Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#GEC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22418">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100096"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22418"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>COVID-19</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36893367+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission-1 (REACT-1) Study was funded by the Department of Health and Social Care in England to provide reliable and timely estimates of prevalence of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) infection over time, by person and place.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36893367+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The study team (researchers from Imperial College London and its logistics partner Ipsos) wrote to named individuals aged 5 years and older in random cross-sections of the population of England, using the National Health Service list of patients registered with a general practitioner (near-universal coverage) as a sampling frame.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41159539</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>&quot;I Put a Lot of Emphasis on Work Because I Want to Keep My Job&quot;: A Population-Based Interview Study of Long Covid and Employment Changes in England.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41159539</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41159539+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We conducted a qualitative analysis of data from the Real-time Assessment of Community Transmission (REACT) Study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples of people aged 5 years and older, drawn from National Health Service general practice registers, SARS-CoV-2 swab tests (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36893367</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37733993</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3000000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>people consenting to recontact and/or health-data linkage (stated as &apos;over 3 million&apos;)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>REACT Cohort is now made up of over 3 million people who have consented to follow-up by providing permission for us to contact them future research and/or to link to their health data.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>REACT</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22425"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:36006149</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities&apos; disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">301</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/3xG</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
