    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22425"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental and lifestyle exposure</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>environmental exposures via biomonitoring</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10058482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The aim of the 3xG study is to follow-up the health and development of growing children as a sentinel population and to study the influence of environmental exposures via biomonitoring.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10058482/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The 3xG study (Health—Municipalities—Birth, translated from Gezondheid, Gemeenten, Geboorten) is a birth cohort study that monitors and promotes health of the inhabitants of three bordering rural communities (Dessel, Mol, and Retie) in Flanders, Belgium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:36006149</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Glyphosate and AMPA in Human Urine of HBM4EU Aligned Studies: Part A Children.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:36006149</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9415901/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The urinary data on Gly and AMPA were obtained from Germany (GerES V-sub; 2015–2017), Cyprus (ORGANIKO; 2017), Slovenia (SLO CRP; 2018), France (ESTEBAN; 2014–2016) and Belgium (3XG; 2019–2020).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities&apos; disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:36976969</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://studie3xg.be/nl</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
