    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22517"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chile"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/SouthAmerica"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:40399555</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile&apos;s Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2262</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>C19-GenoNet</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>COVID-19 Genomics Network</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Chilean COVID-19 Genomics Network Biorepository</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>RED GENÓMICA COVID-19</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chilean COVID-19 Biorepository</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22517">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0100096"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22517"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>COVID-19</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection provided broad informed consent.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chile"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This paper reports the articulation of a network across Chile and the creation of the Chilean COVID-19 Biorepository, the first nationwide multicenter repository built under biobanking standards to ensure the high quality, reproducibility, and interoperability of samples and data as a resource for collaborative multi-omics research.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:40399555</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Genome-wide association study of long COVID.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40399555</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12165857/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>For the replication of the FOXP4 lead variants, we obtained data from the following nine additional studies: COVID-19 cohort at LGDB (LatviaGDB), COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet), COVID-19 Host Immune Response Pathogenesis Study (CHIRP), Estonian Biobank (EstBB), Fondazione Genomics SARS-CoV-2 Study (FoGS), GENCOV Study (GENCOV), Mass General Brigham Biobank (MGB), The Post-hospitalization COVID-19 study (PHOSP-COVID) and VA MVP.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile&apos;s Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119> https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:39596552 </obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2262</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection enrolled (2020-2021)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39596552</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In five months, 2262 participants were enrolled, pseudonymized, and sorted by disease severity.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>C19-GenoNet</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22524"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:42167794</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women&apos;s health as they age.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1300000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Million Women Study</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://www.millionwomenstudy.org/introduction/"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22524">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/is_population_study_of"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0007254"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22524"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>breast cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13913/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The main purpose of the Million Women Study is to examine the relationship between breast cancer and use of HRT, in a context where use of hormonal therapy is recorded as reliably as possible and breast cancers are diagnosed as uniformly and consistently as possible.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13913/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Women are asked to join the Million Women Study when they are invited to routine screening for breast cancer at 61 of the screening centres of the UK National Health Service Breast Screening Programme (NHSBSP).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:42167794</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Risk factors for multimorbidity of cardiovascular diseases in the prospective Million Women Study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42167794</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13202100/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Million Women Study is a population-based cohort study of 1.3 million UK women.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women&apos;s health as they age.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:11056681</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1300000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women aged 50-64 recruited 1996-2001 (rounded figure as stated)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:42167794</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>1.3 million women aged 50–64 years were recruited into the Million Women Study in 1996–2001.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saudi_Arabia"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:33194979</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">60000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Saudi Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SBB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SNB</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Saudi National Biobank</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Saudi Biobank</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saudi_Arabia"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Saudi Biobank is one of the important medical research projects in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia to study the impact of a healthy lifestyle, genes and the environment in the Saudi population.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:33194979</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Predictors of Seatbelt Use Among Saudi Adults: Results From the National Biobank Project.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:33194979</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7649265/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This cross-sectional study was performed using data from the Saudi National Biobank (SNB).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:33194979</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41721974</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">60000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>participants enrolled to date (lower bound, &apos;more than 60,000&apos;), recruitment ongoing (2026)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41721974</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>With more than 60,000 participants enrolled to date—and a target of 200,000 participants—the Biobank integrates rich datasets, including EHRs, self-reported information, and diverse biospecimens [3].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SBB</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
