        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:41469377</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>The Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS) Study: delivering precision medicine research for Asian populations.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:41469377</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12764833/supplementaryFiles</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Panel a) admixture analysis of the HELIOS (labelled SG100K) data using SCOPE with k=6 populations.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A collection of four longitudinal population health cohorts in Singapore (HELIOS, the Singapore Population Health Studies, the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases and SingHeart), brought together under an NMRC grant and in partnership with Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE) and the Genome Institute of Singapore in phase II of the National Precision Medicine programme, whose multi-ancestry Asian participants were whole-genome sequenced and linked to electronic health records to study the determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41469377</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">100000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>approximate number of Singapore residents across the four member cohorts in the PRECISE-SG100K dataset</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The PRECISE-SG100K resource is a unique multi-ancestry Asian population cohort dataset of ~100,000 Singaporean residents, jointly created by PRECISE, SG100K Institutions and GIS.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000001"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912"/>
        <coho:hasCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Southern_Africa"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:39282516</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa&apos;s Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">355000</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SAPRIN</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SAPRIN (South African Population Research Infrastructure Network)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>SAPRIN population cohort</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#IHCC_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">South African Population Research Infrastructure Network</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/"/>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10030929/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The MRC/Wits Rural Public Health and Health Transitions Research Unit and Agincourt Health and Socio-Demographic Surveillance System, a node of the South African Population Research Infrastructure Network (SAPRIN), is supported by the Department of Science and Innovation</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>What has been done?Since SAPRIN’s inception in 2016, three existing health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa have been brought together to form a harmonized national network, namely: MRC/Wits University Agincourt HDSS in Bushbuckridge District, Mpumalanga, established in 1992 with a 2019 population of 115 000 individuals2; University of Limpopo DIMAMO HDSS in the Capricorn District of Limpopo, established in 1995, with population of 8000 individuals, then expanded to 42 000 individuals in 2010, and expanded again in 2019 to 100 0003; and the Africa Health Research Institute (AHRI) HDSS in uMkhanyakude District, KwaZulu-Natal, linked to the University of KwaZulu-Natal,4 established in 2000 with a 2019 population of 140 000 individuals.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/South_Africa"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Since SAPRIN’s inception in 2016, three existing health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa have been brought together to form a harmonized national network, namely: MRC/Wits University Agincourt HDSS in Bushbuckridge District, Mpumalanga, established in 1992 with a 2019 population of 115 000 individuals</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:39282516</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Dataset: A consolidated and harmonised Verbal Autopsy dataset from Health and Demographic Surveillance Sites in South Africa.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:39282516</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399759/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The dataset harmonises and links routinely collected VA data from the South African Population Research Infrastructure Network (SAPRIN).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa&apos;s Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:34966919</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">355000</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>individuals under surveillance in the three founding HDSS nodes in 2020</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC9365637</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In 2020, the SAPRIN population cohort covered 355000 individuals for whom data on births and deaths, residency status and migration, household asset ownership status, and measures of well-being including employment, education and social protection are updated three times a year.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SAPRIN</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>SAPRIN (South African Population Research Infrastructure Network)</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


