        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:37337639</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Trans-ethnic polygenic risk scores for body mass index: An international hundred K+ cohorts consortium study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:37337639</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10280047/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As a collaboration model of the International Hundred K+ Cohorts Consortium (IHCC), we endeavored to develop a globally applicable trans‐ethnic PRS for body mass index (BMI) through this relatively new international effort.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium of large population cohorts, established in 2018 to work beyond the constraints of individual health and population cohorts, whose members are chosen for size, longitudinal health follow-up, broad participant selection, biological sample collection and a commitment to data sharing, and which maintains the IHCC Cohort Atlas, a directory of the data its member cohorts hold.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:40841586</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">33872619</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>unique participants across the 69 member cohorts that reported (approximate, summed by the consortium), 2025</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12371067/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>A Breakdown of ~33,872,619 unique participants across 69 reporting sites.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
