    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid22912"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Asia"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia"/>
        <coho:isCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PGS001776</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:35765848</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A population-based colorectal cancer case-control collection in Shanghai, China, assembled for genetic studies in the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium from the Shanghai-1, Shanghai-2 and Shanghai-3 sample series. The early series include colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study and Shanghai Men’s Health Study, with additional controls from Shanghai breast cancer studies; Shanghai-3 includes colorectal cancer cases newly recruited through the Shanghai Cancer Registry in 2009–2011, with controls from the health cohorts and breast cancer studies.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym Shanghai also denotes Shanghai Study (COHO:0000153); this term is Shanghai CRC Study.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <coho:numberOfCases rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2368</coho:numberOfCases>
        <coho:numberOfControls rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8219</coho:numberOfControls>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Studies</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Studies (Shanghai-1,2,3)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Shanghai Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#PGS_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Shanghai CRC Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid22912">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0005575"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid22912"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>colorectal cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Colorectal cancer (CRC) cases for the project were derived from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) and the Shanghai Men’s Health Study (SMHS), both population-based cohort studies which are being conducted in urban Shanghai, China.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/China"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Briefly, 728 cases and 728 matched controls in these two studies were identified from among participants of the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) 2 and the Shanghai Men’s Health Study (SMHS) 3 , two population-based cohort studies conducted in Shanghai, China, with a combined sample size of 136,631 participants.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PGS001776</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Ability of known colorectal cancer susceptibility SNPs to predict colorectal cancer risk: A cohort study within the UK Biobank.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:34525106</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:35765848</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Developing and validating polygenic risk scores for colorectal cancer risk prediction in East Asians.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:35765848</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9509464/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Shanghai Studies (Shanghai-1,2,3) Chinese 3,303 4,612 50.2 85.0 61.3 ± 8.52 54.7 ± 9.60</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A population-based colorectal cancer case-control collection in Shanghai, China, assembled for genetic studies in the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium from the Shanghai-1, Shanghai-2 and Shanghai-3 sample series. The early series include colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study and Shanghai Men’s Health Study, with additional controls from Shanghai breast cancer studies; Shanghai-3 includes colorectal cancer cases newly recruited through the Shanghai Cancer Registry in 2009–2011, with controls from the health cohorts and breast cancer studies.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:23263487</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:24836286</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:35765848</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002708"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">2368</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Pooled Shanghai-1, Shanghai-2 and Shanghai-3 sample described in the 2014 ACCC GWAS, PMID:24836286; an analysis collection, not a claimed lifetime recruitment total.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This study included 2,368 cases and 8,219 controls from three case- control collections, Shanghai-1, Shanghai-2 and Shanghai-3.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
