        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:19706757</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Polymorphisms in DNA repair genes, smoking, and bladder cancer risk: findings from the international consortium of bladder cancer.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:19706757</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study we present results from meta- and pooled analyses conducted as part of the International Consortium of Bladder Cancer.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium formed in 2005 that pools comparable data from independent bladder cancer studies to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors and their interactions. Its collaborative analyses combine case-control and case-only data, including investigations of DNA repair gene variation and cigarette smoking in bladder cancer susceptibility.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:19706757</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfCases"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6348</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Case and control data contributed by the twelve case-control studies and one case-only study in the 2009 ICBC DNA repair analysis, before restricting to non-Latino white origin; not a lifetime unique consortium enrollment total.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Twelve studies contributed case-control data and one study provided case-only data, to the ICBC, for a total of 6,348 cases and 6,752 controls (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfControls"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">6752</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Case and control data contributed by the twelve case-control studies and one case-only study in the 2009 ICBC DNA repair analysis, before restricting to non-Latino white origin; not a lifetime unique consortium enrollment total.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Twelve studies contributed case-control data and one study provided case-only data, to the ICBC, for a total of 6,348 cases and 6,752 controls (Table 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
