        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:26656478</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An international consortium that studies inherited susceptibility to glioma through a familial glioma study and the Glioma International Case-Control Study. It recruits families affected by multiple gliomas and coordinates multisite case-control recruitment, questionnaire data and biospecimen collection to investigate genetic risk and gene-environment interactions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GLIOGENE Consortium also denotes Gliogene study (COHO:0001812); this term is Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">The acronym GLIOGENE also denotes Gliogene study (COHO:0001812); this term is Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium.</obo:IAO_0000116>
