        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:31792088</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Alcohol Consumption, Cigarette Smoking, and Risk of Breast Cancer for &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;BRCA1&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;BRCA2&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; Mutation Carriers: Results from The BRCA1 and BRCA2 Cohort Consortium.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:31792088</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7611162/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The combined cohort (“The BRCA1 and BRCA2 Cohort Consortium”) included data from 21 centres in Western countries (supplemental Table 1S).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:28632866</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31792088</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32665703</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">9845</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Women with BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants in the BBCC pooled dataset described by PMID31792088, after excluding 14 carriers of variants in both genes; includes women eligible for retrospective and/or prospective first-breast-cancer analyses. (2020)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7611162/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The total cohort enrolled 9,845 BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers aged 18-80 years (after excluding 14 carriers of a mutation in both genes) (19, 23).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722"/>
