        <obo:IAO_0000116>Participants enrolled in GENEPSO in the updated database as of December2019 (dataset2 of the record-linkage paper).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8320036/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>This optimal linkage method was then applied on the updated version (dataset 2) of the two studies as of December 2019. The updated version counted 6375 participants for GEMO (i.e. 1687 new participants), and 4925 participants for GENEPSO (i.e. 1586 new participants).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>GENEPSO</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid23154"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:18930283</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide clinical prostate cancer registry in Sweden, originating from a regional register established in 1987 and covering the country since 1998, that records newly diagnosed prostate cancer, diagnostic workup, tumour characteristics and primary treatment to support quality assurance, benchmarking and clinical research on care and outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NPCR</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>National Prostate Cancer Register</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid23154">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid23154"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12516312/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The National Prostate Cancer Register (NPCR) of Sweden is a clinical cancer register with the aim of increasing the quality of care for men with prostate cancer by providing data to assess adherence to national guidelines [1, 2].</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22561842+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Other health-care regions joined and since 1998 virtually all prostate cancer (PCa) cases are registered in the National Prostate Cancer Register (NPCR) of Sweden to provide data for quality assurance, bench marking and clinical research.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:18930283</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Surveillance and deferred treatment for localized prostate cancer. Population based study in the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:18930283</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18930283+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with a 98% coverage vs the compulsory Swedish Cancer Registry, we identified 8,304 incident cases of prostate cancer in 1997 to 2002 with age younger than 70 years, clinical local stage T1 or 2, N0 or Nx, M0 or Mx and serum prostate specific antigen less than 20 ng/ml.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide clinical prostate cancer registry in Sweden, originating from a regional register established in 1987 and covering the country since 1998, that records newly diagnosed prostate cancer, diagnostic workup, tumour characteristics and primary treatment to support quality assurance, benchmarking and clinical research on care and outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:22561842</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:41078339</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NPCR</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <rdf:type rdf:nodeID="genid23160"/>
        <coho:hasSubCohort rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <coho:isSubCohortOf rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>PMID:20562373</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7960</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NPCR Follow-up Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>NPCR of Sweden Follow-up Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid23160">
        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_patients_with"/>
        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008315"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:nodeID="genid23160"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>localized prostate cancer</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Follow-up Study was an observational study in the NPCR, with the aim of assessing outcome among patients with localized prostate cancer who were diagnosed after PSA testing had become prevalent in Sweden and for whom curative treatment may have been indicated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweden"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Verification of eligibility, data on treatment, and the date that surveillance was terminated were extracted from medical records by research nurses in each of six health-care regions in Sweden at a median time of 4 years after the date of diagnosis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/isSubCohortOf"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>The Follow-up Study was an observational study in the NPCR, with the aim of assessing outcome among patients with localized prostate cancer who were diagnosed after PSA testing had become prevalent in Sweden and for whom curative treatment may have been indicated.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>PMID:20562373</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Outcomes in localized prostate cancer: National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden follow-up study.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:20562373</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study, a nationwide cohort, we identified 6849 patients aged 70 years or younger.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:20562373</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:31343436</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">7960</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Patients accepting inclusion in the original NPCR Follow-up Study, with diagnoses/registration 1997–2002; eligible frame8304. (1997–2002 diagnoses)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In total, 8304 patients fulfilled these criteria and 7960 accepted inclusion to the study (Figure 1).</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>NPCR Follow-up Study</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
