    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>MTBLS12705</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A study of adult AARP members aged 50 to 74 years recruited from the Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, United States, in 2012 and followed for 12 months with repeated dietary, physical activity and biomarker measurements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1110</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IDATA</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>IDATA Study</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#MetaboLight_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Interactive Diet and Activity Tracking in AARP Study</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12091781/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In brief, IDATA participants were recruited from a list of AARP members, aged 50–74 years, who resided in or nearby Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, spoke English, had internet access, were not on a weight-loss diet, and were free of major medical conditions and mobility limitations.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MTBLS12705</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Identification and validation of poly-metabolite scores for diets high in ultra-processed food: An observational study and post-hoc randomized controlled crossover-feeding trial.</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PMID:40392756</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metabolights/ws/studies/public/study/MTBLS12705</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>We aimed to identify poly-metabolite scores in blood and urine that are predictive of UPF intake.METHODS AND FINDINGS: Of the 1082 Interactive Diet and Activity Tracking in AARP (IDATA) Study (clinicaltrials.gov ID NCT03268577) participants, aged 50-74 years, who provided biospecimen consent, n=718 with serially collected blood and urine and one to six 24-hour dietary recalls (ASA-24s), collected over 12-months, met eligibility criteria and were included in the metabolomics analysis.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A study of adult AARP members aged 50 to 74 years recruited from the Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, United States, in 2012 and followed for 12 months with repeated dietary, physical activity and biomarker measurements.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:32819883</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1110</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>adult AARP members aged 50 to 74 recruited (2012)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32819883+AND+SRC%3AMED&amp;format=json&amp;resultType=core</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>From January through September 2012, 1,110 adult members of AARP, 50 to 74 years of age, were recruited from the Pittsburgh, PA, area to participate in the Interactive Diet and Activity Tracking in AARP (IDATA) study.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002735"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>IDATA</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasSynonymType rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000"/>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002736 -->

    <owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002736">
        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000000"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <coho:has_data_collection_location rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Europe"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000112>MTBLS7389</obo:IAO_0000112>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A citizen-science cohort of women in Belgium who provided self-collected vaginal samples and completed extensive questionnaires, to characterise the vaginal microbiome and its associations with health, lifestyle and life-course events.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <coho:numberOfParticipants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3345</coho:numberOfParticipants>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Isala citizen-science project</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Isala program</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho#MetaboLight_subset"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Isala</rdfs:label>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002736"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/has_data_collection_location"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Belgium"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10627828/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>As only participants who understood Dutch were allowed to participate, most participants were from the Northern part of Belgium.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002736"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>MTBLS7389</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dcterms:title>Riboflavin produced in the vagina by lactobacilli as symbiotic factor</dcterms:title>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/metabolights/ws/studies/public/study/MTBLS7389</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>In this study, we analyzed the vaginal microbiome and metabolome of 258 healthy women from the Isala program.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002736"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A citizen-science cohort of women in Belgium who provided self-collected vaginal samples and completed extensive questionnaires, to characterise the vaginal microbiome and its associations with health, lifestyle and life-course events.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>PMID:37884815</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
        <dcterms:contributor>Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09</dcterms:contributor>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002736"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/numberOfParticipants"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3345</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>women whose self-collected vaginal samples were analysed (of 6,007 who registered), 2020</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10627828/fullTextXML</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <rdfs:comment>Here we established the Isala citizen-science project to analyse the vaginal microbiomes of 3,345 women in Belgium (18–98 years) through self-sampling, 16S amplicon sequencing and extensive questionnaires.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


