        <rdfs:comment>Women were defined as being at risk of preterm birth if they had a history of cervical excisional treatment for pre-cancerous cells, a previous preterm birth or mid-trimester loss, or other risk factors such as previous caesarean section at full cervical dilation or congenital uterine anomaly.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Axiom>
