        <obo:IAO_0000115>A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.</obo:IAO_0000115>
